window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: A Mixed Bag of Emotions, Celebrating the New Year Amidst Busyness","paragraphs":["The moment the door closed, the smile on Dongfang Yukun's face gradually faded.","With a serious expression, he questioned Song Qiming, Did you know that Lord Cai wanted to send you to the southwest?","Song Qiming set down his chopsticks and looked at Dongfang Yukun.","I knew. In fact, it was my idea.","Dongfang Yukun's eyes widened. He stood up abruptly, pointing at Song Qiming, and said, I was just saying that Lord Cai hasn't targeted you since he took power, so why would he send you to the southwest? It turns out you asked for it yourself!","What were you thinking? Even if you're transferred out of the capital, you should have chosen a better place. Did you really have to go be the prefect of Suining?","That place borders the territories of foreign tribes. The people are fierce, and it's a chaotic mix of good and bad. If a war breaks out with the tribes, your situation will be terrible.","Song Qiming reached out and pulled him back down to his seat.","I know martial arts. Even if a fight breaks out, I'll be fine. The southwest may be chaotic, but it also holds great opportunities. I just want to go there to gain some experience.","Dongfang Yukun furrowed his brows tightly.","Does County Princess Linghui know? Can she really be at ease letting you go?","Song Qiming replied with a faint smile, My sister is going too.","Dongfang Yukun's brows relaxed slightly. So the whole family is moving?","Song Qiming nodded. Recently, the Emperor's attitude toward Prince Ying has softened. Coupled with the matters concerning my teacher and Lord Fei, I just wanted to leave the capital and return in a few years.","Seeing that his mind was made up, Dongfang Yukun picked up his wine cup and took a large gulp.","Leaving is fine, and being transferred as the prefect of Suining is considered a promotion. I just feel that the southwest is unstable, and being a prefect there will be very difficult.","Song Qiming raised his cup and clinked it against Dongfang Yukun's. It is exactly because it is difficult that it will be easier to make significant political achievements. I also want to see the southwest for myself; after all, it is a major hidden danger for the imperial court.","Dongfang Yukun looked at Song Qiming, his eyes full of helplessness.","How can you have such grand ambitions at such a young age? Once you actually get to the southwest, you will definitely regret it.","Hearing this, Song Qiming did not know whether to laugh or cry.","You are only two years older than me, yet your way of thinking is exactly like Lord Dongfang.","Turning his head to look out the window, he saw snowflakes falling in thick clusters.","At a glance, the world was completely silent, and the entire capital seemed to be weighed down by the heavy snow.","Dongfang Yukun said slowly, Since I was young, my grandfather and father have placed great hopes on me. I grew up listening to matters of the officialdom, and being constantly exposed to it, I've long grown accustomed to certain things.","Song Qiming twitched the corners of his mouth, turning his head to look out the window as his thoughts gradually drifted away.","The four members of the Song family spent this New Year in a flurry of busyness.","Song Jinzhao was busy handling their businesses in the capital.","Aside from going out for small gatherings with friends, Song Qiming stayed at home to review information on the eighteen foreign tribes of the southwest.","He learned about local customs, even picked up a few phrases in the local dialect, and dug up records of their past grievances, reading them over two or three times.","Song Shixue ran back and forth between the study and the pharmacy, occasionally coming over to ask Song Jinzhao about a few difficult medical cases.","The youngest, Song Anhao, wandered around all three of them.","In the morning, she stayed by Song Jinzhao's side to accompany her as she reviewed the account books; in the afternoon, she stayed in the pharmacy to help Song Shixue pound medicine; in between, she had to study under Song Qiming's watchful eye; and during her free time, she still had to play with Xuetuan.","The busier they were, the faster time flew. In the blink of an eye, it was time for the imperial court to resume official duties after the New Year.","The Ministry of Personnel submitted the compiled list of official transfers from various regions.","At night in the imperial study, a whole row of backlogged memorials from various regions was laid out, with several more stacks piled on the adjacent table.","Xiao Chengjing was hunched over the imperial desk, working diligently. In just one night, Zhao Yande had already trimmed the lamp wick three times.","Seeing that it was getting late, Zhao Yande walked over cautiously to remind him, Your Majesty, it is already the third watch. It is time to rest.","With only a few memorials left unread in the stack at hand, Xiao Chengjing decided to finish them before going to sleep."]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: Can I smoothly transfer to the Southwest","paragraphs":["Picking up the last memorial and seeing that it was a transfer list submitted by the Ministry of Personnel, Xiao Chengjing glanced over it and was about to approve it immediately.","But when he saw the name Song Qiming, his gaze paused.","Song Qiming had not even been in the Hanlin Academy for a full three years. Why was he being transferred to be the Prefect of Suining? Was this the Ministry of Personnel's idea, or...?","Xiao Chengjing thought for a moment, then closed the memorial and set it aside.","He turned his head and instructed Zhao Yande, After tomorrow's morning assembly, summon the Minister of Personnel and the Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy for an audience.","Yes. Zhao Yande bowed his head in compliance. His eyes secretly swept over the memorial, already understanding the situation in his heart.","After the morning assembly the next day, the Minister of Personnel, Zhu Hanzhi, and the Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy, Cai Qiong, were called to the Imperial Study.","The two had mentally prepared themselves in advance.","What should they say? How should they say it? They had rehearsed it long ago.","Your subjects greet Your Majesty.","Xiao Chengjing opened yesterday's memorial, his gaze sweeping over the calm faces of Zhu Hanzhi and Cai Qiong.","Transferring Song Qiming to be the Prefect of Suining, whose idea was this?","In Xiao Chengjing's view, it was impossible for Song Qiming to volunteer to go to the southwest to suffer; he must have been forced into the transfer.","Cai Qiong cupped his hands and answered, To answer Your Majesty, it was I who recommended him to Minister Zhu.","Since Compiler Song entered the Hanlin Academy, whether compiling history or drafting documents, he has been extremely rigorous and meticulous. However, he is still young and inexperienced. Although he has thousands of books in his heart, it is ultimately just theoretical knowledge that cannot be put into practice. Therefore, I wanted to send him out to gain some experience, so that he can take on heavy responsibilities in the future and share Your Majesty's burdens sooner.","Xiao Chengjing stared deeply at Cai Qiong.","Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang had insisted on punishing Prince Qi and were demoted together. Since Song Qiming was Ye Liangyu's only student, Cai Qiong probably wanted to drive him away.","A promotion in name but a demotion in reality, not wanting to leave any evidence behind.","Beloved Subject Zhu, do you think Song Qiming can shoulder the heavy responsibility of being the Prefect of Suining?","Even though Suining Prefecture was a rotten bone that everyone despised, the official sent there could not be without talent.","It was already a place where dragons and snakes mixed; if he could not suppress them, chaos would surely erupt.","Zhu Hanzhi raised his head to answer Xiao Chengjing's question. There was no abnormality on his face; instead, he looked righteous and stern.","To answer Your Majesty, during the palace examination three years ago, when asked how the imperial court should handle the rise of the southwestern foreign tribes, Compiler Song's policy essay was graded as the best of the first class.","The current Prefect of Suining has encountered fleeing bandits multiple times while out observing the people's conditions. Since then, he has to bring hundreds of yamen runners every time he goes out. I have heard that Compiler Song knows martial arts, so he is an excellent candidate to go to the southwest.","Xiao Chengjing frowned in deep thought. Looking at it this way, Song Qiming was indeed very suitable to go to the southwest.","It was just that...","Thinking back to the many merits Song Jinzhao had achieved, would it not be somewhat inappropriate to send her younger brother to the remote southwest?","His fingers, which had developed slight calluses, tapped the desk absentmindedly. For a moment, Xiao Chengjing was a bit hesitant.","You may step down first. I will consider this matter further.","Cai Qiong and Zhu Hanzhi bowed and withdrew. Just as they stepped out the door and wanted to exchange a few words, they saw Prince Ying approaching with a box in hand.","The two cupped their hands, stepped to the sides, and bowed. Greetings, Your Highness Prince Ying.","At this moment, Xiao Rongyan was in a fairly good mood. He nodded at them and had the eunuch go in to announce his arrival.","After being brought into the Imperial Study, he smiled broadly and said to Xiao Chengjing, Imperial Father, I have recently obtained an authentic painting of River Sails and Maple Leaves by Li Sunxun, and I have specially come to admire it with you.","Hearing that it was an authentic work by Li Sunxun, Xiao Chengjing's attention was successfully piqued.","Is it really authentic? He stood up and walked down the steps.","Xiao Rongyan took the painting out of the box and showed it to Xiao Chengjing.","I have already had it appraised by multiple master painters; it is absolutely an authentic work by Li Sunxun.","After viewing the painting, Xiao Chengjing's brows were filled with smiles, and he could not suppress the corners of his mouth.","Fondling it admiringly, he placed the painting on the desk to appreciate it once more.","Seeing that the Emperor liked it so much, Xiao Rongyan took the opportunity to curry favor. This painting is a gift for Imperial Father. I will have people keep an eye out for more in the future.","The memorial on the desk was swept onto the floor by the painting scroll. Xiao Rongyan bent down to pick it up, and upon seeing its contents, his expression froze slightly.","Noticing that the dropped memorial was the one concerning Song Qiming, Xiao Chengjing, who was in an excellent mood, asked casually.","The Ministry of Personnel wants to transfer Song Qiming to be the Prefect of Suining. What do you think?","Xiao Rongyan clenched his jaw, desperately suppressing the joy that gushed forth in his heart.","I do not pay much attention to the affairs of the Ministry of Personnel, but Compiler Song is young, promising, and quite talented. I am sure he can shoulder this heavy responsibility.","Not even a dog would go to a place like the southwest. It would be best if he never came back for the rest of his life, taking Song Jinzhao with him. If they could end up with the same fate as Xiao Rongche, that would be even better."]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: Successful Provocation and Preparations Before Departure","paragraphs":["Xiao Chengjing signaled with his eyes for Zhao Yande to put the painting away.","\"The southwest is remote and prone to unrest. Transferring Song Qiming there will inevitably be dangerous; it cannot be compared to other places.\"","Xiao Rongyan quietly took a deep breath.","He had to take this perfect opportunity to get rid of Song Qiming and make them roll out of the capital.","\"It is precisely because the position of Suining Prefect is difficult that it requires a fearless young official like Compiler Song to govern it.\"","\"As a minister, one should be loyal to the sovereign, love the country, and take the world as one's responsibility. To be able to share Imperial Father's burdens is Compiler Song's honor.\"","Xiao Chengjing thought about it and felt it made sense. As an emperor, why should he have so many reservations about the transfer of a single official?","But as the words reached his lips, a hint of hesitation arose in his heart.","\"County Princess Linghui has contributed greatly. If I transfer Song Qiming to the southwest, I worry she will harbor resentment.\"","Xiao Rongyan furrowed his brows slightly, a look of strong disapproval on his face.","\"Although County Princess Linghui has made many contributions, Imperial Father has also rewarded her handsomely. From a lowly peasant girl to an esteemed county princess, even Song Qiming was appointed as Tanhua by Imperial Father, and the position of sixth-rank compiler was an exceptional promotion.\"","\"Gold, silver, treasures, and a grand mansion, which of these was not bestowed by Imperial Father? If she harbors a grudge because of this, then she is truly ungrateful.\"","\"Furthermore, the Suining Prefect is a lower fifth-rank official. Jumping two ranks is a major promotion. If Song Qiming were sent out as a regional official in half a year, he would be at most a sixth-rank official. How could that compare to the high rank in Suining?\"","As he spoke, Xiao Rongyan suddenly lowered his head and sighed softly.","\"But it is not strange for Imperial Father to have such concerns. After all, ever since eldest brother returned from the southwest, his eyes have never been cured. They all say County Princess Linghui possesses superb medical skills. I presume she is dissatisfied with me and my imperial brother, which is why she did not do her best.\"","Faced with Xiao Rongyan's series of instigations, Xiao Chengjing gradually fell silent.","His expression darkened. Recalling the grievances between Song Jinzhao and his two sons, and then thinking of Prince Qi being reduced to a cripple and sent to Jinzhou to fend for himself, a surge of anger swelled in his heart, growing into deepening dissatisfaction.","\"You are right. The Song family has indeed become somewhat arrogant from favor. I had Ye Liangyu flogged, so presumably, Song Qiming is also resentful. He is young and aggressive; he should go to the southwest to gain experience and properly temper his character.\"","Seeing that his goal had been achieved, Xiao Rongyan lowered his head and smiled smugly.","Daring to oppose him, this time he absolutely had to banish the Song family so they could never return to the capital.","This time, Xiao Chengjing did not hesitate. He picked up his brush and wrote the word Approved on the memorial.","After writing, he looked down at the memorial for a few seconds, then puffed out his chest and ordered, \"Deliver this memorial to the Ministry of Personnel. Tell them I have approved it. Let Song Qiming work hard in Suining; I think highly of him.\"","\"Yes,\" Zhao Yande replied, bowing deeply, not daring to breathe loudly.","He had heard Prince Ying's instigations loud and clear. Unfortunately, those involved are often blind while bystanders see clearly. The emperor had likely been blinded and carried away by the other party's provocative words.","However, even if he thought it through later, he probably would have already developed a rift with County Princess Linghui.","One naturally protects one's own son, while outsiders can be dealt with however one pleases.","Although Song Qiming was prepared, when he personally received the appointment documents, he could not help but heave a heavy sigh of relief, feeling a vast sense of finality that the grand scheme had been set.","The departure time was set for three days later.","Song Anhao withdrew from the Dongfang family's school. The servants in the manor gradually loaded all the luggage onto the carriages, while Song Jinzhao took a carriage to the estate outside the city the next day.","In the simple front hall, the doors and windows were tightly shut, and servants guarded outside to prevent anyone from approaching.","Even the managers, Chen Fu and Li Hou, were not allowed inside."]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: Want to Bring Quya and Guan Nianshan Along","paragraphs":["Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan, who had been summoned suddenly, looked at Song Jinzhao with apprehension, unsure of what this was all about.","The young master had been gone for so long; surely she wasn't going to pursue the matter now.","Seeing the two men gradually losing their composure, their fingers rubbing nervously against their clothes and their eyes darting around, Song Jinzhao knew the atmosphere was just right.","She slowly lifted the lid of her teacup and took a light sip.","\"According to the imperial court's transfer order, Qiming will be going to the southwest to take up a post in a few days, and I, the County Princess, will go with him.\"","\"I hear that you two know martial arts. Would you be willing to serve me and go to the southwest together?\"","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan's eyes widened sharply.","The young master was in the southwest. Was County Princess Linghui doing this on purpose, or...?","At the thought that Song Jinzhao might know Huo Chong's true identity, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan broke out in a cold sweat.","Guan Nianshan swallowed hard, his heart pounding.","\"It is this humble one's honor to be valued by the County Princess, but my eyes are impaired, and my wife and children are all here on the estate. I truly do not wish to leave the capital, so I beg the County Princess for forgiveness.\"","After giving the token to Huo Chong, the heavy burden in Guan Nianshan and Qu Ya's hearts had been completely lifted.","Now they just wanted to live a good, quiet life on the estate and think of nothing else.","Qu Ya nodded cautiously in agreement, his heart full of wariness toward Song Jinzhao.","Seeing them so vigilant, a sharp glint flashed across Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Changing her tone, she said slowly, \"Suining Prefecture is close to the territory of the foreign tribes in the southwest, and Huo Chong is an old friend of yours. Taking you there is also a way for me to forge a good connection. You can bring your families. If you stay in the capital, you will only be able to hide on this estate and eke out a meager existence for the rest of your lives, and even your wives and children will have to suffer along with you.\"","\"Once you go to the southwest, the ocean is boundless for fish to leap, and the sky is vast for birds to fly. You will no longer have to worry about your identities as the Wu Family Army being discovered. Not only can you hold posts in the government office, but I can also arrange for your sons to attend a private school. If they want to practice martial arts, you can teach them yourselves or send them to a martial arts academy. At the very least, they won't end up achieving nothing, trapped on this small farm for their entire lives like you. Do not let your own choices ruin your children's futures.\"","Hearing the last sentence, Qu Ya clenched his fists, but Guan Nianshan's eyes genuinely lit up.","He stared straight at Song Jinzhao. Seeing that she didn't seem to be lying, he began to hesitate in his heart.","Before the incident, he had been the Marquis's most trusted subordinate, his personal bodyguard, managing over a thousand men under his command. Anyone who saw him had to respectfully call him General.","But after the incident, he became a stray dog. Not to mention losing an eye, he had to live an ignoble life, unable to go anywhere.","As time passed, he had accepted his fate, but whenever he looked at his son, he felt a stifling pain in his chest.","If nothing had happened, whether his son entered an academy or practiced martial arts, he would have had a promising future, rather than working on an estate like now, with no way out forever.","\"What does the County Princess want me to do?\"","Qu Ya's expression changed, and he turned his head to shout at him, \"Old Guan, what are you trying to do?\"","County Princess Linghui clearly wanted to use them. What if this harmed the young master?","Seeing them start to fight among themselves, Song Jinzhao stood up and said, \"I'll give you half an hour to consider.\"","While walking on the path to inspect the farm, Qingshuang couldn't help but ask, \"County Princess, why must we bring them along?\"","\"As your servant sees it, Huo Chong probably won't pledge allegiance to the County Princess just because of Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan. They don't carry enough weight to be hostages, and even if we bring them, they don't seem like people who would be entirely loyal to you.\"","Especially that Qu Ya. Just now, when Guan Nianshan was speaking, he looked as if he wanted to eat him alive.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan's attitude toward Huo Chong is unusual. I suspect he must be a descendant of Marquis Wuying. The fact that he sought out Zeng Qing shows he still wants revenge.\"","\"As long as our goals are the same, we can cooperate. Bringing those two along will make it easier to gain Huo Chong's trust. If we can get him on our side, with Huo Chong's status in Ning Prefecture, many things will be much easier to handle.\"","For parents, their children are their greatest weakness.","Especially for people like Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan who had fallen from high places, it only took a little bit of temptation to stir up the unwillingness hidden deep in their hearts."]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: Persuasion","paragraphs":["The moment the door clicked shut, Qu Ya could no longer suppress his inner anger.","His face was livid as he turned to face Guan Nianshan, immediately demanding, \"What exactly are you trying to do? Betraying The Marquis to serve County Princess Linghui is absolutely out of the question.\"","With no one else in the room, Guan Nianshan dropped his reservations.","He spoke in a calm tone, their eyes meeting. His gaze seemed to be looking far into the distance, yet also directly at Qu Ya.","\"I never thought of betraying The Marquis, but The Marquis is already dead.\"","Qu Ya choked up, his lips parting and closing for a moment without a sound.","He swallowed hard to force down the lump in his throat, his eyes growing slightly damp.","\"Even though The Marquis is dead, the young master is still here. Didn't we agree to stay on the estate to watch over our brothers and live a peaceful life?\"","They had refused to leave with Huo Chong back then, partly because they felt they would be a burden, and partly because they couldn't abandon the other surviving soldiers of the Wu Army on the estate.","Compared to Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan, the others were missing arms or legs, and they couldn't just leave them be.","Guan Nianshan clenched his jaw, spitting out his words one by one, even his brows furrowing with the effort.","\"Do you think that by refusing County Princess Linghui's invitation, our brothers will have a good life? The owner of the Daohua and Shiquan estates is the princess; this is her territory.\"","\"Think about the lives we led when this was still an imperial estate, and look at the lives we lead now. She didn't expose our identities, and she even gave us such high wages. This proves she is a good person.\"","Guan Nianshan grew more agitated as he spoke, his spit nearly flying into Qu Ya's face.","\"If we can work for the princess, we can protect the other brothers on the estate. They can live even better than they do now.\"","\"The young master hasn't yet gathered all the military forces of the southwestern tribes. The day he attacks the imperial court to avenge The Marquis and our brothers is still far away. Since that's the case, he won't be clashing with the princess anytime soon.\"","\"Besides, have you ever thought that if they really do fight one day, our staying by the princess's side to work for her might be an opportunity? We might even be able to help the young master.\"","Qu Ya took a step forward, staring intently into Guan Nianshan's eyes as he asked, \"Is that really what you think?\"","Guan Nianshan resisted the urge to swallow and said firmly, \"Of course.\"","\"The young master is the only bloodline of The Marquis. I will never do anything to harm him.\"","After saying this, he threw a question back at Qu Ya.","\"Think about what County Princess Linghui has done over the past two years. Do you think she is the kind of ruthless person who cannot distinguish right from wrong?\"","His rough lips pressed into a thin line, Qu Ya fell silent.","Although they stayed on the estate, they had heard a lot about matters on the outside.","Song Jinzhao had high prestige among the common people. When discussing her deeds, people could only sigh and say it was a pity she was born a woman.","The wind began to blow outside, rustling against the windows.","After an unknown amount of time, Qu Ya raised his head as if accepting his fate.","He said solemnly to Guan Nianshan, \"Then let's go. It would be even better if we can help the young master.\"","Guan Nianshan's tense shoulders suddenly relaxed.","The corners of his mouth turned up slightly, and his tone when speaking to Qu Ya became as familiar as before.","\"We will definitely see him when we reach the southwest. I think this is a good thing.\"","After strolling around the estate, Song Jinzhao went to the perfume factory, where Fushun was doing the final handover with Lan Xi.","The business in the capital was too large, so someone trustworthy had to stay behind. This person also needed to be capable and familiar with all the shops. As the steward, Fushun was the most suitable candidate.","Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, the two immediately stopped and bowed to her.","\"Greetings to the princess.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"We depart the day after tomorrow. Is the handover complete?\"","Fushun smiled and replied, \"Please rest assured, Princess. This servant has stayed on the estate for a month and understands all matters, big and small, thoroughly. Nothing will go wrong.\"","Lan Xi nodded at Song Jinzhao.","\"For the latter half of the month, Fushun has been managing the factory's affairs while I just watched. He is already very proficient.\"","As the three were talking, Chen Fu walked in from outside, his footsteps appearing somewhat hurried.","\"Princess, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan said they want to see you.\" They wouldn't say what it was about, and it felt a bit strange.","Even though he and Li Hou were more heavily relied upon, the princess had sought those two out privately.","Song Jinzhao blinked slightly.","They couldn't wait to call for her before even half an hour had passed. It seemed they had made their decision."]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: A Conversation Between Master and Disciple Before Parting","paragraphs":["Back in the room, before Song Jinzhao could even sit down, Guan Nianshan spoke up impatiently, As long as what the Princess just said is true, Qu Ya and I are willing to go to the Southwest to work for you.","Qu Ya cast a somewhat disgusted glance at Guan Nianshan.","Being so impatient, it felt like he was bound to be played by the other party sooner or later.","We will not do anything that violates the laws of heaven and reason; that is our bottom line.","Song Jinzhao nodded without hesitation. Of course. I have always been a law-abiding citizen, and I only do good deeds.","I am only hiring you. I am not asking you to sell yourselves into slavery or sign a contract. If you are unwilling, you can leave at any time.","Given that they could live incognito for so many years waiting for Huo Chong's return, and considering their loyalty to the Marquis of Wuying, Song Jinzhao did not expect them to be dead set on serving her.","Similarly, she would not completely rely on them; everything was just a tie to maintain a connection with Huo Chong.","As long as their goals aligned, everything could be discussed. It would be even better if she could convince Huo Chong to work for her.","Go back and pack your things first. Someone will come to call for you the day after tomorrow when we depart.","By the time she returned to the Princess's estate, many of the furnishings in the room had already been cleared out, making it look quite empty.","On the night before their departure, Song Qiming went to the Ye residence to bid farewell to Ye Liangyu.","Teacher, there will definitely be personnel transfers in the court after this year's metropolitan examination. The Emperor's attitude toward you is not good right now. Have you considered being transferred to a provincial post?","If his sister really led an army to attack the capital one day, he didn't want his teacher to suffer the consequences.","Ye Liangyu looked at Song Qiming with eyes full of gratification.","He had only taken in one student in his entire life. He had originally planned to protect him so he could rise peacefully, but the world was unpredictable, and he himself had stumbled first.","Fortunately, Princess Linghui was there to support him. Over the years, he had come to see that she was a formidable person.","If she were a man, she could absolutely pierce the heavens. It was just a pity she was a woman.","Ye Liangyu smiled and slowly shook his head. I want to stay in the capital. This is the closest place to the court, and I need to keep watching.","Song Qiming understood what he meant.","But precisely because he understood, he was secretly stunned and shifted his gaze away.","His teacher still hadn't given up on the Emperor; he was worried about the future of the Dongzhao Kingdom and wanted to keep a close eye on it himself.","Thinking of this, he couldn't help but start to ponder.","If his teacher ever found out about his sister's intention to rebel, which side would he stand on?","The more he thought about it, the more confused his mind became.","Ye Liangyu said, Qiming?","Seeing Song Qiming suddenly space out, Ye Liangyu put on a stern face and shouted at him, Qiming.","His eardrums vibrating, Song Qiming instantly snapped back to reality. He looked at Ye Liangyu with a slightly flustered expression. What is it, Teacher?","Ye Liangyu's expression turned serious. Listen carefully and remember everything I say.","The Southwest is impoverished, and multiple factions are mixed together. Once you arrive in Suining, you must listen to Princess Linghui.","There is also Gu Zhongxun. This man is a good official, but if he finds out that you want to be the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest, he will definitely not give you a good look.","Song Qiming nodded. I know. My sister said he wants his son to take over his position.","Ye Liangyu nodded heavily. So, after you arrive in the Southwest, you must say that you are there to gain experience and that you will return to the capital after a few years. With Princess Linghui there, they will believe this story. It is difficult for others to be transferred back to the capital, but it will not be difficult for you.","Do not make enemies with the Gu family, and be modest in all things. If the foreign tribes in the Southwest ever really go to war against the imperial court, remember to protect yourself. If you ever find yourself in a near-death situation, remember to run for your life.","Song Qiming looked into Ye Liangyu's eyes in astonishment. I thought Teacher would say that I must live and die with the people and never be a fleeing official.","Ye Liangyu smiled, but his smile was a bit bitter.","If a man of my age dies, then he dies. You are still young, and you have a long life ahead of you. Staying alive is more important than anything else.","Song Qiming looked into his deep eyes and seemed to understand why.","His throat bobbed, and he gradually became a little choked up.","Teacher, please take care of your health and wait for my return."]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: Leaving the Capital","paragraphs":["On the day they left the capital, the grand convoy loaded with luggage consisted of a full ten carriages.","Young Song Anhao waited for Xuetuan to get into the carriage before turning his head to look back at the gates of the Song Manor, feeling more dejected than ever before.","His memories of their time living in the capital were the deepest. He had even made several good friends at the Dongfang household. Knowing they were leaving, he had been sad for days.","\"Sister, can we still come back?\" Song Anhao looked up with eyes full of reliance, his large eyes welling with tears.","Song Jinzhao bent down and scooped him into her arms, his warm breath brushing against her face.","\"Of course we can. By the time we return, you will have grown up.\"","Some endeavors took three to five years just to get off the ground. With four years left before Gu Zhongxun retired, they definitely wouldn't be returning to the capital anytime soon.","Song Anhao turned and wrapped his arms around Song Jinzhao's neck, burying his face against her. \"Ah You said Suining is very far away, and it will be hard to meet. What if I miss him?\"","Song Jinzhao carried him into the carriage and set him down, affectionately stroking her younger brother's hair.","\"You can write letters to him. It's about as far as going back to Song Family Village.\"","The convoy consisted of over a hundred servants and guards, most of whom were relatively young.","They flanked the carriages, longswords equipped at their waists, their vigilant eyes constantly scanning the surroundings to prevent any assassinations.","As they passed the official road leading to the farmstead, Manager Chen Fu, along with the Qu and Guan families, had already been waiting at the intersection for quite some time.","Despite all his calculations, he never expected Song Jinzhao to take Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan to the southwest. Ever since Chen Fu found out the day before yesterday, his mood had been incredibly complicated.","Even as the wives and children of Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan boarded the carriages, Chen Fu couldn't help but admonish the two men one last time.","\"Work hard by the County Princess's side, and absolutely do not cause trouble. Don't forget there are still so many people back at the estate.\"","The former subordinates of the Wu Family Army were no ordinary people. These two were considered relatively able-bodied, but if they angered the County Princess, Chen Fu feared it would implicate the other tenant farmers on the estate.","The moment Guan Nianshan, who hadn't ridden a horse in over twenty years, swung himself into the saddle, memories of leading troops into battle in his youth instantly surged into his mind.","He took a deep breath and let out a long sigh, then said to Chen Fu, \"Rest assured, Manager Chen, we know our limits.\"","Beside him, Qu Ya's gaze swept over each of the guards.","They uniformly possessed broad shoulders and narrow waists, with well-built, muscular limbs that exuded strength.","Regardless of gender, their straight backs were like taut lines. When they walked, their strides seemed precisely measured by a ruler; their center of gravity fell on their heels, yet their footsteps were incredibly quiet.","These people had undoubtedly undergone rigorous training. County Princess Linghui had such high standards for her guards that they could already compare to the Wu Family Army's most formidable Black Armored Cavalry from back in the day.","This time, Song Jinzhao took all the horses raised on the farmstead with her.","Each of the over one hundred guards had a horse, and even the kitchen maids rode on horseback in the middle of the formation. Their overall speed wasn't exactly fast, but they didn't dawdle on the road either.","On the afternoon they left the capital, upon hearing a eunuch's report in the imperial palace, Xiao Chengjing looked up in surprise.","\"County Princess Linghui also went to Suining?\"","Zhao Yande nodded. \"It seems she was worried about Prefect Song going to Suining alone. The County Princess took her other two younger siblings and went as well.\"","Ink smudged the writing as Xiao Chengjing put down his brush with a hint of displeasure.","\"They truly have a deep bond as siblings, to actually be willing to move the whole family to Suining to suffer.\"","Zhao Yande smiled but said nothing.","How could he not see through the Emperor's thoughts?","It was nothing more than wanting Song Jinzhao to stay in the capital while letting Song Qiming go suffer in Suining Prefecture alone.","County Princess Linghui possessed excellent medical skills. Although there were imperial physicians in the palace, keeping her in the capital was always a good precaution. What if she was too far away when an emergency arose?","Xiao Chengjing pondered for a moment before picking up his brush again.","Let her go, then. He was in good health and wouldn't need her for the time being anyway.","With her martial arts skills, her presence in Suining might even intimidate the foreign tribes in the southwest. Fewer disturbances would bring more stability to the imperial court."]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: The Gu Family: Father and Son","paragraphs":["Songzhou City, the provincial capital of the southwest.","Two massive stone qilin statues stood tall at the entrance of the Gu Residence. Their spherical eyes gazed straight ahead, exuding an air of solemn majesty.","The clattering of hooves came to a sudden halt. A young soldier in an armored helmet hurriedly tied his horse's reins to a wooden post by the door, then turned and dashed into the manor.","In the spacious martial arts arena, the father and son of the Gu family were sparring with longblades.","Seeing them, the soldier offered up a red-painted bamboo tube with both hands and shouted loudly, My Lord, a letter from the capital!","The intense clash of blades abruptly ceased. Gu Zhongxun wiped the sweat from his chin with his sleeve, breathing heavily as he ordered, Bring the letter here.","Opening the lid of the bamboo tube, which was filled with rice husks, Gu Zhongxun pulled out a slightly damp piece of letter paper.","Tiny, densely packed characters covered the page; though only the size of a palm, it contained hundreds of words.","Song Qiming, a compiler at the Hanlin Academy... why has he been transferred here? Gu Zhongxun furrowed his brows in confusion.","Gu Zhongxun's eldest son, Gu Gaoyuan, who was also the Prefect of Songzhou, leaned over to read the letter.","This name looks a bit familiar. Where have I seen it before?","Gu Zhongxun rolled up the letter and held it in his hand. The third-place scholar in the civil examinations of the twenty-seventh year of Yongyuan. He is only seventeen this year.","Gu Gaoyuan thought for a moment, then his eyes widened abruptly, his eyebrows shooting up.","The biological younger brother of County Princess Linghui, Song Jinzhao?","Yes, Gu Zhongxun nodded. His furrowed brows relaxed slightly, but his heart remained full of doubt.","He muttered to himself, With his status, even if Ye Liangyu was demoted, County Princess Linghui shouldn't be willing to let her brother come to the southwest. Why would he be transferred here to be the Prefect of Suining?","Gu Gaoyuan clicked his tongue and said, That's simple. The imperial court just negotiated the salt field profit-sharing with Panzhou, so there definitely won't be a war in the short term. This Song Qiming is absolutely here to build his credentials. After serving his three-year term, he will return for a major promotion.","Gu Zhongxun shook his head slightly.","He could go anywhere to build credentials. Suining Prefecture is not a good place.","Gu Gaoyuan replied, This is what they call a newborn calf unafraid of tigers. The more dangerous and difficult the place is, the more they want to go.","Gu Zhongxun sighed helplessly, feeling mentally exhausted.","Youthful hot blood. He'll be done for after just three months.","And in the end, it will be me who has to clean up the mess.","What are you talking about? A gruff male voice came from behind. Gu Huaiyuan, the garrison commander of Songzhou City sporting a short beard, walked toward them. He was Gu Zhongxun's second son.","Gu Gaoyuan smiled and put his blade back in its place. We're talking about the new Prefect of Suining sent by the imperial court. He is the biological younger brother of County Princess Linghui, only seventeen this year.","Gu Huaiyuan's footsteps paused for a moment, and a bright gleam flashed in his eyes.","Is County Princess Linghui coming?","Song Jinzhao's formidable reputation had shaken the entire Dongzhao Nation ever since she defeated Gong Linjue.","Especially in the hearts of military generals, her existence had already surpassed that of the Duke of Qing, Chu Liuyun.","Gu Gaoyuan curled his lips into a smile.","Definitely not. Suining Prefecture is remote and treacherous, not a good place at all. Why would she go there to suffer?","Gu Huaiyuan glared unhappily; in his heart, Song Jinzhao's image was incredibly grand.","Just because others wouldn't be willing doesn't mean County Princess Linghui wouldn't. Otherwise, how could she allow her brother to be transferred to Suining as Prefect? They might even be moving the whole family.","Stop arguing. Gu Zhongxun, who knew his two sons well, interrupted them.","We'll know whether she's coming or not when the time comes. By my calculations, Song Qiming will arrive in Songzhou City in a month.","Before taking up his post as the Prefect of Suining, Song Qiming would first need to visit the provincial capital to pay his respects to Gu Zhongxun. Before he assumed office, he had to be given a few words of instruction according to protocol.","However, he shared the same thought as his eldest son; he did not believe Song Jinzhao would come along with Song Qiming.","Building credentials would likely only take three years, and then he would quickly return. There was no need to drag the whole family over—it would be too much trouble."]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: A Narrow Path on the Precipitous Cliff","paragraphs":["The journey from the capital to Suining passed through three provinces and fourteen prefectures, and the road was far from peaceful.","However, Song Jinzhao's group was large, and everyone was armed. Whenever mountain bandits spotted them, they rarely dared to show their faces, opting instead to hide in the shadows and watch them pass.","They traveled like this all the way to the southwestern border, and the journey was relatively smooth.","The further southwest they went, the higher the temperature rose. The landscape transitioned from ice and snow to the first hints of spring. By the time they neared the southwestern border, the surrounding vegetation had grown lush and green.","Looking up at the towering peaks in the distance, Song Qiming opened the map and said, \"Sister, once we pass through these mountains ahead, we will reach the Southwestern Province.\"","\"But the map indicates that a section of the road in the middle is extremely dangerous. We have to walk along a cliff edge right against the mountain.\"","Song Jinzhao took the map and examined it carefully. There was only one path leading southwest; the surrounding areas were completely blank.","\"Let's rest here and eat lunch early. There might be falling rocks in the mountains, so we'll push straight through without stopping. We should be able to reach Longshan Town before dark.\"","Song Qiming gave a slight nod. He turned and ordered his subordinates, \"Rest here for an hour and eat lunch early.\"","Everyone dismounted, took out the dry rations they had bought that morning from their bundles, and began to eat.","They set off an hour later. At first, they traveled along a mountain trail, but after passing the first mountain, the path began to slope upward and grew increasingly narrow.","After passing through a pitch-black cave, a stone path built into the steep cliffside came into view.","The six-foot-wide path could only accommodate a single carriage. Right beside it was a bottomless abyss; with no guardrails, it felt as though one could fall over the edge at any moment.","Looking down, the mountain face stood almost perpendicular to the ground.","At the bottom of the cliff, a turbulent river constantly churned with white foam, occasionally revealing dark brown rocks. If someone were to fall, even if they didn't drown, they would likely be smashed to pieces against the rocks.","\"Have everyone form a single file line, stay close to the wall, and walk slowly.\"","As she walked, Song Jinzhao used her telescope to search the ground below for any possible mountain trails.","But after walking for nearly two miles, right up until they entered another cave, she didn't see any path suitable for horseback riding.","At the narrowest part of the river, huge boulders lined both sides, forming a small waterfall in the middle.","It wasn't impossible to cross there, but one could only pass through alone, and it would require someone exceptionally agile.","In other words, if they wanted to march through, their only option was this narrow mountain path built along the cliff.","The pace was slow, and with caves at both ends, it would be extremely dangerous if someone were lying in wait to ambush them at the entrances.","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows, her mind racing as she tried to think of alternative solutions.","The temperature on the mountain was low. Inside the carriage, Song Anhao still felt cold despite being wrapped in a blanket.","This was mainly because the carriage's curtains and windows were open, allowing the cold, biting wind to blow right through.","He pouted, feeling his heart beating a little fast.","\"Second Sister, I'm a bit cold. Can we pull the curtains down? Plus, it's so high up, I'm a little scared.\"","Beside him, Song Shixue was leaning over the table, her pen constantly sketching the surrounding routes and environment on paper. She added small notes beside her drawings with place names and areas to watch out for—this was the task Song Jinzhao had assigned her.","Although local government offices had maps of various regions, and they were also sold among the common folk, the only way to have a map that was one hundred percent accurate and reliable was to travel the route personally and record it.","Song Jinzhao had asked Song Shixue to draw it because sitting inside the carriage, she wouldn't attract any unwanted attention.","Hearing the fear in Song Anhao's voice, Song Shixue lifted her head.","Along the journey, the originally blank booklet had been mostly filled. Even the distances had been carefully calculated into miles based on time and speed, marked alongside the routes. It looked incredibly detailed.","\"Afraid of heights?\"","\"Yeah.\"","Song Anhao nodded, tightly hugging Xuetuan's neck and burying his face into it.","He didn't dare to look outside, but his curiosity got the better of him, making him steal glances every now and then.","And then he would feel even more scared.","Song Shixue first pulled down the door curtain, then unfolded the bedding stacked behind her and covered her younger brother with it.","\"Lie down and go to sleep. Cover your head, and you won't be able to see it.\""]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: Overnight in Longshan Town","paragraphs":["After passing through the cave again, the path ahead was all downhill.","The convoy began to travel through the gorge between two mountain peaks. On the steep rock faces, only a few short, yellowish-green blades of grass could be seen growing out of the crevices, along with some sparsely leaved shrubs. The entire mountain looked completely barren.","Once the ground leveled out, Song Jinzhao and the others began to speed up. They traversed six mountains in a row over the course of six hours, not arriving at Longshan Town at the foot of the mountain until the sun was nearing sunset.","A worker squatting at the entrance of the town spotted the approaching convoy from afar. He immediately stood up and took a couple of steps forward to get a clearer look.","Seeing a white towel draped over the man's shoulder, which indicated he was likely an inn or tavern worker, Song Jinzhao brought his horse to a halt.","Seeing this, Qingshuang was just about to ask a question when the worker beat him to it, calling out to Song Qiming, Are you looking for a place to stay, guest? My inn is just ahead. We have plenty of food and fodder.","Thank heavens, they had not had a single customer in over a month, and he finally saw some people. It was just that there seemed to be too many of them to fit.","They were led to the entrance of the inn, which was essentially just a large courtyard enclosed by a fence. In the middle was a row of houses built from stacked stones, with only five doors visible from the outside.","Afraid that they would find it too shabby, the worker began to explain as soon as they entered the yard.","Things are kept simple in a small place like this. There are only forty-two households in all of Longshan Town, and mine is the only inn. Please bear with us if anything is lacking.","Song Qiming swallowed hard; his stomach was already rumbling with hunger.","We have a lot of people, so I do not think we will all fit. Are there more rooms in the back?","The worker pointed at the house and said with a straight face, You will absolutely fit.","We have one superior room, and the other three are large communal sleeping quarters. One room can sleep thirty people. When there are too many people, they can also sleep in the lobby at night, which holds fifty people.","In truth, no one had ever slept there. The most guests they ever had at once was fifty, and that was three years ago.","Song Jinzhao handed the reins to Qingshuang.","We will spend the night here. Let us eat first.","They still had to cross another mountain to reach the next resting place, and the sky was already growing dark. No matter how primitive the conditions were, they had to spend the night here. Having an inn was better than nothing.","Hearing this, the worker beamed with joy and immediately shouted toward the house, Ah Fei, come out quickly and attend to the guests!","Soon, a young boy wearing a sheepskin hat ran out of the house. Coincidentally, at that exact moment, Xuetuan emerged from the carriage.","Before the boy could even clearly see how many people there were, he was so frightened by the tiger that he stumbled backward repeatedly.","His back hit the wall, and he screamed at the top of his lungs for his father to save him, Dad, there is a tiger!","The worker's reaction was half a beat slow. When he turned his head, his eyes met Xuetuan's pale blue gaze.","In an instant, the blood drained from his body. His knees went weak as he shielded his son, ready to bolt into the house.","Do not be afraid, that is our family's pet, Song Qiming hastily explained.","The old man and the young boy looked at Song Qiming as if they had lost their souls.","A pet? A tiger?","Song Qiming nodded. We raised it from a cub. It is quite docile.","He had already said the exact same thing hundreds of times on the road and was long used to it.","After all, very few people actually kept tigers as pets; most people could not run away fast enough when they saw a wild beast.","Cautiously, the worker led the group into the lobby. There were only four tables inside, so those who could not fit had to sit on the floor.","The entire inn had a staff of three: the worker was the boss, the cook was the boss's wife, and the young waiter was their son.","There were only four dishes on the menu. The only meat dishes were chicken and duck, which were raised in the backyard and slaughtered on the spot. There were only two vegetable dishes, one of which was dried vegetables.","Seeing that the three of them were too busy to handle it, Song Jinzhao, wanting to eat sooner, had his servants go help.","Even so, it was over an hour later by the time they finally got to eat.","With one hundred and thirty-eight people, a single meal consumed half of the inn's food reserves. The rest would be just enough for breakfast tomorrow morning."]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: Night Peep","paragraphs":["While eating, Song Qiming would pause from time to time to chat with the innkeeper.","\"So the bandits in Longtou Mountain are very formidable?\"","Longtou Mountain was the last mountain Song Jinzhao and her group had to cross tomorrow; once through, they would be in the Southwest Province.","The innkeeper nodded and explained, \"Originally, there were several dens of bandits in the surrounding mountains, but they were all wiped out by the bandits of Longtou Mountain. Their numbers have only been growing.\"","\"For the past two months, the weather was cold and heavy snow sealed the mountains, so there wasn't a single traveling merchant. You must be extremely careful when you pass through tomorrow.\"","Song Jinzhao took out a small silver ingot and placed it on the table.","\"Boss, you've run this inn here for so many years, you must know the background of these bandits very well. Is it convenient for you to tell us about them?\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao take out the silver, the man's eyes lit up.","He excitedly tucked the silver into his robe, nodding with a face full of flattering smiles.","\"Of course, of course. When it comes to the bandits of Longtou Mountain, they are...\"","He knew they would ask, but he didn't expect them to be so generous.","One tael of silver was enough to cover the inn's profits for several days.","The innkeeper spoke in detail, and Song Jinzhao and the others listened attentively.","At the door of the back kitchen, a young boy clung to the doorframe with both hands, secretly watching Anhao feed Xuetuan. His initial fear had already turned into envy.","\"Mother, I want to keep a tiger too.\"","A capable-looking woman slapped the boy on the shoulder.","\"What nonsense are you talking about? Keeping a tiger is so dangerous; it will eat people.\"","The boy pointed at Xuetuan and said, \"But how come it looks more obedient than a dog to me? That little brother was just rubbing its face hard, and it was so well-behaved and good.\"","The woman looked at Song Anhao and saw his soft little hands petting the top of the tiger's head back and forth, truly like petting a dog.","\"I guess it's because they raised it from a young age so it's close to them. They carry swords and are no ordinary people. You're even afraid of the snow leopards on the mountain, so don't even think about keeping a tiger. You wouldn't even be enough for one bite.\"","Not to mention anything else, seven chickens a meal was something their family couldn't afford to feed it.","After dinner, everyone briefly washed up and returned to their rooms to rest.","The moonlight shone on the bare mountains, making the night seem less dark.","The night was quiet and silent. Having traveled all day, everyone slept very soundly.","The superior room only had one bed. With the four Song siblings plus a tiger, Song Qiming could only sleep on the floor.","In the thatched hut behind the inn, a thin and small man had been continuously lying by the window.","It wasn't until the dead of night that he carefully opened the door and squeezed out sideways.","The man hunched over, pressing his body close to the fence as he circled to the front of the inn to look into the courtyard.","He saw ten horse-drawn carts full of boxes parked in the courtyard, and under the eaves were two more horse-drawn carriages with cabins.","Over a hundred horses crowded the entire courtyard to the brim.","The man gulped, his eyes flashing with excitement.","A big business, an absolutely huge business.","As long as he told the bandits this news, the reward would certainly not be small.","In the room, Song Jinzhao, lying on the bed, and Xuetuan, resting on the floor mat, opened their eyes at the same time.","Seeing it open its mouth to roar, Song Jinzhao immediately shot it a threatening look.","Xuetuan swallowed a mouthful of air and shook its head aggrievedly.","Song Jinzhao got up from the bed, pressed her finger against its forehead, and pushed it down.","Xuetuan lay back on the ground in frustration, covering its face with its paws, not wanting to speak.","The temperature at the foot of the mountain was low, so the windows were closed for sleeping at night.","Song Jinzhao walked to the window and listened carefully, but the footsteps had disappeared again.","After a while, the footsteps sounded again; it was the sound of shoe soles rubbing against gravel.","Judging by the sound, there should be only one person.","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes, a hint of danger showing between her brows.","Just as she wanted to wait for the other party to get closer, she found the footsteps getting further and further away, as if they were leaving."]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: I Will Tell the Truth in Half an Hour","paragraphs":["Opening the window, she followed the direction of the sound with her gaze.","Through the gaps in the fence, a black shadow could be seen moving.","It moved as slowly as a turtle; had Song Jinzhao not possessed such sharp hearing, she might not have noticed it at all.","After confirming there was no one else around, Song Jinzhao raised her right hand and aimed at the figure.","The next second, a short arrow flashing with a silvery white light pierced through the night sky.","\"Ah—\" A cry of pain rang out.","The man clutched his arm, looking at Song Jinzhao with a face full of astonishment.","Inside the carriage, the guards responsible for the night watch snapped their eyes open. The two of them quickly rushed out, and upon meeting Song Jinzhao's sharp gaze, any lingering drowsiness vanished instantly.","With anxious hearts, the two vaulted over the fence and apprehended the man.","Terrified of being reprimanded by Song Jinzhao, the guards furiously interrogated the man, \"Who are you? What are you trying to do?\"","This commotion woke up everyone else who had been sleeping soundly in their rooms.","Qu Ya rushed out and stopped at the door of the adjacent room. Seeing that everything was fine inside, he finally relaxed; he and Guan Nianshan's wife were sleeping next door.","Song Jinzhao walked out. Xuetuan, pressing against her leg, caught the scent of blood, raised its head, and let out a long roar.","The tiger's roar echoed through the valley, jolting the villagers of Longshan Town from their slumber.","\"What was that sound? A wolf howling?\"","A woman instinctively shielded her child, her tone trembling slightly.","\"With a sound that loud, could the wolves have come down the mountain?\"","\"I'll block the door with the table.\" Saying this, a man climbed out of bed, not only moving the table but also checking the windows.","Other households that had been awakened took the exact same precautions.","Afterward, they didn't dare to go back to sleep, sitting with machetes in hand for nearly an hour before finally daring to close their eyes.","In the woodshed in the inn's backyard, the innkeeper hid by the door, too afraid to go inside.","\"Do you know him?\" Lan Xi nodded toward the man.","The innkeeper shrank his neck and nodded.","\"His name is Wang Er. He lives in the house right behind the inn and is a notorious ruffian in town.\"","Wang Er was pinned to the ground, barely able to catch his breath, sweat dripping endlessly from his forehead.","Surrounded entirely by outsiders, the innkeeper was the only person he knew.","\"Uncle Yuan, save me! I just came out to use the latrine, it's all a misunderstanding.\"","Pressing a knee forcefully into the man's shoulder blade, the guard snapped, \"Do you need to sneak around and peek just to use the latrine? Tell me the truth, right now!\"","Noticing the bloody hole in Wang Er's arm, the innkeeper covered his eyes in fear.","\"Do as you please. I have to get up early to make breakfast tomorrow, so I'm going to bed.\"","Not to mention that Wang Er usually liked to engage in petty theft, even if he were a good person, the innkeeper wouldn't dare to speak up for him.","The other party had numbers, weapons, and even kept a tiger as a pet. Crossing them was practically a death wish.","Seeing the innkeeper turn and walk away, Wang Er instantly felt as if the sky had fallen.","He was dead for sure now. Had he known he would be caught, he never would have come.","Not wanting to die, Wang Er struggled to lift his head and pleaded with Song Jinzhao, his face full of bitterness and a forced, fawning expression.","\"I really just came out to use the latrine. I beg you, Miss, spare my life! I will work like a horse and toil like an ox for you in my next life.\"","Not wanting to waste time, Song Jinzhao handed the man directly over to Lan Xi and the others to handle.","\"I want the truth in half an hour. Everyone else, go back to rest.\"","It was so late, and everyone was tired; getting covered in blood would just mean having to bathe all over again.","\"Yes.\" Lan Xi nodded vigorously, bouncing the leg that was pressing down on Wang Er.","After the crowd dispersed, the simple slatted door of the woodshed slammed shut with a bang. Wang Er was instantly scared so badly he wet himself.","A stench of urine spread through the air, and Qingshuang held her breath in disgust.","Lan Xi shoved a piece of firewood, thick as half a fist, into Wang Er's mouth, scraping the mucous membrane inside. Soon, the metallic taste of blood mingled with the scent of sawdust."]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: The Informant of Qingfeng Stockade","paragraphs":["In less than half an hour, the room door was pushed open by Qingshuang.","\"County Princess, Wang Er has spoken. He is an informant for the Qingfeng Stronghold on Longtou Mountain.\"","Song Qiming, who had been resting on the floor, suddenly sat up. \"Qingfeng Stronghold? Isn't that the bandit lair the innkeeper mentioned?\"","Qingshuang nodded.","\"Whenever merchants stay overnight at the inn, Wang Er rushes to Qingfeng Stronghold overnight to deliver the news. If they successfully ambush them on the road, he gets a reward. His peeping earlier was also for this purpose.\"","The sound of their voices woke up Song Anhao. He had just opened his eyes and mumbled a few words before Song Shixue coaxed him back to sleep.","\"Sleep well, we have to wake up early tomorrow.\"","Drowsy, Song Anhao turned over, buried his head in the quilt, and went back to sleep.","Song Jinzhao signaled to Song Qiming with her eyes to step outside together. Seeing this, Song Shixue moved closer to her youngest brother.","The southwest was a chaotic mix of good and bad people. If they were already encountering bandits who dared to target them right at the beginning, the rest of the journey would definitely not be peaceful.","After leaving the room and stopping in the courtyard, Song Qiming bit his lip and said to Song Jinzhao, \"There are nearly two hundred bandits on Longtou Mountain. Charging in directly will definitely result in casualties. It would be best if we could outsmart them. Sister, I think Wang Er is our best opportunity.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly and raised her eyebrows. \"What do you think we should do?\"","Song Qiming swiped his hand across his neck.","\"Have Wang Er lead the way. We can launch a night raid on Qingfeng Stronghold and completely take down this group of bandits.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"There must be lookout posts on the way to Qingfeng Stronghold. A large group going up the mountain will easily be discovered, and the stronghold is their territory. It would be best to lure them out to an open area.\"","Song Qiming thought for a moment and looked toward the woodshed.","\"Perhaps we can use Wang Er to pass fake news to the bandits, but I'm afraid he won't be obedient.\"","Song Jinzhao gently curled the corners of her lips, not thinking this would be a difficult task at all.","Walking into the woodshed and seeing that the knife cuts were all concentrated on Wang Er's chest and shoulders, while his face remained perfectly clean, Song Jinzhao felt even more satisfied.","Once bandaged up, no one would likely notice.","When Wang Er saw Song Jinzhao enter, he quickly knelt on the ground and kowtowed for mercy.","\"I've said everything I was supposed to say. I beg you, Miss, spare my life.\" His wounded throat ached with every word he spoke.","Song Jinzhao's smile did not reach her eyes. \"I can spare your life, but you must do something for me.\"","Wang Er's face stiffened. He was both relieved and terrified. \"What is it?\"","Song Qiming forcefully pinched Wang Er's chin.","\"Go up the mountain and report to Qingfeng Stronghold. Tell them we are few in number but have a lot of money, and trick them all into coming down the mountain.\"","Wang Er swallowed in horror, his heart leaping into his throat.","\"You want to deal with the bandits?\"","After speaking, he subconsciously shook his head, his face full of disagreement.","\"The bandits on Longtou Mountain are extremely vicious and evil. They have thousands of lives on their hands. You definitely can't beat them.\"","\"There are bandit lookouts on both sides of the official road. As long as you let me go, I will help you leave.\"","Song Qiming stood up with a dark face. \"If the soft approach doesn't work, we'll use the hard one. Sister, you do it.\"","Since they had run into them, they definitely had to wipe out this group of bandits; otherwise, they would continue to rob and kill commoners on the road, and more people would die.","Song Jinzhao took out a medicine bottle and handed it to Qingshuang.","The latter quickly pulled out the stopper and poured out a black pill.","Seeing this, Wang Er was so frightened that he backed away repeatedly. He looked at the pill as if it were a death warrant; eating it meant death.","He cried out in fear, the word poison being the only thing left in his mind.","\"I'm willing to deliver the message! I'll say whatever you want! I don't want to die, please spare me!\"","Seeing Qingshuang reach out to him, Wang Er immediately shut his mouth tightly, shaking his head and dodging.","Lanxi pointed her sword at him and spoke coldly, \"If you don't want me to pry your mouth open with my sword, then open it.\"","Choking back sobs, Wang Er opened his mouth, his face covered in snot and tears.","\"I've never killed a single person. I just earn a little reward money. I'm a good person.\"","The pill was stuffed into his mouth. Not daring to spit it out, he could only let it melt and slide down his throat along with his saliva.","Song Jinzhao said, \"As long as you do as I say, I will give you the antidote once the matter is settled.\"","If you were a good person, there would be no bad people in the world.","Not having blood on your hands doesn't mean you haven't killed anyone. Passing information about passing merchants to the bandits in advance is no different from killing them with your own hands."]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: Wang Er's Panic, Another Group of People","paragraphs":["On a dark and windy night, Wang Er wiped away his tears as he trudged toward the Qingfeng Stronghold.","His numbed wounds, slathered with anesthetic, felt no pain, but his heart was as dead as ashes, as if he might drop dead the very next second.","Behind him, Lan Xi, dressed entirely in black, followed from a distance.","After an unknown amount of time, two figures suddenly dashed out from behind a rock. The light of their torches illuminated Wang Er's face, and the tense atmosphere instantly dissipated.","Wang Er stopped in his tracks and offered them a fawning smile.","\"Brother Hu, Brother Mang, are you two guarding the mountain today?\"","The man called Brother Hu looked Wang Er up and down. \"You coming up the mountain at this hour, does the inn have new traveling merchants?\"","Wang Er forced a couple of cheerful laughs.","He smiled and shook his head. \"Not merchants, but a wealthy family from Jiangnan. They are all women, carrying ten carriages of luggage, and they will be passing through Longtou Mountain tomorrow.\"","Zhao Mang's eyes widened abruptly, his pupils flashing with pleasant surprise.","\"How old are they? Are they pretty?\"","Wang Er blinked in terror, his throat trembling as he spoke.","He nodded hastily and replied, \"Beautiful. Young ladies around twenty years old, bringing along quite a few maids. You will absolutely love them when you see them.\"","Though he feared they wouldn't live long enough to enjoy it.","\"Then what are we waiting for? Come on, let's go see the boss.\"","Zhao Mang reached out and patted Wang Er's shoulder. He swallowed hard, itching with unbearable anticipation, his mind already fantasizing about pinning a beauty beneath him tomorrow.","The mountain path was winding and entirely uphill. Afraid of being discovered, Lan Xi didn't dare get too close.","He only stopped his steps when he caught sight of the bandits at the second lookout point.","It was just as the County Princess had suspected. Not only was the road treacherous, but there was more than one lookout point. The enemy was highly vigilant.","Now, it all depended on whether Wang Er could successfully deceive the bandits of Qingfeng Stronghold.","Less than an hour later, the Qingfeng Stronghold, built halfway up the mountain, was brightly lit. The torches illuminated the inside of the stronghold, making it brighter than daytime.","Draped in a wolf pelt, the chieftain of Qingfeng Stronghold, Zhao Jiutou, sat in his python chair, his hands resting on the armrests, his eyes burning with a dark gleam.","\"How many guards did they bring in total? How are their skills?\"","Wang Er swallowed subconsciously, his voice slightly hoarse.","\"Ten. I don't know about their skills, but they all carry swords.\"","Seeing this, Zhao Mang couldn't wait to step forward and say, \"Boss, the brothers have been eating plain food all winter and have long wanted a taste of meat. Jiangnan is full of rich people. This is definitely going to be a big haul.\"","Zhao Jiutou puffed out his chest and waved his arm forcefully.","\"Brothers, sharpen your blades. Tomorrow, we go big.\"","Knowing there were ten carriages of luggage and female relatives, the bandits were already itching for action.","Hearing that Zhao Jiutou was going to make a move, they all raised their fists and began to cheer: \"Yeah!\"","\"Yeah!\"","\"Yeah!\"","...","Blocked at the back of the crowd, Wang Er saw that the deed was done and nervously began to wipe away his sweat.","He prayed he wouldn't be found out; he still wanted to live.","Meanwhile, in an Earth God temple fifty miles away from Longtou Mountain, Gu Huaiyuan's son, Gu Jinghong, was leading his people to spend the night in the ruined temple.","Waking up in the middle of the night, unable to suppress his excitement, he walked outside and looked toward Longtou Mountain, secretly making a resolution in his heart.","This time, I must let my father see what I am capable of.","He stood there for a moment before returning to the room to continue sleeping.","Gu Baozhu was awakened by the rustling sound of the straw being pressed down. She opened her eyes just in time to see Gu Jinghong lying down.","Their eyes met, and after a moment's thought, Gu Jinghong sat back up.","\"Little Aunt, how about I have someone escort you back tomorrow?\"","Gu Baozhu rolled her eyes straight at him.","\"If you dare send me back, I will make all of them leave. Let's see what you use to attack Qingfeng Stronghold then.\"","Gu Jinghong opened his mouth in frustration, but could only stare speechlessly at Gu Baozhu's back as she rolled over.","Half of the guards he brought to attack Qingfeng Stronghold were his, and the other half were his little aunt's. But if his little aunt gave the word, he really wouldn't be able to keep a single one of them.","Forget it. If she comes, she comes. Fortunately, his little aunt's martial arts skills were pretty good, so self-defense wouldn't be an issue.","At worst, he would just assign a few more people to protect her when the time came. Nothing should go wrong."]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: Ambush and Counter-ambush","paragraphs":["The next morning, Longtou Mountain was shrouded in thick mist, which did not dissipate until half an hour after the sun had risen.","Song Qiming had led his men to ambush both ends of the official road in advance, waiting only for Song Jinzhao's order to strike.","Around eight in the morning, when the sun was high in the sky, Zhao Jiutou led nearly two hundred bandits out of Qingfeng Stronghold. Upon reaching the foot of the mountain, they lay in ambush in the ditches flanking the official road.","Meanwhile, on a hillside two hundred meters away, Song Qiming lowered his telescope and instructed Lan Xi.","\"There are about two hundred of them. Tell Sister she can set off now.\"","According to the innkeeper and Wang Er, the Qingfeng Stronghold had roughly two hundred bandits, so this had to be their entire force.","After waiting for nearly half an hour without seeing a single soul, Zhao Jiutou questioned Wang Er.","\"Where are they? Why aren't they here yet?\"","Wang Er answered tremblingly, \"I reckon it's because the womenfolk can't get up early. How about I go take a look?\"","Zhao Jiutou pondered for a moment before nodding. \"Alright. Zhao Mang, you go with him.\"","Wang Er, who was just about to rejoice, instantly lost his good mood. With a troubled expression, he said, \"Chief Zhao, Brother Mang is burly and has an unfamiliar face. The villagers will get suspicious if they see him. It's better if I go alone.\"","Broad-shouldered, thick-waisted, and with a face full of fierce flesh, Zhao Mang did not look like a good person at all. Taking him down the mountain would definitely arouse suspicion.","Zhao Jiutou looked Zhao Mang up and down.","Thinking about it, it was true; he looked too much like a villain.","In fact, not just him, but everyone in Qingfeng Stronghold looked like a villain. Just standing there was enough to strike fear into people's hearts.","\"Fine, go and come back quickly. Once this is done, I'll give you double the reward.\"","Wang Er agreed gleefully, nodding so hard his chin looked like a chicken pecking at grain.","He turned and ran, quickly disappearing into the forest.","Before Wang Er could return, a quarter of an hour later, the convoy slowly appeared in the sights of Zhao Jiutou and his bandits.","Looking at the guards on horseback, they counted and found there were indeed only ten of them.","Maids sat sideways on the handcarts laden with luggage, and more maids walked alongside the horse-drawn carriages. It clearly seemed to be a wealthy family.","Zhao Mang licked his lips impatiently, his lustful gaze landing on the decent-looking maids and refusing to look away.","\"Boss, do we strike?\"","Zhao Jiutou shook his head in refusal. \"Wait until they enter the ambush ring before we make a move.\"","Zhao Mang's Adam's apple bobbed as his gaze shifted to the carriage the maids were following.","The people sitting inside had to be the madams and young ladies of this wealthy family. If the maids were this pretty, the young ladies must be absolutely stunning!","The movements on both sides of the official road could not be hidden from Song Jinzhao. Seeing that they were in about the right position, she pretended nothing was wrong and lifted the window curtain to glance at the scenery on both sides.","Zhao Mang's eyes lit up. She really was a young lady from a wealthy family.","There seemed to be an even younger one inside the carriage, a pair of beautiful sisters.","Seeing that the convoy had reached directly in front of the ditches, Zhao Jiutou suddenly raised his saber, climbed out of the ditch, and shouted, \"Brothers, charge! Tonight at the celebration banquet, there will be enough beauties and fine wine for everyone!\"","Hearing Zhao Jiutou's promise, the other bandits charged forward with the strength of bulls, running incredibly fast.","The lustful Zhao Mang abandoned his good Brother Hu and sprinted madly toward the carriage where Song Jinzhao was.","Amidst the chaotic noise, a shout of \"Beauty, here I come!\" could be heard. Song Jinzhao's face instantly darkened, her grip tightening on her Lingyun spear, which could no longer wait to draw blood.","In the other carriage, Song Anhao held down the eager Xuetuan and lectured in her sweet, childish voice, \"Don't move. Sister told us to stay here. It's dangerous up front.\"","Xuetuan twitched its tiger nose indignantly.","So many people, there is a threat, I want to go at them.","Song Anhao seemed to understand its gaze, hugging its neck tightly and continuing to shake her head.","\"Sister and the others will win a great victory. They don't need you to go over there. Be good and stay here to protect me.\"","Xuetuan lay down dejectedly in the carriage, in a bad mood but still maintaining its vigilance at all times.","At the same time, the shouts of the charging bandits echoed for hundreds of meters.","Gu Jinghong and her group, who were heading toward Longtou Mountain, suddenly stopped in their tracks, their ears pricking up.","\"Judging by the sound, there must be at least several hundred people. It must be the bandits from Qingfeng Stronghold coming down the mountain to kill again.\"","Riding on horseback, Gu Baozhu clamped her legs around her horse's belly with an excited expression and galloped forward. \"Then what are we waiting for? Hurry up and save them!\"","\"Auntie, slow down! Stay behind me!\" Gu Jinghong shouted as she chased after her.","The hundred or so guards beside them quickly followed, forming a dense, dark mass that made the very ground tremble beneath them."]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: Archery, Victory","paragraphs":["The moment Zhao Jiutou led his men out of the ditch, Song Qiming, who was crouching on the distant hillside, immediately raised his hand. The others instantly raised their bows and arrows, taking aim.","Song Jinzhao quickly emerged from the carriage. Seeing that the number of bandits had reached her expectations, she decisively waved her Lingyun spear to signal Song Qiming.","\"Defend!\" Her clear voice reached everyone's ears.","At the command, the guards who had been riding on horseback immediately jumped down, pulled back the tarps on the carts, and raised shields over their heads.","At the same time, Song Qiming roared, clenching his fist and swinging it down forcefully.","\"Loose the arrows!\"","Zhao Jiutou paused for a moment, mistakenly thinking the shields were meant to block their charge, and shouted again, \"Kill them! Leave no one alive except the women!\"","Every time the Qingfeng Stronghold bandits raided, they would spare the female family members and kidnap them for their own amusement.","To them, women were spoils of war. Once they grew tired of violating them, they could be sold for money; killing them outright was a waste.","Just as all the bandits charged toward Song Jinzhao and her group like hungry wolves eyeing a piece of fat meat, a dark, dense cloud of arrows rained down on them from the sky.","The first bandit to notice looked up at the sky in terror and screamed, \"Arrows! Everyone, dodge!\"","Unfortunately, it was already too late.","By the time the bandits looked up, the arrows were already upon them.","Caught completely off guard, many were unable to dodge in time and were struck down.","Zhao Jiutou turned pale with shock. It was an ambush!","He slashed away the incoming arrows with his saber while advancing toward Song Jinzhao.","It was obvious this woman was the leader; he had to capture her first.","After the volley of arrows ended, Song Qiming took the lead, raising his weapon and charging down the hillside, with the others closely following.","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan were faster than the rest. They killed everyone in their path, like fierce wolves bursting into a flock of sheep.","When Gu Jinghong and his group arrived, the scene was completely different from what they had imagined.","At a glance, the ground was covered with bandits who had fallen to arrows, a dense mass that looked like the work of professional archers.","On the chaotic official road, two groups of people were clearly engaged in fierce combat.","Among them were quite a few women who appeared highly trained, not at all like ordinary commoners.","Gu Baozhu's eyes shone brightly. She stared at Song Jinzhao, who was fighting Zhao Jiutou, with uncontrollable excitement.","\"Jinghong, look, that woman is amazing!\"","She wielded her long spear with fierce, wind-whipping power; her opponent was no match for her at all.","Gu Jinghong frowned in confusion.","\"Something isn't right. These people don't look like the guards an ordinary merchant would bring.\"","Gu Baozhu stroked her chin thoughtfully, her amazement growing as she watched the battle unfold.","\"They look a bit like a well-trained army. Could they be official troops sent to wipe out the bandits?\"","Gu Jinghong shook his head. \"If they were official troops, there wouldn't be so many women.\"","As the two spoke, Song Jinzhao thrust her spear into Zhao Jiutou's chest and swept him into the air.","His body slammed heavily against a tree trunk before crashing to the ground. A wave of agonizing pain radiated from his chest to his stomach, feeling as if he had been shattered.","To think a woman's martial arts could be this formidable, her strength even greater than his own. He had miscalculated this time.","Lying on the ground, Zhao Jiutou was filled with regret. He could not care less about Wang Er's deception; right now, he only wanted to escape.","Seeing their boss injured and outmatched by Song Jinzhao, Zhao Mang lost all lustful thoughts toward her. Raising his blade, he and Brother Hu charged at Song Jinzhao together.","Zhao Jiutou struggled to roll over and crawl to the side. Just as his right hand touched the grass, a sharp longsword pierced right through his palm.","Gu Jinghong immediately ordered his subordinates to tie him up. \"Trying to run? Not a chance.\"","Zhao Jiutou was the chief of the Qingfeng Stronghold. With him captured, his father would have absolutely nothing to complain about.","With the intervention of a third party, the bandits, seeing that they were facing a dead end, dropped their weapons and crouched down in surrender. Soon, the fighting came to a complete halt."]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: Gu Family Aunt and Niece","paragraphs":["Song Qiming stared warily at Gu Jinghong and his group, who had suddenly barged into the battlefield.","Seeing them approach, Lanxi and Qingshuang immediately led their people to block the way, shielding Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming.","Gu Baozhu abruptly halted her forward charge, her eyes flashing with a hint of bewilderment.","She hurriedly waved her hands and explained, We came from Songzhou City to wipe out the bandits. We are not bad people.","Song Jinzhao lifted her eyelids, her gaze sweeping over their guards with a heavy, assessing weight.","They wore no armor, and the young man leading them was so youthful; they were likely not official soldiers.","Seeing the other party pointing swords at him, Gu Jinghong cautiously pulled Gu Baozhu behind him to protect her.","Who are you people?","Reporting their origins before figuring out the other party background, how could his little aunt have no sense of vigilance at all?","What Gu Jinghong did not know was that Gu Baozhu had already been completely won over by Song Jinzhao previous moves. In her eyes and heart, there was nothing but pure admiration for her.","Besides, how could someone who killed bandits be a bad person?","Song Qiming reached out to move Lanxi aside and spoke with righteous authority, I am the Prefect of Suining, personally appointed by the imperial court. Who are you?","A flash of surprise crossed Gu Jinghong eyes.","He knew the former Prefect of Suining was stepping down due to illness, but to think the newly appointed prefect was this young, looking not even twenty years old.","He raised a hand, signaling his subordinates to lower their weapons. My name is Gu Jinghong. Gu Huaiyuan, the Garrison Commander of Songzhou City, is my father. May I ask for Your Excellency honorable surname?","Gu Huaiyuan son, that meant he was the grandson of Gu Zhongxun, the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest.","Having sorted out the relationships, Song Qiming dropped his guard and replied in a calm tone, My surname is Song, and my given name is Qiming. Did you come to exterminate the bandits under General Gu orders?","Gu Jinghong looked guiltily at the ground. After stammering for a long while, he gave a slight nod.","My father is busy with official duties. Knowing the bandits at Longtou Mountain were running rampant, I decided to come scout the situation first. I did not expect to run into Lord Song here.","Gu Baozhu lowered her eyes, suddenly realizing something. She snapped her head up and stared at Song Jinzhao in astonishment.","Is Lord Song older sister County Princess Linghui?","Her gaze then shifted to Song Jinzhao. Looking at the Lingyun Spear in her hands, Gu Baozhu could hardly conceal her excitement.","She bit her lip desperately but still could not suppress the joy lifting the corners of her brows.","Standing to the side, Gu Jinghong completely froze in place upon hearing Gu Baozhu words.","County Princess Linghui? The same County Princess Linghui who beat the Prince of Wei from the Shuobei Kingdom to a pulp? The one his father constantly talked about?","The aunt and nephew looked at Song Jinzhao uncertainly, holding back their inner excitement as they waited for a response.","Song Jinzhao calmly handed the Lingyun Spear over to Lanxi, and a nearby guard hurriedly stepped up to help.","Aside from the princess herself, it took two people just to barely lift this spear.","You know me?","As soon as the words fell, Gu Jinghong and Gu Baozhu immediately cupped their hands and bent their knees in a half-kneeling bow to Song Jinzhao.","Greetings to County Princess Linghui.","When Gu Baozhu looked up, the corners of her mouth were raised high, and the light sparkling in her eyes was more dazzling than the stars at night.","Princess, you are the paragon of women in this world. Not just in the Southwest Province, but even the foreign women of Panzhou, Ningzhou, and other regions deeply admire you.","Song Qiming was going to Suining to be the prefect. Did that mean County Princess Linghui would also stay in the Southwest?","Just the thought of this possibility made Gu Baozhu heart beat faster.","Zhao Jiutou, along with the other surviving bandits, was brought before Gu Jinghong securely tied up.","Second Young Master, how should we deal with these bandits?","Should we execute them on the spot or take them back?","Gu Jinghong swept his gaze over the bandits kneeling on the ground.","Originally, he wanted to use the annihilation of the Qingfeng Stronghold to prove his capabilities to his father, but County Princess Linghui had confronted the bandits first.","By the time he arrived with his men, her side already had the upper hand. Taking down the bandits was a breeze for them, which meant this merit could no longer be his."]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: There Are Many Guards in the Gu Mansion","paragraphs":["Without thinking for too long, Gu Jinghong looked up to seek Song Jinzhao's approval.","\"County Princess, the commoners traveling on this official road are terrified of the bandits from Qingfeng Stronghold. I suggest we take Zhao Jiutou back to the city and behead him in public as a warning, so the people can feel at ease.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded slowly and methodically.","\"Do as you say. Tie him up first and bring him back to Songzhou City.\"","Song Qiming glanced at the mountain peak.","\"Sister, there might still be bandits in Qingfeng Stronghold who haven't come down. It's best to make a trip up there to avoid leaving any future troubles.\"","Gu Jinghong quickly raised his hand, \"How could we trouble the County Princess with such a trivial matter? I will take some men over.\"","Song Jinzhao was happy to have the leisure and turned her head to instruct Lan Xi.","\"Bring Wang Er over and hand him to Young General Gu so he can lead the way.\"","Lan Xi put her index finger in her mouth. Not long after the whistle sounded, a carriage slowly approached, with Wang Er tied to the back of it.","Song Anhao lifted the carriage curtain. Seeing the ground covered with bloody corpses pierced by arrows, she became momentarily frightened, her mind going completely blank, unable to think of anything.","Xuetuan let out a long roar at the sky, and the few birds remaining in the surrounding woods hastily flapped their wings and fled.","\"S-Sister!\"","Song Anhao subconsciously called out to Song Jinzhao, her panicked eyes searching everywhere for that familiar figure.","Song Jinzhao rode over, lifted Song Anhao onto horseback, and softly comforted her, \"Don't be afraid, the bad men are all dead.\"","Watching the fierce white tiger leap down, Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong were stunned.","Such a massive tiger, and it had been sitting in the carriage? Was this raised by County Princess Linghui?","They rested on the spot while Gu Jinghong took his men up to Qingfeng Stronghold, returning shortly after.","He pointed to one woman and four men who were tightly bound and said, \"There were only five of them. Zhao Jiutou had them stay in the kitchen to cook, saying they were going to celebrate their victory.\"","Thinking of how arrogant Zhao Jiutou was, Gu Jinghong couldn't help but kick him again.","\"County Princess, it is still a two-day journey from here to Songzhou City. We can spend the night at Yunshan Temple midway. Let us set off quickly.\"","There were thirty-two captives kept alive; they had to be brought back quickly.","Song Jinzhao's gaze rested on the young girl's face.","Little aunt, Gu Jinghong was Gu Huaiyuan's son, so this girl should be Gu Zhongxun's most precious youngest daughter, Gu Baozhu.","The captive Wang Er, seeing that Song Jinzhao seemed to have forgotten him and worried about the poison flaring up, couldn't help but howl out loud.","\"My lady County Princess, I have already deceived the people of Qingfeng Stronghold according to your demands. Now that they have all been caught, shouldn't you give me the antidote?\"","A cold glint flashed in Song Jinzhao's eyes.","She took a medicine bottle from her robes and tossed it to Qing Shuang. \"Feed it to him, and hand him over to Young General Gu to deal with.\"","Wang Er, who had just opened his mouth, was stunned.","He widened his eyes in panic. \"You promised to spare my life!\"","Song Jinzhao said coldly, \"I promised to give you the antidote. Whether the government is willing to spare you, I do not know.\"","Wang Er choked on the antidote, his eyes rolling back repeatedly.","In the next second, Gu Jinghong directly ordered his subordinates to drag the man away.","On the way to Yunshan Temple, Gu Baozhu chattered non-stop.","When Song Jinzhao didn't bother to respond, she turned to ask Song Shixue and Song Qiming.","She asked about affairs in the capital, especially the time when Gong Linjue came to the capital, showing a posture of getting to the bottom of everything.","Song Jinzhao casually swept her gaze over the men Gu Jinghong had brought, and lightly slipped a question into the conversation.","\"Are the military supplies allocated by the imperial court to the southwestern province every year insufficient?\"","Gu Jinghong raised his eyelids in confusion, \"Why does the County Princess say that?\"","Song Jinzhao gestured toward the men on both sides.","\"They are not even wearing armor. Is it not because military supplies are lacking?\"","Gu Jinghong smiled, his eyes curving.","\"The County Princess has misunderstood. They are guards of my Gu manor, not soldiers from the military camp, so they cannot wear armor.\"","A dark gleam flashed through the depths of Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Fifty men were all guards of the Gu manor, and this was merely what the aunt and nephew had brought out. There were definitely more left behind.","Their eyes met, and Song Qiming tacitly followed up with a question for Gu Jinghong.","\"Your respected father is the garrison commander of Songzhou City and has three thousand soldiers under his command. Why hire so many guards? The money alone must be a vast sum.\"","Gu Jinghong replied, \"Those are officially registered troops of the government and cannot be diverted for private use.\"","\"The southwest is a mix of dragons and snakes, with many outlaws committing crimes. These guards are meant to protect us, especially the female family members. We must always bring some along when going out.\"","After speaking, he looked at Song Qiming.","\"Lord Song will understand once you reach Suining. Suining Prefecture has the most yamen runners, a full five hundred men. Every time the prefect goes out, he is guarded by three inner and outer layers. However, he uses the prefecture's funds, so the tax revenue submitted by Suining Prefecture every year is the lowest, and they often cannot make ends meet.\""]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: You can openly expand your workforce","paragraphs":["Song Qiming blinked, his mind a bit bewildered. \"Commissioner Gu doesn't intervene?\"","Gu Jinghong smiled bitterly. \"If we don't hire them, accidents easily happen. We can't just keep replacing people as they die. The imperial court rarely allocates funds to the southwest. Both the commoners and the officials suffer. Sometimes, turning a blind eye is the only way to get by.\"","He turned his head and glanced at the guards Song Jinzhao had brought.","\"If my grandfather knew that the guards the County Princess brought were so capable in combat, he would surely feel more at ease about you, my lord.\"","Song Qiming's lips twitched, speechless for a moment.","To say something like that, just what kind of situation was Suining Prefecture in?","Caught in the middle, Song Jinzhao fell into deep thought.","Her gaze stared into the distance, her mind already beginning to ponder the matter of private soldiers.","Behind them, Gu Baozhu curiously asked Song Shixue, \"Second Miss Song, I saw many women who know martial arts just now. Are they also guards?\"","To bring so many female guards, County Princess Linghui was indeed different from ordinary women.","Song Shixue shook her head. \"They are all maids from the estate. We have a martial arts training ground at home, so everyone knows a little.\"","Gu Baozhu smiled sweetly, turning to stare fixedly at Song Jinzhao's back, her eyes sparkling.","\"That still requires the County Princess's permission. I see their martial arts are quite good. Did the County Princess teach them personally?\"","Song Shixue said, \"My elder sister hasn't taught them. They all practiced by following others, and they only do it half-heartedly.\"","By the time they arrived at Yunshan Temple, the sky had grown dark. Gu Jinghong had his men lock the bandits in the woodshed while leading Song Jinzhao toward the backyard.","The ground was covered in fallen leaves that rustled as they walked.","Logically, it wasn't time to sleep yet, but the temple's windows were completely dark.","Despite such a commotion, not a single monk came out, as if no one lived there.","\"Young General Gu, are there any monks in Yunshan Temple? With so many fallen leaves on the ground, no one seems to be sweeping.\"","Gu Jinghong held up his fingers. \"There are two monks.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Why so few? I see there are many buildings here.\"","Gu Jinghong replied, \"Yunshan Temple is quite far from Songzhou City. Plus, the abbot was once forced to be a bandit, so very few commoners come here to offer incense.\"","Forced into banditry and then turning over a new leaf to become a monk? Looking at Gu Jinghong's attitude, this abbot most likely had a story.","Walking into the guest room, it was quite clean, as if it had been specially swept.","\"County Princess, please rest for a moment. The vegetarian meal will be ready soon.\"","A quarter of an hour later, all the people Song Jinzhao had brought were properly settled by the Gu family aunt and nephew.","Lan Xi knocked and entered.","\"Your subordinate heard from the Gu family guards that they originally planned to stay at Yunshan Temple for several days. As for why they suddenly went to investigate Qingfeng Stronghold, they all kept their mouths shut.\"","Over the course of the afternoon, Song Shixue had become quite familiar with Gu Baozhu.","\"I think they must have gone to investigate secretly on their own, and no one else knew. Otherwise, Gu Baozhu's father wouldn't have let her come.\"","Even if she knew martial arts, he wouldn't let his daughter go out and risk her life with his grandson. Qingfeng Stronghold had hundreds of bandits, and they had only brought fifty guards. If they were discovered, it would be very dangerous.","Song Qiming nodded in agreement. \"I think so too. Gu Huaiyuan has troops at his disposal. Even if Gu Jinghong went to investigate, he should have brought the regular army instead of just guards.\"","Song Jinzhao's index finger, which had been tapping on the table, stopped.","\"We'll know everything once we enter the city tomorrow. What I'm thinking now is that perhaps we can buy more guards.\"","Song Qiming pondered for a long while before nodding in agreement.","\"You are a County Princess, sister, Shixue is a woman, and Anhao is still young. Even if we double our manpower, I'm sure Gu Zhongxun won't say a word.\"","In the capital, keeping too many guards would be labeled as maintaining a private army by those with ulterior motives, but here in the southwest, no one cared.","The current prefect of Suining was a precedent; five hundred yamen runners had long exceeded the standard limit by several times. And they were using the prefectural office's money, yet Gu Zhongxun didn't intervene."]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: Brotherly Respect and Harmony","paragraphs":["At the temple entrance, Gu Jinghong looked slightly apprehensive as he instructed his subordinate. \"Ride back through the night as fast as you can and tell Grandfather that County Princess Linghui and the Prefect of Suining are resting at Yunshan Temple tonight. They will arrive in Songzhou City tomorrow, so tell them to prepare.\"","Wearing a bamboo hat, his personal servant cautiously probed, \"Should I tell the Old Master and the Second Master about the eradication of the Qingfeng Stronghold?\"","The Young Master had wanted to establish his merits and make a name for himself. Under the guise of visiting Yunshan Temple, he had taken the Young Lady along to wipe out the bandits, even threatening the other guards to follow him.","Fortunately, everyone was safe and sound now, or they would definitely be punished.","Gu Jinghong rubbed his nose.","\"Just say that County Princess Linghui caught them, and we simply lent a helping hand because we happened to run into them.\"","The servant frowned in a dilemma. \"But you told the County Princess that you were ordered to scout the area. When the two of you compare stories, won't the lie be exposed?\"","\"My father won't expose me in front of the County Princess. When Grandfather and Father question me later, my little aunt will protect me.\"","Gu Jinghong put his hands on his hips, still feeling a bit of regret in his heart.","If County Princess Linghui hadn't happened to appear, the Qingfeng Stronghold would have absolutely been in the bag. Even if his father punished him verbally, he would definitely approve of him in his heart. But now everything was ruined, and all his efforts were for nothing.","It was already midnight by the time the servant rode non-stop to Songzhou City.","The soldiers guarding the city gates heard the galloping hooves and poked their heads over the wall. Seeing that the rider was Gu Jinghong's attendant, they looked surprised and shouted down.","\"Lord Laixi, why have you come here in the middle of the night? Where is the Young General?\"","A few days ago, Gu Jinghong had marched out of the city in a grand procession, and the city guards had all been informed. Why was he returning alone now? And in the dead of night, no less.","The servant looked up and replied, \"The Young General sent me back. Hurry and open the gate!\"","The soldiers ordered the city gates to be opened, and the servant galloped into the city.","By the time he returned to the manor, Gu Zhongxun and the others were already fast asleep.","\"My Lord, Laixi is outside requesting an audience. He says he has an important matter to report.\"","The door was knocked three times before there was any movement inside.","Gu Zhongxun rubbed his eyes and opened the door. \"What is it at this late hour?\"","The servant bypassed the other attendants and walked up to Gu Zhongxun. \"Old Master, the Second Young Master sent me back to report: County Princess Linghui and the newly appointed Prefect of Suining have arrived at Yunshan Temple. They will reach Songzhou City tomorrow.\"","Gu Zhongxun's eyes snapped wide open, his sleepiness vanishing without a trace in an instant.","\"County Princess Linghui! Song Jinzhao?\"","The servant nodded. \"Not only that, but while passing through Longtou Mountain, the bandits of the Qingfeng Stronghold attempted to rob and kill the County Princess. However, they were counter-killed by her, and the bandit leader Zhao Jiutou and his men have all been captured.\"","\"The Second Young Master happened to run into them while leading his men to scout the area. The prisoners are currently being held at Yunshan Temple and will be escorted into the city tomorrow.\"","\"Scout what?\"","\"Why on earth did he run off to Longtou Mountain?\"","The voice arrived before the person did. Gu Huaiyuan's gruff voice reached the servant's ears, making his body instinctively tense up.","Turning around, he saw Gu Gaoyuan and Gu Huaiyuan walking over with stern expressions.","Looking at the ground, the servant whispered, \"The Second Young Master heard that the bandits at Longtou Mountain have been rampant lately. He wanted to share the Second Master's burdens, so he took some men over to have a look.\"","Gu Huaiyuan's tiger-like eyes widened drastically as he snorted and roared at the servant.","\"There are no traveling merchants in the winter, so the bandits at Longtou Mountain couldn't find anyone to rob even if they wanted to. Not a single case has been reported since the snow mountains thawed. Where did Jinghong hear that they were being rampant?\"","The servant swallowed hard in fear and explained tremblingly, \"It was precisely because merchants would be passing by after the snow mountains thawed, and the Second Young Master happened to hear the commoners worrying about the bandits on the road, that he took his men to investigate.\"","Seeing the servant in this state, the three men looked away speechlessly, too lazy to listen any further.","Gu Huaiyuan sneered, his eyes looking as if they were about to pop out of their sockets.","He knew his own son's personality best.","\"I think he was just trying to show off and be competitive, greedy for merits and acting rashly. He wanted to go eradicate bandits with just a few guards. What about the Young Lady? Is she hurt?\"","With his lie exposed, the servant didn't even dare to lift his head, his voice dropping even lower.","\"The Young Lady didn't lose a single hair. By the time we arrived, the bandits had already been mostly killed by County Princess Linghui's people. The Second Young Master just cleaned up the rest.\"","Seeing his younger brother so enraged, Gu Gaoyuan signaled for the servant to leave.","\"You may step down first.\"","\"Yes.\" The servant bowed and turned to leave, not daring to straighten his posture until he had disappeared from the courtyard.","Seeing that his younger son's face remained cold, Gu Zhongxun advised, \"What young person isn't impulsive? You were just like that in your youth.\"","\"Ever since Jinghong entered the military camp, you've always kept him by your side. You don't give him important tasks, treating him like a lowly foot soldier. It's no wonder he's so eager to prove himself.\"","Gu Huaiyuan furrowed his brows. \"What I'm angry about is that he actually took our little sister with him. What if something had happened?\"","Gu Zhongxun shook his head helplessly.","\"I know Baozhu's personality better than you do. If she weren't a girl, she would have joined the military camp long ago. You can't blame Jinghong for this.\"","Gu Gaoyuan casually chimed in.","\"If our little sister hadn't agreed, those guards wouldn't have taken orders from Jinghong either.\"","\"Fortunately, they are fine now and happened to run into County Princess Linghui. I think we should just let this matter rest. Don't be too hard on them.\"","Gu Huaiyuan glared at his older brother with disdain.","\"My eldest nephew is obedient, well-behaved, and only focuses on reading the classics of the sages. Of course it's easy for you to talk, Big Brother, since you have nothing to worry about.\"","\"If Congwen were like Jinghong, I'd like to see if you could still sit still.\"","Gu Gaoyuan retorted, \"Dragons beget dragons, phoenixes beget phoenixes, and the son of a mouse knows how to dig holes. You shout about fighting and killing all day long, so it's no wonder Jinghong wants to eradicate bandits every day. This is called a son carrying on his father's legacy.\"","\"If he were to hole up in the city as an idle, wealthy young master, then you would truly be anxious.\"","Seeing his two sons start bickering again, Gu Zhongxun didn't want to listen and took a step back into his room.","As he closed the door, he left them with one sentence: \"Order the servants to clean the post house. Prepare to welcome County Princess Linghui into the manor tomorrow.\"","Looking at the tightly shut door, they saw the lights inside the room go out.","Gu Gaoyuan and Gu Huaiyuan were also too lazy to continue their argument, turning around to leave the doorway.","They had only taken two steps when the topic shifted to Song Jinzhao, and their attitudes suddenly became extremely brotherly and harmonious again.","The two brothers had a very good relationship, though they frequently bickered. After an argument, as long as one of them spoke first, they would make up immediately.","And it would be just as if nothing had ever happened; the matter would blow over before the wind even blew."]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: Arrival at Songzhou City","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, just as the sun peeked over the horizon, Gu Baozhu came over to call Song Jinzhao and the others to the dining hall for breakfast.","Gu Baozhu stuck close to Song Jinzhao, their clothes brushing against each other, not at all acting like they had only met a day ago.","\"Jinghong sent a messenger to my father overnight yesterday. They already know the County Princess has arrived in Songzhou. Once we enter the city, you can get a good rest.\"","Squeezed to the back, Song Qiming looked helplessly at his sister, mouthing the words silently. Isn't this girl a bit too overly familiar?","Song Shixue opened her mouth and wiggled her eyebrows: She was like this yesterday too, naturally sociable?","The brother and sister were old enough to be sensible, so they could tolerate it.","But Song Anhao, who had tried to speak several times but couldn't get a word in, couldn't hold back anymore.","He squeezed between the two of them, putting his hands on his hips to separate them. \"Sister, how far is Songzhou City from Suining Prefecture? How long until we get there?\"","Having sat in a carriage for two months, he had long lost his patience.","Worried that Song Jinzhao would leave soon, Gu Baozhu immediately said, \"Songzhou City has lots of delicious food and fun things to do. The County Princess can stay a few more days to rest up before heading to Suining.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled and shook her head, but didn't say anything.","Seeing that she didn't respond, Gu Baozhu had no choice but to look away, appearing slightly dejected.","After breakfast, the large entourage set off for Songzhou City.","The scorching sun hung high in the sky, making everyone sweat profusely. It wasn't until late afternoon, when the sun was about to set, that they finally saw the walls of Songzhou City.","Outside the city gates, seeing a large group approaching from afar, a carriage driver immediately lifted the curtain and spoke inside, \"My Lord, they are here.\"","Gu Gaoyuan emerged from the carriage, standing on the frame to look into the distance, a hint of joy in his eyes.","\"After waiting all afternoon, they have finally arrived.\"","\"There are many of them, at least a hundred,\" came Gu Huaiyuan's voice from behind him.","Gu Gaoyuan turned his head. \"If there were too few, they wouldn't have been able to wipe out the Qingfeng Stronghold.\"","A moment later, just as Gu Jinghong was about to make introductions, Gu Huaiyuan bowed to Song Jinzhao first. \"I, Gu Huaiyuan, the Defender of Songzhou City, pay my respects to County Princess Linghui.\"","Gu Gaoyuan's expression paused slightly before he spoke a step late, \"I, Gu Gaoyuan, the Prefect of Songzhou City, pay my respects to County Princess Linghui.\"","This woman was dressed simply; how could his younger brother be so sure she was County Princess Linghui? Shouldn't the County Princess be sitting in a carriage?","Song Jinzhao stared at the two men bowing before her. \"This is the first time I have met you two lords. How did you know I am County Princess Linghui?\"","Gu Jinghong blinked; he was wondering the same thing. He hadn't even spoken yet, so how did his father and uncle recognize her?","Gu Huaiyuan pointed to the fine steed Song Jinzhao was riding and said, \"This horse is a Ferghana horse, the very one County Princess Linghui must have won from Prince Wei of the Shuobei Kingdom. The only woman who could ride such a horse is you, Your Highness.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile. This Defender of Songzhou City was a capable man.","\"For Lord Gu to be a military officer yet so meticulous is truly rare.\"","Gu Baozhu rode forward a step. \"Eldest Brother, Second Brother, the County Princess is exhausted from the journey. Let's hurry and enter the city.\"","Gu Jinghong followed closely behind and called out, \"Father, Uncle.\"","Gu Huaiyuan glared fiercely at his son: I'll deal with you when we get back.","Understanding his father's meaning, the corners of Gu Jinghong's eyes couldn't help but droop.","Gu Gaoyuan looked at Song Qiming. \"I presume this is Lord Song?\"","So young and accompanying County Princess Linghui, with a similar resemblance in their brows and eyes, he had to be her younger brother.","Song Qiming dismounted and greeted them, \"I pay my respects to the two lords.\"","Although the Prefect of Suining and the Prefect of Songzhou were of the same level, Song Qiming was of the secondary fifth rank, while Gu Gaoyuan was already of the primary fifth rank, meaning Song Qiming was one grade lower in official rank.","Gu Gaoyuan quickly stepped forward to support Song Qiming's hands.","\"Lord Song, there is no need for such formalities. I have long heard that you are young and promising, a rare talent seen only once a century in the Dongzhao Kingdom. Seeing you today, you truly live up to your reputation.\"","Saying he was young was almost an understatement; he looked like a mere youth.","To be of the secondary fifth rank at seventeen meant that when he returned to the capital in three years, he would surely be promoted further. It could be said that his future was boundless and enviable.","Thinking of this, Gu Gaoyuan settled his mind and reached out his hand to gesture to Song Jinzhao.","\"After receiving the letter last night, my father had people tidy up the relay station overnight for the County Princess to stay temporarily. Please, enter the city.\""]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: Aunt and Nephew Punished","paragraphs":["After entering the city, there were many commoners on the streets, but Song Jinzhao noticed that the way they looked at her was rather strange. Along with curiosity, their gazes carried a hint of vigilance.","It would have been one thing if it were just one or two people, but every single person was like this, and not even the women were an exception.","When they reached the center of the main street, a row of sedan chairs blocked the way ahead.","Gu Huaiyuan spoke in a hearty tone, \"It is almost mealtime. The guests of Ruyi Pavilion must have blocked the road again. Men, quickly go and have them make way.\"","Seeing the guards run over to disperse the crowd, a flash of interest crossed Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Gu Baozhu poked her head out from behind.","\"County Princess, the food at Ruyi Pavilion is highly renowned in Songzhou City. Every mealtime, there are no empty seats, and sometimes you even have to wait in line. You simply must try it. I will have someone reserve a table in a moment.\"","Song Jinzhao asked in return, \"Is it truly that delicious? Can it compare to the capital?\"","Gu Baozhu pondered for a moment.","\"I have never been to the capital, so I do not know if the food at Ruyi Pavilion is better than there, but it is absolutely the best in the entire Southwest Province.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows slightly, seemingly intrigued by Gu Baozhu's words.","\"In that case, we must go and taste it tomorrow.\"","Hearing Song Jinzhao agree, Gu Baozhu's eyes instantly curved into a smile.","She wanted to stay with County Princess Linghui and see exactly what kind of person she was. Unfortunately, Song Qiming was the Prefect of Suining. How wonderful it would be if they could stay in Songzhou City.","If she could learn even half of the County Princess's skills, her life would be without regrets.","About half an hour later, the two Gu brothers stopped at the entrance of a courtyard, with a row of yamen runners standing guard outside.","Gu Gaoyuan extended his hand in invitation, \"County Princess, this is the post house.\"","After dismounting, everyone entered the building, while a few guards silently took their places beside the yamen runners.","As Gu Huaiyuan left, he took note of this and kept it in mind.","\"What is wrong?\" Gu Gaoyuan asked instinctively when he saw his younger brother pause, noticing something amiss in his expression.","Gu Huaiyuan shot a glance behind him.","\"Those guards look more like soldiers than the actual soldiers in the military camps.\"","Gu Jinghong, who was following beside them, chimed in, \"Father, you did not see them when they fought the bandits. They are much fiercer than the soldiers you trained.\"","Gu Baozhu echoed, \"Not just them, even the maidservants waiting on the County Princess know martial arts, and they are not weak either. That is why I say County Princess Linghui is amazing.\"","Gu Gaoyuan cast a surprised glance back at the guards standing beside the yamen runners.","\"Let us head back first. Father is still waiting at the estate.\"","Gu Gaoyuan nodded.","Inside a room at the post house, Song Qiming sat on a chair.","\"After entering the Southwest territory, apart from the bandits of Qingfeng Stronghold, we have not encountered any other thieves. The situation is actually better than we imagined.\"","Song Jinzhao did not agree with her younger brother's assessment.","\"Coupled with the guards Gu Jinghong brought, we have nearly two hundred people in total. What thief would dare to strike?\"","\"The commoners in Songzhou City are highly vigilant, as if it is carved into their bones. This shows that this place is not peaceful.\"","Song Shixue bit her lip in worry.","\"Suining Prefecture is even closer to the southwestern foreign tribes than Songzhou City. Would the situation not be even worse there?\"","Song Qiming smiled fearlessly, showing not even a trace of worry.","\"No matter how bad it is, there is no war right now. It will just be a bit more difficult to govern. We will know once we reach Suining Prefecture.\"","In the main hall of the Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner's residence, Gu Zhongxun grabbed Gu Baozhu's ear and scolded, \"You have quite the nerve, daring to deceive me alongside Jinghong? I am punishing you to reflect on your mistakes behind closed doors and practice the stance for three days.\"","Gu Baozhu jumped in panic, her voice so piercing it seemed it would bring the roof down.","\"No! I already made an appointment with the County Princess to take her to dine at Ruyi Pavilion tomorrow.\"","\"Besides, I only found out that Jinghong was going to wipe out the bandits after I arrived at Yunshan Temple. I was afraid something would happen to him, so I went along.\"","Kneeling on the ground, Gu Jinghong looked at Gu Baozhu in disbelief.","\"Little Aunt, how could you do this? You were the one who insisted on going. What do you mean you were afraid something would happen to me? It was clearly because you wanted to go too!\"","You promised to plead for me, yet you act like this!","Gu Huaiyuan grabbed Gu Jinghong's ear and twisted it a hundred and eighty degrees.","\"Your Little Aunt is your elder. Since you dare to speak to her like that, get lost to the ancestral hall and reflect on your actions.\"","With a bitter face, Gu Jinghong was led away by the servants.","Every single time, he was the only one being punished. This was far too unfair.","Seeing her nephew being taken away, Gu Baozhu clutched her stomach, hoping to gloss over the matter quickly.","\"Father, my stomach is so hungry. Can we eat now?\"","Gu Zhongxun stared at her intently, though there was not much anger on his face.","\"Jinghong does not even get to eat, and you still want to eat?\"","He poked his index finger on Gu Baozhu's nose and pushed her away, \"You will reflect behind closed doors after County Princess Linghui leaves. The three days are now changed to a month. I must make you learn your lesson this time.\"","\"Father...\" Gu Baozhu pleaded unwillingly.","Gu Zhongxun waved his hand and led his two sons outside, leaving Gu Baozhu standing alone in place, helplessly accepting her fate."]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: Gu Baozhu Soothed People with Just a Few Words, Delivering Meals to the Ancestral Hall","paragraphs":["After everyone in the Gu manor went back to rest for the night, Gu Baozhu sneaked into the kitchen to find something to eat.","Seeing some leftover white steamed buns in a basket, she quickly grabbed one and bit into it, then carried three more to the ancestral hall.","Under the dim candlelight, Gu Jinghong was kneeling on a futon, nodding off. Having traveled all day, he was already exhausted and sleepy.","Hearing the door open, the startled Gu Jinghong jolted awake.","Turning his head and seeing that it was Gu Baozhu, he stubbornly turned his back to her.","Gu Baozhu wasn't angry at this sight. With an ingratiating smile, she walked over to Gu Jinghong, took out a steamed bun, and offered it to him.","\"They wouldn't let you eat, and they wouldn't let me eat either. I just stole these from the kitchen, quickly have a bite to fill your stomach.\"","So his little aunt had been punished too.","The anger pent up in Gu Jinghong's chest instantly dissipated by more than half.","But the moment he remembered how she had thrown all the blame onto him, Gu Jinghong still felt a bit resentful.","Keeping a straight face, he gritted his teeth and turned his head away again, giving Gu Baozhu the back of his head.","\"If you had just stayed at Yunshan Temple, Father wouldn't have been so angry.\"","\"Not only did you not plead for me, but you also threw me under the bus. I'm never taking you out with me again.\"","Gu Baozhu crouched down and leaned her head in front of Gu Jinghong, blinking her large eyes pitifully.","\"It's better to save at least one of us. If I didn't say that, who would bring you food? Besides, your grandfather punished me by grounding me for a month after I finish hosting County Princess Linghui tomorrow. That's way worse than you kneeling in the ancestral hall.\"","Gu Jinghong's expression suddenly changed. \"Really?\"","Gu Baozhu pouted and nodded. She stuffed the steamed bun into Gu Jinghong's hand, her face falling into a depressed look.","\"Exactly. When the time comes, you have to plead for me.\"","Gu Jinghong's stomach was already growling with hunger. He bit off a third of the steamed bun in one go, the awkward resentment in his heart completely vanishing.","\"Don't worry, Little Aunt. Once I'm out of here, I'll definitely plead for you in front of Grandfather.\"","Just as the two were eating their steamed buns, the door to the ancestral hall was suddenly opened.","In a panic, Gu Jinghong hastily shoved the rest of the bun into his mouth. He didn't expect it to be so big and nearly choked, swallowing hard several times before finally getting it down.","\"Congwen, why are you here?\" Gu Baozhu stared in surprise at Gu Congwen, who was closing the door.","Gu Congwen was Gu Gaoyuan's son, and also Gu Baozhu's eldest nephew.","\"I heard from the servants that Jinghong was punished by Uncle to kneel in the ancestral hall and hadn't even eaten dinner, so I wanted to bring over some food.\"","\"Little Aunt, why are you here?\"","Gu Baozhu held up the half-eaten steamed bun in her hand and smiled, \"I'm here to deliver food too.\"","Gu Congwen walked over and opened his food box, revealing a sliced roast duck inside.","\"I was originally going to save it for a midnight snack, but it comes in handy right now.\"","Seeing the roast duck, the aunt and nephew's eyes lit up.","The steamed buns were too plain and they were craving meat, and now they had it.","\"Cousin, I knew you were the best to me.\"","Gu Jinghong said excitedly to Gu Congwen, then picked up a duck leg and took a big bite of meat.","Gu Baozhu picked up the other duck leg, eating just as boldly.","Watching the two devour the food, Gu Congwen felt both helpless and heartbroken for them.","\"Wiping out the mountain bandits is Uncle's job. Don't take such risks next time. If something were to happen to you, Grandmother and Aunt would be worried to death.\"","After finishing the duck leg, Gu Jinghong picked up a wing.","\"Cousin, you devote yourself entirely to reading the books of sages. Whenever Uncle talks about you, his face is full of smiles, and he is full of praise in front of outsiders.\"","\"But my dad treats me like a personal servant and won't let me participate in any important matters. I just want to prove myself to him.\"","Gu Congwen replied, \"Uncle is just worried about you. Besides, you are still young and have a lot to learn. What better way to learn than by staying by Uncle's side?\"","Gu Baozhu kept her head down and silently ate the roast duck. While the two were talking, she had already eaten over a dozen pieces.","Her eldest nephew was even more long-winded than her father and eldest brother. She wondered who he learned it from.","After lecturing his younger cousin, Gu Congwen looked toward Gu Baozhu.","Just as he was about to speak, Gu Baozhu jumped up and ran outside, her figure blurring as she moved faster than a cat.","\"I'm full, I'm going back to sleep first!\"","Gu Jinghong shoved the food box, now full of bones, into Gu Congwen's hands.","\"Cousin, you should go back quickly. It won't be good if my dad finds out.\"","Gu Congwen glanced at the bones in the food box, stood up, and took off his outer coat, handing it to Gu Jinghong.","\"It's cold at night, drape this over yourself.\"","Gu Jinghong nodded his head rapidly like a chick pecking at rice.","\"Don't worry, Cousin. I have a strong physique, I won't freeze.\""]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: An Audience with Gu Zhongxun","paragraphs":["Half an hour after breakfast the next day, Song Qiming put on his official uniform and prepared to visit the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest, Gu Zhongxun.","\"Sister, I will go over first. You all can come to the Gu residence to meet up with me closer to noon.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded slightly. \"Tell Miss Gu I will arrive a bit later.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath, his expression incredibly serious.","Arriving in the Southwest meant a new beginning, but it also represented immense pressure.","This was especially true regarding the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest, Gu Zhongxun. If he wanted to develop and grow stronger under his command, this man was crucial.","In four years, he had to become the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest himself, but he had already met Gu Zhongxun's eldest son, Gu Gaoyuan, yesterday.","This man was no fool. Just as his sister had expected, he would be his biggest competitor for the position of Provincial Administration Commissioner!","When he arrived at the commissioner's residence, a steward was already waiting at the door.","Seeing a young official emerge from the sedan chair, the steward quickly ran down to welcome the guest.","Song Qiming glanced at the plaque and the furnishings at the entrance.","The main gate of this residence was half a zhang taller than those of officials of the same rank in the capital, and the vermilion doors looked as if they were made of iron plates.","There were several guards at the door, dressed just like the escorts Gu Jinghong had brought with him that day.","At a glance, there were no fewer than twenty of them; the security could be described as extremely strict.","\"I am Song Qiming, the newly appointed Prefect of Suining Prefecture. I have come today specifically to visit the Lord Commissioner.\"","The steward lowered his eyes, his gaze falling on Song Qiming's collar.","He spoke in a respectful tone, \"My lord knew that Prefect Song was coming today and specifically instructed his subordinate to wait here. Prefect Song, please come in.\"","Walking into the Gu residence, there were also guards on both sides of the stone path leading to the front hall, about ten in total.","Passing through the front hall to the second hall, the number of guards on both sides did not diminish.","The more Song Qiming looked, the heavier his heart became. If the residence of the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest was already like this, what would Suining Prefecture be like?","Stepping into the second hall, the back of a figure wearing a red official uniform appeared before Song Qiming's eyes.","Hearing the footsteps, Gu Zhongxun turned around. His calm gaze swept from top to bottom, and the look in his eyes was gradually replaced by admiration.","\"I knew beforehand that Lord Song was young and promising, but seeing you today surprises me even more.\"","Song Qiming cupped his hands and bowed to Gu Zhongxun. \"Your humble servant, Prefect of Suining Song Qiming, pays his respects to the Lord Commissioner.\"","Gu Zhongxun gently raised his hand.","\"I have already heard from Jinghong about what happened at Longtou Mountain. I am very pleased that Prefect Song eradicated the bandits of Qingfeng Stronghold and eliminated a local menace for the people as soon as you arrived in the Southwest.\"","Song Qiming curled his lips into a shallow smile, not letting Gu Zhongxun's praise show too much on his face.","\"It was all my sister's doing. Your humble servant merely killed a few bandits, and Young General Gu also helped a lot by arriving in time.\"","Gu Zhongxun stroked his beard. He agreed with his youngest son punishing his grandson, but he was still satisfied with Gu Jinghong's performance.","He was happy in his heart that the Gu family had a worthy successor.","\"It's just the younger generation playing around. As long as they didn't cause any trouble for County Princess Linghui, it is fine.\"","After a brief casual chat, Gu Zhongxun led Song Qiming to the private office where he handled official business.","\"Suining Prefecture is the imperial court's gateway to the foreign tribes of the Southwest, and it is also the prefecture with the most frequent exchanges between the two sides. There are some situations I still need to brief you on.\"","\"Especially after the salt fields in Binzhou were discovered, the imperial court has already reached an agreement with Panzhou...\"","Song Qiming nodded in response from time to time, committing Gu Zhongxun's words to memory so he could verify them one by one once he arrived in Suining.","Meanwhile, in a boudoir in the backyard of the Gu residence.","\"Has County Princess Linghui not arrived yet?\" Gu Baozhu asked her maid in confusion.","The maid shook her head. \"I heard from the steward that only Prefect Song came.\"","Gu Baozhu picked up a pearl hairpin from the vanity and placed it in her hair.","\"It must be that Prefect Song needs to discuss official business with my father, which is why County Princess Linghui is arriving later. Go to Ruyi Pavilion first and secure the ingredients, lest the food we want to eat is sold out by then.\""]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: Going to Ruyi Zhai","paragraphs":["Mid-morning, Song Jinzhao brought her two siblings to the Gu Manor.","\"Greetings, County Princess,\" Gu Zhongxun said, rising to welcome them along with the two Gu brothers.","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly, her gaze fixing on Gu Zhongxun's face.","Compared to the officials in the imperial court, his physique was much more robust—not fat, but solid muscle.","\"Lord Gu, there is no need for such formality. I have just arrived in Songzhou City, and I fear I will be residing in the Suining Prefecture for the next few years. I will have to rely on your support in many matters to come.\"","Gu Zhongxun invited Song Jinzhao to take a seat in the main hall.","\"You are too modest, County Princess. You wiped out the Qingfeng Stronghold as soon as you arrived in Songzhou City. It is this official who should be relying on you.\"","Upon hearing the maid's report, Gu Baozhu hurriedly called for Madam Gu to come out and welcome the guests.","Seeing that all four members of the Song family were present, she couldn't hide the excitement in her eyes.","Since the County Princess valued their agreement so much, it would be a breeze to ask her out to play in the future.","After exchanging a few pleasantries, Gu Zhongxun's wife smiled and extended an invitation.","\"It is nearly noon, and the food in the manor has already been prepared. How about the County Princess stays for a meal?\"","Gu Baozhu grew anxious upon hearing this and hastily shot her mother a look.","\"Mother, the County Princess and I already agreed to go to the Ruyi Pavilion. I've even booked a private room.\"","The rest of the Gu family frowned and looked at Gu Baozhu.","They knew the two had an appointment, but the invitation had to be offered, otherwise it would be far too impolite.","Gu Baozhu didn't understand, but Song Jinzhao understood the Gu family's intentions perfectly.","She helped smooth things over, saying, \"I've heard that the dishes at Ruyi Pavilion are the best in the southwest. I would love to try them, so I won't be dining at your esteemed manor today.\"","Madam Gu smoothly seized the out.","\"In that case, we shall do it next time.\"","Gu Zhongxun instructed, \"Baozhu, the County Princess and her family are new here and unfamiliar with Songzhou City. You must host them well.\"","Gu Baozhu's eyes curved into smiling crescent moons.","\"Don't worry, Father. I will definitely take good care of the County Princess.\"","After stepping out of the manor's gates, Gu Baozhu looked back toward the ancestral hall and pursed her lips, seemingly a bit conflicted.","Seeing her hesitation, Song Shixue subconsciously called out to her.","Gu Baozhu turned around with a sweet smile, ultimately deciding not to bring Gu Jinghong along.","If she called him out of the ancestral hall now, he would definitely be punished upon his return. It was just a meal, after all; if a one-month grounding turned into two months, it would be too great a loss.","Having thought it through, Gu Baozhu neatly stepped into the stirrups and swung onto her horse's back.","By the time they arrived at Ruyi Pavilion, the first floor was already packed with no empty seats.","A waiter came up to greet them with an enthusiastic smile.","\"Miss Gu, you're finally here! If you had come any later, the river crabs in the kitchen wouldn't have been saved for you.\"","Behind the checkout counter on the right side of the first floor, the manager cast a glance at Qingshuang, who was following behind Song Jinzhao. His gaze narrowed slightly before he casually lowered his head and continued calculating his accounts as if nothing had happened.","Heading up to the third floor, the private room Gu Baozhu had booked was the Heaven Number One room, which boasted the best view. Inside, the bowls and chopsticks had already been neatly arranged.","The waiter bowed and said, \"Please wait a moment, esteemed guests. I will go and serve the dishes right away.\"","Once the door was closed, Gu Baozhu looked at Song Jinzhao.","\"I ordered all the signature dishes of Ruyi Pavilion. They are all the most delicious ones.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up her teacup and took a sip.","\"Do you often come to Ruyi Pavilion to eat, Miss Gu?\"","Gu Baozhu replied, \"Of course. The food here is great, and they have new dishes from time to time. Jinghong and I come here to eat every few days.\"","The dishes were continuously brought in by the waiter. In the meantime, Gu Baozhu's mouth never stopped as she introduced each dish to Song Jinzhao one by one. She was even more detailed than the waiter; just listening to her was enough to make one's mouth water.","After eating and drinking their fill, everyone rested for a while in the private room.","Seeing that it was about time, Song Shixue, having received a signal, looked at Gu Baozhu and said, \"I'd like to go for a stroll in the market downstairs. Could Miss Gu accompany me?\"","The highly curious Song Anhao grabbed Song Shixue's sleeve. \"Take me with you.\"","Gu Baozhu stuck out her full belly a bit. \"Of course.\"","After saying that, she noticed Song Jinzhao was still sitting there. \"Is the County Princess not coming? The market in Songzhou City is quite bustling.\"","A hint of fatigue appeared on Song Jinzhao's face.","\"I feel a bit sleepy after eating. You all go ahead. I'll head back to the relay station shortly.\"","Song Qiming said, \"I'll stay with my sister.\"","Gu Baozhu nodded. \"Alright, then I'll take Shixue and Anhao downstairs.\"","After the three of them left with their maids and guards, Qingshuang silently knocked on the door of the adjacent room.","A short while later, the manager of Ruyi Pavilion entered the Heaven Number One room.","\"This subordinate greets the County Princess, and greets the Eldest Young Master.\""]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: The Affair of Suining (1)","paragraphs":["Inside the Heaven Number One private room, all the other servants had been dismissed, leaving only the Song siblings and Qingshuang.","Rise, Song Jinzhao said with a smile. She was highly satisfied with this man's performance since his arrival in the Southwest.","Feng Yi stood up and remained respectfully in place, quietly waiting for Song Jinzhao's questions.","Song Jinzhao's bright eyes swept over him as she asked leisurely, How much have you found out about the situation in Suining Prefecture?","Before leaving the capital, Song Jinzhao had instructed Qingshuang to have Feng Yi investigate Suining Prefecture. He was to look into every detail, gathering intelligence not only on the officials but also on the common people.","Feng Yi raised his head and began to explain slowly.","Upon receiving the County Princess's orders, your subordinate dispatched men to Suining Prefecture to gather information. Suining Prefecture governs four counties: Qingxia, Yunzhu, Songhe, and Yanshan. Among them, Qingxia and Yanshan border the settlements of thirteen foreign tribes in the Southwest. Therefore, compared to Yunzhu and Songhe, the situations in Qingxia and Yanshan are much more complicated.","Sitting in his chair, Song Qiming narrowed his eyes. Complicated in what way?","Earlier that morning at the Gu residence, Gu Zhongxun had already given him a general overview of Suining Prefecture, specifically mentioning Qingxia and Yanshan counties.","He had repeatedly warned that the border regions could not afford any unrest, advising him to turn a blind eye to certain matters, as nothing was more important than the stability of the Southwest.","When he tried to ask for more details, Gu Zhongxun had deflected his questions, simply telling him to go and see for himself after taking office.","Feng Yi looked at Song Qiming, his tone growing noticeably heavier as he spoke of these two counties.","Since the territories are adjacent, interactions between the commoners are inevitable. However, due to their different tribes, disputes frequently break out, especially with the people of the Wumeng and Shimen tribes.","If a dispute occurs within the county town, it ranges from verbal abuse to physical brawls. But in the villages, fights involving dozens or even hundreds of people are a common occurrence.","Whenever such incidents happen, the magistrates of Qingxia and Yanshan counties always placate the situation by holding their own local citizens accountable. The locals are full of complaints, and public resentment is incredibly high. Over the past two years, there have even been two civilian uprisings, though both were suppressed by the local magistrates.","Hearing this, Song Qiming abruptly stood up, a look of disbelief on his face.","Civilian uprisings? Has it really gotten that severe? Is the Prefect of Suining aware of this?","Feng Yi nodded emphatically.","Of course he is aware. The constables in Qingxia and Yanshan were insufficient, so Suining Prefecture had to send additional manpower.","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows and asked, To make the local governments of both places so wary, the opposing forces must be quite substantial.","How many people are there in the Wumeng and Shimen tribes, and how large are their settlements?","There were hundreds of tribes, big and small, in the Southwest. Not all of them were as powerful as the Yang clan of Panzhou or the Mu clan of Ningzhou, but there were a few tribes just below them in strength that had relatively large populations and settlements.","Feng Yi shook his head. In terms of numbers, even if you add up all the elderly, weak, women, and children, the Wumeng and Shimen tribes only have about ten thousand people each. Their settlements are only a third of the size of Qingxia County, with sixty percent of that being mountainous forests. Among the hundreds of foreign tribes in the Southwest, their power can only be considered lower-middle tier.","Song Jinzhao lifted her eyelids, her gaze focusing into a sharp point.","Do they have a backer?","Feng Yi gave a knowing smile, his tone carrying a hint of flattery toward Song Jinzhao.","The County Princess is wise. Their backers are exactly the Yang clan of Panzhou and the Mu clan of Ningzhou.","Song Qiming suddenly understood. He sat back down and leaned against his chair. So it's them. No wonder the magistrates don't dare to provoke them.","Feng Yi nodded. The daughter of the current Wumeng tribal chief married the third son of the Panzhou Pacification Commissioner, and the same goes for the Shimen tribe. Because the Wumeng and Shimen tribes border Qingxia and Yanshan counties respectively, they act as the eyes and ears for Panzhou and Ningzhou within Suining Prefecture. Any news from the entire Southwest or even the imperial court is immediately relayed back to them."]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: The Affair of Suining (2)","paragraphs":["The room grew increasingly quiet, and the expressions on Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming's faces became more and more serious.","Song Qiming's mind was racing like a raging storm.","After a long moment of deep thought, he asked, \"What is the story behind the repeated assassinations of the Suining Prefect?\"","A mocking smirk tugged at the corners of Feng Yi's mouth, almost as if he took pleasure in the news of the assassinations.","\"It can be considered bringing it upon themselves. The people who assassinated the Suining Prefect were actually commoners forced into becoming bandits. Some of them have never even robbed civilian homes; they specifically target officials. The officials in Qingxia County and Yanshan County have faced even more assassination attempts than the Suining Prefect.\"","\"The magistrates of those two counties send out their runners to arrest these people en masse, while they themselves hide in their county offices all day, too afraid to step outside. It is no exaggeration to say that the people in these two counties live in precarious times, constantly suffering in deep waters and scorching fire.\"","Having found out about this situation, Feng Yi truly felt a sense of panic for Song Qiming.","This was more than just a mess; calling it an eternal cesspit would not be an overstatement.","Song Qiming's brows furrowed deeply into three distinct creases. For a moment, he felt as if a massive mountain was pressing down on his head. Yet, at the same time, a part of him was eager to try his hand, wishing he could rush to Suining Prefecture immediately and do something great.","A hint of sarcasm appeared on Song Jinzhao's lips.","\"The situation in Suining Prefecture is so terrible, yet when we met Gu Zhongxun today, he showed absolutely no sign of it.\"","Suining Prefecture was located in the Southwest Province and fell under the jurisdiction of the Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner. If one were to claim that Gu Zhongxun was unaware of these circumstances, not even a ghost would believe it.","Song Qiming clenched his jaw. \"It seems that Lord Gu has not been very responsible in his position as the Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner.\"","At least in his eyes, it was an absolute disaster.","To avoid sparking conflicts in the southwest, he yielded at every turn; calling it groveling would not be an exaggeration.","But this approach would only feed the growing appetites of the foreign tribes in the southwest, while simultaneously losing the hearts of the common people.","Hearing Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming blatantly criticize Gu Zhongxun for his inaction, Feng Yi's heart skipped a beat, and he silently kept his mouth shut.","For a moment, the private room fell silent once again.","After a long while, Song Qiming seemed to have made a resolution. With a determined look in his eyes, he said to Song Jinzhao, \"Sister, I want to head to Suining Prefecture to take up my post as soon as possible.\"","The former Suining Prefect had left at the beginning of the year, and there was no telling how much official business was waiting to be handled at the government office. He could not wait to go and see the situation for himself.","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"We will rest for the night and set off tomorrow morning.\"","The more difficulties there were, the more time was needed to solve them. She was not afraid of failing to solve them; she was only afraid of running out of time.","By the time Song Shixue and Song Anhao returned to the relay station, it was already late afternoon.","She widened her eyes in surprise. \"We are leaving tomorrow? Didn't we say we were going to rest for two days?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"The situation in Suining Prefecture is not looking good, and your brother wants to take up his post as soon as possible.\"","Song Shixue nodded and recounted the details of her afternoon shopping trip with Gu Baozhu to Song Jinzhao.","\"Judging from what Miss Gu said, Lord Gu indeed intends to have his son succeed him.\"","Song Jinzhao sneered. Initially, she had thought Gu Zhongxun had some capability and had managed the Southwest Province well, but she never expected it to be just a facade. The hidden dangers had already been buried hundreds of meters deep.","If she were him, let alone having a son succeed him, she would not leave a single Gu family descendant behind. After retiring, she would definitely take her entire family and hide far away, lest the situation erupt one day and the imperial court behead them all.","Early the next morning, Song Qiming went to the Gu residence to bid his farewells.","Gu Zhongxun asked in surprise, \"Leaving so soon? Wouldn't it be better to stay and rest for a few more days?\"","Song Qiming cupped his hands in apology. \"After receiving your guidance yesterday, My Lord, this humble official wishes to take up the post in Suining as quickly as possible. I presume a great deal of official business has piled up there.\"","Gu Zhongxun smiled and stroked his beard.","\"It is truly a blessing for the people of Suining that you think this way.\"","Based on their official ranks, Gu Zhongxun did not need to be so modest and polite to Song Qiming, but who could ignore the fact that his sister was County Princess Linghui.","With a powerful backer, one's status was always different from that of ordinary people."]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: Muddy Road, Sheltering from the Rain","paragraphs":["Knowing that Song Jinzhao and his group were leaving, Gu Baozhu's mood suddenly sank.","Seeing his sister so upset, Gu Gaoyuan instinctively tried to comfort her, \"Father told you to reflect on your mistakes behind closed doors starting tomorrow. Even if Princess Linghui stayed in Songzhou City for a few more days, you still wouldn't be able to go out.\"","Hearing this, the disappointment in Gu Baozhu's heart instantly turned into displeasure.","She jerked her head up, her brows furrowed tightly as she glared at her older brother, her lips pouting longer than a duck's bill.","Gu Gaoyuan was so frightened that he held his breath, his lips pressed tightly together as if sewn shut by a thread.","He stammered, \"Little sister, I was wrong. I'll go plead with Father for you right now.\"","\"Hmph!\" Gu Baozhu raised her chin and turned to leave, without saying whether she forgave him or not.","Gu Gaoyuan remorsefully slapped his own mouth.","If he had known, he would have kept his mouth shut.","The capital of Suining Prefecture was located right in the center of the entire prefecture, surrounded by Qingxia County, Yunzhu County, Songhe County, and Yanshan County. Starting from Songzhou City, one only needed to pass through Yunzhu County to arrive there.","According to the original plan, Song Jinzhao and the others would spend the night in Yunzhu County after dinner. But unexpectedly, just as they entered the borders of Yunzhu County, a heavy downpour began.","Raindrops the size of beans pattered down, making the already potholed dirt road even more difficult to travel.","The muddy yellow earth stuck to the horses' hooves, making them very slippery. Coupled with the numerous puddles on the road, the carts carrying their luggage frequently got stuck, cutting their travel speed by more than half.","Seeing the procession stop several times, Song Jinzhao lifted the carriage curtain and said to Lanxi, who was following alongside, \"Let's go to the village ahead to take shelter from the rain.\"","Wearing a bamboo hat, Lanxi looked ahead. The village built in the distance was clearly visible to the naked eye, only about a mile away.","He turned his horse around and called out to those behind him, \"Everyone, put in a bit more effort! The Princess said we will take shelter in the village ahead.\"","Even though everyone was wearing rain capes, the rain was so heavy that it soaked through to their clothes, making them feel colder and colder.","Hearing that there was a place to take shelter, the crowd excitedly held their breath and pushed the carts forward, their speed actually a bit faster than before.","Fifteen minutes later, Qingshuang dismounted and arrived at the door of a household. Through the half-open gate, she could vaguely see a few people sitting inside.","\"Excuse me, could we borrow your house to take shelter from the rain?\"","Seeing that the visitor was a woman, the wariness of the three people inside instantly diminished quite a bit.","A woman wearing a gray cloth shirt walked over. Her clothes were covered in patches from top to bottom, without a single intact spot to be found.","Qingshuang blinked. Just how many years had this garment been worn?","\"Little sister, are you alone—\" Before she could finish her sentence, she saw the massive convoy behind Qingshuang, and the woman's expression instantly froze, as if a basin of cold water had been poured over her.","She paused for a moment, her tone sounding a bit stiff.","\"With so many people, I'm afraid my broken-down house isn't big enough for you all to take shelter. Why don't you try another house?\"","At a glance, they were clearly outsiders. With horses and carriages, and all of them carrying swords, she didn't want any trouble.","Hearing there were many people, the man who had been sitting on a stool also walked over.","He craned his neck to take a look outside, and his expression also grew wary.","Qingshuang took some silver from her clothes and handed it to the woman.","\"Auntie, we are passing merchants. The rain is too heavy and the road is too slippery. Please let us borrow a place to stay.\"","When she came over just now, she had already noticed that this house was the largest in the entire village.","At a glance, it had three rooms and a woodshed, while the others only had two rooms.","Staring at the silver in Qingshuang's hand, the couple was tempted.","It looked like about two taels. If they could pay, they probably weren't bad people.","The two exchanged a glance. The woman took the silver, and the man opened both sides of the door. \"Come in.\"","Qingshuang immediately waved to the people behind her.","After leaving some men in the carriages to guard the luggage, everyone else entered the house to escape the rain.","A dark crowd packed the three rooms. Seeing that it was too crowded, Song Jinzhao had Lanxi send some people to the woodshed; it had a roof there, so they wouldn't get wet either."]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: The Current Situation of the People","paragraphs":["In the shabby main room, the male host sat restlessly on a long wooden bench, as if he had hemorrhoids, his eyes filled not only with fear but also with curiosity.","With so many people here, he hadn't expected the leader to be a young lady, and such a young one at that, looking only slightly older than his own daughter.","\"Noble guests, where have you come from, and where are you heading?\"","Ordinary merchants wouldn't travel with so many women, and their attire was entirely different. At first glance, it was obvious they were young masters and misses from wealthy, prominent families.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"We came from the capital and are heading to the prefectural city.\"","The host's eyes widened in surprise. He turned his head to glance outside at the row of handcarts covered with tarpaulins, which were clearly loaded with a substantial amount of goods.","Judging by their direction, they must have come from Songzhou City and were heading to the prefectural city of Suining Prefecture.","\"This is your first time here, isn't it?\"","Song Qiming nodded. \"How did you guess?\"","The host smiled and answered, \"I've seen many merchants over the years, and you clearly look like newcomers.\"","Hearing this, Song Qiming asked with interest, \"I heard that bandits and robbers often appear in Suining Prefecture. Are there still many merchants traveling through?\"","Logically, chaotic places would have fewer merchants. Suining Prefecture had a terrible reputation, so very few merchants should be willing to come.","The host explained, \"There are still quite a few merchants going to Suining City. There are robbers on the road, but they generally don't kill. As long as you pay a toll when you meet them, they'll let you pass. It's not like Qingxia and Yanshan, where they want both your money and your life. Wealthy merchants aren't willing to go there.\"","Song Jinzhao remarked, \"These bandits are quite smart. They know that if they push things to the extreme, they won't be able to rob anything in the future.\"","The host nodded. \"They can't completely stop goods from being sold in Suining. If they make too much trouble, the government will still intervene on the road from Songzhou City to Suining City.\"","Half an hour passed, and the rain outside grew heavier, showing no signs of stopping.","Looking up, the entire sky was filled with moisture and covered in a misty haze.","\"It's always like this during the rainy season. It won't stop anytime soon.\"","Seeing that the rain was relentless, when it was time to eat, Song Jinzhao had the servants borrow the villager's stove to heat up their food.","Looking at a table full of meat and vegetable dishes, along with white steamed buns larger than a fist, the family of three who hadn't tasted meat in months and had never eaten their fill couldn't help but swallow their saliva. The sound of their gulping was so loud that everyone in the room could hear it.","Song Qiming didn't hesitate to pick up a steamed bun and place it in the host's bowl.","\"We burned quite a lot of your firewood. Consider this meal our treat. Please, eat more.\"","The host hastily tried to put the bun back.","\"I can't possibly accept this, I can't. These are all very expensive.\"","How much could firewood be worth? Not to mention, Song Jinzhao and her group had already paid them in silver.","Song Jinzhao pushed a dish of spicy pork toward the hostess, and Song Shixue helped move it closer as well.","\"It's fine, we brought plenty. If we don't eat it, it will just spoil.\"","Seeing that the servants around them were all eating, and under the warm invitation of the three Song family members, the host finally picked up the steamed bun. A simple, honest smile of a poor farmer appeared on his face. \"Thank you, noble guests.\"","Seeing the head of the household start to eat, the woman and the young man sitting nearby finally began to dig in.","\"Brother Chai, who are these people?\" Five men wearing straw rain capes walked up to the door and stopped in their tracks when they saw the room full of people.","The host stood up, holding half a steamed bun; this was already the second bun he was eating.","\"Village Chief, they are passing merchants taking shelter from the heavy rain.\"","Rainwater slid down his face. Seeing that everything was fine inside, the white-haired old man felt half his worries dissipate.","The other four men looked at the lavish spread on the table and the steamed buns the three members of the Chai family were eating, their eyes brimming with so much envy it practically spilled over.","They had originally thought the Chai family might be in danger from these strangers, but they never expected them to be eating so well. This meal was worth at least a few hundred copper coins.","\"Noble guests, this is the Village Chief of our Baijia Village.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded slightly in acknowledgment, a polite smile on her face.","All five men were carrying hoes; the vigilance of the commoners here was truly strong.","Seeing that Brother Chai's family was in no danger, the Village Chief took his leave. \"Since everything is fine, we will be going now.\"","After saying that, he turned to leave. When the other four turned around, their gazes still hadn't left the food. If only they could stay and eat together.","Call us back, call us back to stay.","To their disappointment, even after walking a dozen steps, no voice called out for them to stay for a meal. Helpless, the four men had no choice but to follow the Village Chief away.","Worried that Song Jinzhao might misunderstand, the host immediately explained.","\"During the harsh winter, bandits occasionally come to the village to steal grain, so whenever strangers enter the village, every household is on high alert.\"","Seeing this situation, Song Qiming's heart sank to the bottom. Such deeply ingrained, subconscious reactions were definitely not formed in a day or two.","The common people's lives were already difficult enough; with bandits coming to rob them from time to time, how could they possibly survive?"]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: Wave After Wave of Bandits","paragraphs":["As they were finishing their meal, the rain began to lighten, and a quarter of an hour later, it stopped completely.","Qingshuang whispered a reminder, \"Miss, if we don't leave now, we won't make it to the campsite.\"","The mud on the road wouldn't dry in a single day, and judging by the weather, it might rain again soon. Setting off as soon as possible was the best plan.","Song Jinzhao said gently, \"We depart immediately. Hitch two horses to each cart instead of one.\"","They had plenty of horses; let alone two horses pulling a cart, even three wouldn't be a problem.","Just as she stepped into the carriage, Song Jinzhao heard a flurry of hurried footsteps, sounding like a large crowd running toward them.","She poked her head out to look ahead and saw dozens of villagers staring blankly at her, including quite a few children.","When the male host noticed this, he awkwardly twitched the corners of his mouth and waved his hands, urging Song Jinzhao and her group to leave.","\"The villagers are just curious seeing so many strangers. You noble folks should hurry and leave.\"","Every one of them looked as if they had starved for over ten days. More than a decade ago, during a famine in the village, the villagers would resort to robbing when begging failed. He was more or less afraid.","Seeing the man's apprehension, Song Jinzhao entered the carriage without a word. When the apocalypse had arrived, she had seen it all; this was just a small scene.","However, Song Qiming, who was following beside her, looked grim. Recalling the civilian uprisings mentioned by the shopkeeper of Ruyi Pavilion, he felt as if they were about to happen right before his eyes.","The worrisome event did not occur. After the convoy moved forward, the villagers of Baijia Village did not chase after them, but instead stood in place, chattering and discussing.","When the male host walked over, the village chief finally asked, \"Brother Chai, where are they going to do business?\"","The host replied, \"They came from the capital and are heading to Suining City.\"","The chief of Baijia Village couldn't help but scoff, \"Bringing so many goods and so many women, how much will be left by the time they reach Suining City? Are they fools?\"","The host gave a fake chuckle. \"They are all carrying swords and blades; they must be capable.\"","Seeing the convoy moving far away, the villagers' discussions grew louder, all predicting how many bandits Song Jinzhao's group would encounter and how much they would be robbed of.","Four hours later.","After driving away highwaymen demanding money for the fourth time, everyone's mood had become remarkably calm.","There was someone blocking the road to rob them on every mountain, and even on flat roads, people would suddenly pop out clamoring for money.","Their weapons were a motley assortment, and their attire didn't look like professional bandits; they just looked a bit fiercer than ordinary villagers.","The guards would only strike a couple of times before the attackers fled, making it feel like child's play.","Lanxi knitted her brows, already somewhat annoyed. \"These bandits have no situational awareness at all.\"","Twenty against one hundred and thirty-eight, how could they possibly win? They didn't look like they had any formidable martial arts skills either.","Inside the carriage, Song Qiming stared blankly out the window, his expression never having improved.","After chasing off yet another wave of unprofessional robbers, Song Qiming closed his eyes, took a deep breath, and let out a heavy sigh.","He lamented with a heavy tone, \"Ah-jie, Suining Prefecture is too chaotic. It truly won't do if it isn't governed properly.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. Only through personal experience could one know how severe the situation was.","According to what Feng Yi had said, Yunzhu County was relatively well-off. How terrible must Qingxia County and Yanshan County be?","They would probably run into a bandit with every step they took.","\"Their movements are clumsy, their weapons are mismatched, and even their expressions are tense. They must have recently turned to banditry, or they are nearby villagers acting as part-time robbers. Catching them isn't hard; the difficulty lies in figuring out how to stop the common people from coming out to rob.\"","Song Qiming pressed his temples in distress, rubbing them vigorously. His chest felt as hot as if it were on fire.","\"At the end of the day, they are just too poor. We have to give them hope first.\""]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: Suining City Has Inner and Outer City Walls","paragraphs":["From Songzhou City to Suining City, a three-day journey, there were a staggering nine highway robberies, big and small.","Song Qiming's expression went from heavy to blank. It wasn't until he caught sight of the city wall's silhouette that he finally regained a bit of spirit.","He made a solemn vow, as if to encourage himself.","\"Sister, I must govern Suining Prefecture well as soon as possible, so the commoners can live a good life.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at him. The youth's eyes were firm and his face serious, bearing a bit of Ye Liangyu's shadow.","\"I believe you can do it.\" Although she had been highly involved in his life, it was a fact that he had placed third in the imperial examination at the mere age of fourteen. Song Jinzhao believed in his abilities.","Hearing this, Song Qiming clenched his fists, silently cheering himself on.","The plans he had envisioned before coming to Suining needed to be revised; he would start tonight.","As they gradually approached the city wall and got a clear look, they realized it was merely a crude barrier built of yellow earth, visually estimated to be only about ten feet high.","One must know that a prefectural city wall should be at least twenty-five feet high and built with brick and stone. This was completely against regulations.","Being so low and made entirely of dirt, it could easily be breached by enemy forces. It served no defensive purpose at all.","The archway was very small, about the width of a regular household's main gate, looking like it could only accommodate a single horse carriage passing through.","Song Qiming blinked, feeling a lump in his throat.","Song Jinzhao looked at the guards checking travel passes at the gate.","The entry and exit inspections were actually stricter than in Songzhou City, but why were these men all wearing commoners' clothes instead of official yamen uniforms?","They even had red cloth strips tied around their cuffs, looking somewhat like Young Pioneers checking for red scarves at an elementary school gate.","They reached out to block people using wooden sticks rather than swords.","A man stretched his neck to look behind Song Jinzhao and her group.","There were at least a hundred people. What were they here for?","He asked sternly, \"Where are you from? What is your business in Suining City? Take out your travel passes.\"","Song Qiming dismounted his horse. He looked up at the three characters for \"Suining City\" carved roughly into the wall, feeling even more stifled.","\"Are you yamen runners of Suining City? Why doesn't this city wall even have a proper plaque?\"","Were they already poor to this extent?","The man looked Song Qiming up and down. His luxurious silk clothes and the jade pendant tied at his waist looked very expensive. This was a wealthy person.","\"You must be outsiders. Here, only the inner city wall has a plaque. The outer city wall was built by the commoners themselves, so there is no plaque.\"","\"Although we are not yamen runners, we are militiamen officially recognized by the government. We are completely legitimate. Hurry up and take out your travel passes.\"","This single sentence left Song Qiming dumbfounded.","What did he mean by built by themselves? Suining City had an inner and outer wall?","\"The prefectural office didn't provide the funds?\" he pressed in disbelief.","The man complained, \"The prefectural office's money was all used to build the inner city. Our Suining City is too big, you will understand once you go inside.\"","After their travel passes were checked and they entered the city, not only did Song Qiming's footsteps halt, but even Song Jinzhao froze in place.","As far as the eye could see, there were only farm fields. Behind the fields were a couple of houses. It looked neat, but it was just too bizarre.","It was possible to have fields inside a city wall, but usually not this many, and they were always located in unpopulated areas. Where else would you find farmlands right upon entering the city gates?","Song Jinzhao took out her binoculars and looked around.","\"Every household is exactly the same. Is Suining City really this big?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"I've seen the Ministry of Revenue's records. Suining City covers an area of three thousand two hundred mu. It's considered relatively small for a prefectural city.\"","Turning her head to look at the crude city wall, Song Jinzhao squeezed her horse's belly and moved forward.","\"What you're talking about must be the inner city. We probably haven't even entered the actual city yet.\"","Song Qiming was extremely puzzled.","\"The Ministry of Revenue's records don't mention an outer city. Does the imperial court not know about this?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Let's find the inner city first. We'll know once we get to the prefectural office.\"","The fact that Feng Yi hadn't specifically mentioned it meant it wasn't important.","Suining City had probably always been like this."]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Entering the Inner City, Arriving at the Government Office","paragraphs":["In the farmlands on both sides of the road, peasants bending over their work raised their heads one by one to watch the large group of people and horses pass by, their eyes filled with curiosity.","After traveling in a straight line for an hour, the city walls finally came into view.","The twenty-foot-high walls were entirely constructed of dark cyan bricks. Yamen runners stood guard at every gateway along the wall, looking as heavily guarded as if an enemy attack were imminent.","Song Qiming puffed out his chest, took a deep breath, and exhaled.","\"Now this is a proper city wall. It actually looks quite similar to the one in Songzhou City.\"","Seeing their large numbers, the yamen runner in charge of inspections immediately waved over three of his companions to block the gate.","\"Take out your travel permits one by one. You guys, go over there and check the items on their carts.\"","As he spoke, he took the travel permit from Lan Xi's hand and opened it. A few breaths later, his expression changed drastically.","He suddenly jerked his head up, his urgent gaze quickly finding Song Qiming's face behind Lan Xi, and dropped to his knees with a heavy thud.","\"This lowly one, Liu Hucheng, head of the yamen runners of Suining City, greets the Lord Prefect!\"","For a brief moment, the city gate fell dead silent. Once the others realized what was happening, they instinctively dropped to their knees and shouted, \"Greetings, Lord Prefect!\"","The voices rose and fell. The yamen runners had loud, booming voices, while the commoners were generally much quieter; from their tones and expressions, it was clear they were afraid.","Song Qiming straightened his spine, swept his gaze over the crowd, and then withdrew his eyes.","He spoke in a calm tone, \"All of you, rise.\"","Liu Hucheng slowly stood up and raised his head, his heart pounding so hard it felt like it might leap out of his chest.","He hadn't expected the newly appointed Lord Prefect to be so young; he looked like he hadn't even reached his twentieth year.","\"The prefectural office has already been prepared. This lowly one will lead Your Excellency there right away.\"","He took hold of Song Qiming's horse reins to lead the way, signaling his companions with his eyes to hurry back and report the arrival.","\"Liu Hucheng, when I entered the outer city earlier, there were also people inspecting travel permits. They claimed to be militiamen, but they didn't seem to know how to read.\"","Liu Hucheng's Adam's apple bobbed, his eyes darting around rapidly in slight nervousness.","\"There is something Your Excellency might not know. These so-called militiamen are just commoners living in the outer city. Most of them have never been to school, so they know very few characters.\"","Song Qiming frowned and pressed further, \"If they can't read, how do they check the travel permits?\"","The man from earlier had barely even looked at it.","Liu Hucheng took a deep breath and continued explaining, \"Some of them can recognize a few words, but they mostly rely on asking questions.\"","\"This is a spontaneous initiative by the commoners of the outer city. The local government felt it brought more benefits than harm, so we simply allowed it. However, the inner city strictly follows the regulations.\"","Song Qiming continued to ask, \"When did Suining City get an outer city?\"","Liu Hucheng tilted his chin up, thought for a moment, and then shook his head blankly. \"It has been there since this lowly one was born. As for exactly when it was built, I do not know.\"","Compared to the outer city, the inner city truly looked like what a proper city should be.","The ground was no longer full of potholes; instead, it featured flat roads paved with rammed earth, flanked by drainage ditches.","Both sides of the streets were lined with shops. At a glance, the shelves were stocked with a dazzling array of goods, and customers could be seen shopping inside.","From entering the inner city gates to arriving at the entrance of the prefectural office, it took about half an hour of slow horseback riding.","As Song Qiming dismounted his horse, a man in his fifties wearing official robes hurried down the steps.","\"This lower official, Co-Prefect of Suining Prefecture Shi Simian, greets the Lord Prefect.\"","Song Qiming wore a smile and slightly raised his hands in a gesture to help him up.","\"From now on, you and I are colleagues. There is no need for such excessive formalities.\"","Shi Simian looked up and observed Song Qiming.","He was truly young, arguably about the same age as his own grandson.","\"Your Excellency has reached the high position of Prefect before even being crowned a man at twenty; this lower official is left far behind in the dust.\"","After speaking, he noticed Song Jinzhao standing in the back.","Was she a female family member of the Song household?","She looked to be a bit older than Prefect Song.","Noticing the other man's gaze falling behind him, Song Qiming took a step back to make room.","\"This is my older sister, the imperially bestowed County Princess Linghui.\"","Shi Simian's pupils dilated. For a moment, he froze in place, his breathing coming to a complete halt.","He knew that Song Qiming had a sister who was a County Princess, but he never expected she would come to Suining with him.","County Princess Linghui held a noble status and should have remained in the capital. Why would she come to suffer in a remote, impoverished backwater like Suining?","Lord Gu hadn't mentioned this in advance either. This was truly catching them completely off guard."]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: The warehouse is empty, with three thousand in external debt.","paragraphs":["The cold wind blew into Shi Simian's wide sleeves, making him shiver all over and instantly bringing his mind back to its senses.","He hurriedly bent down, bowing his body at a ninety-degree angle.","\"Greetings to County Princess Linghui.\"","Liu Hucheng stared blankly, his knees suddenly going weak and making it hard for him to stand steady.","He never expected that the woman he had been ignoring was actually a County Princess.","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes to look over, paying no mind to the crowd's shock.","Shi Simian turned to look at the government office behind him; when he turned back, a trace of apprehension colored his eyes.","He immediately apologized, \"This humble official did not know of the County Princess's arrival. I fear this government office is somewhat shabby. I will order someone to renovate it right away.\"","In past years, the prefects of Suining had always lived in the government office of Suining City—firstly, for the convenience of working, and secondly, for security.","With the new prefect taking office, Shi Simian had ordered people to do a simple cleaning of the backyard. But since Song Jinzhao was also going to stay there, the furnishings in the rooms were simply not exquisite enough.","Song Jinzhao said in a calm tone, \"It is fine. The government office looks as grand as new; I think it is quite good.\"","Walking into the inner residence of the government office, the space was large enough and there were plenty of rooms. Accommodating one or two hundred people would absolutely not be a problem.","Song Jinzhao instructed Qingshuang and Lanxi to take people to settle in, while Song Qiming directly asked Shi Simian to take him to the second hall to inspect the official business accumulated over the past few months.","The news of the new prefect taking office and County Princess Linghui arriving in Suining City—and planning to reside there permanently—quickly spread, sparking much discussion among the commoners.","Besides wanting to gaze upon the esteemed countenance of this commoner-born County Princess, they also speculated whether the new prefect would be a good official.","An hour later, Song Qiming returned from the second hall. In the inner residence, Song Shixue and Song Anhao were already so exhausted that they had fallen asleep.","He sat on a chair in the front hall, repeatedly rubbing his temples with his fingers. Aside from sleepiness, he was also filled with frustration.","\"You don't need to be too anxious right after arriving in Suining City. Take things one by one, and they will eventually be sorted out.\"","Song Qiming opened his eyes and looked up. Seeing that the person approaching was Song Jinzhao, he couldn't help but rouse his spirits and sit up straight.","Even so, his expression remained bitter as he spoke.","\"Sister, Suining Prefecture is truly so poor. Not to mention the empty storehouses, the accounts even show a debt of three thousand taels of silver owed to local wealthy merchants. My head swelled just hearing about it.\"","\"I've never heard of a government office having external debts.\"","Song Jinzhao's footsteps paused slightly, hesitating for only a few breaths.","\"Are there any problems with the accounts?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"I gave it a rough look. Aside from the bailiffs' wages being exceptionally high, I haven't spotted any other issues for now.\"","Suining City had five hundred bailiffs alone, and their monthly wages required a massive expenditure.","Only half of the commoners' tax silver from last year had been collected. It was safe to say they were failing to make ends meet.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Roughly how much commercial tax does Suining Prefecture collect each month?\"","Song Qiming pondered for a few seconds before answering, \"The account books record that last month it was less than five hundred taels.\"","\"...\"","Qingshuang suddenly raised her eyes to look at Song Qiming.","Five hundred taels was far too little; even the monthly profit of Dingfei Restaurant was more than that.","After a long silence, Song Jinzhao spoke, \"Bring the account books over tomorrow first. I will look at them before we say anything more.\"","The government's silver was the government's silver. No matter how wealthy she was, she couldn't use her private treasury to fill the gap.","Even if she were to lend the money, they first had to find a way to generate income; otherwise, the government office wouldn't be able to pay back the loan.","Song Qiming nodded heavily.","When the kitchen finished preparing dinner, they came to call everyone. After three days of traveling, most people had no appetite. They ate something light and went back to continue sleeping.","A good night's sleep lasted until the next day before they finally recovered.","Song Qiming started handling official business early in the morning, and all the servants in the backyard also began to take action.","Those who needed to clean cleaned, and those who needed to purchase supplies went shopping, striving to get everything done in a single morning."]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: The accounts are riddled with holes, eradicate bandits and raid their strongholds","paragraphs":["After lunch, the originally vacant room had been arranged into a study.","Two boxes of account books were placed on the table by year. Song Jinzhao and the others sat around the table, flipping through the ledgers of Suining City from the past five years page by page.","The only sound in the quiet study was the rustling of pages. Whenever they saw something noteworthy, they jotted down a few notes on paper with a brush and inserted a bookmark to mark the spot.","An hour passed, and the four of them had not taken a single sip of tea, not stopping until they had finished reading everything.","Song Shixue was the first to hand her notes to Song Jinzhao. The paper displayed clear percentage data and statistical charts.","The labor expenses of Suining Prefecture have been increasing every year. By last year, they had reached sixty percent of the revenue.","Qingshuang handed her notes over.","The commercial tax of Suining Prefecture is mainly concentrated on grain and liquor, and it has been dropping every year. Previously, it was three or four thousand taels a month, but last year it plummeted to only a few hundred taels. Suining City, Yunzhu County, and Songhe County account for the majority of this, while Qingxia County and Yanshan County are almost negligible.","Lanxi spoke up, The prefecture can only collect half of its annual grain tax, and last year it was a mere third. The grain seeds for this year were also borrowed from the government office, with a unified agreement to return them after the autumn harvest.","Song Jinzhao leaned back in her chair. The dense data and charts on the paper felt heavy and oppressive.","No matter how low the grain and commercial taxes were, a portion still had to be handed over to the imperial court every year. Less than twenty percent was left behind, which was not even enough for self-sufficiency.","Over these five years, the government office had solicited donations from local wealthy merchants thirty-two times, with the amounts showing a downward trend.","By the second half of last year, donations had turned into loans. That was how the three thousand taels of silver owed on the books came to be.","Given the current situation in Suining Prefecture, what do you think can be done to quickly fill the treasury?","Song Jinzhao crossed her arms over her chest, her gaze sweeping across the faces of the three as she intentionally tested them.","The three secretly exchanged glances before burying their heads in deep thought, their brows furrowing tighter than the last.","After Song Jinzhao finished her third pastry, Song Shixue was the first to look her directly in the eye.","Save on labor costs. Brother knows martial arts and doesn't need so many yamen runners to protect him. We should lay off the three hundred extra runners in Suining City.","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips and shook her head in rejection. Your brother doesn't need them, but the commoners of Suining do. These people are useful and cannot be dismissed.","She planned to recruit more people in the future, so she certainly could not drive away the existing official troops.","Song Shixue sounded slightly disappointed. If cutting expenditures won't work, then we can only increase our sources of income.","Qingshuang raised her hand. The commercial tax in Suining Prefecture is decreasing every year. Many local merchants have moved to Songzhou City. If we can get them to return, the commercial tax will definitely grow.","Lanxi suggested, There is a lot of wasteland outside the city. We can have the idle yamen runners clear the land, and then sell the grain for money once it is harvested.","Qingshuang added, We can replicate our businesses from the capital here. Not only will it earn silver, but it will also set a leading example.","Before coming here, they had already planned to expand their business empire into the southwest. They might as well start with Suining City.","Song Jinzhao twisted her stiff and aching neck. The wasteland needs to be cleared, but we still need to add more people.","The three looked confused.","Song Jinzhao spoke with absolute certainty. Suining Prefecture has so many bandits and robbers. Their mountain strongholds must hold plenty of gold, silver, and treasures. Wiping them out will fill the treasury, and the people can be used as free labor. It kills two birds with one stone.","Song Shixue's eyes glazed over, her mind going completely blank.","Wiping out bandits and raiding their strongholds? This sounded a bit like what her elder sister had mentioned before about raiding the homes of corrupt officials to fill the national treasury.","Qingshuang and Lanxi had already lowered their heads, thinking about the specific steps to take.","With the guards plus the yamen runners, suppressing the bandits would definitely not be a problem.","The only questions were how much silver there was, and whether there were many people.","They still needed to gather intelligence on the various bandit factions and strike the richest one first."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: Opposition and Accountability","paragraphs":["Song Qiming threw a stack of documents onto the table and stood before the map to begin his briefing.","\"According to the intelligence we've gathered, there are over a hundred bandit groups of varying sizes in Suining Prefecture. Among them, the most notorious and powerful number twenty-four. They all have their own territories and strongholds scattered across the four counties. The top six are comparable to Qingfeng Stronghold, while the remaining eighteen have far fewer men. Taking them all down will absolutely not be a problem.\"","The current state of the prefectural office was worrying, so upon hearing Song Jinzhao's suggestion, Song Qiming fully supported it.","In fact, he was even more eager than she was, wishing he could immediately lead the bailiffs out to eradicate the bandits.","Looking at the twenty-four red dots marked on the map, Song Jinzhao formed a plan in her mind.","\"You and I will each lead a team of men, spreading outward with Suining City as the center. We will split our forces into two routes and take them down as quickly as possible.\"","Song Qiming nodded in agreement. \"Leave Yunzhu County and Qingxia County to me. I'll leave Songhe and Yanshan in your hands, Ah Jie.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Let Lanxi and Qingshuang go with you. I will take Shixue.\"","She believed that Song Qiming could hold his own, but she still felt uneasy and had to send two highly capable people with him.","Song Qiming did not object. He sat down and began discussing when they would set off and which routes they would take. A detailed plan had to be drawn up tonight.","The lamp oil burned until midnight, and several copies of marching route maps were drawn up in the room.","They clearly marked the corresponding times and numbers of troops needed to attack each stronghold.","Song Jinzhao instructed Qingshuang, \"Send our people out to first figure out the specific details of these twenty-four strongholds, especially their locations and the routes leading to them. Remember to conceal your tracks when scouting, and do not alert the enemy.\"","A new official must make a strong impression, and once the fires were lit, they had to yield results.","Aside from replenishing the prefectural treasury and gaining free labor, Song Jinzhao hoped even more to use this bandit eradication campaign to establish Song Qiming's prestige.","She wanted to sweep away the cowardly and incompetent image of the Suining Prefect in the eyes of the commoners, letting them know that Song Qiming was a resolute, decisive, and caring official.","After a night of discussion, Song Qiming did not immediately inform his subordinates of the plan the next day. Instead, he waited for the scouts to return with intelligence. Only on the morning before their planned departure did he officially announce the decision to wipe out the bandits.","Shi Simian was taken aback at first, then shouted at Song Qiming in disbelief, \"My Lord, you want to eradicate all the bandits in Suining Prefecture? Isn't this a bit too sudden?\"","Song Qiming's expression remained unchanged as he said, \"The bandits in Suining Prefecture are running rampant. I have long wanted to capture them all in one fell swoop. This matter is not up for debate; we depart tomorrow morning.\"","Shi Simian was so anxious over his resolute tone that he stamped his feet, the veins on his forehead and neck bulging.","\"My Lord, there are numerous bandits in Suining Prefecture; they cannot be wiped out overnight. If we fail and these bandits unite in rebellion, Suining Prefecture will be in grave danger!\"","Youth is indeed arrogant, but rushing to make political achievements should not be done like this.","Song Qiming narrowed his eyes, staring at him with displeasure.","\"Fearing the battle before it even begins, Lord Shi, you are far too cowardly.\"","\"It is precisely because there are so many bandits that we must eradicate them. Over the years, they have blocked roads, robbed, and killed at will. How many commoners have died at their hands? Merchants do not even dare to travel the roads. If we do not kill them, more and more people will be forced to become bandits, and that is when Suining Prefecture will truly perish.\"","Seeing Song Qiming's voice grow louder and his expression sterner, Shi Simian took a step back, his momentum entirely suppressed.","He stammered, \"Going out to eradicate bandits requires rations. Right now, the prefectural office is empty of both money and food. Where will you get so much grain, My Lord?\"","Sending bailiffs out to fight meant they had to eat and drink, and the prefectural office had to provide for that.","Five hundred bailiffs would consume eight hundred catties of grain a day. Over thirty days, that would be twenty-four thousand catties, or two hundred shi.","Adding salt, vegetables, meat, firewood, and fodder, it would cost at least two thousand taels of silver. Where would this come from?","Unless Song Qiming paid out of his own pocket, the prefectural office certainly had no money.","Song Qiming spoke the words he had prepared long ago: \"I, on behalf of the prefectural office, have borrowed three thousand taels of silver from Ah Jie. It will absolutely not be a problem to last thirty or forty days.\"","Shi Simian's pupils trembled.","\"Borrowing again! We already owe three thousand taels. How will we repay so much external debt?\"","Song Qiming glared and stepped closer.","\"If it weren't for the fact that the prefectural office has no money, would I have the thick skin to borrow from Ah Jie?\"","\"The storehouses are empty. As the Vice Prefect, do you bear no responsibility at all, Lord Shi?\"","\"As an official of the imperial court, one should perform their duties properly. Eradicating bandits is a matter of course. Yet, it has been delayed for so many years, simply watching them grow stronger day by day, completely ignoring the lives and property of the common people. If it weren't for the fact that you have served for many years and are getting old, I would have long since submitted a memorial to the Emperor accusing you of dereliction of duty!\"","The pent-up anger of these past few days was entirely vented onto Shi Simian's head by Song Qiming, terrifying him so much that he hurriedly cried out in grievance.","\"My Lord, you wrong me! These were all decisions made by the previous Prefect. I could only obey.\"","Song Qiming put his hands on his hips and roared, \"The man is already gone! You can spin it however you want!\"","Seeing this scene, the guards standing nearby were so frightened they didn't dare to move a muscle, forcing down any reluctance in their hearts.","Even Lord Shi was being scolded. If they dared to say a single word of refusal, their fate would surely be miserable."]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: Catch one alive for one tael of silver, set out","paragraphs":["Just as the yamen runners were preparing to go home and pack their luggage, a notice regarding incentives for bandit suppression was posted on the government office's bulletin board.","A runner read the bulletin board word by word.","\"For every bandit captured alive, a reward of one tael of silver will be given. There is no upper limit, and it will be settled on the spot once they are escorted back to the government office.\"","Hearing this, the crowd quickly gathered around, their eager eyes scanning the notice up and down.","One tael of silver?","Their monthly wage was only two taels.","Catching one meant one tael; wouldn't catching ten mean ten taels?","\"Isn't the yamen out of money? Where is this silver coming from? It's not a scam, is it?\"","A colleague standing next to him bumped his arm hard, his voice louder than a beating drum.","\"I heard the prefect borrowed three thousand taels of silver from County Princess Linghui, and all this money is going to be used for bandit suppression.\"","The news exploded in the crowd like a bomb. For a moment, everyone had only one thought in their minds: catch bandits and earn silver.","Shi Simian abruptly raised his head, his heart filled with astonishment.","\"County Princess Linghui is going too!\"","Song Qiming rolled his eyes at him.","\"My sister and I will each lead a team and act separately.\"","The heart Shi Simian had in his throat calmed down by half.","\"In this humble official's opinion, it would be the best plan for Your Excellency to travel with the County Princess; the odds of winning would also be higher.\"","County Princess Linghui possessed formidable martial arts skills. None of the military generals in the entire Dongzhao Kingdom were her match, and she had even defeated Gong Linjue, the number one master of the Shuobei Kingdom.","With her around, this bandit suppression campaign might actually succeed.","Song Qiming saw through his thoughts at a glance, his back teeth grinding audibly as he spoke.","\"My martial arts were personally taught by my sister. Dealing with a few bandits will be a piece of cake.\"","Shi Simian's expression turned awkward, his throat feeling as if a stone was lodged in it, scraping painfully as he spoke.","\"Your Excellency is wise and mighty; this humble official bows in admiration.\" He cupped his hands and lowered his head, though his heart was full of dissatisfaction.","So young and a civil official at that—how could I feel at ease placing the lives of hundreds of yamen runners in your hands?","It would be better to follow County Princess Linghui into battle; at least the chances of winning were greater.","As soon as the night watchman's clapper sounded for the fifth watch, the runners who heard it quickly climbed out of bed and rushed to the government office.","It wasn't long before the corridor from the main gate to the front hall of the yamen was filled with runners, fully equipped and ready to go.","The clerks, forced to wake up early, pushed wooden food buckets and handed out breakfast to them one by one. At the very front, Song Qiming was making his pre-departure declaration.","When everyone saw Song Jinzhao walk out wearing armor, they couldn't help but straighten their spines a bit.","A woman leading troops to suppress bandits was absolutely a first in the world.","Yet no one dared to say a word of dissent. Aside from hesitation, their hearts were filled with excitement and urgency.","Song Jinzhao's prestigious name had long spread across the lands. They had heard so much news about her, but now that she was standing right in front of them in the flesh, was she really that formidable?","They would find out soon enough.","With a single command, the two teams marched out of the city side by side, only going their separate ways after passing through the outer city.","Guan Nianshan sat excitedly on horseback, his heart surging as he gazed into the distance.","\"I never thought we would see this day again.\"","After twenty years of living with their faces to the yellow earth and backs to the sky, they had finally returned.","Qu Ya smiled faintly, a touch of emotion appearing in his calm eyes.","He lifted his chin, gesturing toward Guan Nianshan's injured eye. \"Don't let people look down on you your first time out.\"","Guan Nianshan didn't get angry; instead, in a good mood, he pointed at Qu Ya's left hand.","\"Can your left hand even hold a blade?\"","One of them was blind in one eye, and the other was missing three fingers on his right hand, yet they were the least disabled among the surviving veterans of the Wu Family Army.","Qu Ya gripped his sword hilt and rapidly performed a flourishing sword trick, the sharp wind whistling as the blade cut through the air.","\"One strike, one head.\"","Guan Nianshan raised an eyebrow. \"Beheading definitely won't work. This time, they want them captured alive.\""]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: Seventeen Corpses, the Tiger Head Stronghold Celebrating Its Victory","paragraphs":["On a mountain peak two hundred miles west of Suining City, the bandits of Tiger Head Stronghold were gathered together, celebrating wildly.","In the backyard, box after box of fine silks and satins were being carried into the storehouse, while down below on the official road, the blood had not yet fully dried.","After two hours of baking in the harsh sun, the stench of blood was thick enough to make one retch. The ground was swarming with dense clouds of flies, a sight that would give anyone goosebumps.","Song Shixue bent down to carefully examine the bloodstains seeping into the soil.","\"Dark brown. Given this morning's weather conditions, it shouldn't be more than four hours old.\"","\"There are a lot of rut marks here!\" a bailiff called out, pointing at the tracks on the ground.","Following the tracks all the way, they found four carriages scattered in the woods, alongside severed reins.","\"County Princess, there seems to be something here!\" a searching bailiff shouted toward Song Jinzhao's direction.","Walking over, they found the soil to be very loose, clearly having just been dug up.","Her eyes darkening, Song Jinzhao ordered coldly, \"Dig it up immediately.\"","A few minutes later, two human faces were simultaneously revealed to the crowd.","As they kept digging, more bodies appeared. Once all were pulled out, there were seventeen corpses in total.","Upon getting a clear look at one of the faces, Liu Hucheng widened his eyes in shock.","\"County Princess, I recognize this man. He is a manager of the Fu Family Fabric Store in Suining City, named Fu Yong.\"","\"The Fu Family Fabric Store is one of the top three fabric stores in Suining City. They frequently travel to Songzhou City to restock. It's not like they haven't been robbed in previous years, but at least they were left with their lives. I never expected them all to be killed this time.\"","The bandits of Tiger Head Stronghold were growing increasingly ruthless. The County Princess and the Prefect were right; if they weren't eradicated soon, it would truly become impossible to live in peace.","Looking at the seventeen corpses laid out on the ground, the attire of seven of them clearly indicated they were armed escorts, and they bore the most wounds.","\"Leave three men behind to guard the bodies. The rest of you, follow me.\"","The bandits of Tiger Head Stronghold had just finished a successful raid and were currently letting their guard down. Now was the best time to launch an attack up the mountain.","In the kitchens of Tiger Head Stronghold, cooking smoke billowed upward like pillars. The long tables were piled high with large cuts of meat and fish.","Once everything was served in the main hall, Hu Meng, the chief of Tiger Head Stronghold, raised his wine cup and roared at the packed room, his tone sounding exceedingly heroic and ambitious.","\"Brothers! The first fat sheep of the spring is already in our bags. Today, there's plenty of meat and wine for everyone to eat and drink their fill. Tomorrow, we divide the spoils!\"","As his words fell, a subordinate at his table immediately shouted in flattery, \"The boss is mighty! With the boss, we get to eat meat. We brothers are bound to follow you for the rest of our lives!\"","As soon as he said this, the others chimed in with agreement, their voices ringing out and startling a flock of birds in the surrounding area.","Song Jinzhao, who was climbing up the mountain, suddenly stopped in her tracks. From the distance came what sounded like the flapping wings of a large flock of birds.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"How much longer until we reach Tiger Head Stronghold?\"","The guard who had been sent ahead to scout hunched over and walked up, answering in a low voice while pointing toward the front right.","\"Less than an hour. The first hidden sentry is just up ahead.\"","The higher they went, the colder the temperature dropped. They were covered in cold sweat.","Half an hour later, the first hidden sentry concealed in a tree had his throat silently pierced by an arrow from Song Shixue.","As the body fell from the tree, a quick-reacting guard decisively stepped forward, caught the man, and set him aside.","Accompanied only by the rustling of leaves, the entire process did not alert a single soul.","After downing over a dozen cups of strong liquor, Hu Meng roughly grabbed a woman by the waist.","He kissed her bright red lips, pale yellow liquor dripping steadily down from the corners of his mouth.","Hu Meng let out a couple of hearty laughs and began groping her right in front of his many underlings.","Seeing this, a bandit sitting opposite them couldn't help but gulp, his lower body immediately reacting as unbearable lust flared up.","Noticing this, the bandit sitting next to him covered his mouth and whispered to him.","\"The boss is already tired of the younger one. She's locked up in the woodshed right now. I'll take you over there a bit later.\"","Hearing this, the man whipped his head around and pressed, his eyes full of pleasant surprise.","\"Really?\" If he could get it immediately, who would wait until tomorrow to visit a brothel?","The bandit nodded, an insatiable smile hanging in his greasy eyes.","\"She was just tossed out yesterday. I've already had a go at her—she's incredibly tender.\"","The man gulped again. Unable to wait for nightfall, he immediately stepped over the bench and headed outside."]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: Attack on Tiger Head Fortress","paragraphs":["On a pile of withered, yellow straw, a woman lay wearing only a thin gauze dress. Her eyes stared blankly at the roof beams, looking like a soulless corpse.","The woodshed door was violently pushed open. Accompanied by bursts of lewd laughter, the woman's body began to tremble.","Her pupils dilated; even her very soul seemed to shiver.","Through her spyglass, Song Jinzhao could see the situation inside the mountain stronghold with absolute clarity.","They were drowning in wine and flesh—it was the perfect time to attack.","She brought her hand down sharply. The archers swiftly stepped forward.","A sky full of arrows rained down, and the bandits guarding the entrance fell to the ground one after another, pierced by the volley.","Led by Song Jinzhao, three hundred men swarmed into the Tiger Head Stronghold as swiftly as a plague of locusts.","\"The government troops are here!\" A scream pierced the sky, and the stronghold instantly descended into chaos.","Hu Meng jerked his head up. Upon confirming the shouts, he violently shoved the woman to the ground.","He grabbed the heavy broadsword leaning against the wall, swung it fiercely, and roared with a savage expression, \"How dare they attack our Tiger Head Stronghold! Brothers, come out with me and slaughter all these government dogs!\"","\"Kill! Kill! Kill!\"","The furious roars whipped up a majestic bloodlust. Footsteps, as dense and loud as thunder, rumbled into Song Jinzhao's ears.","However, in the eyes of Liu Hucheng and the many other yamen runners, every bandit that popped up looked like a tael of silver. Their fear was entirely offset by the prospect of the bounty.","Seeing the stronghold crawling with yamen runners and guards in official uniforms, Hu Meng's steps faltered for a moment, his grip on his broadsword subconsciously tightening.","Why were there so many of them?","Did they bring every single runner from Suining City?","Song Jinzhao brandished her long spear, sending four bandits who charged at her flying backward.","\"Ah—\" Blood scattered through the air like fireworks.","Song Jinzhao looked up toward the direction of the screams.","She immediately planted the shaft of her spear diagonally into the ground and vaulted into the air. Upon landing, she gripped the tail of the spear and shook the sharp tip, thrusting it straight toward Hu Meng's face like a viper flicking its tongue.","Hu Meng instinctively dodged, simultaneously shoving a yamen runner toward the spearhead with a backhand motion.","In a flash of lightning, Song Jinzhao leaped forward and grabbed the center of the spear shaft.","With a push from the back of her hand, the spearhead spun clockwise in a half-circle before she caught it firmly in her grip.","\"You're courting death, you filthy bitch!\" Hu Meng swung his heavy blade and attacked Song Jinzhao from behind, spit flying from his foul, yellowish mouth.","Feeling the cold, murderous wind on her neck, Song Jinzhao sidestepped to dodge while sweeping her arm backward in a half-circle.","Unable to dodge in time, the silver-gleaming spearhead pierced directly through Hu Meng's heart.","Lifting the corpse high above her head, the icy glint in Song Jinzhao's eyes was even colder than before.","She shouted at the top of her lungs, \"The bandit leader is dead! Those who drop their weapons and surrender will be spared!\"","The bandits turned to look. Seeing Hu Meng dead, their morale instantly plummeted to rock bottom.","As the first bandit dropped his weapon, the others quickly followed suit.","Song Jinzhao issued her orders: \"Tie them all up. Turn this entire stronghold upside down. Do not leave a single grain of rice behind.\"","\"Yes!\"","The men quickly dispersed. Soon, they carried out dozens of chests, along with bag after bag of rice and flour.","Opening the lids, brand-new fabrics greeted their eyes.","Liu Hucheng said, \"This should be the fabric from the Fu Family's Fabric Shop.\"","\"Sister!\" Song Shixue opened a chest at random and, seeing its contents, shouted joyfully to Song Jinzhao.","The eyes of the yamen runners standing nearby were glowing, their gazes shining brighter than lanterns in the night.","The chest was filled to the brim with gold, silver, and jewels. There were hairpins and bracelets made of gold, silver, and jade, flawless white saltwater pearls, and pressed at the very bottom were several silver ingots as large as half a palm. It was definitely worth no less than ten thousand taels.","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile and had her men open every chest for her to inspect.","She hadn't expected to seize so much gold and silver from their very first bandit lair. It seemed the start-up capital for Suining City was finally secured."]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: Conquer the Black Wind Stronghold","paragraphs":["On the other side, Song Qiming's eyes were firm. He raised his sword toward the Black Wind Stronghold and shouted, \"Open the gates! Those who surrender will not be killed!\"","\"Open the gates! Those who surrender will not be killed!\" the yamen runners and guards shouted in unison, their voices thick with murderous intent.","Inside the stronghold, a bandit gripping a long saber gritted his teeth and said to the Chief of Black Wind Stronghold, \"Boss, let's fight them to the death.\"","\"If we get caught by the yamen, we'll be beheaded anyway. If we escape, we can still make a comeback.\"","The Chief of Black Wind Stronghold turned his head and instructed his own younger brother, \"I will hold them off here. You go immediately and move the gold, silver, and treasures from the storehouse out through the back mountain. We'll meet at the old place.\"","The Second Boss nodded with a resolute gaze, turned around, and led a few bandits toward the back mountain.","The massive stone doors were pushed open from the inside.","\"Hurry, hurry,\" an urging voice sounded as a man who looked like a leader walked out from within.","Following closely behind him were eight men, each holding a small wooden chest. They hurried straight toward the small path.","In the nearby bushes, Lan Xi clenched his left fist. When the nine men walked right in front of him, he immediately lunged out.","\"Do it!\" The shout startled a flock of birds into the air.","The other guards ambushing in the bushes sprang up one after another.","\"It's an ambush, run!\" The bandits turned pale with fright and immediately turned to flee.","But Lan Xi did not give them a chance to escape. He and his guards fired their hidden sleeve arrows in unison, shooting the nine men to the ground.","Seeing the signal flare explode in the sky, Song Qiming took the lead in scaling the wall.","Just like Song Jinzhao, Song Qiming took down the bandit leader first.","\"The bandit leader is dead. Lay down your weapons, and I shall spare your lives.\"","...","At the entrance of the prefectural office, Shi Simian stood stiffly on the steps, his astonished gaze following the chests being carried away.","At a table temporarily moved outside the storehouse, the Treasury Officer was recording all the spoils of war being put into storage.","Shi Simian walked over and asked, \"Second Miss Song, hasn't the County Princess and the others returned?\"","Song Shixue replied, \"My older sister took people to attack the second stronghold and had me transport the goods and prisoners back first.\"","Curling the corners of her mouth, she added, \"Please trouble yourself, my lord, to lock those bandits outside into the prison cells first. My brother said he wants to make them do hard labor to clear the wasteland.\"","Shi Simian's eyes widened, and it took him a long time to process this.","So they wanted to use the bandits as free labor; no wonder they wanted to capture them alive.","Walking up the steps, he suddenly turned around to look at the storehouse.","So much wealth from just one stronghold. If they wiped out all twenty-four of them, wouldn't they make an absolute fortune?","At the thought of this, the joy in Shi Simian's heart could no longer be suppressed.","He stood there watching for a long time, his mind completely filled with mountains of gold and silver.","Half an hour later, all the bandits from Tiger Head Stronghold were locked in the prison cells.","Song Shixue handed the prepared medicine to the yamen runner guarding the prison.","\"Distribute this to the injured bandits and let them bandage themselves. They cannot die yet.\"","The yamen runner bowed and scraped, smiling as he promised, \"Rest assured, Second Miss Song, this humble one will distribute the medicine right away.\"","They injured them and still had to treat them; couldn't they have struck a bit lighter?","Medicine costs money too. It would have been great if that money could have been saved and shared with him.","In the evening, just as Shi Simian was preparing to get off duty, a shout came from the doorway.","\"Hurry out and move these things!\"","The same scene played out once again.","The handcarts were piled high with chests and sacks, while nearly a hundred bandits, their hands bound and mouths gagged, squatted to the side, looking utterly exhausted.","Lan Xi jumped down from his horse, holding his sword.","\"The Lord Prefect has ordered that all stolen goods be immediately registered and placed in the storehouse, and all bandits be locked in the main prison.\"","Shi Simian craned his neck to look behind them but did not see Song Qiming.","\"The lord didn't return?\"","Lan Xi shook his head. \"The lord has already taken the others to the next stronghold.\"","Shi Simian furrowed his brows, feeling a bit worried.","\"Fighting for days on end makes one extremely fatigued. The lord should have come back to rest and reorganize for a few days before setting out again.\"","Lan Xi replied, \"Do not worry, Lord Shi. It didn't take us much effort to take down the Black Wind Stronghold.\"","While moving the items into the storehouse, he noticed that over a dozen camphor wood chests were already placed inside.","Lan Xi turned his head and asked the Treasury Officer, \"Where did these come from?\"","The Treasury Officer answered, \"Second Miss Song brought people back this morning. These were all transported back from the Tiger Head Stronghold.\"","Lan Xi's breath hitched slightly. \"When did the Second Miss leave?\"","The Treasury Officer said, \"She left after lunch. It's been two hours already.\"","\"Is the Second Miss alright?\"","The Treasury Officer shook his head. \"The Second Miss is perfectly safe and sound. Only a few yamen runners were injured.\"","Lan Xi nodded slightly, breathing a sigh of relief in his heart.","Even though the County Princess was there, he still could not help but worry about Song Shixue's safety.","If Song Jinzhao hadn't ordered him to protect Song Qiming, he actually would have much preferred to travel alongside Song Shixue."]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: Make Bandits Tremble with Fear, Living in Constant Dread","paragraphs":["In just half a month, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming led their men to heavily eradicate bandits in Suining Prefecture, sweeping clean every mountain stronghold they visited without leaving even a single grain of rice behind.","The bandits were struck with terror, not even daring to step out of their doors, and some even entertained the thought of disbanding their crews to flee for their lives.","The commoners, on the other hand, were overjoyed, raising their voices to the heavens: Long live the County Princess! The righteous officials have finally arrived.","Despite this, the bandit eradication plan did not stop.","After clearing out Yunzhu County and Songhe County, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming directly led their men toward Yanshan County and Qingxia County, not even returning to Suining City to rest and regroup.","In a mountain col of Mount Feiyun within Yanshan County, the Tiangang Stronghold, which ranked third in power, had been steeped in an oppressive atmosphere for many consecutive days.","No voices could be heard in the stronghold, and even footsteps were exceptionally light.","Inside the hall, the five bosses gathered around a table, each looking worse than the last.","Sitting at the end, the Fifth Boss said, News just came that Duanlong Stronghold has been overrun by the government troops. I am afraid we are next.","As soon as these words were spoken, the scene fell into an even deeper silence.","After a long silence, the Third Boss slammed his fist hard onto the table, gritting his teeth, his chest aching with anger.","Wiping out all the mountain bandits in Suining Prefecture—they sure have the nerve to dream big!","The Fourth Boss looked up, his eyes filled with gloom, his tone laced with heavy frustration.","They are almost there. If we do not do something soon, we are dead meat.","At first, they thought the government would stop after wiping out a few strongholds, assuming it was nothing more than new officials trying to establish their authority.","Who could have imagined that this sweep would last so long? In just one month, seventeen strongholds had already been destroyed. The speed and determination of this eradication campaign were terrifying.","The Fifth Boss asked in bitter anguish, questioning both the others and himself.","Do we have any other choice but to make a last stand?","The Third Boss and Fourth Boss fell silent.","Unable to think of a way out, the three of them turned their gazes to the other two who had remained silent all along.","Big Brother, say something.","Seeing them not utter a single word, the three younger brothers felt incredibly frustrated.","Staying silent when the fire was burning their eyebrows—did they want their brothers to just sit and wait for death?","If that was the case, they might as well open the stronghold gates and surrender. At least they could save their own lives.","But not a single one of them dared to say those words out loud.","After an unknown amount of time, the Second Boss of Tiangang Stronghold, Poison Scorpion, said, As long as the green hills remain, there will be no shortage of firewood.","Big Brother, let us leave Mount Feiyun, head to Songzhou City, and find another mountain to start over. The Suining prefectural office has no jurisdiction there.","The chief of Tiangang Stronghold, Xiong Batian, said with a heavy tone, The Suining prefectural office might not have jurisdiction, but the Songzhou prefectural office does. They have three thousand soldiers; who could they not attack?","The newly sprouted hope was instantly shattered, and the three men lowered their heads in silence once more.","After pondering for a long time, Xiong Batian closed his eyes and slowly exhaled.","He clenched his fists and subtly swept his gaze over the four men.","Take your men immediately and set up ambushes on the four mountain paths. As soon as the government army arrives, strike at once. I want them all to die halfway up the mountain.","Exchanging glances, the four helplessly nodded in agreement.","The government troops brought by Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming were highly capable in combat. Even if the ambush succeeded, victory was not guaranteed. They were truly finished this time.","Over half of the stronghold's manpower was led out by the four men.","In the middle of the night, when the bandits assigned to keep watch had fallen asleep, Xiong Batian secretly jumped out of his room's window.","Clutching his chest and looking around, he carefully navigated his way through the stronghold.","Reaching the southwest corner of the wall, he decisively crouched down and pushed aside the rocks blocking a small hole.","Xiong Batian paused to listen carefully for any movement outside. Once certain that no one was there, he decisively crawled out through the hole."]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: The Silver in the Warehouse Has Flown Away","paragraphs":["Moonlight cascaded like water through the gaps in the leaves, illuminating the mountain path as Xiong Batian eagerly made his way down in the dark, clutching his bank notes.","As early as five days ago, he had gradually exchanged the silver in his private vault for bank notes. Tiangang Stronghold was no match for the government troops. Once it fell, as the stronghold leader, he would surely die. Therefore, Xiong Batian had long decided to abandon the stronghold and flee, taking all fifty thousand taels of silver with him.","Sending the other four leaders away that afternoon had been precisely for this purpose.","At night, the cries of various animals in the mountains rose and fell. Against the backdrop of the dark night, everything seemed particularly eerie, as if a malicious ghost was chasing behind his hurried footsteps.","Seeing that he was about to reach the main road, Xiong Batian's tense heart finally began to relax. A future of luxurious leisure felt well within his grasp.","A cold wind blew past, and a corner of dark green clothing emerged from behind a large tree.","Just as Xiong Batian was about to leave, the second boss of Tiangang Stronghold, Poison Scorpion, appeared.","The atmosphere instantly became tense. Xiong Batian asked in astonishment, Why are you here?","Poison Scorpion's lips curled into a smirk, every word he spoke laden with profound meaning.","To wait for you, of course.","Xiong Batian subconsciously covered the bank notes tucked against his chest. He calmed himself down and forced a tough tone, trying to overwhelm the other party with his imposing aura.","Wait for me for what? The government troops are about to attack Feiyun Mountain. Instead of setting up an ambush, you are wandering around here! How do you explain this insubordination?","Poison Scorpion sneered and mocked, As the stronghold leader, you abandon your brothers and flee for your life. What right do you have to lecture me?","I do not want to talk nonsense. Give me half of the bank notes and I will let you go.","Xiong Batian's expression changed. How did you know?","Poison Scorpion tightened his grip on his weapon. How I know is not important. What is important is how you choose.","A flash of realization crossed his mind, and Xiong Batian suddenly understood.","You sneaked into the private vault.","Poison Scorpion replied, If I did not go in, how would I know you stole all the silver?","Xiong Batian hated him so much that he almost crushed his own teeth. He threw away his scabbard and charged at Poison Scorpion.","In your dreams! Today, either you die or I do.","In an instant, the two men were locked in deadly combat, the sharp clash of their weapons ringing out clearly in the night.","Just when Xiong Batian thought he could defeat Poison Scorpion, the very next second his body slumped to its knees, as if all its bones and sinews had been drawn out.","His heart contracted sharply, accompanied by a violent, throbbing pain.","He looked at the wound on his arm in shock. You poisoned your blade?","Poison Scorpion walked towards him with a mocking expression.","Otherwise, why do you think I dared to wait for you here?","Blood flowed from the corner of Xiong Batian's mouth, and he soon stopped breathing.","Poison Scorpion searched his body, found the bank notes, and smiled.","Fifty thousand taels. He was rich now.","The next morning, the bandits lying in ambush on the mountain paths around Feiyun Mountain were discovered in advance by the guards sent by Song Jinzhao.","Their disguises were pure child's play to the hidden guards who had received special forces training.","In less than half an hour, Tiangang Stronghold was taken down, and the three remaining bosses were captured alive on the spot.","A short while later, Liu Hucheng ran into the front hall holding a handful of stones.","With a livid face, he said, Princess, the boxes in the warehouse of Tiangang Stronghold are full of stones. Only the very top layer is covered with broken silver.","Over the past month, every stronghold they raided had yielded several boxes of gold, silver, and treasures. Using stones as silver meant they had been deceived.","Song Jinzhao's face darkened, and she went to the warehouse to inspect it herself.","All the boxes contained only a few silver ingots; the rest were entirely stones.","Has the leader of Tiangang Stronghold been found?","Song Shixue shook her head.","Not yet. The captured bandits said they also have a second boss who left last night and has not returned. The silver must have been taken away by them.","Song Jinzhao commanded, So much silver cannot be transported away by just two people, let alone in a single night. Scatter our people immediately. Even if we have to turn Feiyun Mountain upside down, we must find all the silver.","Twenty fully loaded boxes would amount to at least tens of thousands of taels. If they could not find it, it would be a massive loss."]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: Discovery of Xiong Batian's Corpse","paragraphs":["\"County Princess, Xiong Batian's body was found at the foot of the back mountain. It has already been brought back,\" a guard ran over and reported.","Upon seeing the corpse, Song Shixue narrowed her eyes in suspicion.","The face was pitch-black, an obvious symptom of poisoning.","Song Jinzhao lifted the slashed sleeve, revealing that the dried blood around the wound was entirely black.","\"It's a knife wound. The poison must have been coated on the blade.\"","After saying this, she turned her head to ask the guard, \"Did you find the missing silver?\"","The guard shook his head.","\"We found nothing but the body. There were many footprints on that path, most of which matched Xiong Batian's. However, there was another very clear set of footprints that didn't belong to him. They were likely left last night.\"","Song Jinzhao ordered, \"Bring those three bandit leaders here.\"","When the three bosses of the Tiangang Stronghold were brought over, their eyes held anger in addition to fear.","The stronghold leader was missing, and even the second-in-command had vanished without a trace. They must have fled ahead of time.","Despicable and shameless! Even if they became ghosts, they wouldn't let those two off.","\"Look and see if this knife wound was left by Poison Scorpion,\" Song Jinzhao commanded the three men.","Seeing the corpse laid out on the ground, the three men's expressions changed drastically.","The stronghold leader was actually dead!","Their hands trembled as they touched the skin. After clearly seeing the marks left in the flesh, the three collapsed to the ground, motionless and in a daze.","The guard sharply rebuked, \"Speak.\"","The three nodded in disbelief. They never could have imagined that Poison Scorpion would kill Xiong Batian.","\"It's Poison Scorpion's curved ring blade. He is the only one in the Tiangang Stronghold who uses this kind of knife.\"","Song Jinzhao continued to ask, \"All the silver in the storehouse was swapped with stones. Do you know when it was switched?\"","Before they could recover from their shock, another bombshell was dropped on them. The three men's pupils shrank, and they looked as if they were about to pass out.","\"How could that be! I even went in to take a look a few days ago.\"","Song Shixue thought they just hadn't dug through to check.","\"Only the topmost layer was silver; everything underneath was stones.\"","\"Impossible, I even thrust my hands into it at the time,\" the third boss retorted with a resolute tone.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Exactly how many days ago?\"","The three furrowed their brows in thought.","\"Six days ago. At the time, we had just robbed a batch of—\" His shoulder was nudged, and realizing his slip, the third boss quickly shut his mouth.","He guiltily lowered his head, not daring to meet Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Seeing that they were intentionally hiding something, Song Jinzhao took a step forward and interrogated them directly.","\"Robbed a batch of what?\"","The three kept their heads down, too afraid to answer, their palms covered in sweat.","Seeing this, Song Jinzhao straightened her back and gave the guard a meaningful glance.","The next second, a sharp longsword rested against the third boss's neck.","The sudden stinging sensation scared him stiff. He closed his eyes and blurted out, \"Salt! We robbed a batch of salt.\"","As soon as these words came out, everyone present widened their eyes.","In the Dongzhao Kingdom, only the government could sell table salt, and there were specialized soldiers responsible for escorting it. How could it be so easily robbed by the men of the Tiangang Stronghold?","Realizing the severity of the matter, Song Jinzhao's voice grew heavy.","\"Did you rob smuggled salt or official salt?\"","The other two hastily defended themselves, deeply afraid of being charged with an even greater crime.","\"How could we dare to rob official salt? It was smuggled salt transported from Binzhou. The people transporting it were all from Binzhou, which is why we robbed them.\"","Liu Hucheng walked up to Song Jinzhao and whispered, \"County Princess, the Binzhou salt mines are split half and half between the Yang family and the imperial court. Their salt can only be sold in places like Panzhou and cannot cross into Yanshan County and Qingxia County. This matter is not simple; I fear there will be major trouble.\"","The officials in the southwest region feared nothing except conflicts with the southwestern foreign tribes.","Whether it was killing people from Binzhou or discovering them smuggling salt over to sell, neither could be handled as an ordinary situation. They had to be extremely careful and think twice, even thrice, before acting."]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443: The Stolen Silver Notes","paragraphs":["Compared to Liu Hucheng's worry, Song Jinzhao's expression was quite lively, as if she were happy.","She raised an eyebrow and asked the others, \"I, the County Princess, have never seen smuggled salt, and there is none in the Tiangang Stronghold either. Have you seen any?\"","The people around her were stunned for a moment, but Song Shixue was the first to react.","She smiled and shook her head, \"Never seen it. What we lost was silver; it has absolutely nothing to do with smuggled salt.\"","Liu Hucheng's eyes lit up. He quickly nodded and covered his ears.","\"My ears hurt a little. What was just said? I couldn't quite hear it.\"","Song Jinzhao was amused by his theatrical act. If this were a TV drama, he could barely manage to play a background extra.","\"Silver doesn't just vanish into thin air. If one person managed to take it all away, it was likely exchanged for bank notes.\"","Ordering the guards to bring pen and ink, Song Jinzhao quickly sketched a portrait based on Xiong Batian's corpse, then turned to question the bandits.","\"What does Poison Scorpion look like? Does he have any distinguishing marks on his body?\"","The bandits scrambled to speak, terrified of being beaten to the punch by the other two.","\"Yes, yes, yes! He has a large dark mole on his cheek right next to his ear.\"","\"His eyes are long and narrow. When he squints, they look just like slits.\"","One of them gestured with his hands, \"He is about this tall and quite skinny. Most notably, his curved ring-blade never leaves his side.\"","\"His eyebrows are thin, and he's a bit bald. He has a long face, a slightly flat bridge of the nose, and a scar on his chest.\"","\"...\"","With everyone chiming in one after another, Song Jinzhao quickly drew out Poison Scorpion's likeness.","\"Does it look like him?\" Song Jinzhao held the portrait up in front of the three men.","\"It does, it looks exactly like him!\"","The three nodded in unison, their eyes filled with shock.","It wasn't that the government hadn't posted wanted posters of them before, but they had never been drawn so accurately. It looked just like a real person.","Song Jinzhao handed the two portraits to Yao Ye, the captain of the guards.","\"Go immediately to the nearby banks and ask if these two men have visited recently. Report back as soon as you have any news.\"","\"Constable Zhao, is there anyone among the yamen runners who is very familiar with Yunzhu County? Have them go with Yao Ye.\"","Liu Hucheng thought for a moment and nodded.","\"There are two. I will go call them right away.\"","Song Jinzhao looked around.","\"We will spend the night in the stronghold tonight, rest for a day tomorrow, and set off for Mount Tianlang early the morning after.\"","It was also the last bandit lair they planned to attack.","In the dead of night, in the deep forest at the eastern foot of Mount Feiyun, Song Jinzhao was leading her guards to dig up the corpses of the salt transporters that had been buried by the bandits.","\"It's a good thing the temperature here is low, otherwise the bodies would have decayed much worse.\"","With the torches illuminating the slightly decomposed faces, Song Jinzhao quickly sketched out the features of all the corpses.","Since the Yang Clan dared to transport table salt from Binzhou over here, what was the harm in robbing them a few more times?","As long as they could find out the transportation route and the contact person, the bandits could hijack the salt a few more times. How could they miss such a great opportunity?","At noon the next day, Yao Ye led his men galloping back to the Tiangang Stronghold.","\"The clerk at the Jufeng Bank said that six days ago, a man exchanged fifty thousand taels of bank notes there over the course of dozens of visits. The man wore a mask, but his build was extremely similar to Xiong Batian. It must have been him.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"Only Xiong Batian had the key to the storehouse. Other than him, no one could have transported fifty thousand taels of silver away in dozens of trips.\"","Song Shixue stroked her chin and said, \"Xiong Batian was killed by Poison Scorpion. He must be the one who snatched the bank notes.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"What were the denominations of those bank notes? Can they be cashed at any Jufeng Bank across the entire Dongzhao Kingdom, or only in Yanshan County?\"","Yao Ye: \"They were all bank notes with a face value of one thousand taels. They can be exchanged at other Jufeng Banks, but they must be within the Southwest Province.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"Send people out immediately. Do not miss a single Jufeng Bank in the Southwest Province until Poison Scorpion is found.\"","No merchant would accept large denomination bank notes like one thousand taels because they wouldn't have enough change.","To use them, one would have to go to a bank to exchange them for smaller denominations."]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444: Song Anhao, Left in the Government Office, Can't Hold It In Anymore","paragraphs":["Outside the city of Suining Prefecture.","Inside the carriage, Yao Ying pressed his back tightly against the compartment walls, his face full of conflict.","He pleaded bitterly, \"When the County Princess left the government office, she specifically instructed you to stay in the estate and not come out. Can we please go back?\"","Song Anhao gave a cold snort in a childish, milky voice. He crossed his arms and lifted his chin high.","\"I have been bored to death for a whole month.\"","As he spoke, he rested his right hand on the head of the white tiger and raised his bow and arrows with his left.","\"Even Xuetuan is getting stifled. With so many people protecting me, nothing will happen. Today, I am definitely going to do something big.\"","Looking at the bow and arrows in the boy's hands, Yao Ying twitched the corners of his mouth, revealing a smile uglier than crying.","He had been trying to persuade him the whole way but failed to change his mind. Now they were completely doomed.","He lifted the carriage curtain and shook his head at the men outside.","The guards sighed helplessly, \"If we had known, we shouldn't have come out.\"","They originally thought they would just play in the inner city, but at the gates, the boy clamored to go to the outer city, claiming he wanted to experience the commoners' living conditions and investigate business opportunities.","In the end, once they reached the outer city, he wanted to go outside the city walls entirely. When they disagreed, he threatened to take the white tiger and leave on his own, truly leaving Yao Ying and the others at their wits' end.","After arriving at the foot of the mountain, Song Anhao spiritedly picked up his bow and arrows and rushed off the carriage, leaving the others with no choice but to follow.","If anything happened to this little ancestor, the County Princess would definitely skin them alive when she returned.","Having been cooped up for a month, Xuetuan started running as soon as it got off the carriage, darting into the woods and quickly disappearing from sight.","Song Anhao chased and shouted, running until he was out of breath. In the end, it was Xuetuan who turned around to come back for him.","With his hands on his hips, he grabbed the tiger's ears. \"Don't run around blindly. If you meet a real tiger, you won't be able to beat it.\"","The tiger tilted its head, its pale blue eyes so adorable that it was impossible to stay mad.","Song Anhao compromised and gave it a kiss, then straightened his back and walked forward, \"Let's go, I will take you hunting.\"","Yao Ying and the group of guards following beside him felt utterly exhausted, their footsteps growing a bit heavier.","Fifteen minutes later, the sound of horse hooves echoed on the official road.","As the distance closed, a man's face that had once appeared on Song Jinzhao's drawing paper came into view.","After a whole day of jolting, Poison Scorpion was already starving. Keeping his back in the same position for so long had long since made it as stiff as an iron plate.","The next second, the horse collapsed to the ground with a loud thud. With a crack, Poison Scorpion was thrown into the bushes, his facial features contorting as he cried out in pain.","The pain in his lower back pierced his bones, and it took him quite a while to recover.","As the pain gradually subsided, Poison Scorpion struggled to get up and check on the horse.","The black horse lying on the ground was foaming at the mouth, its pupils rapidly dilating. It was clearly about to die.","Poison Scorpion kicked it in the ribs. \"Useless thing, I should have slaughtered you long ago.\"","After getting the banknotes, Poison Scorpion did not dare to stay in Yanshan County any longer. Worried about being discovered by Song Jinzhao, he traveled overnight to escape.","Before setting out, he figured that since the government troops of Suining Prefecture were all suppressing bandits in Yanshan County and Qingxia County, Suining City must be poorly defended.","Coupled with the fact that both Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming were absent, he decided to head north, fleeing along the route of Suining City, Yunzhu County, and Songzhou City, until he left the Southwestern Province.","All three places had branches of the Jufeng Bank. After reaching Suining City to exchange money for equipment, his speed would be even faster.","But plans could not keep up with changes. The black horse he brought from the mountain stronghold was of poor quality and collapsed before even reaching Suining City, leaving him with an injured back.","Poison Scorpion took out a map to compare it with the surrounding mountains and forests.","After a long while, he muttered softly, \"Fortunately, it is not far from Suining City. I should be able to get there before dark.\"","He put away the map and, using his sword sheath as a walking stick, slowly walked forward along the official road."]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445: The Carriage Was Stolen, the Horse Was Killed","paragraphs":["A moment later, Poison Scorpion plopped down on the ground, panting. He couldn't walk any further.","Dizzy, drained of energy, and with an aching lower back, he decided to rest for a while before moving on.","He collapsed into the grass by the official road, closed his eyes, and quickly fell asleep.","Three quarters of an hour later, Poison Scorpion's eyes snapped open.","His neck was drenched in sweat, and his heart was pounding.","He had dreamed of stepping into thin air and plunging down a bottomless cliff. The surroundings were pitch-black, and he couldn't even see the ground. It was truly terrifying.","Upon sitting up, he found the pain in his lower back had worsened; needless to say, he had definitely injured a bone.","After struggling forward for half a quarter of an hour, Poison Scorpion stopped with a dark expression. His heart was filled with not only frustration but also burning anger.","At this pace, let alone reaching Suining City today, he might not even make it in tomorrow.","Neigh— A horse's snort came from the woods.","Poison Scorpion turned his head to look. Through the gaps between the tree trunks, he could faintly see a horse's tail swishing, and it seemed there was a carriage as well.","The thought of being able to ride in a carriage lifted Poison Scorpion's spirits.","Approaching, he discovered five horses and a carriage tied to a tree trunk. Judging from the carriage's decorations, it definitely belonged to a wealthy family.","In the past, Poison Scorpion would have absolutely waited for the owners to return to rob and kill them, but right now, he only wanted to steal the carriage.","To prevent anyone from chasing him, he killed all five of the other horses tied to the trees before leaving.","Gusts of wind quickly scattered the scent of blood.","Six miles away, halfway up the mountain, Xuetuan, who was hiding in the bushes with Song Anhao, suddenly stood up and looked down the mountain.","Its nose twitched as it faintly caught the scent of blood, and the pupils of its pale blue tiger eyes involuntarily narrowed into slits.","Not far away, a sika deer turned around and fled.","Seeing his feathered arrow miss its mark, Song Anhao puffed up his cheeks and glared at Xuetuan.","Why did you stand up all of a sudden? The deer ran away.","He had waited so long for them to enter his shooting range, and this sudden startle ruined everything.","Xuetuan bit his clothes and dragged him backward. Seeing that his clothes were about to tear, Song Anhao crouched down in confusion and held its tiger head.","What's wrong?","Awoo~ Xuetuan raised its head and roared toward the bottom of the mountain.","Yao Ying, who had been following along but was not allowed to help, guessed, Could it be that a wild beast is approaching, and Xuetuan senses danger?","Song Anhao's eyes lit up. If it can make Xuetuan scared, it must be a tiger.","Yao Ying closed his mouth, wishing he could swallow his words.","If it really is a tiger, the six of us probably can't defeat it. Young Master, let's head back. You're already amazing for hunting down two rabbits.","It wasn't that they couldn't fight it, but with Song Anhao around, they didn't want to take the risk.","A guard standing nearby nodded in agreement. We've been out long enough. We should head back immediately.","Awoo~ Xuetuan was still calling out, and after roaring, it went to tug at Song Anhao again.","Seeing that he was slow to react, it simply let go and ran down the mountain by itself.","Xuetuan— Song Anhao immediately grew anxious and sprinted after it.","Yao Ying and the others hurriedly followed.","The horses collapsed on the ground, the grass stained with blood—sweating profusely, Song Anhao felt his entire body turn ice-cold.","The five guards turned pale with grim expressions. Yao Ying stepped in front of Song Anhao, using his body to block his view.","Unclenching his fists, Song Anhao reached out and pushed Yao Ying aside, saying in a firm tone, Move out of the way.","Meeting his calm and stubborn gaze, Yao Ying hesitated for a long time before finally stepping aside.","After finishing their inspection, a guard said, Their throats were slit with a single strike. This is definitely the work of a professional killer.","The other two guards searched the surroundings. The carriage is gone.","As soon as these words were spoken, everyone immediately realized why the culprit had killed the horses—they didn't want anyone to give chase.","Awoo~ Xuetuan let out a long roar and turned its head, signaling for Song Anhao to follow."]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446: Chased to the City, Discovered a Venomous Scorpion","paragraphs":["A moment later, Song Anhao and his group found the black horse collapsed on the official road.","Yao Ying said, \"This should be that assassin's horse. There are no wounds; it died of exhaustion.\"","The young Song Anhao was already mad with anger. His brows were scrunched up, and his cheeks were puffed out larger than steamed buns.","\"Chase him! We must get the carriage back and make him pay for the damages!\"","Xuetuan seemed to understand its little master's intentions. It took the lead and started walking, occasionally looking back to urge them on if they did not keep up.","A glimmer of realization flashed in Song Anhao's eyes, and he immediately stepped forward to follow.","\"Xuetuan can smell the horse thief's scent. If we follow it, we will definitely find the person.\"","Arriving at the base of the outer city wall, Yao Ying stepped forward to ask the villager on guard duty, \"Sir, did any carriages enter the city this afternoon?\"","\"There were three, but I do not know which one you are asking about,\" the villager nodded while shrinking his body to the side.","He had heard that the newly arrived County Princess Linghui kept a white tiger as a pet. Could this be the one?","Yao Ying clarified, \"The door curtain is gray, embroidered with a mountain and rock pattern.\"","The villager shook his head with a troubled expression, \"I did not really pay attention to that.\"","\"Roar~\" Xuetuan tugged at Song Anhao impatiently, instantly pulling the belt tied around its neck taut.","I smell it right ahead.","The scent is getting fainter, hurry up.","Under the inner city wall, the yamen runners' faces drastically changed when they saw the white tiger running over.","Only upon realizing that it was Song Anhao leading it did their raised hearts finally settle back down.","One of them greeted him with a subservient smile, \"Young Master Song, why did you bring the tiger out today?\"","Even if it was a pet, the common people would still be afraid. Appearing in a crowded place would cause panic.","Panting heavily, Song Anhao explained, \"I took Xuetuan out of the city to hunt, but my carriage was stolen, and the culprit even killed five of my horses.\"","Having run for so long, he was already out of breath from exhaustion. Feeling it was embarrassing, he had rejected his guards' offers to carry him several times.","\"What! The carriage was stolen?\" The yamen runner widened his eyes in disbelief.","To dare steal the prefect's carriage and kill five horses, this person was too audacious.","Was this not just courting death?","He began to recall in a panic.","\"There were a few carriages that entered the city just now, but they all looked about the same. We checked their travel passes and did not see any problems.\"","Yao Ying spoke rapidly, \"The culprit is a professional assassin. The travel pass is definitely fake.\"","Having rested enough, Song Anhao continued charging forward. Seeing its little master move, Xuetuan immediately resumed leading the way.","Seeing them about to leave, the speaking yamen runner quickly instructed his companions to continue standing guard while he took two men to chase after them.","The commoners on the street scattered to make way when they saw the white tiger charging over, and the uproar made people's eardrums buzz.","The yamen runners shouted from behind, \"Everyone, do not panic! This tiger is domesticated and will not hurt people!\"","\"That is my family's carriage!\" Song Anhao shouted upon spotting the vehicle.","Xuetuan jumped onto the carriage and found it empty. After sniffing around for a while, it jumped down and looked around, its round nose twitching rapidly.","After determining the direction, it dashed forward.","On the other side, after exchanging a thousand taels of silver at the Jufeng Bank, Poison Scorpion found a nearby clinic to treat his waist.","When Xuetuan led Song Anhao charging in, he was lying on a sickbed in the back room having a doctor perform acupuncture on him.","\"Ah!\" The medicine boy let out a terrified cry upon seeing the tiger, his entire body going stiff.","Poison Scorpion, who was lying prone on the bed, suddenly opened his eyes. The pores all over his body shrank sharply as he grabbed the curved ring blade placed by his hand and scrambled up.","The doctor hurriedly tried to stop him, \"The needles have not been removed yet, you cannot get up!\"","In the next second, the door curtain was smashed open. Xuetuan roared furiously at Poison Scorpion, and the doctor fainted on the spot from sheer terror.","It was him; it was this exact scent."]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447: Discovery of the Silver Note","paragraphs":["Poison Scorpion was startled to see a tiger charging in. How could there be a tiger in the city?","Just as he endured the pain and leaped off the table, he saw bailiffs rushing in. His initially composed expression instantly shattered.","Song Jinzhao must have sent them to capture him.","Seeing that he was about to escape, Song Anhao opened his mouth and shouted, \"Catch him!\"","The bailiffs and the guards moved simultaneously to apprehend him, and Poison Scorpion immediately drew his blade to fight back.","With eight against one, and Poison Scorpion having an injury on his lower back, he quickly lost the upper hand.","A crisp sound of breaking bones rang out, accompanied by a miserable shriek, as Poison Scorpion crashed heavily to the ground.","Song Anhao stepped out from behind Xuetuan, looking slightly dazed.","Originally, he only wanted the man to pay for killing his horses, but the posture the man just took was clearly aimed at murder.","Yao Ying and the others were right. This man was definitely a professional assassin, and he probably had blood on his hands.","Poison Scorpion's lips turned pale as he glared at the bailiffs through gritted teeth.","\"How did you find me?\"","The bailiffs looked toward Song Anhao.","Song Anhao settled the accounts with Poison Scorpion: \"One horse is a hundred taels of silver. Six horses plus a carriage makes six hundred and thirty taels. For that much money, I would hunt you down to the ends of the earth.\"","\"Huh?\" Poison Scorpion looked at Song Anhao in sheer astonishment.","\"You came for the horses? You aren't sent by the government to arrest me? Then why are there bailiffs?\"","Yao Ying frowned. Realizing something, he bent down and whispered into Song Anhao's ear, \"Young Master, this man definitely has a bounty or a case against him. It's best to let the bailiffs take him back.\"","Song Anhao nodded, glanced at the bailiffs, and then looked back at Poison Scorpion, who was being tied up by the guards.","\"I think so too, but he has to pay up before they can take him away.\"","Realizing he had mistaken their intentions, Poison Scorpion immediately shouted, \"You can't just arrest people indiscriminately! I'm willing to pay!\"","Song Anhao shook his head.","\"Taking without asking is stealing, and thieves should be locked up in prison.\"","Yao Ying reached out to search Poison Scorpion for silver. He felt a thick stack of something, and when he pulled it out to look, everyone was stunned.","\"So many banknotes, and they are all in denominations of one thousand taels.\"","Yao Ying handed the banknotes to Song Anhao in surprise, his chubby little hands counting and calculating.","\"There are forty-five notes in total. Including these smaller ones, it's nearly fifty thousand taels of silver.\"","The eyes of the three bailiffs gleamed at the sight of so much money.","\"This must all be ill-gotten wealth. He probably stole it all. It should be confiscated.\"","The entire government office didn't even have this much money. They had struck it rich.","Yao Ying cast a secret glance at the bailiff who spoke.","Song Anhao thought for a moment, took out six hundred and thirty taels, handed it to Yao Ying, and then rolled up the remaining banknotes and tucked them into his own robes.","\"Escort him back to the government office. Since my brother isn't here, we have to hand him over to Lord Shi to handle.\"","Song Anhao led Xuetuan, walking at the front to clear the way. He was protected by Yao Ying and the guards by his side, while the three bailiffs and two guards escorted the limping Poison Scorpion behind them.","As they walked out of the clinic, the crowd of onlookers parted, pointing and murmuring as they watched their retreating backs.","\"Who did they arrest?\"","\"I don't know. The noise inside was so loud just now. They were fighting.\"","Shi Simian, who was just getting ready to finish his shift, heard a report from a bailiff saying that Song Anhao had caught someone.","He asked the person reporting in confusion, \"The Prefect's younger brother is only seven years old. Who could he possibly catch?\"","These past few days, batch after batch of bandits had been sent back, and the prison cells had long since run out of space.","Since they were all free labor and couldn't be sent away, he had no choice but to rent over a dozen dilapidated houses outside the city for temporary use.","Whether or not to build a labor camp would have to wait until Song Qiming returned to make a decision."]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448: You've Caught the Bandits","paragraphs":["As soon as the words were spoken, Song Anhao's voice echoed from outside the room.","Left with no choice, Shi Simian stepped out to greet him.","Just as he opened his mouth to speak, Song Anhao pulled a thick stack of banknotes from his robes.","In an instant, the words caught in Shi Simian's throat. His mouth opened and closed, but no sound came out.","Song Anhao presented the banknotes to him.","\"Lord Shi, these are the banknotes confiscated from the criminal. I am handing them over to the prefecture office for safekeeping.\"","He then recounted the entire sequence of events to Shi Simian, adding, \"The man is waiting outside. I will leave the subsequent interrogation to you, Lord Shi.\"","Shi Simian took the banknotes with trembling fingers, his grip so weak he nearly dropped them.","He stammered, \"Rest assured, Young Master Song. I will thoroughly investigate the origins of these banknotes.\"","County Princess Linghui and Song Qiming had gone out to suppress bandits and generate income, and now Song Anhao had stumbled upon this sudden windfall. The pressing financial crisis of Suining City was resolved in an instant. Were the Song siblings the reincarnations of the God of Wealth?","The guards dispatched across the Southwest Province rode through the night, heading toward the various branches of the Jufeng Bank.","Yao Ye arrived in Suining City on the morning of the second day after his departure.","Clutching a portrait, he headed straight for the Jufeng Bank branch located on the central street of the inner city. Upon finding the head manager, he immediately unrolled the portrait and asked, \"I am a guard serving County Princess Linghui. Have you seen this man?\"","Over the past month, the formidable reputation of the Song siblings had become known to everyone. Hearing that the man was a guard of County Princess Linghui, the head manager immediately set down his ledger and stepped out from behind the counter.","He craned his neck to take a closer look.","Yao Ye continued, \"He should have come to exchange a banknote, specifically one for a thousand taels.\"","The head manager blinked and waved over the clerk responsible for the exchange counter.","\"Have you seen this person? Did he exchange a banknote for a thousand taels?\"","The clerk leaned in, immediately pointing at the portrait with a nod.","\"I have seen him. He came by the afternoon before yesterday. He broke a thousand-tael banknote into one five-hundred-tael note, four one-hundred-tael notes, and a hundred taels in loose silver.\"","Yao Ye's eyes widened, his heart sinking.","\"He was here the afternoon before yesterday?\"","The clerk nodded. \"Yes. He was clutching his waist at the time, and he walked with a very strange gait.\"","Yao Ye's hand holding the portrait dropped to his side.","Two days had already passed; the man must have long since fled.","He stood rooted to the spot, pondering for a long while before finally turning around, mounting his horse, and galloping toward the city gates.","Did he leave the city? Which direction did he flee? He needed to know that at the very least.","Otherwise, without a single clue, he would have no way to report back to the County Princess.","Arriving at the base of the city wall, he presented the portrait to the guards stationed at the gate.","\"By the order of County Princess Linghui, I am hunting down Poison Scorpion, the escaped second-in-command of the Tiangang Stronghold. Have you seen this man leave the city in the past two days?\"","Hearing that the man was a bandit, the guard was initially startled before squinting to examine the portrait closely.","After a brief pause, he shook his head. \"I have not seen him. Perhaps I was not on duty when he left the city.\"","Yao Ye pursed his lips tightly. Just as he was about to roll up the portrait, another guard nearby leaned over.","He practically pressed his eyes against the paper, studying it repeatedly. Once certain, he looked up at Yao Ye.","\"I have seen this man. Second Young Master Song led some men to capture him the day before yesterday. He is currently locked up in the prefecture office's prison.\"","Yao Ye's eyes widened as if he had been struck by lightning.","Shaking the portrait in his hand, he urgently sought confirmation: \"Are you absolutely sure it is him?\"","The guard nodded vigorously.","\"Absolutely. I saw the black mole by his ear very clearly.\"","Yao Ye flew toward the prison. Upon clearly seeing Poison Scorpion's face, a look of overwhelming pleasant surprise washed over him.","He murmured softly, \"It really is him.\"","Turning his head, he asked the guard, \"Did you find fifty thousand taels' worth of banknotes on him?\"","The guard grinned and nodded. \"Yes, they have already been confiscated.\"","Upon hearing the news, Shi Simian hurried to the prison.","\"He is a bandit from the Tiangang Stronghold?\"","No wonder he had carried so many banknotes on his person and had attacked the guards with lethal intent upon seeing them. It turned out he was a fugitive all along.","Yao Ye's face glowed with excitement. \"That is correct. After discovering that Poison Scorpion had fled with the banknotes, the County Princess ordered us to stake out the various Jufeng Bank branches across the Southwest Province. I never expected that the Second Young Master would be the one to catch him.\"","Shi Simian asked, \"Yesterday, the Prefect sent a letter saying he would return the day after tomorrow. I wonder when the County Princess will return?\"","Yao Ye looked up in thought. \"By my calculations, the County Princess should have already conquered Mount Tianlang by now. I expect she will return within the next few days.\"","A massive grin stretched from ear to ear across Shi Simian's face.","\"Wonderful! With all twenty-four bandit strongholds taken down, the people of Suining Prefecture can finally sleep peacefully.\""]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449: Returning to Suining City, Scolding Myself into Guilt","paragraphs":["Two days later, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming returned to Suining City at almost the same time.","The moment they rode into the inner city, the commoners crowding both sides of the street immediately erupted into cheers.","\"Long live the Princess of Linghui! The Prefect is wise...\"","Their voices, sentence after sentence, seemed powerful enough to overturn the sky of Suining City.","Realizing what was happening, Song Jinzhao offered the crowd a gentle smile, her expression full of warmth and approachability.","Since she had decided to make the southwest her base of operations, winning the hearts of the people was naturally of the utmost importance.","Riding beside her, Song Qiming happily raised his hand and waved to the people.","As an official, nothing gave him a greater sense of accomplishment than the approval of the people.","Every shout praising the wise Prefect was a validation of his efforts.","At the entrance of the prefectural office.","Upon seeing the two riding on their tall horses, Shi Simian rushed down the steps, closely followed by all the officials of Suining City, both high and low.","\"Greetings to the Princess. Greetings to the Prefect.\"","They bowed in unison at a ninety-degree angle. When they raised their heads, the light in their eyes made it seem as though they were looking at their saviors.","After being welcomed into the second hall, Song Qiming could not wait to search the crowd for the treasurer.","Spotting him, he immediately waved him over.","\"Treasurer Yin, bring me the warehouse ledger for the past month and a half immediately.\"","The treasurer froze. They had just returned and already wanted to check the ledgers. Was it really that urgent?","Though he thought this, he still smiled and bowed in compliance.","\"Yes, sir.\"","It did not take long for him to bring the ledger over.","From the first page to the last, the light in Song Qiming's eyes never dimmed.","After finishing, he handed it to Song Jinzhao, his eyes shining so brightly they could almost blind someone.","There were 180,000 taels of silver alone, not to mention the silks, satins, and gold and silver jewelry. He definitely would not be short on funds for his upcoming projects anytime soon.","Under the gaze of the numerous officials, Song Jinzhao casually flipped through it before returning the ledger to Song Qiming.","She stood up with a smile on her lips. \"I have been busy for over a month and I am tired. I will head back to rest first.\"","After Song Jinzhao left, the atmosphere in the room instantly relaxed by half.","Shi Simian's gaze toward Song Qiming also became much calmer.","No matter how capable Song Jinzhao was, she was still a woman; it was inappropriate for her to remain while they discussed official business.","\"My Lord, the number of bandits escorted back these past few days has reached over seven hundred. The prisons can no longer hold them. I suggest we build a labor camp outside the city.\"","Reclaiming wasteland outside the city meant traveling back and forth every day, which was not only a waste of time but also troublesome. Building the camp outside the city would save a lot of hassle.","Song Qiming nodded. \"Tomorrow, I will personally go out of the city to select a site. The buildings must be constructed to be unbreakable, and guards must be stationed there to prevent these bandits from harboring any rebellious thoughts.\"","These people had blood on their hands. Strict precautions were necessary to prevent any uprisings.","Shi Simian's voice softened. \"My Lord, you just returned. Will you not rest for a few days?\"","Something as minor as selecting a site did not require Song Qiming to do it personally.","Song Qiming shook his head.","\"In addition to selecting the site for the labor camp, I also want to finalize the locations of the wastelands as soon as possible, so we can start work early.\"","Over seven hundred mouths to feed meant wasting money on plain rice every single day.","In four years, Gu Zhongxun would retire. He had to achieve political accomplishments as soon as possible to meet his sister's expectations.","After deciding on the tasks for the next day, Song Qiming headed straight for the backyard.","Inside the room, Song Anhao was currently claiming credit from Song Jinzhao.","\"After discovering the corpse, I immediately realized things were not simple. Then I tracked them all the way and finally managed to capture the person at the clinic. A full fifty thousand taels of silver, not a single coin missing. Good thing I was there.\"","Song Jinzhao retorted coldly, \"Could you have tracked the person without Xuetuan?\"","\"I warned you time and time again to stay in the manor. Why didn't you listen?\"","The smile on Song Anhao's face vanished instantly, and his heartbeat began to race.","He stammered an explanation, \"I... I brought a lot of guards. There wouldn't be any danger.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at him quietly.","\"The officials of Suining Prefecture have to bring hundreds of guards when they go out. How many did you bring?\"","\"The bandits in Suining Prefecture have been caught batch after batch. If any of them escaped and wanted revenge, you would be the first one they kill.\"","Song Anhao's heart trembled, and tears instantly welled up and spilled from his eyes.","As the sound of sobbing arose, Song Shixue, who was sitting to the side, instinctively wanted to plead for him, but was stopped by a single glare from Song Jinzhao.","Helpless, she had no choice but to remain silent.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Do you think your martial arts are high enough to protect yourself?\"","\"If he hadn't run out of poison, those three injured guards would already be dead.\"","His thin, small shoulders trembled uncontrollably as his tears fell patter-patter onto the floor.","\"Sis—\" Discovering his younger brother crying, Song Qiming, who had half a foot over the threshold, immediately swallowed his words.","His gaze instinctively turned to Song Shixue.","What is going on?","Song Shixue subtly shot him a look.","Hurry up and persuade her.","Song Qiming stepped lightly onto the floor, walked over to his endlessly crying younger brother, and wiped away his tears.","\"Sis, what happened?\"","Seeing the child she had raised with her own hands crying until he hiccuped, Song Jinzhao also felt a pang of heartache, and her voice could not help but soften.","\"Ask him yourself.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, before Song Qiming could even ask, Song Anhao threw himself onto Song Jinzhao's knees and hugged her legs.","\"Sister, I was wrong. I won't ever dare to do it again.\"","\"You guys were gone for so long, leaving me alone at home. I wanted to get stronger quickly so I could go with you, which is why I wanted to go out hunting. I won't be willful ever again.\"","Snot and tears smeared all over Song Jinzhao's leg, the wetness burning straight into her heart.","Thinking about how they had left their young brother alone in the manor just a few days after arriving in Suining City, she could not help but begin to reflect on her actions.","No matter how many servants there were, they were not family, and it was an unfamiliar place.","Even though he seemed independent, she could not ignore the fact that he was only seven years old, still a child who needed the love and care of adults.","At the thought of this, Song Jinzhao's heart completely softened.","She reached out and lifted Song Anhao onto her lap, picking up a handkerchief to wipe away his tears.","\"I'm sorry, your sister was wrong too. I shouldn't have left you alone at home.\"","\"I was too fierce just now, but you can't be so willful next time. What would we do if something happened to you?\"","Song Anhao wrapped his arms around Song Jinzhao's neck and rested his head on her shoulder.","As his sobbing gradually quieted, he nodded.","\"I know. I definitely won't do it again.\""]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450: Over 800 People Arrested Again Following Public Reports","paragraphs":["When Song Anhao gradually quieted down, Qingshuang waved her hand toward the outside.","A maid brought in the food. Song Qiming sat down and carefully picked up some food with his chopsticks. He waited until the atmosphere had eased up a bit before speaking.","\"Sister, I need to go out of the city tomorrow to select a site. Are we still going to fight the remaining bandits?\"","In addition to the twenty-four bandit lairs in Suining Prefecture, there were also many scattered robbers and thieves. Although these people had never killed anyone, they had stolen a lot of money.","Song Jinzhao unhurriedly picked up a chopstickful of leeks and placed them in Song Anhao's bowl.","The little guy stole a pitiful glance at Song Jinzhao. Seeing her expressionless face, he had no choice but to stuff the leeks into his mouth.","Looking at his deeply aggrieved little appearance, Song Jinzhao secretly curled the corners of her lips.","\"The remaining bandit groups are small and have no fixed dwellings. Many of them are even farmers from nearby villages. They might have already been scared into hiding by now.\"","\"Issue a public notice in the name of the government, asking the commoners to report them. Depending on the severity of their crimes, we will punish them by making them work to atone for their sins.\"","Song Qiming thought this was a good idea. Rather than putting in the effort to catch these people, it would be better to let the commoners report them.","It would be highly efficient and save trouble.","The next day, shortly after Song Qiming led his men out of the city, the government office's notice was already posted on the notice boards in the city.","At the same time, the yamen runners sent to deliver the message to the four county towns also set off.","A sallow-faced woman nudged a scholar who was reading the notice.","Seeing him turn around, she immediately asked, \"Little brother, what is written on this?\"","Seeing that her basket was full of scavenged rotten vegetable leaves, the scholar stood to the side in disgust.","\"The prefectural magistrate is calling on the commoners to report robbers. Providing information that leads to an arrest will be rewarded with ten copper coins.\"","The woman's expression changed suddenly. Thinking of the people in her village who occasionally went out to rob, her eyes shifted repeatedly.","But thinking of the ten-coin reward, her expression became hesitant again.","Ignoring the other party's disgust, she continued to ask, \"Will these people be beheaded if they are caught?\"","The scholar shook his head. \"The government wants to open up wastelands. The notice says they will be made to work to atone for their crimes.\"","The woman stood there thinking for a long time, and was finally squeezed out by the crowd.","The yamen runners who had gone out to suppress the bandits rested well and came to the government office. They heard the sound of an abacus coming from the office room, which hadn't stopped for a quarter of an hour.","\"What's going on?\"","A yamen runner who had arrived a step earlier said, \"Calculating accounts. The prefectural magistrate ordered that the reward money be settled tomorrow.\"","The yamen runner widened his eyes in excitement. \"Really?\"","The other nodded.","\"Not only will the reward money be settled, but each family of a yamen runner who died in the line of duty will be compensated with ten taels of silver. Even the injured will receive dozens to hundreds of copper coins for recovery.\"","The woman hurried back to her village outside the city.","She told her family about getting a reward for reporting.","\"Er Mazi from the head of the village went out to rob two months ago. He took ten people with him. Hubby, do you think we should report them?\"","The man frowned in thought. The woman waited, and the two young boys standing by the door also waited.","Ten copper coins for one person, ten people meant one hundred copper coins. That was enough for their family to save for half a year.","After hesitating and struggling for half an hour, just as he walked to the village entrance to report them, he saw his childhood friend, who was also from the village, leading a dozen yamen runners this way.","His heart skipped a beat, and he had an ominous premonition.","He subconsciously asked in a low voice, \"Liuzi, what are you doing bringing these officials to the village?\"","The man called Liuzi smiled and didn't speak. He just gestured twice with his hands, as if to say it was inconvenient to talk.","In the end, the man could only watch helplessly as Er Mazi and the others were taken away by the yamen runners, feeling endless regret in his heart.","\"These people need to be taken back for interrogation first. Come find me at the government office tomorrow. If there are no problems, the reward will be given to you.\"","Liuzi happily watched them leave. \"Thank you, official. I will go tomorrow.\"","The same thing happened in various villages outside Suining City.","Two days later, the same scene quickly repeated itself in Qingxia County and the other three counties.","In less than seven days, the number of robbers sent to the government office from various places reached an astonishing eight hundred, more than what Song Jinzhao and her people had caught.","Fortunately, there were enough yamen runners in Suining City, and with the additional manpower provided by Song Jinzhao, managing these more than a thousand people was quite orderly."]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451: Build the Labor Camp in Seven Days","paragraphs":["Inside the government office of Songzhou City, Gu Zhongxun called his two sons back and tossed a memorial to them.","It clearly recorded how many bandits Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming had captured during their recent bandit suppression campaign, as well as the amount of stolen goods they had confiscated.","\"To think they actually came up with the idea of replenishing the government treasury by wiping out bandits.\"","He had repeatedly warned Song Qiming to keep a low profile after arriving in Suining City. Who would have thought he would pull off something so massive right from the start?","After reading the memorial, Gu Huaiyuan stroked his chin in admiration.","\"I actually think this is a pretty good method. They eliminated the bandits and obtained wealth at the same time. Perhaps we could give it a try too.\"","Gu Zhongxun rolled his eyes at him. \"Songzhou City is not like Suining Prefecture. There are not that many bandit lairs for you to rob.\"","\"Moreover, the twenty-four strongholds Song Qiming picked were all involved in murder and robbery. Only stolen goods with untraceable owners and unidentifiable origins can be confiscated, otherwise it would all be for nothing.\"","The clearly visible figures of 180,000 taels and 20,000 taels on the memorial shook Gu Huaiyuan to his core. He looked at his father reluctantly.","\"Song Qiming is only giving us 20,000 taels. Is not this a bit against the rules?\"","Confiscating such a large amount of stolen goods required the approval of Gu Zhongxun, the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest. The right to decide how to distribute it also lay with him, but on the memorial, it looked as if Song Qiming had already divided it all up.","Gu Zhongxun sighed; he was also bothered by this.","If it were just an ordinary prefect, he could have easily transferred all the confiscated goods to Songzhou City. But Song Qiming was different.","Song Jinzhao was also involved in this bandit suppression, so he had to show some restraint.","Besides, Songzhou City had not contributed any effort at all.","After struggling with it for a long time, Gu Zhongxun closed his eyes helplessly. Anyone could hear the reluctance in his tone.","\"Forget it, consider it doing a favor for County Princess Linghui. After all, it is all going to be used for the development of Suining Prefecture, which is also within my jurisdiction.\"","Two days later, Song Qiming closed the reply letter with a bright smile and ordered, \"Lord Gu has agreed. Have someone purchase bricks and stones immediately.\"","Saying that, he handed the blueprints drawn by Song Jinzhao to Shi Simian.","\"This is the design blueprint for the labor camp. Build it according to this. Construction starts tomorrow.\"","Shi Simian furrowed his brows after taking the blueprint.","He looked up and advised Song Qiming disapprovingly, \"My Lord, is not it a bit of a waste to build so many houses? Being able to hold a thousand people is more than enough.\"","\"Furthermore, these houses do not look like places to hold prisoners. Building them this way will cost far more silver.\"","The captured bandits who were reported would be released after a period of time. There was absolutely no need to build a labor camp capable of holding two thousand people.","Rows upon rows of houses, each with its own door and courtyard, looked nothing like a labor camp.","Song Qiming replied, \"It is not too much. Once the houses are empty, they will all be sold later.\"","Shi Simian raised his eyebrows in confusion. \"Sold to whom?\"","Building houses to sell? He was having a bit of trouble keeping up with Song Qiming's train of thought.","\"To the people who want to move to Suining City in the future.\"","Shi Simian felt his head throb with a slight dizziness.","Every year, people moved away from Suining City. Trying to get commoners to buy houses here, and outside the outer city at that, was nothing short of a pipe dream.","At the same time, Song Jinzhao was holding a map and weaving through the streets and alleys of Suining City.","\"Sister, out of all these places, which one are we going to choose?\"","It had been six hours since they came out in the morning, and they had only rested for about thirty minutes during lunch. Song Anhao's feet were aching from all the walking.","Song Jinzhao looked down at him.","\"Naturally, we need to choose a place with a lot of people and cheap land prices. If you are tired, you can go back first.\"","Song Anhao twisted his toes. His ankles were incredibly sore, and the soles of his feet hurt.","But he still insisted, \"I am not tired.\"","He had finally gotten his sister to agree to teach him how to do business; he absolutely could not give up so easily.","She knew he was just putting up a brave front, but Song Jinzhao did not call him out on it.","Since he wanted to do it, he had to take it seriously. Only by following through from beginning to end could he be taught properly.","There is strength in numbers. The labor camp, capable of holding two thousand people, was completed in just seven days.","The entire labor camp was arranged in a square, ten rows by ten columns, featuring four hundred individual households, each with two rooms and a living hall.","There was also a large empty space in the middle, left to be used to build courtyards after they were sold.","Just looking at the exterior, no one would think this was a prison.","Over these seven days, the treasurer watched the silver flowing out like water and felt a stabbing pain in his heart.","At the rate the Prefect was spending, over a hundred thousand taels of silver would not last very long.","In the room of the government office's second hall, Song Qiming asked Shi Simian.","\"Suining Prefecture is considered an important border city. Did not the imperial court send any potato seeds over?\"","Now that the houses were built, it was time to reclaim the wasteland, and seeds should be bought.","The plan to build a defensive military farming system using potatoes had already started implementation this year. The seeds had been dispatched to various important military towns long before Song Qiming left the capital, but there was no mention of it at all in the records of the Suining government office.","Shi Simian revealed a bitter smile.","\"My Lord, you might not know this, but all the potato seeds that were sent over were kept in Songzhou City by Lord Gu Zhongxun. No other places received any.\"","Song Qiming blinked and realized that they had all been withheld by Gu Zhongxun.","He lowered his eyes, his voice so quiet it sounded as if he were muttering to himself.","\"Let me think about this matter. You may step down for now.\"","Shi Simian bowed his head and took his leave. \"Yes.\"","It would be great if Prefect Song could manage to get the potato seeds."]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452: Guzhongxun Refuses to Give Potato Seeds to Suining City","paragraphs":["At night, Song Qiming pushed open the door to the study.","\"Sister, how many pounds of potatoes did we bring over from the capital?\"","Song Jinzhao paused her writing, her gaze fixing on Song Qiming's face.","\"Less than two hundred pounds. The Emperor ordered that the entire second harvest of potatoes be handed over to the imperial court. These were secretly kept from the surplus; they cannot be planted openly.\"","Song Qiming sat down in the chair opposite the desk, his furrowed brows holding a thousand sorrows.","\"The potato seeds transported by the imperial court to the Southwest Province were all kept by Gu Zhongxun. This crop has a high yield, and I want to plant them on the newly reclaimed wasteland.\"","Compared to rice, planting potatoes was much more efficient and could help the commoners of Suining Prefecture live a better life much faster.","His fingertips lightly tapped the desk, stopping rhythmically as Song Jinzhao looked up.","\"Then ask Gu Zhongxun for them. We don't need too much; sparing a dozen pounds or so will be enough.\"","\"As long as we do it openly on paper, no one will calculate exactly how much is planted in the end. And how many potatoes we harvest is ultimately up to the heavens.\"","Song Qiming thought about it and found it reasonable. \"Then I will write a letter to Gu Zhongxun tomorrow.\"","...","In the front hall of the government office in Songzhou City.","Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong were just about to head out when they saw a courier hand a letter to the clerk in the dispatch room, mentioning it was sent from the Suining prefectural office.","Gu Jinghong crossed his arms, his eyes full of envy.","\"If I had known that County Princess Linghui and Lord Song would wipe out all the bandits and robbers in Suining City, I would have followed them back then.\"","Such decisive and swift action was exactly what Gu Jinghong had always wanted to do.","Gu Baozhu's eyes carried a look of yearning.","\"Lately, Father has been mentioning County Princess Linghui and Song Qiming more and more. I really want to go to Suining City and see for myself.\"","Their eyes met, and the two sighed at the same time, \"Alas.\"","They had barely managed to beg to be let out early; their family would definitely not allow them to go to Suining City.","Gu Zhongxun opened the letter. After reading its contents clearly, his face darkened.","Asking for this and then asking for that, why are young people so impatient?","Can't they just stay peacefully in Suining City for three years?","Gu Zhongxun brooded for a long time before finally writing a letter in anger and handing it to the clerk.","Upon receiving the letter, Song Qiming's expression dimmed.","Seeing his poor complexion, Shi Simian asked in a low voice, \"Lord Gu is unwilling to give us the seeds?\"","Song Qiming nodded in response, as if a heavy weight were pressing down on his neck.","\"He said that Suining Prefecture has no garrison troops, and once the potatoes are planted, they might be stolen by the people of the Wumeng and Shimen tribes, so he refused.\"","Shi Simian raised his voice, his face full of disagreement.","\"A dozen pounds isn't even enough for half an acre. How could five hundred bailiffs not be able to guard it? Lord Gu simply doesn't want to give them to us.\"","Song Qiming's lips pressed into a thin line.","Gu Zhongxun's letter was tough in its stance, and between the lines, there was a faint hint of dissatisfaction with him. Could it be that he gave too little silver last time?","\"Tomorrow, I will personally go to Songzhou City to plead with him. You must keep a close eye on the reclamation of the wasteland; we absolutely cannot miss the planting season.\"","Shi Simian replied, \"Rest assured, My Lord. I will keep an eye on the progress.\"","The soil of the wasteland was hardened and full of stones. After it was reclaimed, the soil quality still needed to be improved.","With only one month left until the planting season, time was very tight for them.","Riding at top speed, it took Song Qiming only one morning to rush to Songzhou City.","\"My Lord, the Prefect of Suining is outside requesting an audience.\"","Gu Zhongxun suddenly raised his head from behind his desk.","\"Did County Princess Linghui come?\"","The bailiff shook his head. \"Lord Song only brought a servant and four bailiffs. I didn't see the County Princess.\"","Gu Zhongxun breathed a sigh of relief and ordered, \"Bring him in, and treat him with a cold attitude.\"","The bailiff was puzzled but still nodded to show he understood."]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453: Playing Pitiful and Acting Weak, Successfully Obtaining Potato Seeds","paragraphs":["Led into the second hall, Song Qiming noticed that the yamen runners' attitudes were noticeably colder than before, but his tightly pursed lips actually relaxed.","Since he knew what Gu Zhongxun was thinking, he already had an idea of what to do.","\"Your humble official pays his respects to Lord Administration Commissioner.\"","A tense atmosphere filled the air. The sound of pages turning, one after another, echoed like thumping heartbeats in Song Qiming's chest.","An unknown amount of time passed before Gu Zhongxun finally looked up at him.","\"With the heavy administrative duties in Suining City, for what matter do you seek an audience with me?\"","Song Qiming curled his lips into a faint smile, neither haughty nor humble.","Smiling, he handed over a memorial as thick as a finger joint to Gu Zhongxun, with a stack of bank notes pressed beneath it.","\"The construction plan for Suining Prefecture that I submitted to Your Excellency last time consisted of only a few words. After several days of detailed sorting and calculation, your humble official discovered that the required funds could be reduced by twenty thousand taels of silver, so I have come specifically to hand it over.\"","Glancing over the bank notes, the displeasure in Gu Zhongxun's heart eased slightly.","But upon picking up the memorial and opening it, his anger flared up once more.","He waved the memorial at Song Qiming, his eyes as dark and deep as still water.","\"Ideals are grand, but reality is harsh.\"","\"The things written here are beyond your reach for a lifetime. Young people should keep their feet on the ground and stop daydreaming all day.\"","Expanding the population tenfold, increasing tax revenue tenfold, and having every household's granary overflowing with surplus grain—it was simply a pipe dream.","Seeing the memorial forcefully thrown onto the desk by Gu Zhongxun, Song Qiming met his gaze directly and spoke with firm resolve, \"How would we know it cannot be done without trying? Your humble official wishes to give it a try.\"","Gu Zhongxun was so infuriated that he was left speechless. His lips parted and closed, but he ultimately swallowed his words.","Young people had ambitions higher than the sky; it was only right to let them suffer a few more setbacks.","He closed his eyes, and when he opened them again, his gaze was full of warning.","\"Suining Prefecture borders the alien tribes of the Southwest. The recent bandit suppression caused too much of a stir, and it will inevitably make them feel anxious.\"","\"The situation in the Southwest concerns the safety of the entire realm. Whatever you do, you must be extremely cautious.\"","Song Qiming's expression changed, instantly becoming dejected.","He raised his sleeve to wipe the corners of his eyes, endlessly pouring out his grievances to Gu Zhongxun, his voice even taking on a slight whimper.","\"Your humble official doesn't want to risk his own life either, but the prefectural yamen's storehouse is completely empty. Not only can we not produce a single tael of silver, but we also owe the local merchants three thousand taels. Your humble official has truly been driven to a dead end.\"","Seeing him in such a state, Gu Zhongxun felt it was inappropriate to scold him, yet he had no desire to comfort him either.","He said in a deep voice, \"Just this once, and not to be repeated. As long as the alien tribes in the Southwest do not start a war, you may do as you wish regarding the matters in the memorial.\"","After all, it was only that little bit of silver; once it was used up, it would be gone.","Song Qiming gritted his teeth and lowered his tone.","He deliberately stuttered his words, putting on a pitiful appearance.","\"Could Your Excellency perhaps give your humble official a few pounds of potato seeds? I promise to have the yamen runners stand guard day and night to ensure they are absolutely not stolen by the people of the Southwest alien tribes.\"","Looking at his bowed head and submissive demeanor, Gu Zhongxun felt as if he were seeing his own grandson sadly admitting to a mistake. For a moment, his heart couldn't help but soften a bit.","\"The potato seeds sent by the imperial court have already been planted. What do you expect me to give you?\"","Song Qiming abruptly raised his head, his pupils astonishingly bright.","\"It doesn't matter if they were just planted. Even if they have sprouted, they can still be dug up. Your humble official has transplanted them before.\"","Remembering that the potato seeds were originally presented to the imperial court by County Princess Linghui, Gu Zhongxun's anger completely dissipated.","With Song Qiming trusting him so much, coupled with the fact that he had accepted a bribe and thus owed him a favor, he could no longer find it in himself to refuse.","\"You can go and dig up one acre's worth yourself. And cause less trouble for me in the future.\"","Song Qiming nodded rapidly, bowing and cupping his hands toward Gu Zhongxun, the gratitude in his eyes practically overflowing.","\"Thank you, Your Excellency. Your humble official will definitely do his utmost to govern Suining Prefecture and share your burdens in all matters.\"","To be able to obtain an acre's worth of potatoes made this whole act worthwhile. It had not been a waste of the several hours he spent racking his brains last night; he had rehearsed it multiple times alone."]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454: The Song Poetry Snow Should Open a Medical Clinic","paragraphs":["The potato seeds that had been planted for seven days had already sprouted by the time they were dug out.","Song Qiming had someone buy over a hundred flower pots in Songzhou City, preparing to transport them back to Suining City along with the soil.","\"Lord Song, what is the County Princess doing in Suining City right now?\"","Song Qiming looked up and met Gu Baozhu's face. Ever since he left the government office, she and Gu Jinghong had been following him, acting exactly as if they had been waiting specifically for him at the door.","\"My sister wants to do business in Suining City, so she's been looking at storefronts these past few days.\"","\"Oh,\" Gu Baozhu drew out the syllable, her eyes darting around playfully.","\"Suining City doesn't have as many people as Songzhou City. If the County Princess wants to do business, she can come to Songzhou City.\"","Song Qiming moved a flower pot onto the carriage and casually replied, \"Maybe in a few years.\"","Seeing his nonchalance, Gu Baozhu disappointedly puffed out her cheeks into two round balls.","Gu Jinghong, who had failed to get a word in several times, finally found an opening.","He stepped in beside Song Qiming to help him.","Having never seen an imperial official working alongside servants, he felt this Lord Song was very different.","\"Prefect Song, can you bring me along the next time you go bandit hunting?\"","Song Qiming smiled and answered, \"I don't know when the next time will be. The bandits in Suining Prefecture have all been wiped out. They won't be able to pose a threat anytime soon, and I won't let them.\"","Gu Jinghong froze slightly, not expecting Song Qiming to say that.","A civil official saying such ruthless things with a smile was rather chilling.","Worried about the flower pots overturning, they slowed down their pace significantly when they headed back the next day.","Setting out at the crack of dawn, it was already the second watch of the night by the time they returned to Suining Prefecture.","Upon hearing the news early the next morning, Shi Simian ran over without even eating breakfast.","He looked through the flower pots one by one. When he found that they were full of dirt with no potatoes in sight, the smile on his face vanished without a trace.","\"Where are the potatoes?\" he questioned Liu Hucheng, who had gone along on the trip.","Pointing to the dirt in the pots, Liu Hucheng explained, \"They are right inside the dirt.\"","\"By the time we arrived, Songzhou City had already planted all the potatoes. To ensure they wouldn't die on the road, we had to dig them up along with the soil.\"","Hearing this, Shi Simian immediately squatted down and carefully dug with his hands. It wasn't until he saw the sprouted potato tubers that his mind was set at ease.","\"Lord Song truly has great face; he can even get back potatoes that have already been planted.\"","After a few days of inspection, considering Suining City's relatively sparse population, Song Jinzhao ultimately decided to locate the new shop on Tongbao Street, the most bustling street in the inner city.","Song Shixue ran around with her every day, her eyes constantly lingering on medical clinics and apothecaries.","After several long days of internal struggle, she finally went to Song Jinzhao. \"Ah Jie, I want to open a medical clinic.\"","The capital was full of high-ranking officials, nobles, and wealthy people. Since Song Shixue was taught by Song Jinzhao, they trusted her and invited her to their homes for medical consultations.","But Suining City was different. The prefect was the highest-ranking official here. No one dared to invite Song Shixue, mostly out of fear that they couldn't afford her.","Song Jinzhao gazed at her, her eyes holding no surprise, only a smile.","\"Do you have a shop in mind?\"","Compared to Song Qiming, whose ambition was to take the imperial exams and become an official, and Song Anhao, who loved making money, Song Shixue spent almost all her thoughts on studying medicine, apart from practicing martial arts for self-defense.","She was interested and talented. Coupled with her diligence and willingness to endure hardship, she had mastered nearly eighty percent of the modern medical knowledge in Song Jinzhao's head. The remaining gaps could only be refined through continuous practical experience. Therefore, Song Jinzhao wasn't surprised that she wanted to open a clinic; she had already guessed it while they were looking at shops a few days ago.","Song Shixue nodded. \"A few days ago, I saw that the Yang family apothecary in Huaihua Alley was being transferred. I want to take it over.\"","Huaihua Alley was near the south city gate, separated from the outer city by only a wall. It was a rather mediocre location.","The wealthy wouldn't travel that far, and the poor wouldn't enter the inner city to hire a doctor. Not only were the prices double, but the medical skills there were also just average.","Song Jinzhao gave a gentle smile, her eyes full of encouragement.","\"If you want to do it, then go ahead. However much silver you need, Ah Jie will give it to you.\"","Song Shixue smiled and patted the place where she kept her money pouch, affectionately leaning against Song Jinzhao and hugging her arm.","\"No need, I have money.\"","\"I saved up several thousand taels when I was treating people in the capital. It's enough.\"","Song Anhao, who was burying his head in accounting, suddenly looked up.","He stared intently at Song Shixue, his eyes full of surprise and envy.","\"That much? My private savings are only a little over a hundred taels.\"","Song Jinzhao tapped the ledger with her fingertip. \"Your second sister's money was all earned by herself. Your private savings were all given by us.\"","\"Study hard. If you run the shop into the ground, you'll have to use your private savings to make up for it.\"","\"Ah,\" Song Anhao raised his chin and wailed, already feeling the heartache before he had even started."]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455: The Fang Family Illegally Transporting Private Salt","paragraphs":["As the night deepened, Lanxi hurried back and went to the backyard to request an audience with Song Jinzhao.","Qingshuang led him to the adjacent study.","Song Shixue, who was just about to step out, stared at the suddenly appearing Lanxi, her mind going blank for a moment.","\"Second Miss,\" Lanxi bowed with cupped hands, his heart beating uncontrollably.","They had not seen each other for more than half a month; it would be a lie to say he was not overjoyed to suddenly see her.","Sitting on a chair inside the room, Song Jinzhao glanced at the two who were gazing at each other and could not help but sigh inwardly.","Song Shixue nodded slightly in acknowledgment. Her feet, which were originally stepping out, turned around, and she sat back down on her chair.","Lanxi placed the drawn route map on the desk in front of Song Jinzhao.","\"Your subordinate took the portrait to Qingxia County and Yanshan County to ask around, and found that the people transporting the salt are from the Fang family in Qingxia County.\"","\"The Fang family's ancestors used to run a salt shop. After the establishment of the Dongzhao Kingdom, their signboard was taken down and they switched to the grain business.\"","\"The Fang family's smuggled salt is transported from the Wumeng tribe. The most recent shipment was three days ago, but they did not sell the salt; instead, it is stored in the warehouse of the Fang Manor.\"","\"Your subordinate secretly sneaked in to take a look. Judging by the quantity, their previous batch of smuggled salt probably has not been sold either.\"","The Wumeng tribe had marriage ties with the Yang family of Panzhou. The Fang family was clearly colluding with the foreign tribes in the southwest.","If this matter were exposed, it was unknown whether the imperial court would hold Panzhou accountable, but the Fang family would definitely face execution of their entire clan.","Song Shixue looked at Song Jinzhao. \"Sister, could it be that the Fang family does not dare to sell the salt because of the bandit suppression?\"","According to the original plan, after figuring out the salt transport route, Song Jinzhao would send people disguised as bandits to rob the smuggled salt.","But if the Fang family did not transport it out, this business could not be done.","Song Jinzhao memorized the route on the map.","\"They are not afraid of bandits; they are worried about running into the government troops heading out to suppress the bandits.\"","As she spoke, she raised her eyes to look at Lanxi. \"As long as the Fang family still wants to make this money, they will naturally take action once the situation stabilizes. Have your people keep a close eye on them.\"","Lanxi nodded. \"Yao Ye is keeping watch outside the Fang Manor. If there is the slightest sign of trouble, he will send a message.\"","After coming out of the study, Song Shixue just wanted to say a few private words to Lanxi, but they were bumped into by Song Qiming, who had returned late.","Having left early and returned late to guard outside the city for consecutive days, Song Qiming had not only lost weight but also tanned.","\"Lanxi, when did you get back?\"","Song Qiming knew about the smuggling of illicit salt. Since Lanxi was back, he must have found something out.","Lanxi nonchalantly took a small step to the left, distancing himself a bit from Song Shixue.","He respectfully lowered his eyes and replied, \"This lowly one just returned not long ago.\"","Seeing the candlelight on in the study, Song Qiming waved his hand to dismiss Lanxi.","\"You must be tired after being out for so many days. Go back and rest early.\"","Since he had already reported to his elder sister, he could just go and ask her later.","\"This lowly one takes his leave.\" Lanxi stole a quick glance at Song Shixue before walking away briskly.","The man left before she could even say a few words. Song Shixue was quite unhappy in her heart, and even the look she gave her own brother became filled with disdain.","\"It has been several days already. Has the wasteland not been fully reclaimed yet?\"","Song Qiming shook his head weakly.","\"That wasteland is as hard as a brick. It is incredibly strenuous to dig, and we also have to improve the soil. It cannot possibly be finished in less than a month.\"","Song Shixue's eyes widened.","\"Then will we not miss the spring planting?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"The potatoes will be planted first. The rice will be delayed by a month, otherwise the yield will be very low if we plant it now.\"","Rice paddies need to be fertile. These past few days, he had been constantly ordering people to collect plant ash and various livestock manure to mix into the soil, just hoping to improve it. There was also the matter of watering. It was all a time-consuming and labor-intensive massive project, and they were running a bit short on manpower."]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456: Salt Certificate","paragraphs":["A gray carrier pigeon landed in the backyard of the prefectural office. Upon seeing it, a guard hurriedly caught the pigeon and went to find Lanxi.","Untying the light blue strip of cloth, Lanxi frowned in suspicion.","He found Song Jinzhao and handed the note to her.","Unfolding the note, Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise.","Jia Demao, the magistrate of Qingxia County, had taken the eldest daughter of the Fang family as his concubine. This matter was a bit strange.","\"I remember the magistrate of Qingxia County is quite old?\" Song Jinzhao looked up and asked.","Lanxi replied, \"Jia Demao is already over fifty, and the eldest miss of the Fang family is only a teenager. With this age gap, they could be grandfather and granddaughter.\"","The lit candle burned the note to ashes.","\"The Fang family had their salt trading license revoked over twenty years ago. For them to marry their daughter to Jia Demao at this specific time, there must be something going on. Find a way to get our people inside; I need to know the situation in the Jia estate.\"","Lanxi nodded slightly. \"Understood. I will have Yao Ye infiltrate the place.\"","Just a day after the carrier pigeon was sent out, before Yao Ye even had time to infiltrate the Jia estate, the situation changed.","Song Qiming came to Song Jinzhao holding a memorial written by Jia Demao.","\"The head of the Ding family died of illness. According to the law, the county office must take back the salt trading license of the Ding family's salt shop and select a new salt merchant. Jia Demao has recommended the Fang family.\"","A hint of confusion flashed through Song Jinzhao's eyes.","\"Does the Ding family have no heir?\"","Thinking of this, the anger in Song Qiming's heart flared up even more.","He clenched his fists, wishing he could fly to Qingxia County immediately to bring the Fang family—who were colluding with southwestern foreign tribes and smuggling illicit salt—to justice.","\"The eldest son of the Ding family unfortunately fell off a cliff while mountain climbing yesterday and passed away. The head of the Ding family suddenly passed away because he couldn't bear the shock.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes widened in disbelief. \"Is it really such a coincidence?\"","Song Qiming closed his eyes forcefully and then opened them, gritting his teeth, every word filled with anger.","\"I don't think it's a coincidence. The eldest son of the Ding family died the very next day after the Fang family married their daughter to the magistrate. They definitely did it.\"","\"I want to go to Qingxia County to find out the truth of the matter, to see if this Jia Demao knows anything about it and whether he is involved.\"","\"Although the affairs in Suining City are managed by our subordinates, I am still not at ease. I will have to trouble you, sister, to keep an eye on things.\"","Qingxia County was close to the territory of the Wumeng tribe. The commoners had long harbored grievances against Jia Demao's cowardly and unjust behavior, and civil uprisings had occurred more than once.","If he was involved in this matter, it would be the perfect opportunity to strip him of his magistrate position.","Song Jinzhao instructed, \"Take more men with you. Since the Fang family has chosen to collude with the southwestern foreign tribes, it's hard to guarantee they won't act out of desperation once exposed.\"","\"Not to mention Jia Demao, the territory of the Wumeng tribe is right next door.\"","Song Qiming nodded vigorously in agreement.","Jia Demao was completely unprepared for Song Qiming's sudden arrival.","He hurriedly held onto his hat and ran out to greet him.","\"I, Jia Demao, Magistrate of Qingxia County, pay my respects to the Prefect. Please forgive me for failing to welcome you from afar.\"","Staring at Jia Demao kneeling on the ground, Song Qiming simply could not give him a pleasant look.","He questioned with a smile, his tone carrying a hint of mockery.","\"On my way here, I saw that the people of Qingxia County are all emaciated, nothing but skin and bones. Some were even boiling grass roots on the field ridges to fill their stomachs. Yet you, Lord Jia, appear quite plump, with a waistline comparable to a thick tree trunk.\"","Jia Demao's heart pounded like a drum, his face almost buried in the dirt.","\"I am ashamed. The people of Qingxia County are living a difficult life, and they couldn't even afford seeds for this year's spring planting. I have been so worried but unable to come up with a good plan, which is why my body has become increasingly swollen. I have made a fool of myself in front of you, my lord.\"","Song Qiming snorted coldly, flicked his sleeves expressionlessly, and strode into the county office.","Cold sweat trickling from his temples down to his neck, Jia Demao hurriedly got up and chased after him."]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457: Secretly Exhuming the Corpse for Autopsy","paragraphs":["Song Qiming's formidable reputation had long spread far and wide during the recent bandit suppression campaign, putting the nerves of all officials, high and low, in Suining Prefecture on high alert.","A strict, self-disciplined, and highly capable superior was what many officials feared the most.","Sitting in the armchair of the main hall, Song Qiming wore a solemn expression.","\"I have only recently taken office and am not entirely familiar with the situation in the various counties of Suining Prefecture. I have come this time firstly to observe the conditions of the people, and secondly to inspect the governmental affairs of Qingxia County. I will have to trouble Magistrate Jia for the next few days.\"","Jia Demao swallowed hard in sheer nervousness, raising his head with a bitter smile on his face.","\"It is no trouble at all. It is my great honor that Your Excellency has come to inspect Qingxia County. I could not have asked for more.\"","The empty storehouses, the deficit in the accounts, and the hundreds of yamen runners guarding the county office—the situation was almost identical to that of Suining City.","Song Qiming calmly opened the Yellow Register of taxation and corvee, while Jia Demao, sitting beside him, felt his heart pounding like a drum.","However, when he noticed that Song Qiming was turning the pages extremely fast, merely glancing at them briefly rather than reading carefully, his racing heart gradually settled down.","He is young and completely inexperienced. Reading like that, he definitely will not spot any problems.","After flipping through the register, Song Qiming threw it forcefully onto the table, his brows furrowed so tightly they could crush a fly.","He glared at Jia Demao with extreme dissatisfaction.","\"Qingxia County has a sizable population but pitifully little arable land. As the county magistrate, why haven't you mobilized the people to reclaim wasteland?\"","Jia Demao put on a bitter face, regurgitating the exact same excuse he had used thousands of times.","\"In reply to Your Excellency, Qingxia County borders the territory of the Wumeng tribe. The commoners have suffered from their harassment for years. They worry that the crops they work so hard to grow will be stolen by the Wumeng people, so absolutely no one is willing to reclaim the wasteland.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath, his nose twitching as he exhaled, giving the impression of a man forcibly swallowing his raging anger.","\"I am somewhat tired. Let us end things here for today.\"","After escorting Song Qiming to the post house, Jia Demao hurriedly returned to the county yamen.","He summoned his advisor: \"Song Qiming knows martial arts and does not fear death. There is no guarantee he won't go to Yinma Town. Go there right now. The mouths that need to be shut must be shut. If they won't shut up, lock them up. We absolutely cannot let Song Qiming discover the hidden fields.\"","In the tavern opposite the county yamen, a hole had been poked through the paper window of a tightly shut room.","Seeing the advisor anxiously galloping away on horseback, the person in charge of keeping watch immediately picked up a brush to note down the time and the person's name in a ledger.","At the same time, two disguised guards quietly followed him.","In his room at the post house, Song Qiming was rapidly writing down the information he had gathered that afternoon.","On his way to Qingxia County, he had heard something from the local farmers.","There were many reclaimed fields at the border between Qingxia County and the Wumeng tribe's territory.","Some said they were reclaimed by the Wumeng people, while others claimed they were opened up by villagers from nearby settlements. No one could give a definitive answer, but now Song Qiming was certain of one thing: those fields were not recorded in Qingxia County's Yellow Register.","In the pitch-black night where one could not even see their own hand, Song Qiming and Lanxi, dressed in night-stalking clothes, used grappling hooks to scale the city wall and rushed out of the city.","Upon arriving at the ancestral graves where the Ding family members were buried, three other guards had already been waiting for a long time.","Song Qiming bowed deeply to the two newly made grave mounds, then uttered three words to the four men: \"Start digging.\"","He intended to open the coffins and examine the corpses.","Whether it was the illness and passing of the Ding family head or the fatal fall of the young master of the Ding family from a cliff, the corpses were the most likely places to find evidence.","As the shovels dug down, the soft earth was tossed aside.","Half an hour later, the coffin of the Ding family's young master was unearthed first.","Upon prying open the coffin lid, a pungent stench of rotting flesh rushed out, clinging to their noses and mouths, making them nauseous.","The corpse no longer resembled a human form, exhibiting bloated signs of advanced putrefaction.","Song Qiming put on a mask and gloves, jumped into the pit, and leaned over the coffin to examine the body.","Maggots swarmed the top of the head, and the wound itself was especially gruesome to look at.","However, it could basically be determined that the cause of death was blunt force trauma to the head from falling off the cliff.","Yet, Song Qiming discovered a lot of bloodstains and rotting skin flakes under the deceased's fingernails, which were likely caused by scratching an opponent during a struggle.","Unfastening the collar, he found a black footprint on the chest—someone had kicked him.","In other words, it was highly likely that the young master of the Ding family had been kicked off the cliff during a fight.","After digging up the other grave, they found no obvious issues with the corpse of the Ding family head.","Staring at the two bodies, Song Qiming coldly ordered, \"Move the corpse on the left into the coffin on the right. Take the young master's body with you and find a place to preserve it with ice.\"","The three guards nodded in compliance: \"Your subordinates obey.\""]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458: The Riverbed That Has Been Dry for Many Years","paragraphs":["By the river ten miles outside Suining City, Shi Simian said with a look of helplessness, \"The Yongning River is a branch of the Suiyu River. Its flow is already small. After the waterwheels were built, it can barely supply the surrounding fields during the dry season, but it's simply not enough for areas further away.\"","\"The wasteland reclaimed by the government office is ten miles away from here. The frequent water carrying recently has caused complaints among the common people. I'm afraid that when the dry season comes, there won't be any water left to draw.\"","The stones at the bottom of the river were clearly visible. The water was indeed clear, but it was also undeniably shallow.","Song Jinzhao looked around. Not far away, some commoners were watching them, their faces filled with fear and worry.","When the dry season truly arrived, the government certainly could not fight with the people over water.","Looking out at the laborers drawing and carrying water from the end of the main canal, their steps were heavy and slow, clearly showing that their physical strength was failing them.","They had to think of another way.","Song Jinzhao confirmed with Shi Simian, \"There are water wells in the government office, as well as in the inner and outer cities. Why not dig a well here to get water?\"","She hadn't seen a single water well since leaving the city. If they weren't digging any, there had to be a reason.","Shi Simian nodded, his chin dropping to his chest as if it weighed a thousand pounds.","\"County Princess, you might not know this, but the soil layer in many parts of Suining Prefecture is very shallow. The rocks beneath the soil are like mountains, impossible to drill through.\"","\"Suining Prefecture and the other four counties are located in low-lying areas with relatively deep soil layers. Furthermore, groundwater flows down through the crevices of the rocks to these lower places, which is why we can draw water there. Take Suining City for example: from the inner city to the outer city, the water table goes from deep to shallow. Once you pass the outer city wall, any well you dig will be a dry well, completely unable to store water.\"","Returning to the fields being reclaimed, Song Jinzhao said to Shi Simian, \"Go ahead with your work first. I'll just look around.\"","Shi Simian smiled and called over Liu Hucheng. \"Constable Liu and his ancestors for seven generations have been locals of Suining. County Princess, if you have any questions, feel free to ask him.\"","Song Jinzhao walked along the edge of the wasteland being cleared and noticed that the soil to the west was relatively softer and appeared to be more fertile.","She straightened her back, observed her surroundings, and pointed to the wasteland in the west, asking Liu Hucheng, \"Is that area going to be reclaimed as well?\"","Liu Hucheng stood on his tiptoes to look into the distance, then reached out and pointed to a spot far away.","\"Yes, it will be, all the way to the Old Dry Trench over there.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyebrows rose slightly. \"Is the Old Dry Trench a canal that has already dried up?\"","Liu Hucheng replied, \"It's a dried-up riverbed. However, it has been dry for many years, and now it's as shallow as a trench.\"","Her interest piqued, Song Jinzhao stepped toward the direction Liu Hucheng was pointing.","It was indeed a trench, quite shallow, perhaps only a few meters deep.","\"When did it dry up?\"","Liu Hucheng scratched his head and said, \"It was already dry when this humble one was born. I don't know exactly when it happened.\"","Song Jinzhao gazed at the dried-up trench, falling into deep thought.","The soil near a water source was usually better, but the soil here was only slightly better than elsewhere. This indicated that an exceptionally long time had passed—at least a century.","The Yongning River had water, yet this river had dried up. There had to be a problem with the water source upstream.","She picked up her binoculars and looked upstream along the riverbed, faintly able to see a cluster of towering mountains in the far distance.","Seeing Song Jinzhao cover her eyes with two long tubes, Liu Hucheng felt somewhat confused.","He narrowed his eyes and came up with an explanation for himself.","He figured the sunlight was too glaring, so she had to cover her eyes, or else she wouldn't be able to see.","Putting down the binoculars, Song Jinzhao asked Liu Hucheng, \"How far are the mountains ahead from here?\"","Liu Hucheng took a look and answered, \"That is Suiyu Mountain. It's about three hundred miles from here.\"","Song Jinzhao asked in return, \"Is the Suiyu River over there?\"","Liu Hucheng nodded slightly. \"All the rivers inside Suiyu Mountain are called the Suiyu River. Most of the water in the waterways of Suining City flows down from the Suiyu River, and the same goes for the streams.\""]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459: The Cliff That Intercepts the River","paragraphs":["Following the dry riverbed south, Song Jinzhao and her group finally arrived at Mount Suiyu just as the evening sun was about to set.","Song Jinzhao looked toward the small path leading up the mountain. \"Let's go up and take a look.\"","Liu Hucheng looked hesitant.","\"My Lady, it is getting late. Perhaps we should go up tomorrow, otherwise it will be completely dark by the time we come down.\"","The mountain walls were steep and covered in rocks. It would be easy to trip and fall in the dark when they could not see the path.","Song Jinzhao shook her head and pointed to a spot wedged between two mountains. \"We will not go to the peak. Let's just check out that spot first.\"","Half an hour later, looking at the riverbed blocked behind the cliff, Song Jinzhao fell deep into thought.","It was this very cliff wall, piled high with rocks beneath their feet, that had cut off the river water originally flowing toward Laogan Ditch.","Judging by the location, this cliff wall must have been formed by the collapse of the mountains on both sides. As long as they blew up this mountain, the water from the Suiyu River could flow into Laogan Ditch once again.","Seeing that Song Jinzhao remained silent, the impatient Liu Hucheng frequently glanced at the others.","Seeing them looking as if they were perfectly used to this, he had no choice but to suppress his doubts and continue waiting.","Watching the sky begin to darken, Song Jinzhao turned and said, \"Let's go.\"","Liu Hucheng blinked, looking completely bewildered.","He followed her, feeling deeply puzzled.","Riding a horse all day just to come look at a mountain, only to leave without saying a single word—what exactly was this County Princess Linghui planning?","She couldn't possibly just have too much free time on her hands.","It was unrealistic to travel back to Suining City overnight, so they spent that evening at a nearby villager's home.","Seeing Song Jinzhao swallow the wild vegetables that looked like grass roots from her bowl without changing her expression, Liu Hucheng's face showed admiration in addition to shock.","Even though these wild vegetables had been boiled in water, their texture was still extremely coarse.","The fact that Song Jinzhao, as a County Princess, could actually eat them without showing any disgust seemed simply unbelievable to Liu Hucheng.","Song Jinzhao asked as she ate, her tone as casual as if she were making small talk.","\"Old man, do you always eat this?\"","The wrinkled old man's hands trembled as he held his chopsticks.","He sighed, \"The highland barley we harvested last year was just finished off last month. Now we only have wild vegetables. Fortunately, there are plenty on the mountain, enough to last us until the autumn harvest.\"","Song Jinzhao chewed the tasteless wild grass roots in her mouth, only feeling them scratch her throat.","Spring planting had not been long ago; waiting until the autumn harvest would take about four months.","That meant they would have to eat wild vegetables for four months.","She noticed two wooden buckets placed in the corner, one of which still contained water.","\"Where do the nearby commoners get their daily water?\"","Coming from Mount Suiyu, Song Jinzhao had not seen a river, nor even a stream.","The old man smiled and pointed casually toward the window.","\"There is snowmelt flowing out from the crevices in the rocks on the mountain. We all get our water from there.\"","Song Jinzhao did not speak.","She had seen the rock crevices with flowing water at the foot of the mountain just earlier. It was six miles away from here, making it a twelve-mile round trip.","Without any means of transportation, carrying water back and forth by human labor would be incredibly exhausting.","Thinking of Laogan Ditch not far from the village, Song Jinzhao took a deep breath, only feeling the pressure increase.","The day after returning to the government office, Song Jinzhao rode her horse to the lower reaches of Laogan Ditch.","At first, the riverbed was still visible, but later it turned into a plain with villages built on it; the original shape could no longer be seen.","Just blowing up the mountain was not enough; the flowing water needed somewhere to go. She had to find an existing river for it to merge into.","On the map in the study, Song Jinzhao had marked out tributaries of all sizes with a pen.","Too small would not work; it would not be able to handle the water volume.","Too far would not work either; digging it out would be time-consuming and laborious.","Finally, Song Jinzhao set the connection point at the lower reaches of the Yongning River.","The riverbed was wide enough, and the depth was sufficient. The lower reaches led straight to Qingxia County. With an increase in water volume, the water usage problems of the commoners on both banks could also be alleviated."]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460: Jia Demao Embezzled One Hundred Thousand Silver Taels","paragraphs":["With a plan in mind, Song Jinzhao intended to finish making the explosives before Song Qiming returned.","In the posthouse of Qingxia County, Yao Ye, who had been lying low in the Jia manor for three days, finally brought back a piece of news sufficient to nail Jia Demao to the wall.","There is a secret room in Jia Demao's bedchamber, and the silver hidden inside is no less than a hundred thousand taels.","Song Qiming's eyes nearly popped out of his head in shock. Where did he get so much silver?","Even after raiding so many bandit strongholds, they had only confiscated a little over a hundred thousand taels. Even if all the profits from the wastelands around Yinma Town went straight into Jia Demao's pockets, he couldn't possibly have saved up a hundred thousand taels.","By tracking the advisor Jia Demao had sent out, Song Qiming had successfully investigated the wasteland located at the border between Qingxia County and the Wumeng tribe's territory.","Five hundred mu of wasteland had been secretly cultivated by the villagers of Yinma Town under Jia Demao's threats.","The villagers were exploited as free labor, with Jia Demao as the ultimate beneficiary. The headman of Yinma Town and the village chiefs of several subordinate villages were also involved.","They guarded these five hundred mu of land as tightly as an iron fortress. If outsiders occasionally stumbled upon it, they would brush it off by claiming it was cultivated by the Wumeng tribe.","Yao Ye continued his report.","In recent days, the eldest young master of the Fang family has visited the Jia manor every day. Nominally, he is visiting his sister, but in reality, he is secretly led into Jia Demao's study every time. Their relationship can be described as extremely close.","Song Qiming furrowed his brows so tightly they could crush a fly, his chest burning with towering rage.","The silver was very likely given by the Fang family. It is impossible for the coroner to have missed such obvious evidence on the corpse. Jia Demao must have deliberately concealed it.","Lan Xi took a step forward and suggested, According to the plan, we are going out of the city tomorrow to inspect the agricultural work. Why not use this opportunity to expose the hidden fields and condemn Jia Demao? As long as we have a legitimate reason, searching his manor will be perfectly justifiable.","Song Qiming shook his head.","This matter must be handled with lightning speed, leaving no one with the time to react.","Tomorrow, after Jia Demao and I leave the city, you will take my warrant and surround the Fang manor. The salt warehouse plus those portraits are enough evidence.","After capturing them, interrogate them on the spot and make them give up Jia Demao. Then, take the deputy magistrate and the registrar of Qingxia County to search the Jia manor. Your attitude must be unyielding. I will take all the yamen runners of Qingxia County with me tomorrow, and leave all the men we brought from Suining City to you.","Lan Xi shook his head faster than a rattle drum, his solemn eyes full of disapproval.","No way. What if Jia Demao makes a move against you?","Surrounded entirely by Qingxia County's yamen runners, even if Song Qiming knew martial arts, he couldn't fight off that many people.","Song Qiming raised a hand to stop his words.","Yao Ye will take some men and come with me. As long as you keep the news suppressed, Jia Demao won't notice a thing. When we return, we will capture the ringleader first. By the time he realizes what is happening, it will be too late.","Seeing Song Qiming's resolute attitude, Lan Xi had no choice but to obey.","After leaving the room, he pressed down on Yao Ye's shoulder and solemnly urged, You must guard the Eldest Young Master without leaving his side for even a step. If anything goes wrong, prioritize escaping with your lives.","Yao Ye nodded vigorously. Rest assured, Steward Lan. Even if it costs our brothers' lives, we will not let anything happen to the Eldest Young Master.","Before setting out the next day, Song Qiming sent someone to deliver a message to Jia Demao, asking him to bring all the Qingxia County yamen runners along under the guise of protection.","Jia Demao mistakenly thought Song Qiming just wanted to put on a grand show and did not think much of it. It wasn't until they were leaving the city that he realized Song Qiming had barely brought any of his own guards, only twenty or so men in total.","Jia Demao casually asked Song Qiming, Why do I not see Guard Lan?","Song Qiming feigned nonchalance and replied, A letter came from the prefectural office last night saying that the land reclamation progress is falling behind the spring sowing due to a lack of manpower. I had Lan Xi take the men back today. For the next few days, I will have to trouble the county yamen for protection.","Jia Demao was struck by a sudden realization and immediately promised, Once we return, this humble official will dispatch men to the posthouse to ensure Your Excellency's safety.","Over a thousand laborers and it still wasn't enough? Just how much wasteland were they trying to reclaim!","Since the prefectural treasury had plenty of silver, could he perhaps ask for some of it?"]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461: Surrounding Fang's Residence to Obtain a Confession","paragraphs":["From atop the city wall, Lanxi watched them leave the city. Only after confirming they were far enough away that Jia Demao could not return in a short time did he make his move.","The front and back doors were instantly blocked. The servants guarding the gates were about to resist but were immediately shoved into the house by Lanxi.","\"What are you doing? Our master is the county magistrate's father-in-law!\"","Lanxi ordered coldly, \"Gag him. From this moment on, no one leaves the Fang estate.\"","The main doors slammed shut with a loud crash. The onlookers pointed at the entrance of the Fang estate, murmuring among themselves.","\"Did the Fang family commit a crime?\"","\"That can't be. Didn't the eldest daughter of the Fang family marry Magistrate Jia?\"","Inside the chaotic inner courtyard of the Fang estate, bailiffs were searching for people everywhere. Once caught, they were immediately escorted to the front hall to be held under guard.","\"Who gave you the nerve to cause trouble in the Fang family?\" Fang Mo, the head of the Fang family, pointed at Lanxi and cursed. He charged forward with all his might, looking so terrifying that he seemed ready to eat him alive.","Lanxi kicked him squarely in the shoulder. The crisp sound of a dislocation, accompanied by a roaring scream, echoed through the inner courtyard of the Fang estate, making everyone else tremble in fear.","Fang Mo sat on the ground, grimacing in pain, his back already drenched in cold sweat.","\"My family is related to the Jia family by marriage! I want to see Magistrate Jia!\"","Lanxi watched him coldly without saying a word. He was waiting.","Before long, a bailiff who had gone to search rushed over to Lanxi, gripping his sword, and reported.","\"Steward Lanxi, we found the salt warehouse.\"","The eyes of the Fang family members widened simultaneously, their terrified expressions filled with absolute shock.","They were here for the salt warehouse!","Fang Mo's mind went blank. Only then did he realize that these bailiffs were not from the county office.","\"Who exactly are you? Why are you targeting our Fang family?\"","Lanxi waved his hand, ordering his men to take all the adult males of the Fang family away for separate interrogations. He then walked over to Fang Mo and leaned down to look at him.","\"The imperial court has strictly forbidden the sale of smuggled salt, let alone salt transported from Binzhou.\"","Every word hammered into Fang Mo's mind, terrifying him so much that his very soul trembled.","\"You... how did you know...\" Before he could finish, a sudden wail rang out.","Fang Mo turned around in panic. The screams were coming from behind tightly shut doors; it was his sons and brothers.","Lanxi threw a portrait onto Fang Mo, his voice carrying a heavy sense of oppression.","\"If you don't want anyone to know, don't do it. And the murder of the Eldest Young Master of the Ding family to snatch the salt permits—who could you possibly keep that from?\"","Fang Mo stared blankly at the ground, finally realizing something amidst the wails and cries.","\"You are the prefect's man?\"","No one else could command so many bailiffs. The inspection of government affairs was a fake; secretly investigating the smuggled salt was the true purpose.","It was completely over now!","\"You're not too stupid. Whether the Fang family can leave a bloodline depends on whether you tell the truth.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, the female family members behind them immediately started having thoughts of their own.","Within a few breaths, someone holding a child cried out to Fang Mo.","\"Father, Ye'er is still young; nothing can happen to him.\"","The person speaking was the second daughter-in-law of the Fang family, and the child in her arms was her son, born less than three months ago.","\"I'll talk! I'll talk! I'll talk!\" A familiar voice came from the room. Fang Mo collapsed onto the ground, all of his spirit completely draining away.","That was his son's voice.","\"I will tell you everything you want to know.\" The great building was collapsing; there was no longer any room to maneuver.","With both Song Qiming and Jia Demao out of the city, the deputy magistrate and the petty officials of the county office, who had been under heavy pressure for days, finally had some time to catch their breath.","When Lanxi barged in with the confession, they were lying on their chairs taking a nap.","First, they heard footsteps, and upon opening their eyes to see a massive crowd of people, they panicked on the spot.","After clearly seeing Lanxi's face, they breathed a sigh of relief.","The master of records asked, \"Guard Lanxi, why didn't you leave the city with Lord Song?\"","Just as he finished speaking, the deputy magistrate walked out from the inner room. Seeing so many bailiffs, his face was full of confusion.","He was just about to speak when Lanxi handed a warrant right in front of him.","\"This is a warrant personally written by the prefect. Lord Hai will understand after reading it.\""]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462: Take Down Jia Demao","paragraphs":["The county deputy unfolded the warrant, his expression growing more terrified the longer he looked.","He anxiously grabbed Lan Xi's arm, trying to persuade her, How about we wait for the county magistrate to return before searching?","It had been so peaceful these past few days; how could such a thing happen!","Lan Xi's gaze turned cold and sharp as she looked at the deputy. The prefect has ordered that Jia's mansion be searched immediately upon obtaining the evidence. Are you going to defy orders?","The blood instantly drained from the faces of the deputy and the master registrar. Their hearts pounded like rapid drumbeats, feeling as if they would leap out of their chests the very next second.","The master registrar pulled the deputy's hand down, shaking his head at him while explaining to Lan Xi, Of course not. It's just that this happened so suddenly, we haven't quite processed it yet.","The heavy doors of the Jia mansion were smashed open, and Lan Xi led her men straight to Jia Demao's room.","Box after box of silver was carried out, leaving the officials of Qingxia County with faces paler than cold iron.","The county yamen's treasury was tight. They knew about the hidden fields, but they never expected there to be this much silver.","Manager Lan, there is a total of one hundred and three thousand taels of silver. All thirty-two members of the Jia household have been captured; no one escaped.","Meanwhile, Song Qiming and his group had arrived at Yinma Town.","Lord Jia, why are there fewer and fewer commoners on this road? he asked Jia Demao, feigning confusion.","Jia Demao gave a knowing smile, well-prepared for the question.","Yinma Town is only separated from the Wumeng tribe's territory by a single mountain. The people rarely go out; they feel safer staying in their villages.","Song Qiming nodded slightly. Since we are here, I would like to see the border. Lead the way, Lord Jia.","Jia Demao looked nervously at his advisor. Seeing the man give a subtle nod, he took a deep breath and forced a smile onto his face.","Having too many yamen runners is too conspicuous. To avoid drawing the attention of the Wumeng people, it's best not to get too close.","Song Qiming nodded without saying a word.","Following Jia Demao's lead, Yao Ye clearly noticed that this was not the road leading to the hidden fields.","When they arrived and stood on a small hillside, the wasteland originally located at the foot of the mountain was completely blocked by the woods, making it impossible to see.","Song Qiming gazed across the valley toward the other side of the mountain. This place isn't far from the Wumeng territory. Does anyone come over often?","Jia Demao nodded and replied, On the first and fifteenth of every month, quite a few foreigners come to the towns and villages to buy things. However, the people on both sides look down on each other. Whenever a conflict arises, it puts me in a very difficult position.","Song Qiming glanced at him calmly, hiding the sarcasm in his eyes.","Calming conflicts by making the local people suffer the losses—how very difficult indeed.","Originally thinking they could head back after looking around, Song Qiming stubbornly dragged things out for nearly four hours, only suggesting they leave when the sun was about to set in the late afternoon.","After being on edge for so long with his mental focus pushed to the limit, the pot-bellied Jia Demao was not only sweating from exhaustion, but his mind had also begun to grow foggy.","The runners, having walked all day, were even more exhausted. Their legs were so weak they could barely stand, and they could only drag their feet at the back of the group.","If it weren't for Song Qiming and Jia Demao insisting on returning, they would have loved to just lie down on the ground and sleep.","Yao Ye turned his head and scanned the surroundings.","Everything was going according to plan. Now, it all depended on whether Manager Lan had succeeded on her end.","Approaching the city gates, Lan Xi, who had been waiting for a long time, saw the large group approaching and immediately waved the flag planted on the gate three times.","Song Qiming understood immediately upon seeing this. He turned to glance at Jia Demao, who was squinting sleepily.","In a split second, before anyone could react, Song Qiming leaped up from his horse like a dark shadow.","He grabbed Jia Demao by the collar, flew down from the saddle, threw the man to the ground, and forcefully bound his hands.","That instantly chased away any drowsiness.","Jia Demao stiffly turned his neck, looking at Song Qiming with eyes full of shock.","My Lord, what are you doing?","The runners panicked. Some tried to step forward, but suddenly, a group of guards rushed out from inside the city gates.","Song Qiming raised his fist and shouted loudly, Magistrate Jia Demao of Qingxia County has perverted the law for bribes, smuggled salt, and oppressed the people. I am arresting him according to the law. No one is to move!","For a moment, the runners who were about to draw their swords froze. While they hesitated, Lan Xi and her people had already run up to them."]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463: Mid-Valley of Helplessness","paragraphs":["Hearing Song Qiming accuse him of smuggling salt, Jia Demao, pinned to the ground, instantly lost the color in his face.","He tilted his chin up in disbelief, desperately trying to suppress the anxiety surging within him.","\"Without any proof, why would Your Excellency make such a claim?\"","Expressionless, Song Qiming hoisted him up by the rope and handed him over to Lanxi.","\"The hundred thousand taels of illicit silver in the Jia estate is the physical evidence, and the Fang family along with your newly taken concubine are the witnesses.\"","Jia Demao's mouth fell open, his face as pale as a sheet of paper. From Song Qiming's sudden arrival to his own capture, everything suddenly made sense.","\"You lured me out of the city on purpose!\"","He was so young, yet his scheming was so deep. Had he known, he would have killed him right when he arrived.","No matter how much regret filled his heart, it was too late now.","In the county yamen, which was as deathly quiet as a deserted wasteland, officials and clerks hid in their rooms, watching Jia Demao being dragged into the dungeon.","That night, not a single official in Qingxia County could sleep. They tossed and turned in their beds with their eyes closed, their hearts brimming with anxiety for what tomorrow might bring.","The hundred and twenty thousand taels of silver and two thousand catties of smuggled salt confiscated from the Fang estate, combined with the hundred thousand taels embezzled by Jia Demao, amounted to more than what the mountain bandits had robbed.","Seeing that his cause was lost, Jia Demao confessed to all his crimes.","The Fang family had approached him half a year ago, gradually bribing him with thirty thousand taels of silver just so he would turn a blind eye when they smuggled salt.","It was not until the batch of smuggled salt was robbed by bandits two months ago that the Fang family set their sights on the official salt licenses, murdering the eldest young master of the Ding family to achieve this.","To get Jia Demao to recommend the Fang family, Fang Mo married his daughter off to him as a concubine and gave him an additional fifty thousand taels of silver.","He also guaranteed that once they obtained the salt licenses, he would give Jia Demao a fifty percent cut of the profits from the smuggled salt they sold.","Not only that, but the entire history of Fang Mo's collusion with the Yang clan of Panzhou was written down and signed with a thumbprint.","The confession detailed the specific times and locations, as well as the names and identities of the middlemen, revealing that the Wumeng tribe served as their transit hub.","Having stayed up all night, Song Qiming had dark circles under his eyes the next day.","Holding his breath with a heavy expression, he sat on the long bench in the main hall and wrote a memorial to Gu Zhongxun.","He had no authority to decide whether to prosecute the Yang clan of Panzhou for their involvement behind the smuggled salt transported from Binzhou.","Not only could he not make the call, but even Gu Zhongxun could not. This matter had to be reported to the imperial court.","\"Seal the smuggled salt. No one is allowed to move it, and it must be strictly guarded.\"","Song Qiming ordered, staring at the deputy magistrate with a stern expression and a forceful tone.","\"Yes, this subordinate obeys.\" The deputy magistrate nervously kept his head down and gulped, not even daring to steal a glance at him.","Having quietly put on an act for several days, this prefect was clearly not someone to be trifled with. The deputy was truly terrified of being implicated by Jia Demao's crimes.","When Song Qiming departed, he took Jia Demao and several key witnesses from the Fang family with him. The two hundred thousand taels of silver were deposited into the Jufeng Bank and exchanged for banknotes.","This money would definitely have to be handed over to the imperial court. At most, Qingxia County might be allowed to keep a portion of the confiscated salt once the imperial decree was issued.","He just hoped that the candidate for the new county magistrate would be someone reliable.","When Gu Zhongxun received the memorial, he sighed three times in a row.","\"So many troublesome matters. Why can't they just behave themselves?\"","Gu Gaoyuan picked up the memorial and skimmed it rapidly, teasing, \"Does 'they' refer to Song Qiming or Panzhou?\"","Gu Zhongxun rolled his eyes at him with a dark expression, letting out a heavy snort from his nostrils.","\"What do you think?\"","Gu Gaoyuan pursed his lips into a smile. \"I think it's both.\"","Gu Zhongxun took a deep breath and let out a long sigh, sitting down to grind some ink.","\"The Emperor is going to be furious again.\"","Gu Gaoyuan shrugged, not particularly concerned.","\"It will eventually just fade away into nothing anyway, so there's no need to worry too much.\"","\"The imperial court won't initiate a war. Panzhou just fought with Ningzhou last year. Until they finish annexing the other foreign tribes in the southwest, they won't deploy troops against the court.\"","Gu Zhongxun's wrist grew weak as he ground the ink, his already depressed spirit sinking into an even deeper silence."]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464: Explosives","paragraphs":["Song Qiming returned to the prefectural office to look for Song Jinzhao, only to find that she had not been home for several days. Whenever he asked anyone, they all said they did not know where she was.","Just as he was feeling puzzled, Song Anhao walked in with a miserable look on her face.","\"What is wrong? You look so dejected,\" Song Qiming asked.","Song Anhao slumped her shoulders and leaned her head against her brother's chest, seeking comfort.","\"Doing business is so hard. I am going to die of exhaustion.\"","The shop Song Anhao managed had already opened. The business was not exactly bad, but it was not too good either. Compared to earning gold every day in the capital, the gap was simply too large.","Song Qiming pinched Song Anhao's ear and pulled her away.","\"When I came back, I saw that the business in the shop was quite good. Are you not making money?\"","Tongbao Street was the most bustling market street in Suining City, and it was also the only way to get from the south city gate to the prefectural office.","Song Anhao raised her chin and complained, \"There are a lot of people, but the profit margin is too thin. When will I ever be able to recover my costs?\"","Song Qiming said, \"The population of Suining City is not large, and the people are poor. They wish they could split a single copper coin into four to spend. It will get better once the city is developed in the future.\"","\"Where is Ah Jie? Do you know where she went?\"","Song Anhao shook her head. \"Eldest sister went out three days ago and has not returned since. Second sister should know, but she will not tell me.\"","Song Qiming blinked, his mind already beginning to race.","Keeping it a secret from everyone meant it had to be something very important.","In the evening, Song Shixue returned from the medical clinic.","Faced with Song Qiming's inquiries, she grabbed his hand and led him into the study.","\"Ah Jie wants to blow up the mountain to let the water of the Suiyu River flow out again. She said that once you returned, you should go to Suiyu Mountain to find her, and you must only bring Lanxi along.\"","Song Qiming's eyes widened. \"Which mountain? How is she going to blow it up?\"","Song Shixue pointed at the map pasted on the wall and said, \"It is this one right at the front of Suiyu Mountain. Ah Jie said that as long as she blows a hole in it, the river water will flow back into the Laogan Ditch. Then, the newly reclaimed wastelands will not lack water.\"","\"As for how she is going to blow it up, I am not clear. It seems she is making some kind of device.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath and faced the wall, his gaze following the places Song Jinzhao had marked all the way down.","\"I understand. I will go to Suiyu Mountain tomorrow.\"","At the break of dawn, after handing over his tasks, Song Qiming took Lanxi and headed straight for Suiyu Mountain.","When they arrived at the foot of the mountain, a sudden explosion echoed through the sky. The sound came from afar, like a clap of rolling thunder.","Not far away, villagers on the hillside walked out of their houses. They gazed toward Suiyu Mountain and discussed it animatedly.","\"What on earth is that sound? Did the mountain really collapse?\"","\"It has sounded over a dozen times, big and small, since yesterday. It is terrifying.\"","\"...\"","Song Qiming withdrew his gaze and met Lanxi's eyes. Without saying a word, the two continued riding forward.","With such a loud noise, and considering Ah Jie had proposed blowing up the mountain, this sound was very likely her doing.","After reaching the foot of the mountain and seeing no one, Lanxi dismounted and climbed to the top to fire a signal flare.","Two quarters of an hour later, Qingshuang appeared before them on horseback.","\"Eldest Young Master, this way.\"","The narrow mountain path required them to bend down and lower their heads from time to time. They passed through two mountains and entered a sinkhole, where they saw two temporarily erected wooden houses.","Bypassing the uneven, potholed ground, the exposed rocks looked as if they had been chiseled open by someone.","Hearing the footsteps, Song Jinzhao looked up toward the door.","Stripped of her magnificent dresses, she wore only an azure fine cotton ruqun without any embroidery. Her jet-black hair, usually as smooth as silk, was now covered in dust. Even her face was smeared with soot, making her look a bit dirtier than a fire-stoking maid.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"You are back. Have the matters in Qingxia County been settled?\"","Song Qiming's expression was slightly dazed, and he nodded woodenly in response.","\"They have been handled. Jia Demao and the several participants from the Fang family have all been locked up in the prefectural prison. Qingxia County is temporarily managed by the deputy magistrate, and the memorial has already been sent to Songzhou City.\"","Song Jinzhao tied the opening of the hemp bag tightly, leaving only the fuse exposed.","\"Come, let me show you.\"","After hundreds of trials over three days, she had finally figured out the material formula for making explosives. This was already the final version.","She placed the explosive pack in the dirt beneath a rock crevice, ran far away, and lit the fuse.","A sizzling sound rang out. After a half-second pause, the earth shook, the mountain swayed, and the massive boulder blew apart with a deafening roar.","Hiding behind a rock not far away, Song Qiming was so frightened that his whole body trembled, feeling as if an earth dragon were turning over.","Crushed stone debris and dirt fell from the sky like scattering flowers. Unable to react in time, Song Qiming and Lanxi got mouthfuls of dirt, and their exposed skin stung slightly from the falling debris.","On the hillside outside the mountain, the commoners clutched their chests in panic.","\"It is happening again. It must be the gods in heaven getting angry.\"","After the commotion stopped, Song Qiming walked on weak legs toward the place where the explosives had been set, while Lanxi, following beside him, used his sword as a walking stick.","The boulder that originally required two people to wrap their arms around had been blasted into several small pieces. The dirt on the ground was completely gone, revealing the bedrock buried beneath.","Song Jinzhao curled the corners of her lips into a smile.","\"This is the power of just one pack of explosives. If we get a few dozen of them, we can blow open the cliff blocking the Suiyu River.\"","Song Qiming plopped down on the ground. Looking up at Song Jinzhao's glowing face, he felt no excitement, only fear in his heart.","\"Ah Jie, the power of this thing is too great. How do you know how to make such a thing?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"I thought of this when I was making the signal flares. It will be useful in future wars.\"","\"Cough, cough, cough—\" Song Qiming gasped, the foul smell rushing into his throat, making him cough uncomfortably.","No wonder Ah Jie had the intention to rebel against the imperial court. With such a divine artifact, why worry about not achieving great things?","Just bringing it out would be enough to scare people out of their wits."]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465: Resolutely Oppose Cutting Through Mountains to Divert Water","paragraphs":["\"What! You want to clear out that river that has been dry for hundreds of years?\"","Shi Simian looked at Song Qiming as if he had been struck by lightning. His mind buzzed, and he felt as if he would faint in the next second.","Song Qiming nodded. \"The wasteland lacks water. I plan to cut through the mountain so the waters of the Suiyu River can flow out again. The current riverbed is too shallow; it must be dug out.\"","They couldn't reveal the secret of the explosives to outsiders, so Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming planned to use cutting through the mountain as an excuse to first repair the riverbed. Then, they would find a stormy day to blow up the mountain, claiming that a heavenly thunderbolt had struck and split it open.","\"My Lord, that is a mountain of solid stone. To call it an impenetrable fortress would not be an exaggeration. It would take at least decades to carve through it.\"","Shi Simian clutched his chest, gasping for air. He advised earnestly, tears almost springing to his eyes.","Just as Suining City was showing signs of improvement, how could the Prefect's brain suddenly become so foolish?","Song Qiming spoke with righteous conviction, \"As long as it solves the irrigation problem in Suining City, let alone decades, even if it takes a hundred years, I am willing to do it.\"","Shi Simian grew even dizzier. Just as he was about to kneel and continue his pleading, his vision went black, and he collapsed to the ground.","Lan Xi rushed forward and caught him. Shi Simian's eyes were tightly shut; he had passed out.","Song Qiming stood up, a bit bewildered. How could the man faint after just a few words?","\"Someone, quickly fetch a doctor.\"","Not long after, Song Shixue ran in carrying a medical box.","She placed her fingers on Shi Simian's wrist. After a moment, a strange look flashed in her eyes. Her lips parted and closed as she swallowed her original words and phrased it differently.","\"Lord Shi is simply suffering from overwork. He will be fine after a few days of rest.\"","Song Qiming came to a sudden realization, but at the same time, he furrowed his brows.","During the days he wasn't at the government office, Shi Simian had been supervising the work outside the city. But supervising wasn't the same as doing physical labor in the fields—how could he be overworked?","Just as he was about to reflect on this, Song Shixue suddenly nudged his arm. Looking up, he found her winking at him meaningfully.","His heart stirred slightly, and he silently followed her outside to a secluded spot.","Song Shixue looked at him, her voice pitched very low, her face flushing slightly.","\"Lord Shi is nearly sixty years old and needs to exercise moderation in the bedroom. Otherwise, his kidney essence will be depleted, and situations like today's sudden disruption of vital energy will happen again.\"","Song Qiming froze. When he realized what she meant, his face turned red and then dark. The words caught in his throat, and he didn't know what to say.","\"I understand. I'll mention it to him once he wakes up.\"","To still have such vigorous energy in his sixties—it seemed the tasks assigned to him were not enough.","If he were so tired that he fell asleep the moment his head hit the pillow, he wouldn't have the energy for anything else.","Seeing that he understood, Song Shixue pressed her lips into a thin line and nodded.","She had encountered several cases of young men suffering from kidney essence deficiency, but this was her first time seeing it in a sixty-year-old man.","Judging by his pulse just now, the frequency last night was definitely not low.","When Shi Simian woke up and Song Qiming told him the matter, he was so ashamed that he wished he could bury his head under the covers and never see anyone again.","He completely forgot about opposing the river clearing project. By the time he rested for a few days and went outside the city to take a look, Song Qiming had already started the construction.","Looking at the excavated earth, Shi Simian wore a bitter face all morning before finally resigning to his fate.","At worst, they would toil for three years and leave behind an unresolved mess. When the time came, he could just push the blame onto Song Qiming. The new prefect would have to accept the bad luck, and no one would hold him accountable.","Inside the Imperial Study in the capital's royal palace.","Emperor Xiao Chengjing looked at Gu Zhongxun's memorial, his face as dark as the bottom of a pot.","He forcefully slammed the memorial onto the imperial desk, his chest heaving violently.","\"What a Jia Demao, this treacherous ingrate! I will have him executed.\"","\"Cough, cough, cough—\" Choking on a breath, he clutched his chest, his face changing color from the discomfort.","Zhao Yande quickly walked over to rub his back and soothe him.","\"Please do not be angry, Your Majesty. It is not worth damaging your dragon body over such people.\"","Xiao Chengjing slumped back into the dragon throne, his gaze somewhat unfocused.","\"Yande, is my health not as good as it used to be?\"","Alarm bells rang in his head, but Zhao Yande forced a smile and offered comforting words.","\"Your Majesty's dragon body is robust and healthy. It is just that you have been staying up late reviewing memorials these past few days. You should take a good rest.\"","Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes and remained quiet for a long time. Once he recovered some energy, he spoke, his tone somewhat heavy.","\"Draft a decree. The Magistrate of Qingxia County, Jia Demao, colluded with corrupt merchants and smuggled official salt, shaking the foundation of the state. Order the execution of his entire family.\"","\"The confiscated two hundred thousand taels of silver shall be deposited into the national treasury. The remaining smuggled salt is to be handed over to Song Qiming to handle, so his efforts were not in vain.\"","\"As for the Yang clan in Panzhou, hold off for now. Just take careful precautions against them.\"","By the time the imperial decree reached Suining City, two months had passed. Looking at the river channel, which was now over a dozen meters deep, Song Qiming curled his lips in a satisfied smile.","\"Tell Deputy Magistrate Hai to sell the stored smuggled salt to the local salt merchants as soon as possible, and then bring the silver to the government office.\"","The labor was free, but daily food and drink required grain. What he lacked most right now was silver."]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466: Blasting the Mountain, Thunder Strikes from the Sky","paragraphs":["The continuous clanking of metal rang out at the foot of Suiyu Mountain, accompanied by flying sparks.","Nearby, a crowd of commoners gathered to watch, pointing and murmuring endlessly at the yamen runners and laborers who were chipping away at the mountain with hammers and chisels.","\"With a mountain this thick, how long will it take to dig through?\"","The meager piles of stone rubble were almost negligible compared to the massive rocky mountain that stood nearly a thousand feet tall before them.","Seeing no progress over the past two days, the people all felt the government was on a fool's errand.","A two-hundred-mile canal had already been dug. If the mountain could not be moved, this massive project would all be for nothing.","Not far away, Song Jinzhao sat atop her horse, looking up at the sky.","Dark clouds were gathering in the south and drifting closer; it would not be long before it rained.","The rainy season was long, and the weather would not be very good for the next half month.","\"Tell the Eldest Young Master to halt the work once it rains and send everyone back.\"","Qingshuang gave a meaningful nod.","Before long, the wind began to howl. Accompanied by fine raindrops, sand and gravel swept across the ground, stinging people's eyes so badly they could barely open them.","Song Qiming summoned Liu Hucheng and said, \"Take the men back. We will resume work when the rain stops.\"","It was a day's walk from Suiyu Mountain to Suining City. By the time they arrived home, it was already midnight. Everyone's clothes were soaked through; water poured out with a single wring.","In the middle of the following night, the rain poured down even harder. Blinding lightning flashed across the sky, and peals of thunder boomed as if trying to blast a hole in the heavens.","The sound of galloping hooves, masked by the heavy rain, suddenly came to a halt. Only four people made this trip: Song Jinzhao, her brother, Qingshuang, and Lanxi.","After dozens of trips carrying the supplies, they placed the prepared explosives into a circular groove halfway up the cliff face. A fuse, hundreds of meters long and wrapped in waterproof oiled paper, was dragged all the way down to the foot of the mountain.","Once everything was ready, Lanxi used a fire starter to light the end of the fuse, and the four quickly mounted their horses and galloped away.","About the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, the first explosion erupted.","Shattered rocks flew in all directions, and even the ground trembled.","The startled horses bolted like mad. Song Qiming and the other two had to pull hard on their reins to avoid being thrown off.","Boom, boom, boom! A continuous barrage of explosions echoed between heaven and earth.","\"Run! It is an earthquake!\" The villagers living on the hillside stumbled and crawled out of their houses in a panic.","They crouched on the ground, faces full of terror, their lips pale and completely drained of color.","Suddenly, a bolt of lightning struck the peak of the mountain. Under the horrified gazes of the crowd, a massive boulder fell from halfway up the mountain, followed by a surging torrent of river water.","The next second, everything went pitch black. Thunder roared, and the heavy crash of falling objects made everyone shudder in fear.","Song Qiming lowered his telescope, turning his head to look at Song Jinzhao with a face full of excitement.","\"Sister, it worked!\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. Rainwater dripped from her bamboo hat onto the back of her hand. After the rush of adrenaline faded, the chill began to set in.","\"Let us go back immediately. Shi Simian will definitely come looking for you tomorrow.\"","\"Right.\" Song Qiming obediently turned his horse around, galloping through the night toward Suining City.","The misty rain shrouded the landscape; every breath drew in damp, heavy moisture.","Seeing the rain lighten, villagers living near Laogan Ditch, worried about their flooded fields, rushed out in their straw raincoats to check.","Someone suddenly let out a loud shout. Pointing at the turbulent river, he yelled to the figures behind him, \"There is water in the river! So much water!\"","Hearing this, the villagers who were clearing the ditches straightened their backs and looked toward the shouting man.","Seeing him jumping up and down with exaggerated expressions, they walked over with their axes over their shoulders, full of doubt.","\"With rain this heavy, it is normal for the river to have...\" His words trailed off. The villager stared at the churning waves and fell silent.","When he finally reacted, he stumbled back two steps, his eyes wide open, filled with disbelief.","\"Where did all this water come from?\"","He was answered only by silence.","Having already arrived at the government office to work, Shi Simian could not help but feel suspicious when Song Qiming failed to show up.","\"Why hasn't the Prefect arrived yet? It is already late in the morning.\"","Song Qiming was always the first to arrive; how could he be so late today?","A yamen runner guarding the labor camp outside the city rushed in in a hurry, his eyes bright and his face full of joy.","\"Lord Shi, Laogan Ditch is flowing! The river is full of water, so deep that a bamboo pole cannot even touch the bottom!\"","Shi Simian, who had been sitting in his chair, stood up abruptly. \"How is that possible? It has only been raining for two days.\"","The runner shook his head. \"It is not rainwater, it is flowing water, like it came down from upstream.\"","\"Last night, there was a faint earthquake in the direction of Suiyu Mountain. It is possible the mountain collapsed.\"","Shi Simian was so shocked he spaced out, muttering to himself repeatedly, \"The mountain collapsed... the mountain collapsed.\"","His mind was buzzing. Seeing that his complexion was off, a clerk hurried over and helped him sit back down in his chair.","\"My Lord, this is a good thing. You must take care of your health.\"","Shi Simian blinked, and his unfocused eyes sharpened once again.","He stood up abruptly and ordered the runner, \"Take your men upstream immediately to investigate and see exactly what happened.\"","As he spoke, he bypassed his desk and walked out, passing through the second hall and stopping at the entrance to the inner residence.","\"Why hasn't the Prefect come to work today? I have urgent matters to report.\""]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467: That Is the Heavenly Eye Split Open by a Celestial's Thunderbolt","paragraphs":["When Shi Simian was invited into the room, Song Qiming was leaning against the bed frame, his face pale.","His anxious expression instantly retracted. \"My Lord, what is the matter?\" He looked as though he had fallen ill.","Yao Ye removed the warm handkerchief and replaced it with a cold one.","Song Qiming furrowed his brows in discomfort. \"I just caught a chill and have a bit of a fever. Does Lord Shi have urgent business?\"","No one expected that after returning late last night, Song Qiming would start running a fever. He had only slept for a few hours after taking his medicine, and his head was still spinning.","Hearing that Song Qiming was ill, Shi Simian instantly regretted coming.","Lowering his voice, he curled his lips into a flattering smile.","\"I have come to congratulate you, My Lord.\"","\"The bailiffs from outside the city just reported that the water in Laogan Ditch surged overnight. It is suspected that Suiyu Mountain has collapsed. I have already sent men to investigate.\"","\"If this is true, it is an auspicious sign from heaven. Even the heavens have been moved by Your Lordship's love for the people.\"","Knowing the truth, Song Qiming's mouth twitched. He had to clench his jaw to keep from laughing out loud.","He feigned shock, widening his eyes to confirm, \"Is this true? Could it just be rainwater?\"","Shi Simian shook his head firmly.","\"The bailiffs guarantee it is flowing water. There was a faint tremor from the direction of Suiyu Mountain last night. It must be river water flowing out from the Suiyu River.\"","Song Qiming blinked with a smile, looking up as if deeply moved. \"If the heavens truly took pity on us, it is a blessing for the people of Suining Prefecture.\"","A maid walked in from outside carrying a bowl of medicine.","Seeing this, Shi Simian stood up and bowed to Song Qiming. \"Please rest well, My Lord. I will take my leave now.\"","Song Qiming nodded gently. Only after Shi Simian left did the expression on his face finally relax.","He picked up the medicine bowl and downed it in one gulp, the bitterness making the back of his tongue go numb.","Song Jinzhao, who had been listening to the commotion from the next room, walked over. Seeing his pained expression, she couldn't help but scold him.","\"I told you to drink the ginger soup and you refused. Now you're the one suffering from illness. Is it bitter?\"","Song Qiming quickly stuffed a candied date into his mouth and said pitifully, \"I was going to drink it, but I fell asleep while waiting for it to cool. I was just too tired.\"","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips and shook her head.","The round trip last night was indeed exhausting. Coupled with the fact that he had been so busy these past few days that his feet barely touched the ground, it was normal for his body to give out.","He needed some nourishment.","\"Once you recover, I'll have the kitchen make some herbal dishes to build up your health. No matter what you do, you can't let your body fail you.\"","At the foot of Suiyu Mountain, the bailiff stared dumbfounded at the massive, perfectly round hole blasted into the cliff face.","Gushing river water poured out from within, and the drifting mist lingered around the area, making it look like a fairyland.","He muttered to himself, \"What in the world happened here? Could it truly be the descent of a deity?\"","Even if it were an earthquake, the entire mountain should have collapsed. But now, a hole had been carved out right in the middle, with rocks still connected at the top like an archway. It was simply unbelievable.","\"It was the God of Thunder and Goddess of Lightning who struck it with lightning,\" a commoner burning incense nearby while holding an umbrella said to the bailiff, his face full of awe for the heavens.","\"The God of Thunder and Goddess of Lightning?\" the bailiff asked in confusion.","The commoner nodded vigorously and pointed at the entrance of the hole, waving his arms.","\"In the middle of the night yesterday, the earth first shook and the mountains swayed. Suddenly, a beam of light struck the mountain, and thunder resounded through the skies. That was heavenly lightning.\"","\"The Jade Emperor must have seen how difficult it was for the government to excavate the mountain, so he ordered the God of Thunder and Goddess of Lightning to send down heavenly lightning to help. This hole is the Eye of Heaven. The immortals in the sky look down upon us through this.\"","Watching the commoners kneeling, burning incense, and kowtowing, the bailiff looked thoughtfully toward the hole.","It felt as though a pair of eyes were truly watching from the gray sky. He abruptly lowered his head, not daring to look directly at it.","It seemed to make sense. Otherwise, with so many mountains around, why would lightning strike the exact one they needed to dig through?","As the smell of incense in his nose grew stronger, the more the bailiff thought about it, the more convinced he became that it was the work of immortals. He immediately mounted his horse and galloped back."]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468: Breeding High-Quality Rice Seeds","paragraphs":["Shi Simian rushed to report to Song Qiming the moment he received the news, a huge smile beaming on his face.","\"Heaven has blessed Suining Prefecture. We no longer need to dig through the mountain.\"","A century-long project was finished by a single rainstorm. If they had known they would receive Heaven's blessing, they should have started digging much earlier.","Song Qiming, who had recovered about eighty percent of his strength, sat behind his desk and gave a faint, nodding smile.","\"This is excellent. Set up an altar at the West Gate tomorrow; I shall formally offer my gratitude to Heaven.\"","He needed to solidify this narrative so that everyone would believe it was the Heavens that blasted the mountain. He would also need to write a memorial to the capital; pleasing the Emperor would be a great political achievement.","An hour before the thanksgiving ceremony, rumors of deities descending to the mortal realm to help the government cleave the mountain had already spread among the commoners of Suining City.","Seeing the offering table set up at the West Gate, laden with sacrificial items and guarded by yamen runners, the crowd immediately broke into animated discussions.","The news seemed to grow wings. By the time Song Qiming arrived in his official robes, the street leading to the West Gate was packed tightly with onlookers. Had the runners not cleared a path in advance, he wouldn't have been able to get through.","Welcoming the deities, the first offering, reading the prayer, the final offering, and sending off the deities.","Just as they were waiting for the prayer scrolls and silk to burn to ashes, a ray of rosy sunlight suddenly pierced through the dark clouds and landed right on Song Qiming's face. Bathed in the glow, the young man's features were unexpectedly imbued with a touch of divine majesty.","Someone in the crowd shouted, \"An auspicious sign from Heaven!\" Instantly, the surrounding commoners fell to their knees and kowtowed.","\"The Heavens have shown their power! This is the light of merit bestowed upon our righteous magistrate by the gods!\"","\"The Prefect's sincerity has moved the Heavens. Those are the auspicious clouds of the Ninth Heaven!\"","\"...\"","Standing on the platform, Song Qiming listened to the praises from below and looked up, slightly flustered, toward Song Jinzhao, who was standing on the second floor of a nearby tavern.","He swallowed nervously, but gradually calmed down upon meeting her smiling eyes.","By the window of the tavern, Song Shixue tilted her head and leaned close to Song Jinzhao's face.","Covering her mouth, she whispered, \"Sister, how did you know there would be a sunbeam at this exact moment?\"","And for it to land perfectly on their brother's face—it was just too much of a coincidence.","Song Jinzhao looked at the parting clouds in the sky and smiled softly.","\"I didn't expect it to be such a perfect coincidence either. The sky cleared up and the rosy clouds actually appeared.\"","Judging from the commoners' reactions, Qiming's prestige in the hearts of the Suining people would skyrocket after today. This was a wonderful thing for them.","With the water issue resolved, by the time the autumn harvest arrived, Song Jinzhao took Song Qiming down to the fields.","The rice stalks were already bent heavy with plump grains.","Walking along the ridges of the fields, Song Jinzhao observed every inch of the rice paddies with absolute concentration.","\"If we want to cultivate high-yield, premium seeds, the first step is selecting the best ears of grain right here in the fields.\"","Walking beside her, Song Qiming took notes on paper with a quill, his gaze shifting between Jinzhao's face and the direction she was pointing.","Song Jinzhao continued, \"A truly superior rice plant often stands out from the rest. You might only find one in tens of thousands, so you must be extremely meticulous.\"","Song Qiming nodded and jotted it down. \"One in ten thousand. That's a massive undertaking.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"Once I find one, you can instruct the others to do the same using my method. We shouldn't limit this to the government-reclaimed fields; we need to mobilize the commoners to inspect their own land as well. The more premium seeds we find, the better. That way, our cultivation efforts next year will be much more efficient.\"","Song Qiming made another note in his ledger. \"When the time comes, I'll have the runners go village by village to spread the word. If we add a bounty, it should speed things up.\"","\"My Lord—!\"","The rapid thundering of hooves approached from behind. Liu Hucheng hastily dismounted and sprinted wildly toward Song Qiming.","His face was fraught with anxiety, looking as though something major had just happened."]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469: Trouble at the Door: Yang Ce'nan, the Third Son of the Yang Family","paragraphs":["\"My Lord, terrible news! The Deputy Magistrate of Qingxia County sent a messenger. Yang Cenan, the third son of Panzhou's Pacification Commissioner Yang Ruiping, was severely injured after being assassinated in the Wumeng Tribe's territory. He is already on his way to Suining City and specifically asked for the County Princess. Lord Shi urges you and the Princess to return immediately.\"","Sweating profusely, Liu Hucheng rested his hands on his knees, his voice hoarse. He tilted his chin up, his anxious gaze darting between Song Qiming and Song Jinzhao.","Song Qiming turned around in astonishment. \"This is rather strange. Why would someone from Panzhou think to come all the way to Suining City to seek medical treatment from you?\"","Leaving aside the fact that the southwestern foreign tribes were inherently wary of imperial officials, they shouldn't have put such absolute faith in his sister's reputation as a miracle doctor either.","Song Jinzhao released the ear of rice in her hand. The aura around her settled into something heavy, her eyes calm yet serious.","\"Where is he now?\"","\"Did the messenger mention the extent of his injuries?\"","Liu Hucheng struggled to straighten his back.","\"They are traveling by carriage and should reach the city in about six hours.\"","\"The yamen runner who delivered the letter said Yang Cenan was struck by three arrows and stabbed in the stomach. All the doctors in Qingxia County were helpless, which is why they thought to seek the Princess to save his life.\"","Rushing to the city gates without a moment's delay to wait, Song Jinzhao instructed Qingshuang, \"Tell the Second Miss to get ready. The moment he arrives, send him directly to the clinic.\"","Compared to the government office, the clinic run by Song Shixue had a more complete stock of medicines and was closer and more convenient.","Song Qiming furrowed his brows, his heart filled with worry.","He was injured so severely; who knew if he could even be cured?","Although Yang Cenan was assassinated within the Wumeng Tribe's territory, if he died in Suining City and Yang Ruiping decided to vent his anger on them, it would be a massive headache.","Why didn't Lan Wenzhang know how to push this matter away? This was simply an unmitigated disaster falling from the sky.","He could only hope the injuries were on the lighter side and that his sister could treat them.","Two hours later, the carriage appeared before everyone's eyes.","The carriage curtain was lifted, and the first to emerge was a white-haired old doctor.","Song Jinzhao's nostrils flared slightly; she could smell a thick stench of blood.","Lan Wenzhang, the Deputy Magistrate of Qingxia County, dismounted with an anxious face and hurried over to Song Qiming as if grasping at a lifesaver.","\"My Lord, Yang Cenan absolutely cannot die.\"","Song Qiming rolled his eyes at him right then and there.","His angry voice was softer than a mosquito's buzz. \"If you know he can't die, why did you bring him here? Was your brain eaten by dogs?!\"","Lan Wenzhang hastily defended himself, looking incredibly wronged.","\"This humble official didn't want to either, but Yang Cenan insisted on finding the Princess, even threatening war. I truly couldn't stop him.\"","Song Jinzhao climbed into the carriage. The man lying inside had already fallen into a coma.","While ordering the driver to head to Song Shixue's clinic, she questioned the elderly doctor.","\"When did the patient lose consciousness?\"","Lifting the thin quilt covering the man, Song Jinzhao discovered that two arrowheads had not been removed. They were in a precarious position, and the area around the gauze was still bleeding.","The doctor nervously wiped the beads of sweat from his forehead.","Rushing like this at his advanced age left him breathless and nauseous.","\"Starting this morning, the patient gradually became delirious. I used ginseng slices to sustain his life and applied acupuncture every hour. His condition worsened four hours ago, and he hasn't woken up since.\"","The carriage soon stopped at the entrance of the clinic, and the man was carefully placed onto a stretcher.","Heye was just about to close the door when a dark, tanned hand stopped her.","Yang Zhong looked at Heye with a vigilant expression and said, \"Don't close the door. I'm going in to guard my young master.\"","He was Yang Cenan's personal bodyguard; the two had grown up together.","Heye scanned the dried bloodstains on his clothes, her brows twisting into a tight knot.","She scolded, \"You're so dirty. What if you cause an infection?\"","\"The surgery requires silence. You going in will only delay his treatment.\"","Yang Zhong immediately reached to unfasten his robes. \"I can take off my clothes. I can't be at ease with only you people here.\"","Heye's face instantly darkened.","\"If you're not at ease, then take him away. It's not as if I, the Princess, am obligated to treat him.\"","Having already put on her protective surgical gown, Song Jinzhao came to the door.","Realizing he had spoken out of turn, Yang Zhong immediately regretted it. He took a step back and bowed his head in apology to Song Jinzhao.","\"This lowly one was overly worried and spoke rudely. Please forgive me, Princess Linghui. I entrust my young master's life to you, Princess.\"","Right now, he had no other choice but Princess Linghui.","Song Jinzhao turned and returned to the hospital bed. Heye closed the door and slid the wooden bolt into place.","She had a nagging feeling that the man might barge in. If he saw the bloody scene of a body being cut open and impulsively tried to interfere, it would be disastrous."]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470: Afraid He Won't Wake Up and Discover Huo Chong","paragraphs":["The arrowhead, covered in bits of shredded flesh, was extracted and placed on the tray. Song Jinzhao was sweating profusely, but her hand movements were quick and steady.","Beside her, Song Shixue kept a close eye on the trembling silver needles, ready to step in and stop the bleeding the moment the blood flow increased.","Knowing that the person on the bed had a remarkable identity, the two assisting medicine boys by the bed held their breath, not daring to make a single sound for fear of disturbing Song Jinzhao.","Outside the room, unable to see Yang Cenan, Yang Zhong was already jumping with anxiety. He paced back and forth at the door, causing Song Qiming and the others to glance over frequently.","\"Why isn't there any sound? Pulling out an arrow should make him cry out in pain.\"","The smell of blood mixed with the sour stench of sweat was so foul it was nauseating.","The man suddenly rushed over, stirring up a gust of wind. Song Qiming subconsciously held his breath, his lips pressed into a thin line.","\"I don't know much about medical matters, but as long as they haven't come out, it means he is still alive. If he were dead, my sister would open the door and announce it.\"","Saliva blocked his throat; he couldn't swallow it down or spit it out.","Yang Zhong hesitated to speak, almost grinding his back teeth to pieces.","Their tongues were more venomous than the last—no wonder they were siblings.","Lan Wenzhang's heart raced, and his legs grew weak.","He clenched his fists and leaned closer to Shi Simian. \"Lord Shi, isn't the Prefect's attitude a bit inappropriate?\"","Shi Simian was equally resentful of this county deputy who had brought trouble to their doorstep.","\"Do you think everyone is as cowardly as you when facing the southwestern alien tribes? The Prefect has always been upright and unyielding; that man is just a personal servant.\"","Belittled, Lan Wenzhang said nothing, but secretly rolled his eyes at Shi Simian.","He cursed in his heart: Birds of a feather, yet he has the nerve to say such things. Shameless.","The door was opened from the inside. Seeing Song Jinzhao come out wearing a mask, Yang Zhong's heart skipped a beat. Could Song Qiming have been right?","He rushed up urgently to question Song Jinzhao, his lips trembling and his heart filled with terror.","\"How is my young master?\" he asked, about to barge into the room.","Song Jinzhao reached out to stop him, her tone low and serious.","\"The arrowhead has been removed, but he is too heavily injured. We will have to see if he can survive the night.\"","Yang Zhong's mind went blank. His expression shifted rapidly before he finally grabbed Song Jinzhao's arm and pleaded, \"I beg the County Princess to save my young master's life. The madam and the young lord are already dead; nothing can happen to the young master.\"","Song Jinzhao broke free from his grip. Seeing that he was on the verge of tears, the frustration in her heart involuntarily dissipated.","Softening her tone, she said, \"This County Princess will naturally do my best.\"","\"They are wrapping things up inside. There shouldn't be too many people. Clean yourself up first before you go in.\"","Yang Zhong didn't dare to leave but desperately wanted to go inside. Spotting a water well in the courtyard, he quickly ordered his subordinates to go buy some clean clothes.","Song Jinzhao took a deep breath and walked over to stand under the eaves outside the clinic. Song Qiming followed her and lowered his voice.","\"Sister, what are the chances that Yang Cenan will survive the night?\"","Just as Song Jinzhao was about to speak, she spotted a familiar face across the street.","As if startled, the person darted into the crowd and disappeared the next second.","Why would Huo Chong appear in Suining City?","\"Sister?\" Song Qiming asked in confusion.","Song Jinzhao withdrew her gaze.","\"Seventy percent. But he has lost too much blood and has been unconscious for so long. I'm afraid that even if he survives, he might not wake up.\"","Song Qiming stared blankly, his mouth agape. Disbelievingly, he asked, \"A living corpse?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"That is the worst-case scenario.\"","\"He just mentioned a madam and a young lord. Are they Yang Cenan's wife and son?\"","Song Qiming nodded with a dark expression.","\"They were assassinated alongside Yang Cenan and died on the spot.\"","\"Out of a party of thirty, only the four in that room survived.\"","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes. Thinking of Huo Chong's appearance in Suining City, could it be that Ningzhou was behind this?"]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471: Stayed up all night and hadn't woken up yet, Huo Chong reappeared","paragraphs":["\"Guard the clinic strictly. Tonight, no one is allowed to enter except our own people,\" Song Jinzhao instructed Song Qiming in a deep voice.","Song Qiming asked, \"Sister, do you think those assassins will come to Suining City?\"","Song Jinzhao whispered into Song Qiming's ear, \"Huo Chong was right across the street just now. They might have already infiltrated the city.\"","Song Qiming's expression drastically changed. The hairs on his body stood on end as he vigilantly scanned their surroundings.","\"They targeted Yang Cenan. Are they trying to start a war again?\"","The imperial court had only just finished mediating. If it happened again, the entire Southwest Province would be plunged into unrest.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Being assassinated in Suining City is far more serious than dying of illness. Besides the yamen runners, I'll have Lan Xi lead a few guards to lie in ambush nearby.\"","After changing clothes and returning to the clinic, the yamen runners were already in position at the entrance.","Yang Zhong and the others had no objections to this; they were also afraid that the assassins would come back to finish the job if they found out Yang Cenan was still alive.","For safety's sake, Song Shixue had Heye hang a wooden sign indicating the clinic was closed at the door, and the main gate was half-closed.","Song Qiming brought Lan Wenzhang to the government office for a detailed interrogation.","\"How did they find you?\"","\"Did you encounter any more assassins on your way to Suining City?\"","Lan Wenzhang furrowed his brows in distress, feeling extremely frustrated.","\"I also find it baffling. You must know that the foreign tribes of the Southwest have never paid any attention to us, and we have absolutely no dealings with the Yang family of Panzhou.\"","\"But yesterday at noon, Yang Cenan suddenly arrived at the county office seeking help. Before falling unconscious, he specifically asked for the County Princess. With a blade at my neck, I had no choice but to bring him here.\"","\"Worried about further pursuit from assassins, I brought a hundred yamen runners. Fortunately, the journey here was relatively peaceful, and we didn't encounter any assassins.\"","Throughout the entire night, Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue stayed at the clinic, taking turns to keep watch and checking on him every half hour.","Whenever a high fever spiked, it was quickly brought down. The wound felt burning hot, and his body convulsed and trembled unconsciously. They even had to administer anesthesia twice during the process.","After enduring a chaotic and exhausting night, everyone was physically and mentally drained by daybreak.","Looking at Song Shixue, who was constantly yawning, Song Jinzhao said tenderly, \"Go back and get some sleep first. Now we just have to wait for him to wake up.\"","Song Shixue covered her mouth with her hand, her eyes barely able to stay open.","\"Sister, I'm not that sleepy. You go back, I'll stay here.\"","Song Jinzhao wiped away a tear at the corner of her eye.","\"Your eyes are watering and you still say you're not sleepy. Be good.\"","Song Shixue's head felt heavy, and she let out another yawn. \"Then I'll bring lunch over at noon.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded and watched her leave.","For the next four hours, Yang Cenan remained unconscious.","Seeing Song Jinzhao come in to check on him, Yang Zhong, who was sitting on the floor, looked up and asked, his eyes completely bloodshot.","\"County Princess, when will my young master wake up?\"","After taking his pulse, Song Jinzhao gently pulled back Yang Cenan's eyelids to examine his pupils.","\"The patient has been unconscious for too long and lost a lot of blood. The lack of blood and oxygen to his brain has definitely caused some damage.\"","Seeing Yang Zhong's expression freeze, Song Jinzhao shifted her tone.","\"However, the patient has a strong physique. From the looks of it, the chances of him waking up are still very high. We just need to wait a little longer.\"","He should wake up, but whether there would be any lingering aftereffects was unknown.","In the house across from the clinic, Lan Xi stared through the window at that familiar face for a full quarter of an hour.","Seeing him leave, he instructed the guard waiting nearby, \"Follow him quietly, don't be discovered.\"","\"Yes.\"","The guard, dressed in extremely ordinary gray cloth garments, walked out. It was a style worn by three out of every ten people on the street.","Lan Xi calmly walked into the clinic. After finding Song Jinzhao, the two went to the small room used for brewing medicine.","\"Huo Chong was watching from outside for a quarter of an hour just now, and then he left.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Was there anyone else?\"","Lan Xi shook his head. \"Only him. I have already sent someone to follow him.\"","Placing the herbal medicine into the pot to soak, Song Jinzhao's voice sounded very calm.","\"Just keep an eye on him, don't make a move. Offending either side won't do us any good.\"","Lan Xi bowed his head. \"Understood.\""]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472: Sequela","paragraphs":["Not long after, the guard dispatched by Lan Xi returned to report in a low voice, \"That man is staying at the Mingyuan Inn, and he is entirely alone.\"","Lan Xi lowered her eyes and instructed, \"Keep a close watch on him, but do not alert him.\"","The guard nodded, turned around, and went back to continue tailing him.","An hour later, Song Shixue brought over some food. Just as she opened the food box, Yang Zhong rushed out of the sickroom.","His eyes were filled with excitement and his voice was pitched high. \"County Princess, my young master has awakened! Please come quickly and take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao immediately set down her chopsticks and went inside to examine him.","In the quiet sickroom, the breathing of Yang Zhong and the other two guards sounded exceptionally heavy.","Their eyes were fixed intently on Yang Cenan, terrified that something else might happen to him.","\"Who... are you? Why... am I here?\"","Yang Cenan looked at Song Jinzhao with a bewildered expression. As he spoke, the opening and closing of his mouth seemed somewhat sluggish.","Yang Zhong shuffled forward on his knees, leaning his head close with a relieved smile on his face.","\"This is County Princess Linghui.\"","\"Young Master, we are currently in Suining City. This is a medical clinic.\"","To his surprise, upon hearing this, Yang Cenan's eyes grew even more confused.","\"County Princess... Linghui? Aren't we... on our way to the Wumeng Tribe?\"","\"How did I get injured? My head hurts, too.\"","Watching his lips twitch uncontrollably, Song Jinzhao's heart skipped a beat.","Song Shixue bit her lower lip and gently nudged Song Jinzhao's hand.","Sister, something seems wrong.","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod of her chin.","Suspected memory loss, likely an aftereffect of brain damage.","His facial muscle responses were also off; they looked a bit stiff.","Unaware of the problem yet, Yang Zhong blurted out, \"Young Master, don't you remember? We were assassinated by killers at the Caishi Beach. It has already been several days since then.\"","Yang Cenan slowly narrowed his eyes, saliva continuously dribbling from the corner of his mouth and smearing across his face.","\"Assassination? Why don't I remember?\"","\"Where are my wife and Wei'er?\"","Wei'er was Yang Cenan's son, who was only five years old.","The expression on Yang Zhong's face suddenly froze. He stiffly turned his neck to look at Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, what is wrong with my young master?\"","No matter how excited he was, he knew that Yang Cenan's current condition was not right.","His wife and the young master were already dead. How could his master forget such an important thing!","Song Jinzhao extended her index finger. \"Look at my hand. Don't move your head, only move your eyes.\"","The physical pain made Yang Cenan subconsciously obey Song Jinzhao's words.","Her finger slowly moved from side to side, but his gaze always lagged a few seconds behind.","Song Jinzhao: \"Raise your hand.\"","\"Wiggle your toes.\"","\"What is your most recent memory?\"","After a series of checks, Song Jinzhao spoke frankly: \"Temporary memory loss, facial muscle stiffness, and delayed reactions. These are all aftereffects caused by brain damage. It is basically impossible to cure him completely.\"","It took a long time for Yang Cenan to process this. Before he could even open his mouth, Yang Zhong grew frantic.","His eyes went wide, and his lips trembled as he pressed, \"What do you mean? Will my young master always be like this?\"","Delayed reactions—this was a massive problem!","Song Jinzhao replied in a somber tone, \"Temporary memory loss can slowly be recovered, but nerve damage is often irreversible.\"","\"Through follow-up treatment, he can achieve a certain degree of recovery and improvement, but the chances of a complete cure are slim. I cannot say for sure exactly how much he will recover.\"","Yang Zhong slumped weakly to the ground on his knees, his mind going completely blank.","After Song Qiming arrived, Song Jinzhao informed him of Yang Cenan's condition. Lan Wenzhang, who was following behind, clutched his chest and relaxed.","\"As long as he is alive, that is all that matters. Whatever happens afterward has nothing to do with us anyway.\"","The gazes of the others fell upon Lan Wenzhang's face, all of them rendered speechless.","Could he not keep such offensive words to himself?","Saying it so openly, he was not even afraid that the people in the sickroom would hear him.","Song Qiming's face darkened as he reprimanded him, \"Disaster stems from the mouth. Speak with caution.\"","The smile on Lan Wenzhang's face froze instantly. As it receded like the tide, he lowered his head in fear, his voice laced with apprehension.","\"This humble official misspoke.\"","Song Qiming turned his head back and stopped looking at him.","Lan Wenzhang temporarily acting as the magistrate of Qingxia County was absolutely not a long-term solution. He had to urge for a replacement.","He would write a memorial to the throne as soon as he went back tonight."]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473: The Unexpected Visit of Aunt and Nephew","paragraphs":["After Yang Zhong told Yang Cenan about his lost memories, the tall man, standing at one meter eighty-five, lay on the bed and silently shed tears for two hours.","When Song Shixue went in to check on him, she could hardly bear to see him like that.","Losing his wife and child, and being reduced to this state himself—ordinary people would find it impossible to accept.","After confirming that Yang Cenan was out of danger, Song Qiming sent Hai Wenzhang back.","\"The county office cannot be left unattended. There will definitely be movements from Panzhou. Take your people and head back first.\"","Hai Wenzhang was more than eager to leave early. He departed the morning after their conversation.","At the city gates, Shi Simian smiled and shook his head as he watched them leave.","\"He is too short-sighted. No wonder the imperial court preferred to send a new county magistrate rather than promote him. He is truly unfit for great responsibilities.\"","Irresponsible and unwilling to bear the blame—superiors would never like such a subordinate, nor would they ever entrust him with important tasks.","At the riverbank intersection outside Suining City, Gu Baozhu raised her eyebrows in confusion as she watched the massive procession of yamen runners leaving.","\"Looking at their clothes, they seem to be yamen runners from Qingxia County.\"","Gu Jinghong nodded.","\"They are indeed from Qingxia County. What are they doing here? And with so many people.\"","This place was only thirty miles away from Suining City; the appearance of people from Qingxia County was already very strange.","Gu Baozhu raised her hand to shield her eyes from the sun and gazed at the golden rice fields in the distance.","\"With so many fields, the grain yield must be substantial. They shouldn't need subsidies this year.\"","Gu Jinghong's eyes curved in amusement, and she couldn't help but laugh out loud.","In past years, whenever winter approached, the prefect of Suining would go to Songzhou City to play the victim and beg for financial aid. Gu Zhongxun had complained about this at home more than once, and the aunt and niece had heard it several times.","\"We haven't encountered a single petty thief along the way. That would be impossible even in Songzhou City.\"","\"Setting up guard posts along the road for day and night patrols—Song Qiming not only thought of it, but he actually did it.\"","\"We've also met quite a few merchants on the road. To bring about such a huge change in just half a year, Song Qiming is truly not a simple man.\"","...","At the entrance of the prefectural office, Gu Jinghong, who was visiting Song Jinzhao, exclaimed loudly.","\"What! The third son of the Panzhou Pacification Commissioner is in Suining City?\"","Liu Hucheng frantically pressed his palms down, gesturing for Gu Jinghong to lower her voice.","\"When he was brought over the afternoon before yesterday, he had only one breath left. The Princess and the Second Miss Song barely managed to save his life.\"","He sighed, \"His life is saved, but his brain suffered a severe injury. He is still in Second Miss Song's medical clinic.\"","The aunt and niece exchanged a glance and immediately pulled Liu Hucheng along to lead the way to the clinic.","It wasn't until they saw a row of sword-bearing yamen runners standing at the entrance of the clinic that the two completely believed it.","\"Headman Liu, who are these two?\" The yamen runner looked vigilant.","Gu Baozhu excitedly waved her arm at the person inside the house, \"Shixue.\"","\"Miss Gu!\" Song Shixue handed the tray in her hands to Heye and walked out the door to greet them.","\"Why are you here?\"","Gu Baozhu broke into a wide smile and explained, \"It was getting boring staying in Songzhou City, so we thought we'd come over for a few days of fun.\"","Gu Jinghong took a step forward to confirm, \"Is Yang Cenan inside?\"","Song Shixue gave a slight nod. \"He's lying in the ward in the back.\"","\"You came at a bad time. I'm afraid my sister and I won't have time to show you around these few days.\"","Gu Baozhu waved her hand casually. \"It doesn't matter. Stumbling upon Yang Cenan's assassination attempt makes this trip worthwhile for us.\"","\"Can we go in and take a look?\"","Song Shixue pressed her lips tightly together and shook her head.","\"Since waking up, the patient has been consistently depressed and silent. It's better not to see him.\"","\"I heard his brain was injured?\"","Gu Jinghong stretched her neck to look inside, and her eyes happened to meet those of Song Jinzhao, who was walking out, followed by Song Qiming.","\"Greetings, Princess Linghui. Lord Song, long time no see.\"","Song Qiming turned his head to glance at the closed door, walked over, and lowered his voice.","\"This is not the place to talk. Let's go back to the prefectural office first.\"","Song Jinzhao instructed Song Shixue, \"Do not enter the ward unless necessary. Just let the people from Panzhou stay inside.\"","When changing the dressing just now, the atmosphere was so heavy that it was hard to breathe. Such a massive blow definitely requires time to process, and it is inappropriate for outsiders to be present.","Song Shixue nodded in agreement.","\"Don't worry, Sister. I'll have Heye go in to deliver the meals, and I absolutely won't say a single extra word.\"","Since waking up, Yang Cenan's eyes had remained swollen, and she didn't want to stay in there watching a grown man cry either."]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474: Someone from Panzhou","paragraphs":["After dismounting and leading them into the government office, Song Qiming began asking questions the moment he sat down.","\"The memorial was just sent off yesterday, and you're already here. Did Lord Gu have some important instructions?\"","\"Huh?\" The aunt and nephew looked bewildered.","What memorial?","Realizing what he meant, Gu Baozhu quickly explained, \"Jinghong and I have been traveling leisurely from Songzhou City for the past few days, enjoying the scenery. We don't know anything about a memorial.\"","Song Qiming replied, \"I see. I thought you had traveled day and night to get here.\"","It seemed Gu Zhongxun's reply to the memorial would likely arrive in a few days.","As the food was set on the table, Gu Jinghong slowly chewed his rice and pressed Song Qiming with a question.","\"How severe is Yang Cenan's brain injury? Yang Ruiping values this son the most; he is the next patriarch of the Yang clan of Panzhou.\"","A meatball dropped onto the table as Song Jinzhao raised her eyes to stare at Gu Jinghong.","\"Is that confirmed, or just a rumor?\"","Gu Jinghong hesitated for a long moment before answering, \"It's not officially confirmed yet, but compared to his other two sons, Yang Cenan is highly regarded by Yang Ruiping.\"","The sister and brother both fell silent.","No wonder Huo Chong targeted Yang Cenan. It turned out he was the next heir.","Seeing the two remain silent for so long, Gu Jinghong's curiosity was thoroughly piqued.","He slapped his knee and urged Song Qiming, \"Lord Song, just how badly is he injured? Can he be cured?\"","Song Qiming turned his gaze toward Song Jinzhao.","To what extent he could be cured still depended on his older sister.","Song Jinzhao slowly and methodically picked up a piece of cabbage heart with her chopsticks and placed it in her bowl.","\"The superficial wounds will heal in a month, but the chances of completely curing the lingering effects of his brain injury are very slim. It will definitely affect him to some degree in the future.\"","Stiff facial muscles could be passed off as a cold, stoic expression, but a sluggish reaction time wouldn't be so easy to cover up.","Setting aside whether Yang Ruiping would mind, his other two brothers would certainly seize upon this flaw and make a huge deal out of it.","As rumors spread, even the smallest issue would be exaggerated into a massive problem.","His position as the heir would be in jeopardy.","A flurry of hurried footsteps came from outside. Shi Simian unfortunately tripped over the threshold and fell to the ground with a heavy thud.","Grimacing in pain, he scrambled up, hurried over to Song Qiming, and cupped his hands to report.","\"My Lord, the guards at the city gate have reported that Zeng Boyan, a Flying Cavalry Commandant under the Pacification Commissioner of Panzhou, has arrived outside the city with thirty armored cavalrymen. He says he wants to enter the city to find Yang Cenan.\"","Song Qiming abruptly stood up, his brows furrowed tightly.","\"Have they been let in?\"","Shi Simian shook his head. \"Not yet. They are all carrying weapons, so the guards didn't dare let them through and stopped them.\"","Song Qiming took a deep breath. \"Have Yang Zhong go over to identify them, and dispatch another fifty guards from the government office to the gate.\"","Before his words could even fade, Song Qiming suddenly moved to stand again.","\"No, I need to go see for myself.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Have Lanxi go guard the clinic. Don't let Shixue be in any danger.\"","Song Qiming nodded and walked briskly outside. The aunt and nephew sitting opposite them quickly got up and followed.","\"County Princess, we will go take a look too.\"","Their voices trailed off and drifted away with the wind. Song Jinzhao also lost her appetite.","\"Is Zeng Qing's son named Zeng Boyan?\"","Qingshuang nodded and answered, \"I believe that is his name.\"","Leaning back against her chair, Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes and asked, \"Have Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan been behaving themselves lately?\"","A faint smile appeared on Qingshuang's lips.","\"Qu Ya works quietly and rarely interacts with others. Guan Nianshan has a more active personality, and his son has been performing very well at the academy. This servant feels we can put him to use first.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up her chopsticks again.","\"There are Panzhou troops in the city. Take two extra guards with you when you go out tomorrow, and have Guan Nianshan follow along.\"","Whether he could be useful or not, they had to try. Now that Huo Chong was in Suining City, it was about time they met."]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475: Zeng Boyan, Yang Cenan on the Verge of Collapse","paragraphs":["Outside the inner city gates, looking at the tall and straight cavalrymen, Song Qiming could not help but hold his breath.","These thirty men looked like elites.","The gaze of a middle-aged man among them met Song Qiming's.","His bronzed face was marked with scars from old, healed wounds, making him look battle-hardened.","Seeing Shi Simian standing behind Song Qiming, Zeng Boyan threw his reins to a subordinate and stepped forward himself.","\"Your subordinate, Cavalry Commandant Zeng Boyan, pays his respects to the Lord Prefect.\"","He bowed his head and cupped his hands without the slightest hint of disrespect, arousing the suspicion of the aunt and nephew standing behind.","Gu Baozhu covered her mouth and whispered, \"This general from Panzhou seems to have a pretty good attitude.\"","Gu Jinghong lowered his voice even more.","\"A Cavalry Commandant is a lower seventh-rank official, but the soldiers he brought do not look like those a seventh-rank official could command.\"","Facing Zeng Boyan's greeting, Song Qiming gave a slight nod, his back straight.","\"General Zeng, are you here for Third Young Master Yang?\"","A faint smile curled the corners of Zeng Boyan's lips.","However, his facial features were harsh, and his face was somewhat rectangular. His smile was not gentle; instead, it gave off a mocking, superficial feeling.","\"On the way, I happened to meet Lord Hai, the Deputy Magistrate of Qingxia County, and heard that the Third Young Master is out of danger. I am here to thank Prefect Song and County Princess Linghui for saving his life.\"","Yang Zhong ran over rapidly. The moment he saw Zeng Boyan, a long-lost smile appeared on his face.","\"General Zeng, you are finally here.\" His voice choked with emotion; it would not be an exaggeration to say his eyes were brimming with tears.","Zeng Boyan hurriedly asked, \"Is the Third Young Master doing well?\"","Yang Zhong lowered his eyes and sighed.","\"Not very well. I will take you to him right away. The young master really wants to see you.\"","He only hoped that the news from Panzhou could cheer the young master up. How could his body recover if he stayed like this?","Seeing how familiar the two were with each other, Song Qiming could not help but mutter in his heart.","He did not look like Yang Ruiping's man, but rather Yang Cenan's.","Thirty horses parked at the entrance of the clinic made it very crowded, causing none of the commoners on the entire street to dare approach.","Armored cavalrymen who were not from the prefectural office, with so many yamen runners standing guard nearby.","Their expressions were exceptionally serious; it all felt very dangerous.","At the door of the ward, Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong were peeking inside.","\"Why do I feel like Yang Cenan is about to die?\"","Pressing her body against the wall, Gu Baozhu craned her neck so far it seemed like it could stretch for miles.","Gu Jinghong said, \"This is a sickness of the heart. He will not recover anytime soon.\"","He had happily taken his wife and child back to her maiden home, and suddenly both of them were dead.","His own injuries could not be cured either. Being slow to react meant, to put it bluntly, that there was a problem with his brain. How could he not be devastated?","Song Qiming did not stay inside for long before coming out.","The door was closed by Yang Zhong. Standing in the front hall, Song Qiming looked outside.","The thirty men stood motionless beside their horses, looking straight ahead with perfectly straight backs.","\"Brother Gu, are all the soldiers in Panzhou like these men outside?\"","Gu Jinghong furrowed his brows tightly and shook his head.","\"When the Pan and Ning provinces were fighting, I secretly went to take a look. Their military discipline and prestige were much worse than theirs; they were completely different.\"","In the ward, the prefectural doctor brought by Zeng Boyan was kneeling by the bed, taking Yang Cenan's pulse.","\"The knife and arrow wounds on the young master's body are healing well, but his pulse is heavy and weak.\"","\"A deficiency of qi and blood should be carefully nourished, but now his internal organs are knotted with sorrow, which is truly unhelpful for healing. He still needs to pull himself together.\"","Yang Cenan stared fixedly at the doctor, his gaze as gloomy as an undercurrent, as if he wanted to swallow the man whole.","\"My face feels stiff when I speak, and my reactions are slow when I think. Can I be completely cured?\"","The doctor nervously lowered his head, not daring to look at Yang Cenan.","\"There might be a blood clot in the brain. With careful recuperation, it should be alleviated a bit.\"","Hands trembling slightly slowly reached out from under the quilt.","Yang Cenan forcefully swept the medicinal soup on the bedside table onto the floor, throwing his upper body forward to grab the doctor's collar.","\"My head was not injured, so where would a blood clot come from?\"","\"What I want is a complete cure, not alleviation!\"","The agonized roar echoed in the room for a long time.","Watching Yang Cenan's red-eyed, maddened appearance, Zeng Boyan could not help but inwardly cry out that things were bad.","If he could not recover, this pawn would eventually be useless. He needed to hurry and discuss this with Huo Chong."]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476: Huo Chong and Zeng Boyan Meet in Secret","paragraphs":["Song Shixue stood by the bed with a dark expression, re-suturing Yang Cenan's wound.","The catgut stitches had burst, and the gauze was soaked in blood.","\"It hurts! Can't you be a little gentler?\" Yang Cenan's hands were clenched tightly into fists, his face contorted in pain.","Distressed for his master, Yang Zhong stepped forward to plead.","\"Miss Song, don't you have anesthetics? Why aren't you using them?\"","Song Shixue didn't even look up as she replied, \"We ran out, and I haven't had time to make more.\"","He deserved to experience the agony of being stitched up without painkillers; only then would he learn his lesson for next time.","Even after the final stitch was tied, Yang Cenan's body was still twitching. His exposed skin was drenched in sweat, leaving a damp patch on the bedding.","\"The weather is hot now. If the wound takes too long to heal, it will easily become infected and fester. When that happens, the only option will be to carve out the rotting flesh with a knife.\"","Yang Cenan shivered all over, looking in horror at Song Shixue, who was over a decade younger than him.","How could she say such a thing? How was that any different from being sliced to death by a thousand cuts?","Song Shixue walked out of the sickroom. Song Qiming, who had been waiting outside the whole time, immediately came up and looked her up and down. Only after confirming she was unharmed did he ask about Yang Cenan's condition.","\"How is he?\"","Song Shixue handed the tray in her hands to a maid.","\"He threw a tantrum and smashed his soup bowl, which tore his wound open. I've already stitched it back up.\"","\"Given his current mental state, the follow-up treatment won't be very effective. It would be best to send him away in a few days, lest he die of depression here in Suining City.\"","Zeng Boyan chose not to stay at the official post house, but instead booked an entire inn near the clinic.","That very night, guards dispatched by Song Jinzhao lay in ambush around the inn, keeping a close watch on their every move.","Meanwhile, Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong shamelessly took up residence in the backyard of the government office.","Song Jinzhao arranged for them to stay in guest rooms a bit further from the main courtyard, and the servants assigned to attend to them were carefully selected.","In the dead of night, it was pitch black outside, and the surroundings were so quiet that not a single sound could be heard.","A guard leaning against the wall of the wing room suddenly opened his eyes.","His ears twitched; the sound of footsteps was coming from the room next door.","He stood silently by his door, watching closely.","The door next door opened, and soon a dark silhouette slipped past.","Where was he going at this hour?","With a stern face, the guard gently pushed his door open. Waiting until the figure appeared downstairs, he trailed far behind.","He didn't stop until he saw Huo Chong enter another inn.","Inside the door, Huo Chong pulled down his face mask and exchanged a few words with a soldier before being led up to the second floor.","As candlelight flickered on inside the room, the guard took a deep breath and held it.","The group from Panzhou that arrived yesterday was staying at this very inn. Huo Chong obviously knew them. What exactly was going on?","In the lit room on the second floor of the inn, Zeng Boyan sat on the couch with a look of deep worry.","\"Yang Cenan is completely demoralized. If he doesn't recover, everything we've done so far will be for nothing.\"","Zeng Boyan made a throat-slitting gesture.","\"If we turn our backs on him now, he will definitely expose everything. Should we silence him for good?\"","Huo Chong shook his head in disagreement.","\"You and I have already gained Yang Cenan's initial trust. It would be a pity to give up now.\"","Zeng Boyan said, frustrated by his lack of resolve, \"But in his current state, he's practically useless.\"","Huo Chong asked for details, \"To what extent did Song Jinzhao say he could recover?\"","Zeng Boyan replied, \"I didn't see Song Jinzhao. Her sister said the follow-up treatment will take half a year, and no one can say for sure how much he'll recover.\"","Huo Chong stood up and paced back and forth across the room. After pondering for a long moment, he turned to face Zeng Boyan.","\"The clinic is guarded by government runners, so I can't get in. Find a way for me to meet with Yang Cenan. He has to pull himself together.\"","Zeng Boyan lowered his eyes in thought. \"The inn is very close to the clinic. In a few days, I'll have Yang Cenan moved here. You can look for Yang Zhong then.\"","Huo Chong gave a slight nod."]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477: Song Anhao Seeks Gu Baozhu for Business Negotiations","paragraphs":["At the breakfast table the next day, Song Anhao's round eyes kept darting toward Gu Baozhu, his thick eyelashes fluttering.","Just as the aunt and nephew were getting ready to head to the clinic together after the meal, Song Anhao blocked her path in the courtyard outside the guest rooms.","\"Sister Zhuzhu, I have something I want to discuss with you.\"","Gu Baozhu smiled gently, resting her hands on her knees.","\"What is it?\" He was acting like a little adult; he probably just wanted to go out and play.","Song Anhao straightened his back, lifted his chin, and looked at Gu Baozhu with a face full of earnestness.","\"I heard that the Xue family bookstore in the south of the city is Madam Gu's property. Can you sell it to me?\"","Gu Baozhu looked startled. She straightened her upper body and blinked.","\"Does the County Princess want to buy the bookstore?\"","For an eight-year-old child to suddenly ask to buy a bookstore, it had to be an adult's idea.","Song Anhao shook his head. \"I want to buy it myself.\"","His hands, hanging by his sides, gripped his clothes so tightly that they formed several creases.","\"When I went to ask a few days ago, the manager said it was going to be sold, but when I went again yesterday, he said it wasn't for sale anymore. Do you not want to sell it anymore, or do you think the price isn't right?\"","The aunt and nephew exchanged a glance.","They had indeed visited the bookstore yesterday, and it was Gu Baozhu who had instructed them not to sell.","It was her mother's dowry, and Madam Gu had tacitly given it to Gu Baozhu.","Gu Baozhu told the truth, \"Originally, I did want to sell it. But I noticed that Suining City is doing much better than before, and there are a lot more traveling merchants. I figured there will be more and more people in the future, so I decided against selling it.\"","\"Ah,\" Song Anhao's face fell, not expecting this reason.","\"It will take at least a few years for Suining City to fully develop, and it's inconvenient for you to manage it while staying in Songzhou City. Just sell it to me, okay? I can pay a little more silver.\"","Song Anhao widened his eyes, looking incredibly pitiful.","Gu Baozhu asked in confusion, \"Why do you want to buy a bookstore? Does the County Princess know?\"","Song Anhao looked down at the ground, his eyes darting around.","After hesitating for a long time, he finally looked up.","\"I think highly of this business. Once I write the business plan, I'll show it to my older sister.\"","As he spoke, his expression turned determined.","\"Sister Zhuzhu, just sell it to me, alright? I promise to give you a good price.\"","\"Miss Gu, Young Master Gu, the County Princess and the others are already waiting at the door.\" Seeing that the two hadn't come over for a long time, Song Jinzhao sent a maid to hurry them.","Gu Baozhu turned her head to look at Gu Jinghong.","\"You go ahead first. I'll head to the clinic myself a bit later.\"","Gu Jinghong nodded. His gaze swept over Song Anhao before he smiled and turned to leave.","Wanting to do business at such a young age—who knew who had taught him that.","Gu Baozhu walked into the pavilion and sat down, with Song Anhao sitting right across from her.","His unblinking stare made it look like he wouldn't give up until he achieved his goal.","\"My family's bookstore is being sold together with the bookshop and the printing workshop. How much silver are you planning to offer?\"","As long as the price was high enough, she would sell it. She wouldn't go easy on him just because Song Anhao was young.","\"The bookshop plus the printing workshop, and I'll take over all the staff inside. Five hundred taels of silver.\" Song Anhao held up his hand to gesture.","Gu Baozhu shook her head. \"The shop is in a good location, and the workshop covers a large area. Five hundred taels of silver is too little. It has to be one thousand taels.\"","Song Anhao's eyes widened, and he voiced his astonishment, \"That's way too high! North Street isn't considered bustling, and shops there are only a hundred taels of silver each. The workshop is only one mu of land, and it's in the outer city. Six hundred taels of silver at most.\"","Gu Baozhu shook her head again. \"Separated by just a wall isn't that far.\"","\"Suining City will only become more prosperous in the future. Prices will only go up, not down. You have to look at the long term. One thousand taels is definitely not expensive.\"","Song Anhao kept a straight face, his cheeks puffing out in anger.","Using the exact same words to block him—if he had known, he wouldn't have said that earlier.","This was more than just paying a little more; this was her jacking up the price on the spot.","\"Who knows what will happen in the future? If a war breaks out, it's all over. One thousand taels is too much. Six hundred and fifty taels of silver at most.\"","Hearing Song Anhao's gritted-teeth tone, Gu Baozhu couldn't help but curl her lips into a smile.","He really sounded the part. The County Princess must have taught him.","\"For the sake of the County Princess, I'll give you a discount of one hundred taels. Deal at nine hundred taels.\"","Song Anhao's two little eyebrows scrunched together like two caterpillars.","\"I've been to the printing workshop. There are very few orders, and many tools have been left idle for so long that they are ruined. Buying new ones will cost a lot of silver. Drop it by another hundred taels.\"","Gu Baozhu rested her chin on her hand, thinking for a long time before nodding.","\"For the sake of your second sister, eight hundred taels is fine. Do you even have that much money?\"","Hearing Gu Baozhu agree, Song Anhao's eyes instantly lit up.","He leaned on the stone table and moved closer with a smile. \"What do you think about paying in installments?\"","\"I'll give you two hundred taels first, and the remaining six hundred taels will be paid off over half a year, giving you one hundred taels a month.\"","Gu Baozhu stood up, not knowing whether to laugh or cry. \"No way. The eight hundred taels of silver must be paid in full all at once, otherwise I won't sell it.\"","Watching her decisively walk away, Song Anhao felt like crying but had no tears.","Doing business with someone who doesn't lack money is just difficult; it doesn't matter to them whether they sell or not.","\"Fine, all at once it is. Give me a little time to raise the money. Tomorrow morning at the latest, we'll go to the government office to transfer the deed.\"","Gu Baozhu waved her hand with her back to Song Anhao.","\"Hurry up and raise the money. I won't wait if you're late.\""]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478: Useless thing, don't you know blood must be paid with blood","paragraphs":["Lying on the sickbed in the medical pavilion, Yang Cenan's mood was even worse than yesterday.","Pulling his loose clothes together, Song Jinzhao asked, \"Have you remembered any of your lost memories?\"","\"...\" Yang Cenan stared straight out the window, showing no reaction whatsoever.","Song Jinzhao sighed. \"Compared to death, facial paralysis and slow reactions are just minor problems.\"","\"The blind, the deaf, the crippled—who among them isn't worse off than you? Yet they all live perfectly fine.\"","\"To collapse after encountering a setback only proves you were trash to begin with.\"","Waiting by the bed, Yang Zhong opened his mouth to speak but hesitated, swallowing the words back down.","Having kept watch for so many days, he was anxious too.","If the position of the young clan leader fell into someone else's hands, everything would be ruined.","Yang Cenan slowly looked at Song Jinzhao. There was no anger in his eyes, only a dead, silent numbness.","\"The minor problems you mentioned are enough to make my father abandon me. Without the position of the young clan leader, I will die sooner or later, just like this assassination attempt.\"","Staring at him, Song Jinzhao's mind raced.","This meant the assassination had nothing to do with Huo Chong; it was the Yang family slaughtering each other to fight for the position of the next clan leader.","But if that were the case, why would Huo Chong appear in Suining City?","He clearly followed Yang Cenan here.","Was his meeting with Zeng Boyan premeditated or a coincidence?","Unable to calm her mind to think, she simply set the matter aside for now.","Song Jinzhao's tone grew even harsher. Her words fired off like a barrage of cannonballs, smashing right into Yang Cenan's heart.","\"Whether you die isn't up to others; it depends on whether you actually want to live.\"","\"Your wife and son were murdered—can you really swallow this insult? Don't you know that blood must be paid with blood?\"","\"Instead of avenging them, you are here giving up on yourself and waiting for death. Do you deserve to be called a husband? Do you deserve to be called a father?\"","\"As for this young clan leader position you mentioned, if your father won't give it to you, can't you just seize it?\"","\"...\"","Hearing that last sentence, everyone in the sickroom was shocked, except for Song Qiming and Song Shixue.","Gu Jinghong looked at Song Jinzhao in astonishment. After pondering for a long while, a sudden thought popped into his head.","Is she trying to incite an internal rebellion in Panzhou?","Surely not...","At the entrance of the medical pavilion, Zeng Boyan, who had arrived a step late, hurriedly dismounted.","As the distance closed, Guan Nianshan gradually froze in place.","His gaze followed Zeng Boyan, growing more suspicious the longer he looked.","After Zeng Boyan went inside, Qingshuang, who had taken in everything, deliberately asked him, \"What is wrong?\"","Guan Nianshan shook his head absently. \"Nothing, I just feel like this person looks familiar.\"","Qingshuang said, \"His name is Zeng Boyan. He is a Ranger Commandant under Yang Ruiping, the Pacification Commissioner of Panzhou. I heard he trained all these cavalrymen.\"","Guan Nianshan's eyes widened abruptly. \"Zeng Boyan?\"","Qingshuang asked in return, \"Do you know him?\"","Guan Nianshan's heartbeat quickened, and he instantly tensed up.","He immediately shook his head in denial. \"No, I don't. I might have just seen someone who looks like him.\"","He wondered if the young master had managed to get in touch with Zeng Qing. Should he test the waters?","Just as Zeng Boyan pushed the door open, Song Jinzhao was coming out.","He acutely sensed that the atmosphere in the room was off—there was a murderous aura.","As the door closed, he used his eyes to ask Yang Zhong what was going on.","Yang Zhong first shot him a meaningful glance, then dropped to his knees with a heavy thud.","The corners of his eyes were red, and his voice choked with emotion.","\"The bodies of Madam and the young master are still laid out in the Wumeng Tribe. If this continues, they will rot.\"","\"We must return to Panzhou as soon as possible. Without revenge, they will not rest in peace.\"","Zeng Boyan felt a surge of joy, realizing the meaning behind Yang Zhong's glance, and immediately knelt down to add fuel to the fire.","\"The day before this subordinate left Panzhou, the eldest young master welcomed a new pair of twins, a boy and a girl. By the time we get back, it will almost be their one-month celebration.\"","That single sentence ignited the powder keg.","Yang Cenan abruptly turned his neck, his gaze locked dead onto Zeng Boyan's face.","His eyes were practically splitting open, looking as if he wanted to eat someone alive.","He gritted his teeth and said, \"My son is dead, yet he gets to add a pair of children.\"","He suddenly began to laugh. His stiff facial features scrunched together, and the mirthless smile looked exceptionally terrifying."]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479: Refusing to Let Song Shixue Go to Panzhou for Accompanying Clinic Visits","paragraphs":["Hearing the roars coming from the ward, Song Jinzhao, who was preparing medicine, curled her lips into a faint smile.","Gu Jinghong's pupils contracted as a cold sweat broke out on his back.","It was nine times out of ten just as he had guessed; County Princess Linghui's shrewdness was simply too deep.","Not long after the sound stopped, Yang Zhong hurriedly opened the door to look for Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, my young master invites you in.\"","Inside the ward, Yang Cenan asked impatiently, \"May I ask the County Princess, when will the wounds on my chest and abdomen fully heal? Can I ride in a carriage now?\"","He wanted to return to Panzhou as soon as possible, the sooner the better.","\"You should be able to get out of bed and walk around in about three days, but it is best to wait another ten days before enduring the bumps of a carriage.\"","\"The nerve damage in your brain requires acupuncture combined with medication to recover. It will take at least three months, and up to half a year. I can instruct the estate doctor you brought along, so your treatment will not be delayed after you return.\"","Yang Cenan slowly shook his head, looking at Song Jinzhao with eyes full of pleading.","\"His medical skills are far inferior to yours, County Princess. As long as you are willing to stay in Panzhou for half a year, I am willing to agree to any condition.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head without hesitation. \"I cannot. My younger siblings at home are still young, so this County Princess cannot leave.\"","Yang Cenan blurted out, \"Then let Second Miss Song go instead. I trust her medical skills.\"","Since the other party held a noble status, he had not held much hope to begin with.","When Song Jinzhao realized what he meant, her face suddenly turned cold. He had been targeting Shixue from the very beginning.","\"The follow-up treatment does not require highly advanced acupuncture skills. Your esteemed estate's doctor is fully capable of handling it. There is no need for this County Princess's sister to go over.\"","\"She is still young. Let alone staying in Panzhou for half a year, I would not even feel at ease letting her leave for a single day.\"","Yang Cenan still refused to give up. The level of medical skill would definitely affect the treatment's outcome.","What could someone possibly achieve after just a few days of learning? If he was not treated well, would he not be ruined?","\"Second Miss Song is eighteen this year. In an ordinary family, she would have already married and had children. We have many talented young men in Panzhou; it would be a perfect opportunity for her to go and meet them. I promise to find her a suitable husband.\"","Song Jinzhao's displeasure turned into speechlessness.","\"My sister's marriage is none of your concern. The treatment starts tomorrow. If he does not want to learn, you can all leave once your wounds are healed.\"","Watching Song Jinzhao turn and walk away, Yang Cenan grew furious.","Once the door closed, he turned his head to complain to Yang Zhong and Zeng Boyan.","\"I have already made concessions, so why is she unwilling? It is only half a year.\"","\"Even the Emperor would not dare disrespect my father, how dare she refuse!\"","Yang Zhong rubbed the back of his head and cautiously comforted him, \"The Song family has no relatives in Panzhou, so it is only human nature for County Princess Linghui to be worried.\"","Zeng Boyan said without changing his expression, \"The imperial court is highly guarded against the foreign tribes in the southwest. To the Song family, Panzhou is a tiger's den. They will absolutely not go there.\"","\"Since the County Princess said it is not too difficult, it is better to let the estate doctor try. It is more reassuring to rely on our own people.\"","Yang Cenan took a deep breath and closed his eyes.","\"Forget it. At worst, I will just have my father write a letter to the Emperor when the time comes. They would not dare refuse to come.\"","He could not use force against his savior; it would ruin his reputation if word got out.","On the way back, seeing Song Jinzhao keeping a dark expression the entire time, Song Qiming's dissatisfaction with Yang Cenan grew even stronger.","The room was not soundproof, so he had heard all the talking just now, including the two angry sentences Yang Cenan had shouted later.","\"Do not be angry, Sister. In a few days, I will make them leave. Let's not treat his lingering symptoms either.\"","His sister was a County Princess personally titled by the Emperor, while Yang Cenan was merely Yang Ruiping's son.","He did not even hold a proper official position, yet he spoke to his sister with such arrogance and even dared to discuss Shixue's marriage. He had to be taught a lesson.","Song Jinzhao snapped back to reality and glanced at Guan Nianshan, who was following behind them.","\"I was thinking about something else. It has nothing to do with Yang Cenan.\"","\"Turning gratitude into enmity brings us no benefit. Just let the estate doctor he brought along learn the treatment.\""]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480: How dare you cheat children out of their money","paragraphs":["\"You finished so quickly. I haven't even gone over there yet,\" Gu Baozhu said, arriving late.","Gu Jinghong rode his horse around to his aunt's side and smiled at Song Jinzhao. \"We'll take a stroll around the city ourselves. County Princess, you can head back first.\"","Watching the retreating figures of Song Jinzhao and her group, Gu Baozhu nudged Gu Jinghong with her hand.","\"Why did you keep winking at me? Did something happen?\"","Gu Jinghong nodded and slowly recounted the events at the medical clinic, especially Yang Cenan's request for the Song sisters to accompany him to Panzhou for medical consultations.","Before he could even finish, Gu Baozhu exploded.","\"They absolutely cannot go to Panzhou! If the Yang family harbors any ulterior motives, they will never return.\"","Gu Jinghong replied, \"The County Princess has already refused.\"","\"Yang Cenan will definitely seek revenge when he goes back this time. Once they start fighting, it will absolutely be a fight to the death.\"","Gu Baozhu crossed her arms over her chest and said, \"The young patriarch of the Yang family is practically the crown prince of Panzhou. Their internal struggles will only weaken their own power, which is entirely beneficial and harmless to the imperial court.\"","Gu Jinghong nodded. \"The County Princess likely shares the same thought. That's why she strongly encouraged Yang Cenan to go back and seek revenge. She just wants to stir up internal conflict within Panzhou.\"","Gu Baozhu curled her lips into a smug smile, reaching out and clenching her fist to make a gesture.","\"Great minds think alike. The County Princess is extremely brilliant and holds the nation in her heart; how could she possibly let such an opportunity slip by when it delivers itself right to her doorstep?\"","Gu Jinghong lowered his eyes thoughtfully and murmured, \"I truly didn't expect her to react so quickly.\"","\"By the way, what did Song Anhao want with you? Why were you delayed for so long?\"","Gu Baozhu smiled radiantly and said, \"He wanted me to sell the Xue Family Bookstore to him, and I have already agreed.\"","Gu Jinghong opened his eyes wide in astonishment.","\"Buy the bookstore? Song Anhao is only eight years old and he's already doing business?\"","Gu Baozhu nodded. \"I heard the County Princess has already let him manage a shop, but buying the bookstore was his own idea. The County Princess doesn't know about it yet.\"","\"How much did you agree on for the price?\"","The Xue Family Bookstore had been losing money year after year. It had only survived this long by relying on their grandmother's subsidies over the years, so it shouldn't sell for much silver.","Gu Baozhu held up her fingers to indicate the number eight to him.","\"Eight hundred taels. We'll transfer the deed tomorrow.\"","Gu Jinghong stared at her blankly.","\"You really dared to ask for that much. You're even swindling a child's money! That bookstore is worth five hundred taels at most.\"","Gu Baozhu retorted, \"Who says I'm swindling him? Seeing as Suining City is about to prosper, selling it now is already a loss for me. If he wants it, he has to pay a high price.\"","Gu Jinghong shut his mouth, not wanting to argue. He didn't want to interfere in business matters either.","\"Yang Cenan won't be able to leave for a short while. Are we just going to stay here like this? How about we play for a few days and then go back?\"","Gu Baozhu shook her head without hesitation. \"No way. He has his eyes on Shixue. I'm going to the clinic to keep an eye on things later.\"","Gu Jinghong said, \"With so many yamen runners guarding outside, nothing will happen. Besides, Song Shixue knows martial arts herself, and she was personally taught by the County Princess. Even you might not be able to beat her in a fight.\"","Gu Baozhu glared at him. \"Say that again.\"","The curve of Gu Jinghong's lips froze, and he quickly averted his gaze to look straight ahead.","...","The moment Song Qiming stepped into the government office, Shi Simian came up to greet him.","\"My Lord, this is a letter from the Songzhou government office. Lord Gu wants you to build a good relationship with Yang Cenan.\"","Song Qiming took the letter and opened it. Besides instructing him to build a good relationship, Gu Zhongxun had specifically added a reminder at the end: when Yang Cenan leaves, yamen runners must be sent to escort him until he is out of the Suining Prefecture borders.","In the highly restricted study, Qingshuang stood before Song Jinzhao to give a report.","\"Guan Nianshan recognized Zeng Boyan, but Zeng Boyan didn't recognize him. The two of them didn't speak.\"","\"After returning to the inn last night, Huo Chong hasn't left at all. It seems like he is waiting for someone.\"","Song Jinzhao's fingertips tapped repeatedly on the desk, her gaze fixed on the map hanging on the wall for a long time without moving.","\"Keep watching them. I have a feeling there's more to this.\""]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481: Agree to Buy from Bookstore, Remember to Sign an Exclusive Contract","paragraphs":["On the stone-paved path outside the courtyard, upon seeing someone in the study, Song Anhao skipped over.","\"Is my sister inside?\" His eyes were sparkling, full of joy.","He had thought she wouldn't be back until noon, but to his surprise, she had already returned.","The maid respectfully replied, \"The County Princess has just returned.\"","\"Come in.\" As soon as the maid finished speaking, Song Jinzhao's voice came from inside.","Song Anhao immediately pushed the door open and walked in. \"Eldest Sister, I have something to tell you.\"","As soon as his bottom touched the seat, he pushed the book in his hand in front of Song Jinzhao.","\"This was written by a scholar I know. I want to publish a book for him.\"","The Record of Unjust Grievances","A mystery novel?","She turned to the first page.","It told the story of a scholar in Suining Prefecture named Shao Dengke, who had his abdomen cut open and his heart dug out on his wedding night...","After reading the first story, Song Jinzhao leaned back in her chair in surprise.","It featured investigative methods similar to Sherlock Holmes, with a plot full of twists and turns.","One must know that the current detective storybooks on the market mostly featured perceptive government officials or the ghosts of victims appearing at the door for justice.","This Record of Unjust Grievances could be considered an overwhelming strike of superiority; it was hard to imagine it was written by an ancient person.","Seeing Song Jinzhao staring at the storybook in silence for a long time, Song Anhao smugly leaned closer.","\"Eldest Sister, isn't it written very well?\"","Song Jinzhao looked at him. \"Where did you find this person?\"","Receiving her approval, Song Anhao's confidence instantly surged.","He straightened his back and said exultantly, \"Half a month ago, I went to the teahouse to buy some pastries and happened to run into someone pitching his own storybook to the shopkeeper, so I stopped to watch for a while.\"","\"The shopkeeper said the storybook written by Liu Ziyuan was a mess and terrible to read, and drove him out. I picked up the storybook and took a look, and I was instantly captivated.\"","\"I thought he wrote exceptionally well, so I asked him to write a few more stories to compile into a book. When it is printed and sold in bookstores, it will definitely make a lot of money.\"","Saying this, he took out a piece of paper covered with the names of bookstores.","\"Moreover, I found out that there is only one printing workshop in Suining City capable of making books. They only print books used by scholars. Very few bookstores in the city sell storybooks, so the market is completely vacant. I want to seize the initiative.\"","Looking at his raised chin, Song Jinzhao smiled.","\"Have you ever thought about why this part of the market is vacant?\"","Song Anhao replied, \"There are very few people in the city who like to read storybooks. They are used to going to teahouses to listen to storytellers. The printing workshops are unwilling to specially carve blocks for printing just for a few customers because it's not cost-effective.\"","\"But the situation is different now. Brother has governed Suining City very well. There will be more and more commoners in the future, and the demand for storybooks will also grow. Entering at this low point will definitely be profitable.\"","Song Jinzhao's lips paused slightly, a dark glint flashing through her eyes.","Specially carving blocks for printing... She had almost forgotten about movable type printing.","\"Even if the population increases, most of them are illiterate. The growing demand you mentioned might take five years or even longer.\"","Song Anhao held up The Record of Unjust Grievances.","\"If few people buy it in Suining City, we can sell it outside first. There are no bandits on the roads now, so the cost of transporting it out is very low.\"","\"Besides, I asked someone to inquire about it. The storybooks sold in Songzhou City are all about love and romance, and the buyers are all women deep in their mansions. But what Liu Ziyuan writes is different; both men and women can read it. When the time comes, there will definitely be many buyers.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the book title. \"You just said Liu Ziyuan is a scholar. Will he not take the imperial examinations in the future?\"","Being so familiar with the imperial laws and able to describe criminal investigations in such detail, it was impossible for him to have no aspirations for an official career.","Song Anhao shook his head regretfully. \"Liu Ziyuan is missing two toes on his right foot, so he cannot participate in the imperial examinations.\"","Song Jinzhao's expression paused slightly.","\"Was he born with it?\"","Song Anhao shook his head again.","\"He was injured by robbers on his way to take the provincial exam. He is a child scholar and used to teach people in the town. Later, his students became fewer and fewer. Unable to make a living, he thought of writing storybooks to make money. Unfortunately, no one appreciated the stories he wrote. The teahouses in Suining City are too set in their ways.\"","Song Jinzhao took the storybook and looked at it again.","\"Since you are betting on him, you must hold him firmly in your hands.\"","\"Sign an exclusive contract with him so that the storybooks he writes in the future can only be sold to you. It would be best to buy another printing workshop to print them yourself.\"","Song Anhao's eyes lit up, and his grin grew even wider than before.","\"Eldest Sister is right. I will go find him tomorrow to sign an exclusive contract.\"","\"I also thought about the printing workshop. The Xue family's printing workshop belongs to Sister Zhuzhu's family. I have already agreed with her to buy the bookstore and the printing workshop together for eight hundred taels of silver, including taking over all the workers inside. Now I am still short of six hundred taels of silver.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled sweetly. She was not angry at her brother for acting on his own; instead, she felt very proud.","To be able to think of so much at the age of eight and even dare to take practical action, this was already very impressive.","\"Alright, Eldest Sister will provide this six hundred taels of silver for you.\" After saying that, she went back to her room, took out bank notes worth six hundred taels of silver, and handed them to Song Anhao.","\"After the transfer of ownership, find a time to take me to the printing workshop to have a look. Also, I want to meet Liu Ziyuan.\"","She had to determine whether this person was a time traveler, and whether he could only write detective storybooks or if he could write other things as well.","Song Anhao took the bank notes and ran off happily.","\"I am going to find Sister Zhuzhu right now. Tomorrow we will go to the printing workshop.\""]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482: The Gu Family's Concerns about the Next Emperor","paragraphs":["In the courtyard at the northeast corner of the backyard, Guan Nianshan walked to the easternmost room and knocked on the door.","The family of three, who were taking a nap, opened their eyes. Qu Ya got up and comforted his wife.","\"You and the child go back to sleep. I'll get the door.\"","Opening the door, he saw it was Guan Nianshan. Having known him for years, Qu Ya immediately noticed that something was wrong with his expression.","Closing the door, he asked in a low voice, \"What's wrong?\"","The two walked to a corner to speak in hushed tones.","\"Zeng Qing's son, Zeng Boyan, has come to Suining City. I ran into him at the medical clinic.\"","Qu Ya's expression changed, his gaze turning as sharp as a falcon's.","\"Did he recognize you?\"","Guan Nianshan shook his head. \"He didn't recognize me at all.\"","\"I don't know if the Young Master has gone to find Zeng Qing. I was wondering if I should go test the waters with Zeng Boyan.\"","Qu Ya immediately shook his head.","\"No. The situation is unclear right now. Asking Zeng Boyan rashly might bring trouble to the Young Master.\"","Guan Nianshan thought for a long while before sighing.","\"Everything is going well working under the County Princess now. If I wasn't so worried, I wouldn't want to get involved either.\"","Qu Ya fell silent for a moment before speaking in a low voice.","\"Song Jinzhao had a purpose in bringing us to Suining. The Young Master is currently working under Mu Ji'an, and she is just taking precautions.\"","Guan Nianshan lowered his head and muttered to himself, \"If only the Young Master were on good terms with the County Princess.\"","A stable home and job, with his son studying at the academy and having a guaranteed future—he truly didn't want anything to change.","Qu Ya clenched his jaw and said nothing.","Unless Song Jinzhao rebelled against the imperial court, it was impossible for them to ever be on good terms.","But was that even possible?","In the front hall of the clinic, Gu Baozhu sat opposite Song Shixue, watching her grind medicine while occasionally glancing toward the back.","\"I wonder if the true mastermind behind the scenes is Yang Cedong or Yang Cexi. To strike so ruthlessly against their own younger brother's family—it's utterly inhumane. They have no brotherly affection at all.\"","Song Shixue replied, \"The royal family is just the same. Before Prince Qi's downfall, he and Prince Ying fought fiercely. Even the Emperor...\"","Seeing her trail off mid-sentence, Gu Baozhu understood.","She leaned in, resting half her face on the table, and spoke to Song Shixue in a meaningful whisper.","\"The Emperor was also suspicious and wary of Prince Qi and Prince Ying, afraid their power would grow too great and threaten his throne, right?\"","Song Shixue looked around warily.","\"Keep your voice down. If anyone hears us, we could lose our heads. Who told you all this?\"","Songzhou City was so far from the capital, yet Gu Baozhu had hit the nail on the head. Someone must have told her.","Gu Baozhu pouted in tacit admission.","\"I heard my father complain about it a few times. He worries about the country and the people, and he's terrified the next emperor will be an incompetent tyrant.\"","Song Shixue's eyes widened.","She really dared to speak her mind. Being far away certainly made one bolder.","While the people outside were speaking in low voices, the people inside were also whispering.","Sweeping his gaze over his three remaining confidants, Yang Cenan gave a meaningful look to the subordinate standing in the corner.","Yang Zhong looked at him, and the man immediately walked over to the bed and bent down.","\"Return to Panzhou immediately. There is a matter you must handle before I get back...\"","Listening closely by his ear, the man's expression gradually changed.","After pondering for a moment, he stood up, cupped his hands in a salute, and spoke with a resonant and forceful voice.","\"I will not fail the Young Master's trust.\"","Watching the guard turn and leave, Zeng Boyan suppressed his inner doubts, stepped forward, and said, \"The clinic is crude, and there are so many yamen runners standing guard outside. This humble official believes it would be more appropriate to move to an inn.\"","Yang Zhong had his concerns. \"But the County Princess said the Young Master cannot get out of bed yet.\"","Zeng Boyan replied, \"He can be carried out on a stretcher. The clinic has one. The patient rooms aren't soundproof; if we speak even a little too loudly, the people outside can hear everything clearly.\"","\"The inn is right next to the clinic, less than half a quarter-hour's walk away. It's very convenient.\"","Yang Cenan decided, \"Then we shall move to the inn.\""]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483: Pedal-operated Threshing Machine","paragraphs":["\"The patient wants to move to an inn?\" Song Shixue looked at Zeng Boyan in complete surprise.","Zeng Boyan smiled and nodded. \"It will be more convenient for meals and accommodation at the inn. With the Third Young Master staying here, the medical clinic cannot receive other patients. It is also troublesome for Second Miss Song to go out for house calls every time. It's better to move to the inn.\"","After a moment of hesitation, Song Shixue nodded in agreement; she had no choice but to agree anyway.","\"I'll have a medicine boy go with you to ensure everything is fine during the transfer before he comes back.\"","Their eyes met, and Heye immediately put down what she was holding and walked over.","Watching Yang Cenan being carried away, the yamen runners looked at each other, unsure if they should follow.","They had been ordered to guard the clinic and keep outsiders away precisely to prevent anything from happening to Yang Cenan in Suining City.","Now that the person had left, and the inn was guarded by so many attendants, deciding whether to follow or not was quite a dilemma.","Lan Xi looked toward Song Shixue.","\"Follow Heye.\"","Lan Xi nodded and immediately signaled four yamen runners to follow.","Upon arriving at the inn, Heye checked Yang Cenan's wounds and prepared to leave.","Seeing that Lan Xi and the other four had no intention of leaving, Zeng Boyan stepped out of the room and politely smiled to shoo them away.","\"The inn has people protecting it and does not need yamen runners to stand guard. You may leave.\"","Lan Xi was already prepared for this. He didn't force them to stay; he gave a slight nod and led his men away.","\"Steward Lan, are we just going to leave it be?\"","The yamen runners who had followed were concerned, worried they would be held accountable if something happened to Yang Cenan.","\"Send someone back to inform Lord Song. What to do next is a matter for our superiors.\"","Vast stretches of paddy fields sparkled with golden light under the sun.","A gentle breeze blew past, causing the heavy ears of rice to sway back and forth, symbolizing the joy of a bountiful harvest.","Gu Jinghong sat high on horseback, never tiring of the view.","\"Brother Song, what are those people doing?\" Noticing many wooden carts parked in the distance carrying particularly large objects that people were unloading, Gu Jinghong asked curiously.","Song Qiming took a look and replied, \"Those are pedal-operated threshing machines. They will be used to thresh the rice ears for the upcoming autumn harvest.\"","\"Huh?\" Gu Jinghong raised his eyebrows in confusion.","A pedal-operated threshing machine? He had never heard of such a thing.","Song Qiming explained, \"My sister felt that the current threshing methods are too inefficient, so she wanted to create a machine that could speed up the process.\"","\"She pondered over it for days before drawing up the blueprints, and then had the craftsmen repeatedly experiment until this pedal-operated threshing machine was finally made.\"","Walking up to the cart, Gu Jinghong circled the machine, examining it in careful detail.","The outer shell was made of wood, and in the middle was a movable iron cylinder with curved, protruding iron wires on the outside.","He knocked on it twice, producing a crisp, hollow metallic sound; the cylinder was empty inside.","Gu Jinghong looked over at Song Qiming.","\"Brother Song, how do you use this thing? Could you demonstrate it for me?\"","\"Of course.\" Saying so, Song Qiming had someone cut a handful of rice stalks, walked over to the threshing machine, and began to thresh the grain.","Placing the rice stalks over the cylinder, he stepped down on the pedal. As the drum rotated, the rice grains clattered down like hail into the square bin below.","Gu Jinghong, who was used to seeing grain threshed by beating, was stunned by this sight.","He leaned in close to look inside the drum but was stopped by Song Qiming.","\"Don't get too close, you'll get hurt if it scrapes you.\"","Although the iron wires on the drum were not sharp, it spun so fast that bumping into it would still be very painful.","Ignoring the dust and chaff flying into his face, Gu Jinghong squatted down and grabbed a handful of the threshed grain.","\"She truly lives up to the title of County Princess Linghui, being able to create such a miraculous object.\"","Song Qiming smiled proudly and praised, \"My sister has always been intelligent. She often comes up with brilliant and unconventional ideas; I'm already used to it.\""]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484: One Startle After Another","paragraphs":["Walking along the canal, Gu Jinghong couldn't hide the envy in his eyes as he gazed at the crystal-clear water.","\"Once the Mu River flows through, the fields outside Suining City will never lack water again. Even Songzhou City doesn't have such a well-connected network of canals.\"","Looking into the distance, a massive waterwheel tens of meters high turned slowly by the riverbank, the faint sound of splashing water reaching their ears.","Song Qiming said, \"They were all dug during our free time. With so many conscripted laborers needing to be fed every day, we couldn't just let them sit idle.\"","Gu Jinghong didn't know whether to laugh or cry. Raiding the bandits' lair and dragging them back to do hard labor was likely something Song Qiming had planned all along.","As they walked further, they noticed a pole planted in the rice paddy, a strip of white cloth tied to its top.","\"Is there a grave over there?\"","Song Qiming glanced over and shook his head.","\"There's no grave. It's a deliberate marker. The seedlings next to it are high-yield varieties, so they will be harvested separately.\"","Gu Jinghong raised an eyebrow in confusion. \"High-yield seedlings?\"","Weren't all the seedlings in a rice paddy the same?","Song Qiming gave a slight nod, walked over, and carefully navigated his way through the paddy.","The narrow gaps between the plants could only fit one foot at a time, forcing him to move sideways.","Gu Jinghong's hands grew itchy from brushing against the rice ears, so he simply raised his arms high in the air.","Song Qiming gently supported a cluster of rice. \"Look, these few stalks are much plumper than the rest. The stems are thicker, and their color is a deeper yellow.\"","Gu Jinghong looked closely and saw that it was indeed sturdier, noticeably larger than the surrounding stalks.","Song Qiming explained, \"Ah Jie said this is called the ear selection method. We save the seeds from these exceptional stalks separately. Next year, we'll plant them and manage them meticulously. After a few generations, these excellent traits will stabilize, allowing us to breed a completely new variety.\"","\"Pfft, pfft!\" A bug flew straight into Gu Jinghong's mouth, and he hastily spat it out.","After spitting out the ladybug, he spat a few more times to clear his mouth.","Seeing this, Song Qiming said, \"There are too many bugs down in the fields. Let's head back up.\"","Gu Jinghong swallowed hard and followed him. \"Coming to Suining City was definitely the right choice. With so many great developments happening, why didn't you inform my grandfather? He could have requested a commendation for you.\"","Song Qiming smiled, brushing off the grass clippings clinging to his clothes. \"How could I claim credit before achieving any real results? It won't be too late to ask for a reward once the new variety is successfully cultivated.\"","Gu Jinghong countered, \"Even if this doesn't count, the pedal-operated threshing machine certainly does.\"","\"With the autumn harvest upon us, it's the perfect time to put it to use. When I head back, I'll take one with me, along with a craftsman who knows how to build them. That way, Songzhou City can start using them too.\"","Song Qiming replied, \"I was actually planning to write a report to Lord Gu about it. When are you heading back? If you leave too late, you'll have to wait until next year to use them.\"","Gu Jinghong frowned, looking troubled.","\"It's rare for us to get out like this. I don't mind, but my youngest aunt probably won't want to leave so soon.\"","\"Just this morning, she said she wanted to stay at the clinic to guard Miss Shixue and prevent Yang Cenan from secretly taking her away.\"","Song Qiming laughed. \"Shixue knows martial arts, and the clinic has its apprentices. Ah Jie also sent Lanxi over, and there are bailiffs guarding the entrance. Unless Shixue leaves willingly, no one can take her away, let alone harm a single hair on her head.\"","Gu Jinghong shrugged helplessly. \"That's exactly what I told her.\"","\"I even pointed out that Miss Shixue's martial arts skills might be better than hers, but I just ended up getting scolded for it.\"","Song Qiming waved his hand modestly.","\"I wouldn't say her martial arts are exceptionally high. Shixue is mostly skilled in archery. Even Ah Jie praised her as a natural-born sharpshooter.\"","Song Qiming needed to inspect the preparations for the autumn harvest, and Gu Jinghong kept him company throughout.","Being around the same age, and with Gu Jinghong being so eager to learn, the two young men found they had an endless amount of things to talk about."]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485: Remove the Person","paragraphs":["When the yamen runner reported back, Shi Simian was sitting in the second hall reviewing last month’s commercial tax ledgers.","“Moving out of the medical clinic? I thought it wasn’t supposed to be touched?”","Why the rush?","The runner said, “They carried him on a stretcher. That wandering cavalry officer named Zeng Boyan refused our protection, saying they had enough men.”","Shi Simian tossed the ledger onto the table and scratched his head in frustration.","“If they had enough men, they wouldn’t have lost dozens. All trouble, and they couldn’t leave sooner.”","Seeing their superior’s anger, no one in the room dared to speak; they all kept their heads down, avoiding his gaze.","“Since they’re in the city, we have to keep an eye on them. Send two runners disguised as civilians to watch nearby—make sure they’re sharp and don’t get caught.”","Watching the man’s hurried departure, Shi Simian lost all interest in the accounts.","He stepped outside and looked up at the sky. “The prefect should be back by now.”","An hour later, Song Qiming walked in wearing a straw hat.","“Pull back the runners from the inn entrance. Have the patrol keep an eye out, but no need for dedicated surveillance.”","On his way back, he had stopped by the medical clinic and already knew that Yang Cena had moved into the inn and declined the protection of the yamen.","Hearing this, Shi Simian looked up in surprise. “You figured it out, sir?”","Song Qiming pressed his lips in speechless annoyance.","“Four pairs of eyes glued to the inn entrance—if I paid even slight attention, I’d notice.”","Compared to the bodyguards his elder sister had trained, these men were leagues behind.","Shi Simian still wasn’t convinced.","“Can just having the patrol watch really work? What if an assassin sneaks in?”","Song Qiming replied, “The cavalry Zeng Boyan brought are all elites. It’ll be hard for assassins to get close.”","“Since they think our runners are unnecessary, we’ll let it be. No point making them unhappy.”","His sister’s people were already in place, so having the runners there or not wouldn’t matter much.","By sunset, the runners at both the inn and the medical clinic had all been withdrawn.","Zeng Boyan stood on the second-floor balcony, watching. His gaze narrowed as it settled on something in the mouth of an alley.","In a private room of a restaurant a hundred meters away, the bodyguards sent by Song Jinzhao were peeking through gauze curtains with a telescope, spying secretly.","Following Zeng Boyan’s line of sight downward, half a face revealed beneath a bamboo hat was unmistakably Huo Chong’s.","...","Song Anhao burst into the room excitedly, clutching two freshly stamped official deeds.","He couldn’t wait until the next day. After getting the silver notes that afternoon, he had gone straight to Gu Baozhu.","“Sister, I’ve already completed the property transfer with Zhuzhu.”","With connections in the yamen, the paperwork was done in the blink of an eye.","Song Jinzhao took the deeds, examined them carefully, and once satisfied, had him put them away.","“This is the first business you’ve chosen on your own. Do it well. I’ll be waiting for you to make big money.”","The shops she had previously let him practice with were all fully stocked and ready—he only had to glance at the accounts now and then, so losing money was nearly impossible.","Now, running a bookstore and printing house would require learning and stumbling along the way. Song Jinzhao intended to let Song Anhao experience it firsthand—growth comes fastest through real practice.","Song Qiming went into politics, Song Shixue into medicine, and Song Anhao favored commerce. These three paths would each benefit them in the long run.","In the dead of night, the streets were utterly empty.","Under a bright moon, Huo Chong, clad in gray, arrived at the inn’s entrance.","A knock echoed, and the night guard soldier sprang up from the floor as if resurrected from the dead, clutching his sword as if his life depended on it.","“Who goes there?”","Huo Chong glanced back behind him. The empty street confirmed no one was watching.","“I’m looking for Yang Zhong. We arranged this.”","After a moment, the door cracked open from inside. The soldier gave him a thorough once-over, the sword’s tip glinting silver and ready at a moment’s notice to take Huo Chong’s life.","“What’s your name?”","“My surname is Huo. Yang Zhong will know when he hears it.”"]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486: Has Huo Chong Defected to Yang Cenan","paragraphs":["Half a quarter of an hour later, Yang Zhong came down from the second floor, wearing a coat draped over his shoulders.","When he saw Huo Chong, his heart skipped a beat. \"You’re here!\"","The two cavalrymen exchanged a glance and opened the door fully.","In a private room of a restaurant a hundred meters away, the guard, upon realizing it was Yang Zhong who had brought Huo Chong into the inn, couldn’t help but frown.","\"Why him? Shouldn’t it be Zeng Boyan?\"","The other guard, who had just been woken up a second ago, said, \"Quick, check if there’s any movement from Zeng Boyan’s room.\"","The scene shifted to the entrance of the third room on the second floor. Yang Zhong led Huo Chong down the hallway, and they stopped in front of Yang Cena's door. After knocking for a long time, they finally pushed the door open and entered.","Next to that room, Huo Chong’s own door remained tightly shut, showing no sign of being opened.","\"No movement.\"","The guard who had spoken earlier snatched the telescope to look for himself. Seeing that the room didn’t even have a lamp lit, his suspicions were confirmed.","\"Zeng Boyan is a martial arts practitioner. There’s no way he wouldn’t have heard the knocking. He’s definitely staying inside on purpose.\"","\"Just the day before yesterday, he met with Huo Chong. The next day, Yang Cena moved from the medical clinic to the inn, and that very night, this man showed up. They must have planned this long in advance.\"","In the room where candlelight flickered, Yang Cena leaned against the head of the bed, his gaze gentle.","\"Thanks to your strong recommendation of Song Jinzhao, my life has been saved. I owe it to you.\"","Huo Chong immediately knelt down, looking at Yang Cena, his voice firm and resolute.","\"It is my honor to serve the Third Young Master.\"","Yang Cena nodded in satisfaction.","\"I accept the request you made earlier. Once I become clan leader, I will surely raise troops to march north and take the imperial court, allowing you to avenge yourself.\"","Huo Chong’s throat tightened sharply. He prostrated himself on the ground, his voice hoarse.","\"Thank you, Third Young Master. As long as I can take my revenge, I would go through fire and water without hesitation.\"","Three months ago, Huo Chong had sought out Yang Cena, offering to pledge his allegiance. To earn the man’s trust, he had even revealed his true identity without reservation.","Yang Cena had been skeptical, maintaining a lukewarm attitude and never giving a definite answer.","But after learning that Yang Cena was gravely wounded and beyond the help of medicine, Huo Chong immediately realized this was a golden opportunity.","So he had rushed from the Shimen tribe to the Wumeng tribe to recommend Song Jinzhao. Now, everything was unfolding exactly as Huo Chong had hoped.","Half an hour later, Huo Chong left the inn unscathed.","Not long after, one of the guards stationed at the restaurant stood before Lan Xi.","\"We don’t know exactly what was said, but when Huo Chong left, there was a smile on his face.\"","Lan Xi paced back and forth in the room, frowning.","\"Does Yang Cena know that Huo Chong met with Zeng Boyan in private?\"","The guard hesitated for a moment before replying, \"Probably not. Otherwise, Yang Zhong wouldn’t have been the one summoned, and Zeng Boyan wouldn’t have stayed out of sight.\"","The first rays of dawn struck the rooftop. Upon learning that Song Jinzhao had risen, Lan Xi immediately requested an audience.","In the study, aside from Song Anhao, who was still practicing his horse stance, all three of the Song siblings were present.","Song Qiming said in disbelief, \"Huo Chong was Mu Ji'an’s trusted man. That he would defect to Yang Cena...\"","Song Shixue stroked her chin and speculated.","\"If Huo Chong really is a descendant of Marquis Wuying, then the troops in Ningzhou are far weaker than those in Panzhou. He might be defecting to Yang Cena to seek revenge.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"I recall that Mu Ji'an saved Huo Chong’s life.\"","Lan Xi nodded. \"Not just that—Huo Chong was also brought into the military camp and promoted step by step by Mu Ji'an himself.\"","\"Mu Ji'an trusted him deeply. You could almost say he treated him like a godson.\"","Song Jinzhao sat in her chair, pondering for a long time. Her furrowed brow never relaxed.","Meeting with Zeng Boyan had to be kept secret from Yang Cena, and when meeting with Yang Cena, Zeng Boyan had to pretend ignorance. This likely meant the defection wasn’t genuine.","Thoughts surged through her mind like threads, and it took considerable mental effort just to untangle them.","\"On the surface, it looks like Huo Chong has defected to Yang Cena. But in reality, he’s outwardly compliant while inwardly rebellious. It’s highly likely that the defection is fake and being a mole is the real goal.\"","\"By earning Yang Cena’s trust, he could help Ningzhou take down Panzhou. Then, one way or another, he could still march on the imperial court to avenge himself.\"","Song Qiming said, \"For Ningzhou to attack Panzhou would be far more difficult than for Panzhou to attack Ningzhou.\"","Song Shixue raised her hand. \"I feel that Zeng Boyan’s attitude toward Yang Cena is unusual. It’s as if he’s one of Yang Cena’s men.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile and praised unhesitatingly, \"Clever.\"","\"Huo Chong is very likely using the excuse of revenge to win Yang Cena’s trust. Zeng Boyan is the son of Zeng Qing, and Yang Cena couldn’t possibly be unaware of the connection between Zeng Qing and the Wu family army. Pretending they’re not close is a way to lower Yang Cena’s guard.\"","\"By helping Yang Cena become clan leader, and then, when Panzhou attacks Ningzhou, the two of them can stab him in the back from the front and the rear. It’s entirely possible for Ningzhou to take Panzhou.\"","Song Qiming slammed his right fist into his left palm, his eyes flashing with sharp brilliance.","\"If that’s the case, Panzhou’s casualties will be significant. We only need to sit back and reap the spoils, waiting until both sides are worn out from fighting before we make our move.\"","Song Jinzhao tilted her chin back, rotating her stiff neck.","\"Keep watching Huo Chong. Once they leave Suining City, double our manpower in both Panzhou and Ningzhou. Monitor their every move closely.\""]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487: It can't be that he wants his son dead","paragraphs":["Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong woke up an hour later and stood at the courtyard entrance. Under the osmanthus tree, Song Anhao swung his sword in a downpour of sweat, his face and neck drenched.","Seeing a maid carrying the morning meal past them, Gu Baozhu casually asked, “When did your young master wake up?”","The maid paused and replied respectfully, “He rose an hour ago.”","Calculating the time, the two figured Song Anhao had gotten up before the hour of Mao (around five to seven in the morning).","The door to the adjacent study opened, and Song Jinzhao, along with three others, emerged.","As they reached the courtyard entrance, they spotted Gu Baozhu and Gu Jinghong standing ahead.","“What are you standing here for? The morning meal is ready in the inner hall.”","In the rear courtyard of the government office, guards and maids were stationed every ten steps. Apart from when they stayed in their rooms, Song Jinzhao was aware of every move the aunt and nephew made.","The two turned around. In the courtyard, Song Anhao had stopped his sword practice. He handed his blade to Yao Ying and returned to his room to wash up.","Quarter of an hour later, at the dining table, Gu Jinghong said to Song Qiming, “My aunt and I will stay in Suining for a few more days. Let the constables take the threshing machine with them, and I’d trouble you, Brother Song, to deliver my letter as well.”","Last night, no matter how hard he tried, Gu Baozhu refused to leave. And since he couldn’t bear to leave her alone, Gu Jinghong had to compromise.","Gu Baozhu, with a wonton in her mouth, watched Gu Jinghong speak without making a sound.","After breakfast, Song Anhao took Song Jinzhao’s hand.","“Elder Sister, I’m going to the bookshop today. Do you want to come with me?” He couldn’t wait to dive into things.","Song Jinzhao wiped a grain of rice from the corner of his mouth with her handkerchief.","“Can it be this afternoon?”","Song Anhao nodded without hesitation.","“Alright, I’ll go to the academy this morning then.”","The assignments given by the academy tutor were completed by Song Anhao, but he rarely attended classes.","He mostly met the tutor alone, and in the evenings, Song Qiming would often test his knowledge.","They demanded that even if he were to go into business later in life, his scholarly achievements should not be lacking.","When Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue arrived at the inn, the physician brought by Zeng Boyan had already been waiting for some time.","Knowing that Yang Cennan’s follow-up treatment would be handed over to him, the physician felt as if a mountain were pressing down on him, the pressure surging.","First, he examined the three wounds.","“The recovery is going quite well. The sutures can be removed in three days.”","Yang Cennan couldn’t make facial expressions, but his eyes betrayed his mood.","“I would appreciate it if the County Lady teaches him properly. If the subsequent recovery is not satisfactory, it would still be an inconvenience to trouble you again.”","His tone was gentle, yet it carried a faint hint of threat.","Song Jinzhao pulled off her gloves expressionlessly.","The farmer and the snake—if not for having to save him, she would really want to finish him off now.","“Don’t worry, any doctor can learn this.”","She took out a needle case from the medicine box. The slender silver needles glinted, their tips enough to send chills down one’s spine.","Song Jinzhao turned to the physician. “Come here.”","Song Shixue stepped aside to make way for him, eager to stand by and watch. They both couldn’t wait to see the man sent off as soon as possible.","The physician shuffled slowly to Song Jinzhao’s right, his heartbeat thundering like a drum.","According to his diagnosis, there was no chance of recovery for Yang Cennan.","But Song Jinzhao claimed there was. If the recovery went poorly back in Panzhou, with five hundred miles between Panzhou and Suining, she wouldn’t be held responsible—he would be the one to suffer.","“My skills are shallow, so I beg the County Lady to speak slowly. I’ll write everything down.”","Catching the reluctance in his tone, Song Jinzhao said, “Don’t sell yourself short. If your skills were truly shallow, the Pacification Commissioner of Panzhou wouldn’t have sent you here. He surely doesn’t want his son to die.”","The physician looked at Song Jinzhao in disbelief, nearly dropping his paper and brush.","He swallowed nervously, utterly unable to respond.","Yang Cennan lay quietly against the bed, his expression unreadable. No one could guess what he was thinking."]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488: The First Restorative Acupuncture Treatment","paragraphs":["The room was as quiet as water. Song Jinzhao picked up a three-edged needle and quickly pricked Yang Cena’s points behind his ears and at his ten acupoints on his fingertips.","“The brain’s meridians are blocked, and the tendons are obstructed. First, we need to open the orifices, then unblock the pathways.”","The tip of the needle gradually turned a dark purple. Yang Cena clenched his fists tightly, his eyes shut, and his jaw nearly clenched to the point of breaking.","Each prick wasn’t particularly painful, but the continuous, unrelenting stabs felt like venomous insects and snakes burrowing into his brain, gnawing at the flesh. His scalp tingled, and his temples throbbed with a sharp, pulsing ache.","Song Jinzhao put away the three-edged needle and switched to a finer silver needle.","“Don’t move. Relax. I’m about to begin.”","Yang Cena’s eyes flew open, staring at her in disbelief.","“Now you start? How much more will it hurt than before?”","Song Jinzhao twisted the silver needle and said calmly, “It won’t hurt. It might sting a little when it first goes in, like an ant bite.”","She glanced at the house physician, who was writing furiously. “Take notes first. This isn’t just a one-time thing. You’ll need to be here every day from now on.”","The physician stopped writing and looked up. A drop of ink fell onto the paper and spread into a blotch.","Yang Cena closed his eyes again. He found that it didn’t hurt as much as before, and his tense nerves gradually relaxed.","The silver needles lined up along the acupuncture points and meridians, forming three rows across the top of his head. “Lean back and rest for two quarters of an hour. Bring the charcoal brazier over.”","An L-shaped iron bucket covered the brazier, with its end pointed at the back of Yang Cena’s head to provide continuous heat.","“The temperature shouldn’t be too high or too low. It should feel like a hot towel draped over the body.”","The house physician nodded respectfully, his gaze lingering on the charcoal brazier and the L-shaped iron bucket with evident surprise.","Usually, patients were made to sit in a bath. How had she come up with this tool for acupuncture?","Song Jinzhao explained the principles of the restorative treatment in great detail to the house physician, nearly pulling out a textbook to illustrate her points.","Gu Baozhu had been standing in the room initially, but she grew bored listening and eventually stepped outside to wait.","She looked into the distance, then at the surroundings, and gradually her attention was drawn to the corridor and the cavalry posted downstairs.","After two quarters of an hour, Song Jinzhao pulled out all the silver needles from Yang Cena’s head.","“Treating the after-effects of a brain injury is a lengthy process. There are things to pay attention to: daily routine, habits, and diet.”","Song Shixue handed a sheet of paper covered in instructions to Yang Zhong.","When unrolled, it was half as long as Yang Zhong himself, densely packed with nearly a hundred rules. It left him utterly bewildered.","How was this any different from caring for a pregnant woman?","On the way back to the medical clinic, Gu Baozhu looked at Song Jinzhao with some concern.","“The soldiers stationed at the inn have eyes as fierce as wolves, and there are no constables around. I can’t help but feel uneasy.”","Song Shixue chimed in, “The inn is right next to the clinic. If anything happens, we’ll see it from the doorway.”","Song Jinzhao turned around. “The patrolling constables go by once every hour to check on them.”","“Right now, Yang Cena’s only thought is to return to Panzhou as soon as possible. They won’t cause trouble in Suining.”","Gu Baozhu took a deep breath and nodded, but the worry in her eyes didn’t fade.","“The sooner they leave, the better. Having them here always makes me uneasy.”","After returning to the clinic, Song Jinzhao left shortly afterward. Gu Baozhu and Lanxi stayed behind to keep Song Shixue company.","Once the “open for business” sign was hung, Song Shixue was busy before long.","Gu Baozhu sat in a chair, staring blankly at the busy Song Shixue. Her gaze traveled from her shoes to the top of her head, and her thoughts gradually drifted to her age.","Shixue was eighteen this year, two years older than herself. County Princess Linghui was even past twenty. Yet neither of them ever seemed worried about marriage.","Thinking about how Gu Zhongxun and his wife kept urging her to get married, Gu Baozhu let out several long sighs. All the energy and spirit she had—both on her face and in her heart—drained away."]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489: Going to the Bookshop","paragraphs":["The Xue family bookbindery was located on the second street from the outer city to the inner city. Beyond that, all the houses were standalone structures with rice paddies in front.","The narrow, double-leaf wooden door was flanked by two elm trees that blocked all the light from the courtyard. At first glance, the place looked not only cluttered but also damp.","Knowing that a new owner was coming, the bookbindery manager had brought the workers out early to wait at the entrance.","The Gu family had sold off all their shops and land in Suining City over the years, bit by bit. Now, only the bookstore and the bookbindery remained open.","Songzhou City was two hundred li away, and the Gu family rarely paid it any mind. The business had been losing money year after year, and their own circumstances were hardly prosperous.","With a sudden change of ownership, everyone was panicked, afraid of losing their jobs.","Song Jinzhao’s gaze was drawn to the worn tiles on the eaves.","A quick look showed several of them chipped and cracked—clearly old and posing a safety hazard.","Stepping through the cluttered yard into the workshop, a cloud of dust mixed with the smell of ink and paper rushed toward her face.","Song Jinzhao immediately held her breath. On a ten-meter-long worktable lay carved wooden printing blocks, the ink on the brushes still wet.","The manager nervously stole glances at Song Jinzhao, trying to read every expression on her face, wondering if she was pleased or displeased.","Though the official deed listed Song Anhao as the owner, he was so young that everyone assumed the real decision-maker was Song Jinzhao.","She stopped beside the worktable. One of the printing blocks was carved with The Three Character Classic.","A single block was divided into a dozen small grids, each grid representing one page.","Ink was evenly brushed onto the raised characters, a sheet of paper was laid over it, and a clean brush was gently pressed across the surface. The text was thus transferred to the paper. After drying, the sheets were cut and bound into books. That was the entire printing process of the bindery.","The manager gestured. “This is the Three Character Classic printing room. Further inside, we have The Hundred Family Surnames, The Analects, and The Book of Songs.”","Crossing the threshold led to another identical printing room, the only difference being the carved blocks on the tables.","Song Anhao’s eyes were bright with joy as he ran about the printing rooms, as if this was his own conquered kingdom.","“The second half of The Cry for Justice will be finished in five days. We need to start making the printing blocks as soon as possible.”","“Manager Lou, does the bookstore have any skilled block carvers we can hire?”","Song Jinzhao watched quietly.","The manager hesitated, glancing at her first, then turned to Song Anhao when she remained silent.","“We did, but that was more than a decade ago.”","“The bookstore hasn’t replaced the blocks in a long time. Most of the skilled carvers have gone to Songzhou City. The few ordinary ones who stayed have switched trades.”","Song Anhao bit his lip, his brows furrowing. “Can we still find anyone?”","The manager thought for a moment. “We can find people, but I’m worried that after so long without practice, their carving won’t be good. It would be best to hire carvers from Songzhou City.”","The book would be finished in a few days, and proofreading would take some time, so there was still room.","Song Anhao said, “Then go to Songzhou City and hire them. Bring them here to carve.”","The manager asked further, “How many characters does this manuscript have? How many carvers should we hire?”","“More than a hundred thousand characters. Hire several carvers—I want it done quickly.”","Printing earlier meant selling earlier; every extra day of waiting was a cost.","The manager explained slowly, “A skilled carver can carve about a hundred characters a day. Their wages range from seven to ten coins per day, and we also have to cover their room, board, and travel expenses.”","He lowered his head, his voice dropping to barely a whisper.","“And then there’s the cost of the wood. Sending someone to Songzhou also costs travel money. Right now, there’s not a single coin in the accounts. We need an advance.”","The workers certainly couldn’t front the money themselves, and the manager dared not. They still had no trust in the new owners.","Thinking of his own empty savings, Song Anhao couldn’t help but glance at Song Jinzhao.","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow.","Song Anhao understood at once.","He immediately instructed the manager, “Calculate the total amount needed and submit a written request. If anything comes up, you can find me at the government office at any time.”"]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490: Shock Song Anhao Thought of Movable-Type Printing","paragraphs":["On the carriage ride back to the mansion, Song Anhao rested her head against the carriage wall, motionless, her unfocused gaze clearly indicating she was lost in thought.","Song Jinzhao found this strange—just moments ago, she had been brimming with enthusiasm, ready to take on the world. Why had she suddenly deflated?","“Don’t worry about the money. In the beginning, I’ll cover it for you, little sister.”","Song Anhao snapped back to reality and shook her head, a hint of worry in her eyes.","“That’s not what I’m thinking about. As I was leaving the bookshop, it suddenly hit me how many printing blocks we’ll need to carve for all those storybooks in the future.”","“Each one is over a hundred thousand characters. Just carving them out would require three or four craftsmen working for months—not only costly but also time-consuming. What if I could carve each character individually, then assemble only the ones I need? Would that work?”","A handkerchief slipped onto her clothes, but Song Jinzhao was staring at Song Anhao in astonishment.","For an eight-year-old to think of something so innovative without any prompting—printing with individual movable type was the very principle behind movable-type printing.","“Elder sister?” Seeing her sister staring blankly at her, Song Anhao tilted her head questioningly.","“I only said one thing—why are you so shocked?”","Song Jinzhao blinked slowly, then leaned back against the carriage wall, lingering in a daze.","“It’s a good idea. You can find a craftsman to make a prototype and test it out.”","Song Anhao pressed her finger to her chin, her gaze dropping in thought. “I’ll have to discuss it with Manager Lou first. They’re the experts, after all.”","Pausing for a moment, he looked up with a bright smile, then eagerly lifted the carriage curtain and called for the driver to stop.","“I’m heading back to the publishing house now. If this works out, we won’t have to go through all that trouble anymore.”","Watching him jump off the carriage, Song Jinzhao pushed aside the curtain and leaned her head out.","The small figure, framed by the guards, suddenly seemed larger in her eyes. A thought sprang to her mind:","Song Anhao would certainly succeed in creating movable-type printing. And it wouldn’t take long.","Qingshuang lifted the carriage curtain and asked, “County Mistress, shall we still return home?”","With the young master gone, there wasn’t much reason to go back.","Song Jinzhao glanced at the stream of people outside the window.","“The autumn harvest starts today. Let’s go outside the city and take a look.”","Qingshuang steered the carriage around. On the road, she noticed a few commoner households outside the outer city already beginning to harvest their rice.","Song Jinzhao decided to hang the curtain open and sat down by the carriage door.","The sunlight blazed, warm on her face.","Using a sickle to cut the rice, ear by ear—they must be sweating buckets in the heat.","When they reached the wasteland the government had reclaimed outside the city, Song Jinzhao could see the golden rice paddies stretching into the distance, filled with figures.","On the already cleared plots of land sat several foot-pedaled threshing machines, with people busy using them nearby.","“County Mistress, the eldest young master is over there,” Qingshuang pointed toward a figure on a distant ridge.","Dressed in an official robe and riding a horse, he was easy to spot.","Song Jinzhao stepped down from the carriage, and Qingshuang quickly opened an umbrella to follow her.","The constables stationed along the ridges immediately bowed as they recognized her.","“Looks like it’s big sister,” Song Qiming said from afar, craning his neck for a better look.","Her peach-red dress stood out vividly against the ridge.","Urging his horse forward another two steps, he recognized her face and broke into a grin.","He dismounted, leaving Guyue Hong far behind him.","“Big sister, why are you here?”","Song Jinzhao smiled gently. “I knew the autumn harvest started today, so I came to see.”","Song Qiming naturally took the umbrella from her hand and leaned close to her side.","“All the marked premium rice has already been harvested in advance. They’re threshing now. Would you like to go take a look?”","Song Jinzhao nodded. “Sure, let’s see how the yields compare.”"]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491: Output Increases by 30%","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghong couldn’t help but feel a surge of emotion as he watched the brother and sister sharing an umbrella.","Song Qiming, already a prefect of Suining at the fifth rank, was personally holding the umbrella for Song Jinzhao, with half his shoulder exposed to the rain.","All the marked rice stalks had been cut and transported to the empty hut beside the labor camp.","The quantity was small, and when piled together, it only reached Song Qiming’s height.","Liu Hucheng spotted them entering and hurried over to report.","“Paying respects to the Lady of Linghui,” he said.","Then, his eyes lit up as he turned to Song Qiming.","“Your Excellency, all the marked rice from the nearby villages has been brought back.”","“After threshing and weighing, each hundred ears of rice yields thirty percent more grain than ordinary ones.”","A flicker of brightness passed through Song Jinzhao’s eyes.","A universal increase of thirty percent—after several rounds of cultivation, the yield would surely rise even higher.","Song Qiming strode over to two barrels with an expression of excitement.","He grabbed a handful of the high-yield rice and examined it closely. His heart pounded as if it might leap from his chest.","Upon closer inspection, the grains in the left barrel were noticeably plumpier than those in the right.","He carefully peeled off the outer husk: the rice on the left was also cleaner, brighter, and covered in a translucent sheen.","Song Qiming turned to Liu Hucheng and gave orders.","“Thresh and dry all the ears immediately. Not a single mistake is allowed.”","Next year, these would be used for sowing, and the quantity of high-yield seeds could multiply by hundreds of times. In just a few years, farmers across the land would be able to plant this productive rice.","Gu Jinghong cupped a handful of rice, his gaze flickering. In the end, he dismissed the thought of taking some back with him.","It would be unseemly to pluck the fruit of others’ hard work. Better to return and share the method with Grandfather. If Suining could find such seeds, Songzhou surely could too.","Or, he could wait until next year, when this batch of high-yield rice had been cultivated, and then request a portion.","He smiled and congratulated Song Qiming: “When this rice seed benefits millions in the future, your name will surely go down in history.”","Song Qiming’s joy-filled gaze settled on Song Jinzhao’s face, his chest swelling with pride.","“If anyone deserves the credit, it’s Sister. I never imagined the yield gap would be so obvious.”","Song Jinzhao crushed a grain of rice between her fingers. The flour was naturally milky white, carrying a faintly sweet, floury smell, with a rich rice fragrance.","“This is only the first step. The subsequent planting is equally crucial. Even if these are high-yield seeds now, the next crop might not produce as much. We must continuously weed out the inferior to stabilize their quality.”","Song Qiming quickly nodded. In his heart, his sister’s words were like an imperial decree—he had to listen and put in every ounce of effort to carry them out.","Walking out of the hut and looking at the laborers threshing rice with a machine in the fields, Song Jinzhao turned and asked, “Are there any extra threshing machines left in the county office?”","“Are they being sold?”","The light in Song Qiming’s eyes grew even brighter than before.","“I’ve already sent people to promote the threshing machines among wealthy families who own hundreds of acres of good farmland in the city. We’ve also delivered two to each village. Those who want to use them can pay a fee based on the acreage. Of course, they can’t use them for free—we need to recover the manufacturing costs.”","Gu Jinghong raised his eyebrows in surprise.","As expected, he was cut from the same cloth as Song Anhao—the blood of commerce ran in his veins.","Song Jinzhao nodded slightly, very satisfied with both measures.","“Send four more machines to the east, south, west, and north gates of the inner city. There are plenty of people there. Have the constables demonstrate them on the spot for the public—news will spread faster that way.”","Song Qiming nodded vigorously, his chin moving like a chicken’s beak, and immediately ordered the constables to carry it out."]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492: The usage fee for one mu of land is only twenty wen.","paragraphs":["Song Qiming gave the order, and within just one hour, the threshing machines and rice were delivered to all four city gates.","At the south gate of the inner city, yamen runners in official uniforms held handfuls of rice stalks and fed them into the threshing machine to remove the grains, steadily pedaling with their right feet.","As the cylinder spun, the grains fell like rain into the tub below.","The gathered crowd watched in amazement, drawing closer and closer, until some even started asking the yamen runners questions.","“Officer, what is this device?”","With just a pump of the foot, it could thresh rice far faster than beating it by hand.","The yamen runner in charge of introductions lifted his chin. “This is a pedal-operated threshing machine. It was invented by County Princess Linghui specifically for autumn harvests, to thresh rice ears.”","“With this, one person can finish threshing the rice ears from a whole mu of paddy in a single day—many times faster than before.”","An old farmer with a hunched back trembled, stretching his neck to peer into the tub, as if checking whether the grains were damaged.","Seeing this, the yamen runner immediately grabbed a handful of grains and showed them.","“Each grain is distinct, not a single broken husk.”","“And look at the stripped stalks—aren’t they clean?”","He held out a handful of rice stalks to the old farmer, who pinched the husks with his fingers. Not a single grain remained—cleaner than their own hand-threshing.","The old farmer opened his mouth as if to say something, then swallowed his words.","It was made of wood and iron, and so big—it must be expensive.","He slowly turned to leave, but after a few steps, he couldn’t help coming back.","Maybe it’s cheap. Asking won’t cost silver.","“How much silver for this threshing machine?”","The other farmers who also needed to harvest their rice all stared intently. They too wanted to know how much it would cost to buy one.","The yamen runner smiled and held up two fingers.","“At cost, it’s twenty taels of silver. If you have lots of land, consider buying one; if you only have one or two mu, just borrow from your village.”","“The prefect in his kindness has already sent two threshing machines to each village. If you want to use them, you pay a usage fee based on the land—twenty coppers per mu.”","Hearing this price, many people had their hearts set on it.","After all, threshing a single mu by hand would take a family of five two whole days without rest.","With a threshing machine, one person could finish it in one day, freeing up hands and time for other work.","A day of hard labor earned forty coppers; during autumn harvest, wealthy households hiring laborers paid twenty coppers a day plus a meal.","At the very least, one could chop more firewood, weave some bamboo baskets, and bring them to town to sell for some cash—still better than hand-threshing.","The old farmer grew so excited he tried to grab the yamen runner’s wrist.","“Officer, my home is in Han Family Village. Have the threshing machines for our village arrived yet?”","The yamen runner nodded without hesitation.","“This morning, all the machines for each village were delivered to the towns. By the time they reach here, they should already have been shipped.”","The old farmer’s face wrinkled with joy, his eyes disappearing into creases.","“Good, good, good—I’ll head back right now.”","He said “good” three times, swiftly turned, and pushed through the crowd, moving nimbly with his legs.","After pedaling for a while, the yamen runner felt a bit tired and noticed the onlookers all itching to try.","He immediately stepped aside and called out, “Who wants to give it a go?”","In a flash, seven or eight men rushed forward, and the noise exploded. Another yamen runner quickly hurried over to block them.","“No pushing, everyone line up.”","Gu Baozhu, curious, walked out from behind the door of the medical hall and looked westward.","“What’s going on over there? Why so noisy?”","Muttering, she stepped down from the stairs toward the city gate. Seeing the big crowd from afar, curiosity got the better of her, and she immediately ran over to join the fun.","Spotting the villagers gathered around a strange machine, she murmured to herself.","“Is this the pedal threshing machine Jinghong mentioned?”","She squeezed to the front, wanting to try it herself, but saw a queue of dozens of people and had to give up.","If only she had gone to take a look first this morning when her big nephew sent the threshing machines to Songzhou City.","In the end, Gu Baozhu watched the excitement for half an hour before returning to the medical hall.","Song Shixue was just seeing off a patient and, noticing Baozhu’s boredom, said, “How about we go shopping tomorrow afternoon?”","Gu Baozhu’s low mood immediately lifted, and her eyebrows danced.","“Great! These past few days, it’s been the same routine with no time to properly browse. I didn’t bring enough clothes, so it’s the perfect chance to buy a couple.”"]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493: The official in charge disapproved of developing movable-type printing","paragraphs":["On the other side, Song Anhao returned to the bookshop and shared his ideas with Manager Lou.","On the desk, the ink on a half-written application was still wet. Manager Lou pondered for a moment, but did not agree with this move.","\"Boss, there are tens of thousands of characters in this world. Even if we carved every single one, looking for them when needed would be like finding a needle in a haystack.\"","\"Very few workers in our bookshop are literate. As long as the woodblocks remain unchanged, anyone can work on them. But if we change them, things will only get more troublesome.\"","Then, he explained the technical difficulties to Song Anhao one by one.","\"Wood deforms easily when exposed to water. If each piece is different, the surface won’t be level, and the printing will either fail or result in blurred and missing strokes. Repeated disassembly will also damage the blocks.\"","\"For classics like the Four Books and Five Classics, which haven’t changed in a thousand years, a single set of woodblocks can last decades or even centuries. Reprinting costs next to nothing. If we follow your idea of repeatedly disassembling and reassembling the blocks, costs will actually go up—it’s simply not worth the effort.\"","Song Anhao pressed his lips together, his brows knitting into two little knots.","What the other person said made sense, but difficulty didn’t mean it shouldn’t be done.","\"Books like the Four Books and Five Classics, which stay the same for millennia, can still use our current printing method. The woodblocks are already there.\"","\"But if more and more storybooks keep popping up like grass, carving new blocks each time will be expensive, and printing them in small runs wouldn’t be cost-effective either.\"","\"A book with a hundred thousand words contains many repeated characters. Printing one page and then breaking down those blocks to reuse them could save costs.\"","\"Besides, we wouldn’t just print books. We could take on poetry collections, government notices—anything. With just a bit of reordering, we could handle jobs of any size.\"","Song Anhao paced around the room, thinking as he moved.","Finally, he pointed to the wooden blocks on the desk and said, \"If wood is prone to deformation, we can use other materials instead.\"","He tilted his head in thought. \"We could use clay to carve, then fire it—just like making porcelain.\"","\"Or, we could use iron or copper. Hmm—iron rusts, so copper is better. First, carve a negative impression in wood, then pour in molten copper. It wouldn’t deform for thousands of years.\"","\"And as for the trouble of finding characters, that’s easy to solve. Organize them by stroke order and group them in different areas. We won’t need many literate workers. Just divide the work and assign people to specialize in that.\"","Song Anhao shot down each objection one by one, leaving Manager Lou speechless.","He stammered, \"What you’re describing demands incredibly high skills from the craftsmen. Not only carvers, but also woodworkers and metalworkers would need to oversee everything to ensure success. It’s likely far more complicated than it sounds, and the costs won’t be small.\"","Song Anhao lifted his chin with a serious expression.","\"The more we spend now, the less we’ll spend later. In the long run, it’s pure profit. Just send someone to Songzhou City to find the best craftsmen. If we can create a new printing method, our bookshop will be the very forefront of the entire industry.\"","Manager Lou’s lips opened and closed like a goldfish spitting bubbles.","Where on earth had these novel terms come from? They sounded grand, but he only half understood them.","If he said he didn’t understand, he could almost guess the general meaning—but if he said he understood, he truly had never heard such words before.","\"Since you’ve made up your mind, Boss, I’ll follow your orders.\"","Song Anhao nodded with satisfaction. \"Send someone out tomorrow. I’ll have the banknotes delivered later today.\"","Manager Lou lowered his head, sighing inwardly.","Developing a new printing technique—how could that be so easy? Who knew how many failures lay ahead? Was County Princess Linghui really on board with this?","He suppressed his reluctance and tried to change his way of thinking.","If the boss was willing to put up the money, he’d just do the work. If it succeeded, it would be a good thing after all.","By evening, Yao Ying delivered the banknotes. The next day, Manager Lou dispatched his most capable subordinate to set off."]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494: Not Enough, Half Price After All Leased Out","paragraphs":["The threshing machine had only been in the village for a day when the village heads from every settlement came running to the Village Head’s home to complain.","“Every household is harvesting rice, and two threshing machines are far from enough. Last night, Niu Laosan and Niu Datou in our village nearly came to blows. Village Head, how about you go to the county office and ask for two more?”","Another village head pointed at the scratch marks on his face.","“I got these yesterday fighting over the threshing machine. Every family has three or four mu of fields, and they won’t stand for having to wait for dozens of days.”","“...”","Five of them babbled on all at once, crowding in front of the Village Head, forcing him to step back until his back hit the wall before he raised his hand to stop them.","He bellowed, “All of you, shut up!”","Spittle sprayed across the faces of the five village heads, some of it even flying into their mouths.","In an instant, all five mouths snapped shut, and the room fell into an eerie silence.","The Village Head took a deep breath and sighed. “Having two machines is already a blessing. You should be grateful. People in other places don’t have even one—they still thresh by hand, beating the grain with their hands.”","His brow furrowed tightly, the wrinkles between his eyebrows like two small hills.","“If you can’t manage in time, just cut the rice and bring it back first. When your turn comes, then you can thresh it slowly.”","One of the village heads said, “Slowly? When will that ever happen? Everyone’s waiting to dry the grain and sell it for money.”","The Village Head’s face darkened as he roared, “If you can’t wait, then thresh it by hand. There are hundreds of villages in Suining City—if every one of them wanted two more machines, think of the chaos.”","“If you think it’s too slow, then pool your own money and go buy them at the county office.”","The five men were struck silent.","Twenty coppers per mu was cheap enough, but no one could afford a threshing machine costing twenty silver taels.","After great effort, the Village Head managed to shoo the village heads away. He then sat on a long bench in the main hall, pondering for a long time.","He stood up, walked outside, and faced the still-high sun, puffing out three breaths of frustration.","Finally, he said to his son in resignation, “Harness the ox cart and take me to the county office.”","What the Village Head didn’t expect was that when he arrived at the county office, he ran into two other Village Heads.","As the three of them crossed the threshold, they heard someone inside already pressing a clerk for threshing machines.","The three exchanged glances, and in an instant, they charged forward as if their feet were on fire.","“Sir, our town is also short...”","Two quarters of an hour later, Shi Simian took the compiled data and found Song Qiming.","“Sir, the Village Heads from seven or eight townships all say two threshing machines aren’t enough—they want more.”","Having anticipated high demand for rentals, the county office had already ordered the craftsmen to work through the night to produce more, but now they had no surplus.","Song Qiming looked at the list, noting the quantities each village had requested and the final total.","“How many threshing machines are left in the warehouse?”","Shi Simian replied, “We sold three hundred eighty today. There are one hundred twenty left. If we send them to the villages, there’ll be none left to sell.”","Song Qiming said without hesitation, “Harvest season is urgent. Rent out these hundred twenty to the people first.”","“Also, immediately gather all the craftsmen in the city to work overnight and improve efficiency.”","Shi Simian’s face grew even more distressed.","“The harvest season only lasts a few days. If we rent out so many, how will we recover the cost?”","“Originally, fifty households were sharing one machine. Adding two more drops it to twenty-five per machine. If we store them after this year and use them next year, it’ll take years to recoup the cost. It’s really not worth it.”","Tapping his fingers repeatedly on the desk, Song Qiming thought of a solution.","He looked up at Shi Simian. “After the harvest, sell the rented threshing machines at half price. If one family can’t afford it, encourage a village to pool funds and buy one collectively. Divided among households, it won’t be much money.”","Shi Simian’s lips parted slightly, his throat clogged for a moment before he nodded.","“Your subordinate obeys. But it’d be best to announce this only after the harvest; otherwise, no one will buy now.”","Song Qiming nodded. “I’m leaving this to you. Production must be ramped up by tonight. Surplus machines should be sent to the four counties of Songhe, Yunzhu.”","“No need for rentals—sell them directly.”","Shi Simian nodded again, this time slowly. As he left, his steps felt unsteady, as if floating."]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495: Mid-month in the Valley: Receiving the Threshing Machine","paragraphs":["Two days later, at the government office of Songzhou City.","Gu Zhongxun looked at the foot-operated threshing machine that had been unloaded from the carriage with a puzzled expression.","“What is this?”","The courier responsible for delivering the letter handed both the memorial and the letter to him.","After reading the letter, a flash of surprise crossed Gu Zhongxun’s eyes. He walked around the threshing machine to inspect it, bending down to examine the rotating drum and the grain-removing teeth attached to it.","“Someone, bring me a bundle of unthreshed rice stalks.”","Spreading out the design drawings and usage instructions that Song Qiming had included in his memorial, Gu Zhongxun paced back and forth anxiously.","Not long after, a runner came back carrying a pile of rice stalks. The golden rice ears scratched his face with both pain and itch.","Gu Zhongxun quickly grabbed a handful of rice stalks and stepped onto the pedal.","Slowly pressing the pedal with his right foot, he guided the rice ears toward the rotating drum as it turned.","The husks rattled off as the grains were struck down, some falling directly into the collection bin, others bouncing off the wooden panels and landing back inside. In just a few steps, the handful of stalks was completely threshed.","Seeing the layer of grain at the bottom of the bin, Gu Zhongxun broke into a delighted smile.","“Someone, summon the craftsmen immediately to manufacture these threshing machines. It’s the autumn harvest—speed is essential.”","Absent-mindedly, he tightened his grip on the drawing, and accidentally tore through the paper with too much force.","He quickly loosened his hold to check that the illustrations and text were unharmed, then breathed a sigh of relief.","Back inside the room, he gazed at the words in the memorial and sighed inwardly.","“If only these had come two months earlier. By now, even if I sent them to the capital, this year’s autumn harvest would already be over.”","Muttering to himself, Gu Zhongxun still copied the drawing exactly, preparing to send one to the capital.","Since it wouldn’t make it in time for this year anyway, he decided to simply build one threshing machine as a sample and send it along as well.","An hour later, Gu Gaoyuan returned from outside the city, still covered in chaff that hadn’t been brushed off.","“I went to look at that threshing machine just now. Why didn’t Song Qiming send it over sooner? Many families who cut and thresh alongside each other have already finished their harvest.”","Gu Zhongxun handed him the letter written by Gu Jinghong.","“County Princess Linghui thought up the idea of building the threshing machine after seeing the autumn harvest. They moved as fast as they could.”","Gu Gaoyuan took the letter, and after a long moment, an even deeper surprise appeared in his eyes.","He raised a question: “Cultivating high-yield rice? Can that really work?”","Gu Zhongxun did not answer immediately. He pondered for a long while before taking a deep breath.","“County Princess Linghui is exceptionally clever. Most things she sets her mind to will likely succeed.”","Gu Gaoyuan glanced at the letter in his hand.","“She went out and lost herself in fun. It’s been almost half a month, and she still hasn’t thought about coming back.”","On this note, Gu Zhongxun was indifferent.","“They played for several days along the road. Baozhu and the Second Miss of the Song family have similar temperaments, and Baozhu is still eager to meet County Princess Linghui. It will probably be a while before she returns.”","Gu Gaoyuan joked, “If Mother hadn’t been nagging her to marry so much, then little sister wouldn’t have run away from home.”","Gu Zhongxun shot him a stern glare. “If your mother hears you say that, she’ll be angry.”","Gu Gaoyuan sighed and shook his head.","“In my opinion, little sister is still young. There’s no rush to marry her off. It would be better to let her stay home a few more years.”","Gu Zhongxun said crossly, “You don’t have a daughter, so of course, you’re not in a hurry.”","“Baozhu is sixteen this year. From betrothal to marriage, there’s still half a year to go. As of now, there’s not even a hint of a match in sight. And she keeps saying she doesn’t want to marry at all. Why wouldn’t your mother be anxious?”","Gu Gaoyuan countered, “The Second Miss of the Song family is two years older than little sister, yet she hasn’t married either.”","“Given our family’s status, even two years later, matchmakers would still flock to our door.”","Gu Zhongxun’s anger faded into gloom. He stared at the ground, speaking with concern.","“The Second Miss of the Song family isn’t married. County Princess Linghui is twenty-two and still unwed. I’m a little worried about your sister spending too much time with them.”","Gu Gaoyuan: “...”"]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496: Gu Baozhu's Troubles","paragraphs":["On Suining's inner city main street, Gu Baozhu linked arms with Song Shixue as they walked into a ready-made clothing shop.","\"The clothes in this shop are even nicer than those in Songzhou City. What do you think of this one?\"","Gu Baozhu picked up a set of light green long dress and held it up against herself.","Song Shixue nodded. \"If you like it, go try it on. There are fitting rooms in the back.\"","Gu Baozhu turned her head and indeed saw several curtained fitting areas set up behind the clothing racks. Several women stood at the entrance, all wearing identical outfits.","\"It seems this shop has no male staff?\"","Song Shixue explained, \"This store only serves female customers. With fitting rooms inside, it's inconvenient to hire male attendants.\"","Gu Baozhu nodded with some understanding and took the dress into a fitting room.","The space was spacious and clean. The shop owner must be quite skilled.","After changing into the new dress, Gu Baozhu stretched out her arms and spun around, a look of delight on her face.","\"How does it look? Is it pretty?\"","Song Shixue pressed her lips into a gentle smile.","\"It looks good. You can pick out a few more pieces.\"","Gu Baozhu looked down, spun around once more, and nodded with satisfaction.","Since the clothes here were so beautiful, she certainly wanted to buy several pieces.","The female attendant waiting nearby let her eyes wander between Gu Baozhu and Song Shixue.","She wondered which young lady's daughter it was that the second young lady herself would accompany.","Gu Baozhu picked out two more outfits, and the female attendant stepped forward enthusiastically to take them.","\"The shop has new jewelry pieces that are unique to other places. Would you like me to bring some over to match with the young lady's clothes?\"","Gu Baozhu paused her hand from selecting clothes. \"Unique to other places?\"","The clothes were special, and the jewelry was unique too?","The female attendant smiled and nodded. \"They were all drawn by our owner herself. I guarantee there's nothing like them anywhere else.\"","She led them up to the second floor. The display cases were filled with various gold and silver jewelry, their dazzling brilliance nearly blinding the eyes.","Song Shixue looked through each piece one by one. The medical clinic kept her busy, and this was her first time on the second floor as well.","She had to admit the pieces were beautifully crafted. Every style was stunning, none lacking in beauty, all truly eye-catching.","With three dresses in different colors and two pieces of jewelry, Gu Baozhu was still asking questions as they went downstairs.","\"Why would such a wonderful shop be opened in Suining City? If it were opened in Songzhou City, business would definitely be booming.\"","They had been inside for about half an hour. The number of customers who came in wasn't very large, but no one who entered left empty-handed.","The female attendant walked to the counter and packed up the clothes and jewelry.","\"The shop has just recently opened. It might expand to Songzhou City after some time.\"","Song Shixue said, \"No need to settle the bill. Just have it delivered directly to the government office.\"","The attendant's hand, which had been reaching for the abacus, stopped, and she turned to close the box instead.","Gu Baozhu quickly untied her coin pouch to pay. \"Don't put it on the account. I'll pay for this myself.\"","Song Shixue smiled and stopped her hand. \"No need. This shop was opened by my elder sister. Consider it a gift to you.\"","Last night, Song Jinzhao had instructed Song Shixue that if Gu Baozhu came to this shop to buy things, and the amount wasn't too much, she shouldn't accept payment.","Gu Baozhu's hand holding the pouch froze.","Her mouth fell open, her eyes filled with surprise. \"County Princess Linghui?\"","Song Shixue nodded and pulled her out of the shop.","\"Elder sister opened it on a whim, but there aren't enough wealthy people in Suining City. Next month, she plans to open another branch in Songzhou City.\"","Recalling what the female attendant had said earlier, Gu Baozhu asked, \"That attendant said the jewelry was drawn by their owner herself. Was that County Princess Linghui too?\"","For one person to excel at everything, it was truly unbelievable.","Song Shixue said, \"Not just the jewelry. Some of the dress designs were also thought up by elder sister.\"","\"But she only sketched a few lines. The tailors and craftsmen perfected the rest.\"","Gu Baozhu bit her lip tightly as she walked, and the words of Madame Gu urging her to marry popped into her head.","She glanced at Song Shixue and finally couldn't hold it in any longer.","She stepped forward, linked arms with her, and covered her mouth as she whispered, \"Shixue, when do you plan to get married?\"","Song Shixue's steps came to a sudden halt like brakes being applied. Her cheeks flushed red, and she secretly glanced at Lanxi following behind them.","She quickly pulled away. \"Why are you asking about that?\"","Gu Baozhu let out a long sigh. \"It's all my mother's doing.\"","\"In the past few months when I was cooped up at home, she kept nagging me day after day, saying I'm at the right age and should get married.\"","\"Later, she even found over a dozen portraits for me to choose from. I had no choice but to drag Jinghong along to Suining City, using the excuse of finding you and the county princess to play.\"","Song Shixue raised an eyebrow. \"You're only sixteen this year, right?\"","Gu Baozhu nodded, her tone very low.","\"My mother said to get engaged this year and marry next year, so I'd just turn seventeen.\"","She hugged Song Shixue's arm tightly and stared at her with burning eyes.","\"Has the county princess ever urged you?\"","Song Shixue lowered her voice so that only the two of them could hear.","\"Neither my elder brother nor my elder sister are married yet. How could I possibly get married?\"","\"A woman's optimal childbearing age is twenty-four. Elder sister and I don't want to marry too early. We're both going to marry into the family and have our husbands take our surname.\"","Gu Baozhu's eyes flew wide open, her eyebrows shot up, and her voice burst out from her throat.","\"Marry into the family! Doesn't your family have two sons?\"","What about Song Qiming and the younger Song Anhao? Did they still need to marry into the family?","Song Shixue hurriedly covered her mouth, looking around to see people staring. She was both embarrassed and flustered.","She quickly moved away. Only when the surroundings were clear did she let go.","With a sheepish expression, she said, \"Why are you shouting so loud?\"","Gu Baozhu quickly apologized, hugged her arm, and pressed her face against it.","\"I was just too shocked earlier. Usually, it's only families with only daughters who want sons-in-law to take the wife's surname.\"","Song Shixue explained, \"All of us siblings—me, my brother and sister, and Anhao—were raised by our eldest sister. Our parents are gone, and we've never thought about leaving home.\"","Gu Baozhu blinked, the shock still churning in her chest.","The relationship among the four Song siblings was truly unexpectedly good.","She hesitated and asked, \"What if your elder brother's future wife doesn't agree?\"","Song Shixue fixed her gaze on her. \"If she doesn't agree, then she won't set foot through the Song family's door.\"","Gu Baozhu stared at her firm expression, her heart jolting.","Song Shixue was serious.","If she herself wanted to marry a man into her family, would her parents agree?","Once the thought emerged, she couldn't stop pondering it.","Gu Baozhu walked a dozen or so steps in a daze, then suddenly stopped and asked, \"You said earlier that a woman's optimal childbearing age is twenty-four?\"","Song Shixue nodded. \"Twenty-four to twenty-nine is the best.\"","\"A woman's full skeleton, especially the pelvis, usually doesn't fully develop until eighteen to twenty years old. In the womb, the fetus takes the nutrients the mother needs.\"","She raised her hand to indicate height. \"You could have grown a bit taller, but if nutrients are taken by the child, you won't grow anymore.\"","\"If the pelvis hasn't fully developed and is relatively narrow, it can easily cause difficult labor during childbirth.\"","Gu Baozhu stared at her blankly. The mere thought of difficult labor sent shivers down her spine.","This was actually a good excuse to refuse marriage.","\"Did County Princess Linghui tell you all this?\"","Song Shixue nodded.","\"It's a pity that women in the world marry too young and have children too early. Even if you tell people, very few pay attention.\"","Gu Baozhu fell silent.","Everyone says to marry at sixteen or seventeen, at the latest by eighteen, and if there's no son within a year, you have to find a concubine for your husband.","Even if she were twenty-four, let alone twenty, he already has several concubines."]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497: Huo Chong Discovers Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan","paragraphs":["On the second floor of Mingyuan Inn, Yang Zhong stood before Huo Chong.","\"The young master is recovering well. We plan to set out for Panzhou in five days.\"","Huo Chong’s expression was slightly troubled. \"I’ve already been delayed too long on this trip. I must leave tomorrow.\"","Yang Zhong nodded. \"With Zeng Boyan guarding the young master, his safety is not a concern. You may return to Ningzhou without worry.\"","\"The young master instructed you to lie low. Only when Panzhou attacks Ningzhou will it be time to employ General Huo.\"","Huo Chong deliberately put on a delighted expression, clenching his fists to convey his impatience for revenge.","\"I hope that day comes soon. Once the southwest is unified, we can send troops against the imperial court.\"","Yang Zhong smiled in response. \"The young master thinks the same.\"","In the adjoining room, a shadow guard pressed a ceramic listening cone against the wall, eavesdropping on their conversation. With his other hand, he swiftly transcribed their words onto paper, ensuring no important detail was missed.","A moment later, Yang Zhong left. Huo Chong stood by the window, gazing down at the street below.","Only when the man’s figure had completely disappeared did the coldness in Huo Chong’s gaze slowly fade.","Just as he turned away, a convoy of granary workers passed by. Two familiar figures caught his attention.","His eyes locked onto them. As they drew nearer, their faces became clearer.","The eye patch covering the right eye. The missing three fingers on the right hand. Without a doubt, it was Guan Nianshan and Qu Ya.","Weren’t they supposed to be at the estate in the capital? What were they doing in Suining City?","Huo Chong blinked in confusion.","Had the County Princess Linghui brought them here?","As their silhouettes shrank into the distance, they vanished around a corner.","He closed the window and sat on a stool, deep in thought for a long time. Eventually, he resolved to get to the bottom of it.","Early the next morning, Huo Chong waited on the second floor. When he spotted the granary workers returning from the outskirts with harvested rice, he rushed downstairs at once.","The wooden planks on the second floor boomed with each footstep.","The shadow guard stationed in the next room immediately raised a telescope, tracking his movements. When he realized Huo Chong was heading toward Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan, his drowsy eyes flew wide open in alert.","After so many days, they were finally making contact.","Qu Ya, walking in the middle of the group, soon spotted Huo Chong. Seeing the man motioning with his eyes, his heart began to race.","He reached out and tapped Guan Nianshan’s arm, tilting his chin slightly in Huo Chong’s direction.","Guan Nianshan followed his gaze and saw Huo Chong as well.","The three exchanged glances. Huo Chong pointed toward Mingyuan Inn.","Qu Ya understood at once and nodded firmly in agreement.","In the back courtyard of the government office:","\"What was the reaction of Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan?\" Song Jinzhao set down his brush slowly.","The shadow guard replied, \"They didn’t speak, but it seemed they arranged a meeting—at Mingyuan Inn.\"","Song Jinzhao ordered, \"Keep watching. Find out what they say.\"","\"Yes.\" The shadow guard nodded and withdrew.","On the two-meter-long desk lay a detailed map of Suining City, including the outer city.","It was marked with buildings, main roads, and a web of interconnected alleyways.","The newly cleared wasteland had limited nutrients. After the autumn harvest, the land needed to rest and could not be planted again.","Over the coming idle months, Song Jinzhao planned to build roads—especially the main thoroughfares.","\"To prosper, build roads first.\" This principle held true in any era.","The existing dirt paths were potholed and difficult to walk on, becoming utterly impassable in the rain.","If Suining City’s living conditions were to improve and more people were to relocate here, infrastructure development was essential—preferably, paved roads made of cement.","Limestone was abundant. To produce quicklime, it would need to be fired. It seemed a lime kiln would have to be built."]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498: The Meeting","paragraphs":["The moonlight was like water, draping a thin veil over the night.","While everyone else was asleep, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan slipped out the back door and headed straight for Mingyuan Inn.","Huo Chong, who had been waiting in a second-floor room for three hours, saw them coming and immediately opened the window wide, waving downstairs.","“Over here,” his voice drifted down like a midnight ghost’s whisper.","The two men hurried into the inn, saw the clerk dozing on the counter, and quietly turned up the stairs.","Only one candle was lit in the room, casting an orange glow across their faces.","Huo Chong couldn’t hold back the question that had tormented him all night.","“Uncle Qu Ya, Uncle Guan, why are you here in Suining City?”","He had wanted to bring them here before, but they hadn’t agreed—yet now they’d come on their own.","Guan Nianshan sighed. “The County Princess discovered the connection between us. She wants to build a good relationship with you, so she brought Qu Ya and me here.”","Huo Chong’s eyes widened, his heart racing with unease.","“Does she know my identity?”","Qu Ya shook his head uncertainly.","“Probably not. We told her your father was a former subordinate of the Wu family’s army, and she never brought up Marquis Wuying.”","Huo Chong breathed a sigh of relief. “That’s what I told her before. At least the stories match.”","Remembering seeing Zeng Boyan at the medical clinic a few days ago, Qu Ya blurted out: “A few days ago, I saw Zeng Qing’s son, Zeng Boyan, at the clinic. Have you contacted Zeng Qing?”","Huo Chong opened his mouth but didn’t reveal his full plan to them.","Instead, he said in a grave tone: “I’ve already reached out to him. Zeng Qing wants to help me, and Zeng Boyan has met with me too.”","“But over the years, they’ve been repeatedly sidelined in Panzhou. Zeng Qing is old and idle at home, and Zeng Boyan doesn’t have many men under his command. They want to help, but it’s beyond their power. Marching on the capital is as futile as a mayfly trying to topple a tree—next to impossible.”","Qu Ya lowered his head, his eyes dimming with despair.","Guan Nianshan rubbed his hands together, his expression hesitant.","The room was so quiet, you could hear the beating of hearts.","“County Princess Linghui is eager to build ties. Will you consider meeting her?”","Huo Chong paused briefly, then shook his head. “Her goodwill is aimed at helping the court stabilize the southwestern tribes.”","“Song Jinzhao is of noble status, and Song Qiming has a bright future ahead. We’re not on the same path.”","Guan Nianshan’s brows drooped; he didn’t know what to say.","Huo Chong looked at them earnestly. “I’m returning to Ningzhou tomorrow. Don’t let Song Jinzhao know I came to Suining.”","The two nodded, but Qu Ya still had doubts.","“Why did the Young Master come to Suining City?”","He must have had a reason; he wouldn’t just travel here for sightseeing.","Huo Chong replied: “Yang Cenan was attacked. Mu Ji’an wanted to know if he would die, so he sent me to check.”","Qu Ya’s pupils shrank. “Did you orchestrate the assassination of Yang Cenan?”","Huo Chong shook his head quickly.","“It has nothing to do with Ningzhou. The assassins were sent by Yang Ruiping’s other two sons. We just wanted to see if Panzhou could be thrown into chaos.”","Guan Nianshan pursed his lips. “Then there’s hope. Yang Cenan has been saved by County Princess Linghui.”","“A wife’s murder and a son’s loss—he’ll definitely seek revenge when he returns.”","Huo Chong looked at their faces, hesitating for a long moment before asking: “I saw you working in the government office. Does Song Jinzhao treat you well?”","Qu Ya was stunned.","Guan Nianshan, on the other hand, smiled as he replied: “Not bad. We have enough to eat and clothes to wear, and the children are studying at the academy.”","“It’s better than the capital. In Suining, we can live in the open without having to hide.”","A faint smile tugged at Huo Chong’s lips. “That’s good to hear. It puts my mind at ease.”","Qu Ya stared at the smiles on their faces, his heart sinking to the bottom of an abyss."]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499: Four Beats One","paragraphs":["On the way back, Guan Nianshan, feeling relaxed, happened to glance sideways and noticed that Qu Ya’s expression looked somewhat unpleasant.","\"You seem very unhappy. Do you think there's no hope for revenge?\"","Qu Ya stopped in his tracks, stood silent for a moment, then slowly raised his head.","\"He didn’t mention taking us to Ningzhou today.\"","Guan Nianshan blinked in surprise and blurted out, \"You want to go to Ningzhou?\"","Qu Ya’s rough lips pressed into a straight line.","\"I don’t know. I just feel a tightness in my chest.\"","After a moment’s hesitation, Guan Nianshan tried to console him. \"Maybe it’s because he knows we’re doing well here with County Princess Linghui, so he didn’t bring it up. After all, that’s Ningzhou.\"","Qu Ya’s brows remained furrowed with worry. He said softly, \"Maybe so.\"","Seeing this, Guan Nianshan went on. \"Actually, going to Ningzhou would do no good for us or for the Young Master.\"","\"The Ningzhou troops are already exclusive. With me blind in one eye and you handicapped in your right hand, they’d probably look down on us.\"","\"If the two of us bring our families along, we wouldn’t even have a place to settle, and we’d only make trouble for the Young Master.\"","Qu Ya stared at Guan Nianshan and asked a deadly question.","\"What if one day the Young Master leads the Ningzhou army to attack Suining City? Whose side would you take? His, or the County Princess’s?\"","The moonlight shone on Qu Ya’s face, and Guan Nianshan felt a shiver in his heart.","He turned his head away in panic. \"How do you know they’ll definitely be enemies? By the time Ningzhou attacks the imperial court, Song Qiming will have already been transferred back to the capital.\"","Qu Ya clenched his jaw, his eyes seeming clouded with a layer of gray haze.","He dropped his gaze to the ground, his chest feeling even heavier.","\"Maybe so.\"","Returning to the government office through the back door, Qu Ya lay on the bed, staring fixedly at the ceiling beams, sleepless all night.","Guan Nianshan, after taking off his clothes and lying down, fell asleep within half an hour.","As the morning mist dissipated and sunlight spilled into the courtyard,","Song Jinzhao stood alone holding the Cloud Spear, facing Song Qiming, Song Shixue, Gu Baozhu, and Gu Jinghong.","In the blink of an eye, Song Qiming struck first.","He lunged at Song Jinzhao with his longsword. After a failed attempt, he quickly circled behind her, and the other three moved simultaneously.","The four formed an encirclement, trapping Song Jinzhao in the middle.","\"Aooo—wooo—\" Xuetuan couldn’t hold back any longer and let out a long howl toward the sky, even raising its front paws.","Song Anhao quickly grabbed its neck. \"Don’t yell. If you charge in, you’ll be done in by Eldest Sister with one spear strike.\"","Xuetuan refused to accept this and nudged him with its snout.","Spear and sword clashed, the metallic ring lasting long without stopping.","Blade scraping against spearhead produced a grating sound that hurt the eardrums.","As sparks flew, before Song Anhao could retreat, Xuetuan turned its head first and hid behind a rock.","Song Anhao rolled his eyes at it in exasperation and muttered, \"Coward.\"","Xuetuan lay still, pretending to be dead.","\"Clang—\"","Gu Jinghong stared blankly at the broken half of his longsword in his hand, his numbed palm barely able to grip the hilt.","After only a dozen exchanges, it broke. Was his sword too poor, or was County Princess Linghui too strong?","Gu Baozhu got up from the ground, panting, her eyes filled with admiration for Song Jinzhao and helplessness at not being able to win.","\"I give up. There’s no way to beat her.\"","In less than the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, several hundred moves had been exchanged. The opponent was too fast—the four of them together couldn’t keep up.","Song Jinzhao thrust the spear into the ground, a hint of disdain in her eyes.","\"You all have too little muscle on you.\"","Gu Baozhu looked at Song Shixue’s arm, then at her own.","It was a bit lacking—a whole size thinner.","Song Qiming walked over to Gu Jinghong.","He picked up the broken half of the blade from the ground. \"This sword is a bit brittle. I’ll give you a good one in a few days.\"","Gu Jinghong caught it with his left hand.","The fracture was clean, without a single grain of metal shavings, which showed just how fast and forceful the strike had been.","\"This was a gift from my father. I never expected it to break.\"","It must have been the sword’s fault. Otherwise, why hadn’t Auntie’s broken?","What he didn’t know was that when Song Jinzhao parried Gu Baozhu, she had used skillful techniques and deliberately held back some of her strength."]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500: Smashing the Room to Restore Memory","paragraphs":["At breakfast, Gu Jinghong’s shoulder still ached a bit. Seeing this, Song Shixue set down her spoon.","“Should I give you a couple of acupuncture needles?”","Gu Jinghong quickly shook his head in refusal. “It’s nothing, just a pulled muscle.”","Song Jinzhao stood up, walked over, and grasped his wrist.","“Relax, let me take a look.”","When his arm was raised nearly to shoulder level, Gu Jinghong suddenly cried out in pain.","He instinctively pulled his hand back, but Song Jinzhao held on without success.","She pressed her thumb firmly into the junction of his shoulder and armpit, pushing downward. A crisp pop sounded, and Gu Jinghong thought his arm had broken.","“You should’ve said it was dislocated earlier.” Song Jinzhao released her grip. “Does it still hurt?”","Gu Jinghong rotated his arm numbly and, realizing the pain was gone, let out a silent breath of relief.","“I thought it was just a strain. I didn’t realize it was dislocated.”","Song Jinzhao returned to her seat. “It was my fault for not controlling my strength. If there’s a next time, I’ll hold back a bit.”","Gu Huaiyuan was a military officer, and he had trained his own son since childhood. Gu Jinghong had shown decent skill when he killed bandits during their first meeting. She’d intended to test his limits but hadn’t expected to injure him.","Gu Jinghong lowered his head to look at the mushroom noodles in his bowl. “It’s not the County Princess’s fault. It’s just that we’re too weak.”","Song Qiming and Song Shixue shot him a speechless look.","If you’re going to call yourself weak, don’t drag us into it. Who isn’t weak when fighting Eldest Sister?","After breakfast, they went to the inn to treat Yang Cenan’s injuries. As they stepped through the threshold, they heard someone smashing things upstairs.","Zeng Boyan came down with a gloomy face, pausing mid-step when he saw Song Jinzhao.","“County Princess, please wait here for a moment. We’ll go up to treat Third Young Master once he’s calmed down.”","Song Jinzhao frowned with displeasure.","“Excessive emotional swings aren’t good for recovery. Didn’t the physician you brought instruct him on that?”","Zeng Boyan sighed. “He did. Third Young Master is raging because he’s fully recalled how the Young Mistress and the Young Master died. None of us can stop him.”","Song Jinzhao was stunned. “His memory has returned?”","Zeng Boyan nodded. “Before, his mind only held fragmented images.”","“Somehow, after just a cup of tea earlier, everything came back.”","The crashing upstairs continued unabated. The innkeeper, standing behind the counter, shook his head in anguish.","Heavens, at this rate, his inn would be torn down.","When their eyes met, the fear and anxiety in the innkeeper’s gaze instantly turned into pleading.","Song Jinzhao turned to Zeng Boyan and said flatly, “The common folk run small businesses. Make sure you pay for the damaged items.”","Zeng Boyan’s face stiffened, and he gave an awkward twitch of his lips.","“Of course we’ll pay. We’ll certainly give extra.”","After who knows how long, the disturbance upstairs finally stopped.","Yang Zhong quickly led people to clear the wreckage downstairs.","Yang Cenan was staying in the Celestial Best Room, which had been decorated with several vases and ornaments—now all reduced to trash.","Just the porcelain shards filled two dustpans, plus spilled food and soup that left a trail all the way down. Even the clothes rack had been snapped in half.","After throwing everything out, Yang Zhong instructed the innkeeper, “Send a waiter up to clean the room. Buy new furnishings, and make sure they’re finer quality.”","A fifty-tael silver note was placed on the counter. The innkeeper shot it a bitter glance before picking it up reluctantly.","He turned to instruct the waiter, subtly winking as he spoke.","“Hurry up and clean.”","Get it done while County Princess Linghui is still here, in case she loses her temper and no one can shield them.","The waiter assigned to clean moved as if his backside were on fire, his hands flying like invisible shadows. He was done in less than half an hour.","By the time Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue entered the room, the water stains on the floor hadn’t even dried yet.","Throughout the entire treatment, Yang Cenan remained silent. He sat motionless on the bed, his eyes looking as if they wanted to devour someone.","The physician’s hands kept trembling as he held the needle, missing the correct spots several times until Song Jinzhao corrected him.","After leaving the inn, Song Shixue said, “Elder Sister, I don’t think his recovery will go well.”","Song Jinzhao replied, “The nerves in his face haven’t shown any improvement. The facial paralysis probably won’t heal.”"]}]);
